ng_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/0d0d5e3d081c1a15559d75e6406e4e51a3c22b37/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:38:38Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:38:38Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"feat: serve the codex copy from the translations API\n\nThe page was the last hardcoded English on the site. Its text now comes from\napps/api/data/translations.json under codex.subtitle, codex.title, codex.lede,\ncodex.rendering and codex.foundations, in both languages, and the page reads\nthem through TranslationProvider like the homepage does.\n\nHardcoding was also what kept /codex alive when the API is down, so the shell\ngains the fallback snapshot the content app already had, covering codex.* only.\nThe 404 page has its own hardcoded link and the navigation labels never render\nduring an outage, because the nodes resolve to an empty list at the same time.\ntranslation-fallback.spec.ts guards it against drift the same way.\n\nVerified with the API listener stopped: /codex returns 200 with the real copy\nand no bracketed keys.","tree":{"sha":"bf1e8f6487b21b07764e5b379b0b83eb70420ccb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/bf1e8f6487b21b07764e5b379b0b83eb70420ccb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/0d0d5e3d081c1a15559d75e6406e4e51a3c22b37","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/0d0d5e3d081c1a15559d75e6406e4e51a3c22b37","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKDBkMGQ1ZTNkMDgxYzFhMTU1NTlkNzVlNjQwNmU0ZTUxYTNjMjJiMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/bbdf734f16029fdb787df4b3be41eb4bd85ccb9b","sha":"bbdf734f16029fdb787df4b3be41eb4bd85ccb9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/bbdf734f16029fdb787df4b3be41eb4bd85ccb9b"}],"sha":"0d0d5e3d081c1a15559d75e6406e4e51a3c22b37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/0d0d5e3d081c1a15559d75e6406e4e51a3c22b37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/bbdf734f16029fdb787df4b3be41eb4bd85ccb9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:33:20Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:33:20Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"refactor(shell): rewrite the codex copy\n\nNames the pattern in the first line, which tells a technical reader the shape\nfaster than describing it does, and drops the paragraph explaining why a data\nservice exists. Nothing was gained by justifying the presence of something\nunremarkable.\n\nFixes \"it''s federated parts\" to the possessive, hyphenates micro-frontend to\nmatch AGENTS.md and server-side rendered, and capitalises React and TypeScript.\n\nThe Nx caching and per-container deployment lines are gone with this trim. Only\n\"the build process\" in the shared list still points at any of it.","tree":{"sha":"337b319b80ef4a33a072409dcece95c2c8e9321b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/337b319b80ef4a33a072409dcece95c2c8e9321b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/bbdf734f16029fdb787df4b3be41eb4bd85ccb9b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/bbdf734f16029fdb787df4b3be41eb4bd85ccb9b","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKGJiZGY3MzRmMTYwMjlmZGI3ODdkZjRiM2JlNDFlYjRiZDg1Y2NiOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/4b4a843074a5a64d5894374871ced5ad679b37d7","sha":"4b4a843074a5a64d5894374871ced5ad679b37d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/4b4a843074a5a64d5894374871ced5ad679b37d7"}],"sha":"bbdf734f16029fdb787df4b3be41eb4bd85ccb9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/bbdf734f16029fdb787df4b3be41eb4bd85ccb9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/4b4a843074a5a64d5894374871ced5ad679b37d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:21:43Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:21:43Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"refactor(shell): drop the app names from the codex, and stop overselling the API\n\nShell, Content and API are folder names in this repository, not architecture. A\nreader does not need to know what the host is called, only that there is one, so\nthe definition list is gone and the roles are described in prose.\n\nThe API entry was also inventing a rationale. It read as a deliberate\ncontent-as-data layer with a CMS behind it, when the service exists because an\nenterprise application queries data from somewhere and that path has to work\nthrough server rendering and hydration before anything is built on it. Framing\nit as one of three peers gave it a third of the page, which is more weight than\nit earns.\n\nRemoves the dl, dt and dd rules from Codex.module.scss, which now have nothing\nto style.","tree":{"sha":"9ecdec82ce9b8fe04c7b6f8e33943a00ea8e544d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/9ecdec82ce9b8fe04c7b6f8e33943a00ea8e544d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/4b4a843074a5a64d5894374871ced5ad679b37d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/4b4a843074a5a64d5894374871ced5ad679b37d7","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKDRiNGE4NDMwNzRhNWE2NGQ1ODk0Mzc0ODcxY2VkNWFkNjc5YjM3ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/fdb28d36b493065c56122331449e09f861e79073","sha":"fdb28d36b493065c56122331449e09f861e79073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/fdb28d36b493065c56122331449e09f861e79073"}],"sha":"4b4a843074a5a64d5894374871ced5ad679b37d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/4b4a843074a5a64d5894374871ced5ad679b37d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/fdb28d36b493065c56122331449e09f861e79073/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:14:28Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:14:28Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"refactor(shell): write the codex for the reader instead of about the site\n\nThe page opened by describing the homepage the reader had just left, which\nspends the two sentences that matter on what they can already see. Three drafts\nrunning it also opened by apologising for the site being small, a defensive\nframe that makes the page argue against itself before it claims anything.\n\nIt now says what the thing is and what the hard part is: services that deploy\non their own being composed into one server-rendered page while the request is\nstill open. Each entry says what it buys a team rather than what it is made of,\nand the closing paragraph covers the shared layer, which is the part that\nmatters when more than one team is working.\n\nAlso corrects a claim from two commits ago. \"Changing either takes no build at\nall\" was false: translations.json is imported into the API bundle, so copy\nchanges need an API rebuild and redeploy. What is true is that the front end\nnever rebuilds and nothing in it depends on where the data came from, which is\nthe claim worth making anyway.","tree":{"sha":"6ffdd4bf654e91d7b370c1c027bc0c29ba5cfcb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/6ffdd4bf654e91d7b370c1c027bc0c29ba5cfcb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/fdb28d36b493065c56122331449e09f861e79073","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/fdb28d36b493065c56122331449e09f861e79073","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKGZkYjI4ZDM2YjQ5MzA2NWM1NjEyMjMzMTQ0OWUwOWY4NjFlNzkwNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/ec2b7aff1e70ada48f89c1f375ec2aa2ab01d37c","sha":"ec2b7aff1e70ada48f89c1f375ec2aa2ab01d37c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/ec2b7aff1e70ada48f89c1f375ec2aa2ab01d37c"}],"sha":"fdb28d36b493065c56122331449e09f861e79073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/fdb28d36b493065c56122331449e09f861e79073"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/ec2b7aff1e70ada48f89c1f375ec2aa2ab01d37c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:10:31Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:10:31Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"fix(shell): correct two false claims in the codex copy\n\n\"This site is one page\" was wrong twice. The site has /, /codex, /offline and a\n404, and the second of those was added three commits ago. It is also a\nreact-router app, so \"one page\" reads as single-page application, which is a\nclaim about client-side routing and not about scope. The opening now describes\nwhat the homepage actually holds.\n\n\"Design tokens are generated from Figma\" was an overclaim. packages/figma has\none script, style-dictionary build, and no sync of any kind; tokens.json is\nhand-edited in a format the Figma plugin can round-trip. The line now says what\nthe file does.\n\nSentence-length spread drops from 7.7 to 6.0, because the five-word sentence\nholding it up was the false one. The number was measuring something that should\nnot have been in the copy.","tree":{"sha":"5412689666ad11c98dfdc2e8e06800b65517cae2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/5412689666ad11c98dfdc2e8e06800b65517cae2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/ec2b7aff1e70ada48f89c1f375ec2aa2ab01d37c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/ec2b7aff1e70ada48f89c1f375ec2aa2ab01d37c","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKGVjMmI3YWZmMWU3MGFkYTQ4Zjg5YzFmMzc1ZWMyYWEyYWIwMWQzN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/1d3b6ca530ebc0b5a62378a4b857851b871d0a19","sha":"1d3b6ca530ebc0b5a62378a4b857851b871d0a19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/1d3b6ca530ebc0b5a62378a4b857851b871d0a19"}],"sha":"ec2b7aff1e70ada48f89c1f375ec2aa2ab01d37c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/ec2b7aff1e70ada48f89c1f375ec2aa2ab01d37c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/1d3b6ca530ebc0b5a62378a4b857851b871d0a19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:06:20Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:06:20Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"refactor(shell): rewrite the codex copy against the stylometric audit\n\nRan the check the audit says to run after a draft exists, which I had not been\ndoing. Sentence-length spread went from 4.9 to 7.7, the longest sentence from 18\nwords to 34, and four constructions came out.\n\n- \"One page is what it happens to serve.\" An inversion of \"it serves one page\"\n  that bought nothing but the sound of having been composed.\n- \"At this size none of it is necessary. It is here so it does not have to be\n  retrofitted later.\" Paradox as punchline, standing alone to close the page.\n  Both are on the list. The caveat was worth keeping, so it moved into the lede\n  as a plain statement and the page now ends on a fact about containers.\n- \"The structure underneath assumes many more.\" An abstraction given a\n  cognitive verb.\n- \"Copy and navigation live here instead of in a build\" was the X-not-Y flip,\n  and two of the three definitions opened on the same bare noun fragment.\n\nNothing about the architecture claim changed.","tree":{"sha":"77cc46db70692e856cd99e615bed1ab7e056d71d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/77cc46db70692e856cd99e615bed1ab7e056d71d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/1d3b6ca530ebc0b5a62378a4b857851b871d0a19","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/1d3b6ca530ebc0b5a62378a4b857851b871d0a19","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKDFkM2I2Y2E1MzBlYmMwYjVhNjIzNzhhNGI4NTc4NTFiODcxZDBhMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/0e1c504f10f250364aa7cd25cf134137754d2fdd","sha":"0e1c504f10f250364aa7cd25cf134137754d2fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/0e1c504f10f250364aa7cd25cf134137754d2fdd"}],"sha":"1d3b6ca530ebc0b5a62378a4b857851b871d0a19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/1d3b6ca530ebc0b5a62378a4b857851b871d0a19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/0e1c504f10f250364aa7cd25cf134137754d2fdd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:00:15Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:00:15Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"refactor(shell): reframe the codex around what the architecture is for\n\nThe previous copy sold the project as a curiosity — how far server-rendered\nReact gets without a framework — which is the wrong claim. The structure is\nsized for enterprise applications, and this site is the smallest thing that\nexercises it.\n\nEvery entry now says what it buys at scale rather than what it is: the shell\ntakes a new remote as a configuration entry, the content team deploys without\nwaiting on the shell, and copy and navigation are a data change instead of a\nbuild. Closes on the honest part, that none of it is necessary at one page.","tree":{"sha":"9010604313a245ff67e0cb2eedd20f6df6d6aa14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/9010604313a245ff67e0cb2eedd20f6df6d6aa14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/0e1c504f10f250364aa7cd25cf134137754d2fdd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/0e1c504f10f250364aa7cd25cf134137754d2fdd","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKDBlMWM1MDRmMTBmMjUwMzY0YWE3Y2QyNWNmMTM0MTM3NzU0ZDJmZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/a74f2e5a15eb2e813e8f7036a6a0f0f4a99f37b4","sha":"a74f2e5a15eb2e813e8f7036a6a0f0f4a99f37b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/a74f2e5a15eb2e813e8f7036a6a0f0f4a99f37b4"}],"sha":"0e1c504f10f250364aa7cd25cf134137754d2fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/0e1c504f10f250364aa7cd25cf134137754d2fdd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/a74f2e5a15eb2e813e8f7036a6a0f0f4a99f37b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:51:31Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:51:31Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"refactor(shell): cut the codex copy down\n\nFrom roughly 280 words to 110. The section headings went with it — at this\nlength they were scaffolding for text that no longer exists, so the page is now\na lede, the three applications, and a closing line.\n\nDrops the h2 rules from both Codex.module.scss and _global.scss. Nothing in the\nrepository renders an h2 any more, and the global one was added in this branch\nfor headings the codex no longer has.","tree":{"sha":"a61cf668238877fea8a691eb8dbaf3c88f6a5db0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/a61cf668238877fea8a691eb8dbaf3c88f6a5db0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/a74f2e5a15eb2e813e8f7036a6a0f0f4a99f37b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/a74f2e5a15eb2e813e8f7036a6a0f0f4a99f37b4","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKGE3NGYyZTVhMTVlYjJlODEzZThmNzAzNmE2YTBmMGY0YTk5ZjM3YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/b5ba377dac560bb169a5ba63b428f64daf87c656","sha":"b5ba377dac560bb169a5ba63b428f64daf87c656","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/b5ba377dac560bb169a5ba63b428f64daf87c656"}],"sha":"a74f2e5a15eb2e813e8f7036a6a0f0f4a99f37b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/a74f2e5a15eb2e813e8f7036a6a0f0f4a99f37b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/b5ba377dac560bb169a5ba63b428f64daf87c656/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:44:31Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:44:31Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"fix(content): degrade the homepage instead of returning 500 when the API is down\n\nBoth of the content remote''s queries threw, and render.tsx turns anything thrown\nduring SSR into a 500 for the whole page. The shell''s pages were hardened when\nthe navigation was wired up; the homepage was not.\n\n- The navigation query resolves to an empty list, and Content now omits the\n  <nav> entirely rather than rendering an empty landmark a screen reader would\n  still announce.\n- The translation query falls back to a snapshot of the hero copy. Returning\n  empty keys would have rendered [hero.title] and [hero.text] to visitors, which\n  is worse than an error page, so the fallback carries real text.\n\nThe snapshot is the one thing here that can rot: it is only ever rendered during\nan outage, so nothing in normal use would reveal it going stale.\ntranslation-fallback.spec.ts reads apps/api/data/translations.json and asserts\nthe fallback covers every hero.* key with identical copy. Confirmed it fails on\ndrift by changing one character before committing.\n\nReading the file in a test rather than importing it keeps the content app free\nof a build-time dependency on a sibling app.\n\nWith the API stopped: / returns 200 with the real hero copy and no nav, /codex\n200, /nope still 404 with its return link, /offline untouched. Output is\nunchanged while the API is up — the Linux visual baselines still match.","tree":{"sha":"c066dd2a538ba4faf7cd23da6c47601665d849a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/c066dd2a538ba4faf7cd23da6c47601665d849a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/b5ba377dac560bb169a5ba63b428f64daf87c656","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/b5ba377dac560bb169a5ba63b428f64daf87c656","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKGI1YmEzNzdkYWM1NjBiYjE2OWE1YmE2M2I0MjhmNjRkYWY4N2M2NTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/73eab0ca2a31d841d3ecfbc746972ffc05471f09","sha":"73eab0ca2a31d841d3ecfbc746972ffc05471f09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/73eab0ca2a31d841d3ecfbc746972ffc05471f09"}],"sha":"b5ba377dac560bb169a5ba63b428f64daf87c656","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/b5ba377dac560bb169a5ba63b428f64daf87c656"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/73eab0ca2a31d841d3ecfbc746972ffc05471f09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:39:26Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:39:26Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"test(e2e): regenerate the Linux visual baselines\n\nRendered in mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.62.0-noble, the same image the CI\ne2e job pins, so the baselines match what CI will produce.\n\nThe full suite passes in that image: 50 tests, including the four visual specs\nthat skip on macOS.","tree":{"sha":"db921acd560ac800892ceef0f36f9540f27e8c27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/db921acd560ac800892ceef0f36f9540f27e8c27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/73eab0ca2a31d841d3ecfbc746972ffc05471f09","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/73eab0ca2a31d841d3ecfbc746972ffc05471f09","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKDczZWFiMGNhMmEzMWQ4NDFkM2VjZmJjNzQ2OTcyZmZjMDU0NzFmMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/43bda9dfaeb8a41af327d50122d8a97d4ffca865","sha":"43bda9dfaeb8a41af327d50122d8a97d4ffca865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/43bda9dfaeb8a41af327d50122d8a97d4ffca865"}],"sha":"73eab0ca2a31d841d3ecfbc746972ffc05471f09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/73eab0ca2a31d841d3ecfbc746972ffc05471f09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/43bda9dfaeb8a41af327d50122d8a97d4ffca865/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:37:12Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:37:12Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"refactor: drop the Codex nav item, the mark carries it\n\nThe homepage nav is back to the three profile links, and C·V·Q·O is the only way\ninto the codex.\n\nRemoves the `hero-codex` node from navigation.json and the `hero.nav.codex`\ntranslation key along with it — an unreferenced label is the same dead data this\nbranch has been clearing out elsewhere.\n\nThe e2e test that clicked the nav item is gone. What it actually covered, the\nhand-off from a link rendered by the content remote to a route owned by the\nshell, is now covered by the mark, which crosses the same boundary. Its\nassertion on the codex heading moves there.","tree":{"sha":"a822df43c835a1c668c2e122974f530ab9978b4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/a822df43c835a1c668c2e122974f530ab9978b4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/43bda9dfaeb8a41af327d50122d8a97d4ffca865","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/43bda9dfaeb8a41af327d50122d8a97d4ffca865","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKDQzYmRhOWRmYWViOGE0MWFmMzI3ZDUwMTIyZDhhOTdkNGZmY2E4NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/a6aca3e0d43736806a5f1433e049be67d1c3aa5d","sha":"a6aca3e0d43736806a5f1433e049be67d1c3aa5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/a6aca3e0d43736806a5f1433e049be67d1c3aa5d"}],"sha":"43bda9dfaeb8a41af327d50122d8a97d4ffca865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/43bda9dfaeb8a41af327d50122d8a97d4ffca865"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/a6aca3e0d43736806a5f1433e049be67d1c3aa5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:16:57Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:16:57Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"feat(content): make the C·V·Q·O mark the link to the codex\n\nThe mark carries no link styling: no underline, no weight change, no colour of\nits own. It looks exactly as it did before — the screenshots are byte-identical.\nOnly hover, which shifts it from muted to the body colour, and the focus outline\ninherited from the global anchor rule give it away.\n\nBecause nothing visual marks it, it gets an accessible name from a new\n`hero.subtitle.label` key. Read on its own, C·V·Q·O announces as four letters\nand says nothing about where the link goes.\n\nThe mark stays inert on the codex page itself, where it would only point at the\npage you are already on. The Codex entry in the homepage nav stays too, so the\npage keeps one discoverable route to the same place.\n\nAdds e2e coverage for the href, the accessible name, the absence of an underline\nand the navigation. With no visual treatment, those assertions are the only\nthing that would catch this breaking.","tree":{"sha":"358403e51eef72281973ad2a3cff83ba6a158688","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/358403e51eef72281973ad2a3cff83ba6a158688"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/a6aca3e0d43736806a5f1433e049be67d1c3aa5d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/a6aca3e0d43736806a5f1433e049be67d1c3aa5d","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKGE2YWNhM2UwZDQzNzM2ODA2YTVmMTQzM2UwNDliZTY3ZDFjM2FhNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/fdc351ea7c079e1a8e97b2fb50d12c89bc77480d","sha":"fdc351ea7c079e1a8e97b2fb50d12c89bc77480d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/fdc351ea7c079e1a8e97b2fb50d12c89bc77480d"}],"sha":"a6aca3e0d43736806a5f1433e049be67d1c3aa5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/a6aca3e0d43736806a5f1433e049be67d1c3aa5d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/fdc351ea7c079e1a8e97b2fb50d12c89bc77480d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:13:06Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T19:13:06Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"feat: drive navigation from the API instead of hardcoded links\n\nThe API had a whole navigation module — data file, service, controller, two\nroutes, tests — and nothing consumed it. Content.tsx hardcoded its own links.\nThis connects the two.\n\nContract\n- `NavigationNode`, `NavigationResponse` and `NavigationData` move into\n  @cohbrgr/localization, where `labelKey` can be typed as a `TranslationKey`.\n  Navigation data stays language-agnostic; the client resolves the labels.\n- Adds the three translation keys navigation.json already referenced or needed:\n  `notfound.nav.back` (referenced by the data, missing from translations),\n  `codex.nav.home` and `codex.nav.source`, in both languages.\n\nWiring\n- Both apps get a `navigationQueryOptions`, cached like translations.\n- The homepage nav is fetched by the content remote from /navigation/hero and\n  rendered as plain anchors, including for internal paths. The remote must not\n  reach for the host''s router.\n- The shell gets an ApiNavigation component used by the codex and 404 pages. It\n  renders internal paths as react-router links, so client-side navigation off\n  the 404 page still works, and external ones as anchors with rel=noopener.\n- The shell''s translationQueryOptions was dead code; it now backs ApiNavigation.\n\nResilience\n- Offline deliberately keeps its hardcoded link. It is the service worker''s\n  offline fallback and has to render with no network at all.\n- The shell''s navigation and translation queries resolve to empty values rather\n  than throwing. render.tsx turns any error thrown during SSR into a 500, so a\n  throw would have converted the 404 page into a server error whenever the API\n  was down. Verified with the API stopped: /codex returns 200 without a nav,\n  /nope still returns 404 and falls back to a hardcoded return link, /offline is\n  untouched. The homepage still 500s there, which predates this change — the\n  content remote''s own translation query throws.\n\nRendered output is byte-identical to before on every page and viewport.","tree":{"sha":"58e060e76757c7c97c8f43b9db7b54ecfc4aee99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/58e060e76757c7c97c8f43b9db7b54ecfc4aee99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/fdc351ea7c079e1a8e97b2fb50d12c89bc77480d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/fdc351ea7c079e1a8e97b2fb50d12c89bc77480d","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKGZkYzM1MWVhN2MwNzllMWE4ZTk3YjJmYjUwZDEyYzg5YmM3NzQ4MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/52d5aef3f9f68fc02cb3a1cef86908fb1c0f093e","sha":"52d5aef3f9f68fc02cb3a1cef86908fb1c0f093e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/52d5aef3f9f68fc02cb3a1cef86908fb1c0f093e"}],"sha":"fdc351ea7c079e1a8e97b2fb50d12c89bc77480d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/fdc351ea7c079e1a8e97b2fb50d12c89bc77480d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/52d5aef3f9f68fc02cb3a1cef86908fb1c0f093e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:28:21Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:28:21Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"feat(shell): add the /codex route and make the mark mean something\n\nThe monogram was `c.f.k.o`, which looked right and told a visitor nothing. It\nbecomes C·V·Q·O, and there is now a page behind it explaining what the\nrepository is for.\n\n- New `/codex` route rendered by the shell, following the NotFound and Offline\n  pattern. Keeping it out of the content remote means the explainer survives\n  the remote being unhealthy, and it needs no federation config.\n- The homepage nav gains a Codex link. It is a plain anchor rather than a\n  react-router Link: the link is rendered by the content remote, and giving the\n  remote a Link would make it depend on a Router the host supplies, which breaks\n  it standalone. The remote names a URL and the host decides what to do with it.\n- Copy is hardcoded English, as NotFound and Offline already are. The nav label\n  goes through the translation layer since the content remote renders it.\n- `navigation.json` gains the codex nodes so the API data matches what is on the\n  page. That endpoint is still not consumed by the frontend.\n- Monogram tracking drops from 0.32em to 0.2em now that the mark carries its own\n  separators.\n\nPage typography is scoped to Codex.module.scss: the h1 scales against the\nreading measure rather than the viewport, since here it heads a column of\nrunning text instead of acting as a nameplate. Terms in the definition list sit\ntight against their descriptions and apart from each other, so the three\napplications read as three things rather than six.\n\nAdds e2e coverage for the route and for the cross-boundary link.","tree":{"sha":"69b4cc8ce672272a055487d41ba49ed1c6b8a80b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/69b4cc8ce672272a055487d41ba49ed1c6b8a80b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/52d5aef3f9f68fc02cb3a1cef86908fb1c0f093e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/52d5aef3f9f68fc02cb3a1cef86908fb1c0f093e","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKDUyZDVhZWYzZjlmNjhmYzAyY2IzYTFjZWY4NjkwOGZiMWMwZjA5M2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/8e1969de10cf22d8fcb2b226cfbac942b3a9dfe9","sha":"8e1969de10cf22d8fcb2b226cfbac942b3a9dfe9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/8e1969de10cf22d8fcb2b226cfbac942b3a9dfe9"}],"sha":"52d5aef3f9f68fc02cb3a1cef86908fb1c0f093e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/52d5aef3f9f68fc02cb3a1cef86908fb1c0f093e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/8e1969de10cf22d8fcb2b226cfbac942b3a9dfe9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:08:20Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T18:08:20Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"feat(shell): rework homepage design — one composition, stronger type, real links\n\nLayout\n- One composition at every width. `.layout` was `height: 100vh` with\n  `align-content: space-between` below 1024px and `height: unset` above it,\n  which put the empty space in the middle of the narrow view and at the bottom\n  of the wide one. Now a single `align-content: center` grid with asymmetric\n  top/bottom padding, so the block lands around 40% down at any size.\n- Page gutter moves from `main` and `nav` onto the layout, which is what keeps\n  the heading and the link row flush at every width. Drops the duplicated\n  `orientation: portrait` / `min-width: 768px` rule.\n- `min-height: 100svh` replaces the `-webkit-fill-available` hack, and the\n  `overflow-x: hidden` / `max-width: 100vw` workaround on body is gone.\n\nTypography\n- h1 goes from a flat 1.8/2rem to clamp(2.25rem, 6vw + 0.5rem, 4rem) with\n  -0.02em tracking, since Georgia is cut for body copy and loosens when scaled\n  up.\n- Body line-height 1.618 to 1.45; the intro read as two loose lines rather than\n  one block. Heading line-height 1.08 with `text-wrap: balance` so the German\n  title wraps cleanly on a phone.\n- Restores the `c.f.k.o` monogram, which had styling and a translation key but\n  was never rendered.\n\nColour\n- Palette moves out of _variables.scss into the Style Dictionary source, so\n  @cohbrgr/figma generates what the site actually uses instead of emitting\n  unused #fff/#000. Adds muted and accent roles, drops the unused gradient and\n  the nine colours nothing referenced.\n- Dark background warms from #2c2c2c to #2a2926 so both modes share a\n  temperature. Contrast holds at 6.77:1 light and 7.13:1 dark.\n- One accent, terracotta, used on the full stop after the name and on links at\n  hover.\n- `color-scheme` declared per mode so scrollbars and form controls follow.\n\nLinks\n- Resting 1px underline with an offset. Bold alone made the inline Netconomy\n  link read as an emphasised company name, and hover-only affordance does not\n  exist on touch at all.\n- `:focus-visible` outline in the accent, replacing underline-on-`:focus`.\n- Nav list is flex with a real gap, and `role=\"list\"` keeps list semantics in\n  Safari now that `list-style` is none.\n\nThe e2e styling assertions follow the new module rules. Linux visual baselines\nstill need regenerating.","tree":{"sha":"798f296cb6c4a3f144507838d91f4716366bc935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/798f296cb6c4a3f144507838d91f4716366bc935"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/8e1969de10cf22d8fcb2b226cfbac942b3a9dfe9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/8e1969de10cf22d8fcb2b226cfbac942b3a9dfe9","node_id":"C_kwDOFO40ItoAKDhlMTk2OWRlMTBjZjIyZDhmY2IyYjIyNmNmYmFjOTQyYjNhOWRmZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commit/9d0d0d9803435d4f28fa92c3e55113e8f6ad29db","sha":"9d0d0d9803435d4f28fa92c3e55113e8f6ad29db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/9d0d0d9803435d4f28fa92c3e55113e8f6ad29db"}],"sha":"8e1969de10cf22d8fcb2b226cfbac942b3a9dfe9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/8e1969de10cf22d8fcb2b226cfbac942b3a9dfe9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/9d0d0d9803435d4f28fa92c3e55113e8f6ad29db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T20:34:28Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T20:34:28Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"ci: build once and share via artifact; add concurrency, permissions, libc cache key\n\nEfficiency and hygiene pass on the CI workflow:\n\n- Build the workspace once in a dedicated job and share dist/ as an artifact,\n  instead of every job running a full ''pnpm run build''. lint needs no build\n  output so it runs in parallel with build; test/integration/e2e/lighthouse\n  depend on build and download the artifact. Cuts the workspace build from 5x\n  per run to 1x.\n- Add a concurrency group with cancel-in-progress so superseded runs on the\n  same ref stop instead of finishing.\n- Add a top-level least-privilege ''permissions: contents: read''; the lighthouse\n  job opts into ''statuses: write'' for LHCI status checks.\n- libc-aware pnpm store cache key (musl vs glibc): the alpine jobs and the\n  glibc Playwright job no longer share a cache that holds platform-specific\n  native binaries.\n- Narrow triggers to ''main'' (develop is being retired).\n- Remove the now-unused setup-and-build composite action.\n\nVerified locally: lint passes with no dist present (so it needn''t wait for\nbuild); test/integration/e2e require dist (hence the artifact); the build emits\ndist for 3 apps + 6 packages, matching the upload glob.","tree":{"sha":"56e29db1924fcba4add2b2d72a5d41f5f993c550","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/56e29db1924fcba4add2b2d72a5d41f5f993c550"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/9d0d0d9803435d4f28fa92c3e55113e8f6ad29db","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users