:"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/commits/e9a6d7d20618f9fadc7ff1786fa79a7f1cf1d922/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T19:22:21Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T19:22:21Z","email":"c.oberhamberger@gmail.com","name":"Christian Oberhamberger"},"message":"chore(deps): upgrade react-router to 8 and drop react-router-dom\n\nreact-router 8 removes the separate react-router-dom package; StaticRouter,\nBrowserRouter, Routes/Route and Link now all come from react-router. Swap the\nfour import sites and drop the dependency. React 19.2.8 satisfies the new\nreact-router >=19.2.7 peer.\n\nThis was unblocked by the Jest -> Vitest migration (react-router 8 is ESM-only)\nand also clears the one high-severity advisory that reached the shipped bundle\n(react-router RSC-mode CSRF; not exploitable here since this is classic SSR, but\nresolved regardless).\n\nBuild, lint, tests (233) and the full e2e suite (routing, client-side\nnavigation, 404, offline) all pass.","tree":{"sha":"4cb3c707e2ca97097625aecfd7913667781012e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/trees/4cb3c707e2ca97097625aecfd7913667781012e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oberhamberger/cohbrgr/git/commits/e9a6d7d20618f9fadc7ff1786fa79a7f1cf1d922","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8846578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oberhamberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oberhamberger","id":8846578,"login":"oberhamberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDY