"committedDate":"2026-08-13T12:24:21Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","repositoryId":354022557,"sha":"57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"maksimzinchuk","providerType":"User"},"email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-13T09:23:58Z","committedDate":"2026-08-13T09:23:58Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","repositoryId":354022557,"sha":"46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"maksimzinchuk","providerType":"User"},"email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-13T08:10:11Z","committedDate":"2026-08-13T08:10:11Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","repositoryId":354022557,"sha":"9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"maksimzinchuk","providerType":"User"},"email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-13T08:09:46Z","committedDate":"2026-08-13T08:09:46Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","repositoryId":354022557,"sha":"caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"maksimzinchuk","providerType":"User"},"email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-13T08:08:11Z","committedDate":"2026-08-13T08:08:11Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","repositoryId":354022557,"sha":"9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"maksimzinchuk","providerType":"User"},"email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-12T14:41:43Z","committedDate":"2026-08-12T14:41:43Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","repositoryId":354022557,"sha":"a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"maksimzinchuk","providerType":"User"},"email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-12T14:23:00Z","committedDate":"2026-08-12T14:23:00Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","repositoryId":354022557,"sha":"49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"maksimzinchuk","providerType":"User"},"email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-12T14:16:25Z","committedDate":"2026-08-12T14:16:25Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","repositoryId":354022557,"sha":"30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:38:30.899Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/386bac18be966e5ebf976eda22dd523d55299291/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:54:04Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:54:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-file-upload): check dropped files against the rules too (VM-1832) (#385)\n\n## Problem (VM-1832)\nIn `VcFileUpload`, a file **picked** through the browse dialog goes\nthrough `handleChange` and then `validate()`, and `upload` is emitted\nonly if the file is valid. A file **dropped** onto the zone was emitted\nstraight away. Rules such as `mindimensions` and `fileWeight` were\ntherefore skipped for drops.\n\n`VcImageUpload` and the empty state of `VcGallery` render\n`VcFileUpload`, so they had the same gap. vendor-portal''s seller logo\n(`mindimensions: [120, 120]`, `fileWeight: 1024`) is where this was\nfound.\n\n## Fix\n`onDrop` now runs the same check as `upload`. The framework''s file rules\nread `value.files`. A `DataTransfer` carries `.files` just like the file\ninput, so it is passed to `handleChange` as is.\n\n## Tests (`vc-file-upload.validation.test.ts`, new)\nThese use the real vee-validate and the framework''s rules (`fileWeight`,\nsince `mindimensions` loads an image and jsdom cannot):\n- a picked file that breaks a rule is refused;\n- a dropped file that breaks a rule is refused;\n- a dropped file that passes the rules is uploaded.\n\nRED check: with the source reverted, the dropped-file test fails. Full\nframework suite with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`: **425\nfiles / 4273 tests passed**. typecheck, eslint, prettier and\n`check:circular` are clean.\n\n## Verified in a real browser, locally\nvendor-portal was built against this branch and run against vcmp-qa. A\n50×50 PNG was dropped onto the seller logo:\n\n| Build | Result |\n|---|---|\n| this branch | no upload request; the field shows \"Image dimensions\nmust be greater than 120*120\" |\n| stock 2.6.3-rc.0 | `POST /api/assets` fires and the field shows\n\"Uploading...\" |\n\n## Not covered here, for the reviewer\nWhen `VcGallery` already holds images, it has two upload paths of its\nown that also skip `rules`:\n- the header upload input (`onFileInputChange`);\n- the drop-anywhere overlay (`onGlobalDrop`).\n\nBoth call `upload.onUpload` directly. Fixing them needs validation\ninside the gallery and a place to show the error, which is a design\nchoice. I left it for a follow-up.","tree":{"sha":"d666f080c6e4a24cd995c31bb9cf0bd285ababd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/d666f080c6e4a24cd995c31bb9cf0bd285ababd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/386bac18be966e5ebf976eda22dd523d55299291","verification":{"payload":"tree d666f080c6e4a24cd995c31bb9cf0bd285ababd6\nparent 96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1791377644 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791377644 +0300\n\nfix(vc-file-upload): check dropped files against the rules too (VM-1832) (#385)\n\n## Problem (VM-1832)\nIn `VcFileUpload`, a file **picked** through the browse dialog goes\nthrough `handleChange` and then `validate()`, and `upload` is emitted\nonly if the file is valid. A file **dropped** onto the zone was emitted\nstraight away. Rules such as `mindimensions` and `fileWeight` were\ntherefore skipped for drops.\n\n`VcImageUpload` and the empty state of `VcGallery` render\n`VcFileUpload`, so they had the same gap. vendor-portal''s seller logo\n(`mindimensions: [120, 120]`, `fileWeight: 1024`) is where this was\nfound.\n\n## Fix\n`onDrop` now runs the same check as `upload`. The framework''s file rules\nread `value.files`. A `DataTransfer` carries `.files` just like the file\ninput, so it is passed to `handleChange` as is.\n\n## Tests (`vc-file-upload.validation.test.ts`, new)\nThese use the real vee-validate and the framework''s rules (`fileWeight`,\nsince `mindimensions` loads an image and jsdom cannot):\n- a picked file that breaks a rule is refused;\n- a dropped file that breaks a rule is refused;\n- a dropped file that passes the rules is uploaded.\n\nRED check: with the source reverted, the dropped-file test fails. Full\nframework suite with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`: **425\nfiles / 4273 tests passed**. typecheck, eslint, prettier and\n`check:circular` are clean.\n\n## Verified in a real browser, locally\nvendor-portal was built against this branch and run against vcmp-qa. A\n50×50 PNG was dropped onto the seller logo:\n\n| Build | Result |\n|---|---|\n| this branch | no upload request; the field shows \"Image dimensions\nmust be greater than 120*120\" |\n| stock 2.6.3-rc.0 | `POST /api/assets` fires and the field shows\n\"Uploading...\" |\n\n## Not covered here, for the reviewer\nWhen `VcGallery` already holds images, it has two upload paths of its\nown that also skip `rules`:\n- the header upload input (`onFileInputChange`);\n- the drop-anywhere overlay (`onGlobalDrop`).\n\nBoth call `upload.onUpload` directly. Fixing them needs validation\ninside the gallery and a place to show the error, which is a design\nchoice. I left it for a follow-up.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxkDsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFGcQALEqEQSifuYc04P/1jMratFk\nR6g+0BwSOUAsqpte+smby1q5bo57psXQu69kmiPHQOoxQ+R1m6AACHqQNJQo0JBt\nunjd1OdQ/A3EZXwebbi4Rtl5QjINuMxzZoum2MhMHyLGSehpNuAdFqyhpD7FcaDY\ncIntbBk6RUAs9ENIOwwUVkLqfqbABW50QG0gj6jixVTFsgRxKfxDOHHoC9vt2aA5\nRLUqv10m8O97TY8KA2gxEGfv1ZFLoMQeyk3j6Xs9rvaz3zAxJPLTX5rWuiZnSEgr\nkR3MaAzWirETUCfJcXVFqMMSUUVpuX2/tukiOq07WS+wA+dP3f8Sm5cncUW0dWBI\nGsebI8ZhDPtcIXDdJs5iTlOvO1eGVKQi3DmNIhr8hiByU5vxVvujAygcPxqPYwch\niVG8hvEggPMzzSKInSORRfI21DvmQsCpBiJ1gvZ9nHpx2pX6OEEz9vMTRoGsyP0A\nRbfxy7tmc5/9FmS8EemOxtg6lK0xZWgJeEW0yj0B/0Jy74cTzWRC9lN3Pyq6bgY0\nf6N0/qUSQBEqfvE9fmakNx6CCu/UgfgqrHydk2x0n/aMQRla47TeC037wys8ZP05\nFX0LslqcfM0lGu8FxIkllfB4Wl/CaAu5vxlZTcnooOgm/zA0q4rMiELQz1KeXx82\nwzEIrEeoKRs7fmemH8NZ\n=m6+1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T12:54:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/386bac18be966e5ebf976eda22dd523d55299291","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDM4NmJhYzE4YmU5NjZlNWViZjk3NmVkYTIyZGQ1MjNkNTUyOTkyOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19","sha":"96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19"}],"sha":"386bac18be966e5ebf976eda22dd523d55299291","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/386bac18be966e5ebf976eda22dd523d55299291"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:53:47Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:53:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-input): put native input attributes on the input, not the wrapper (VM-1833) (#384)\n\n## Problem (VM-1833)\n`VcInput` sets `inheritAttrs: false` and binds every leftover attribute\nto its **root element**. So native input attributes written on the\ncomponent never reached the `<input>`: `min`, `max`, `minlength`,\n`pattern` and `inputmode` landed on the wrapping div and had no effect.\n\nvendor-portal''s configuration section passes `:min=\"1\"` to its\nmax-length field, and it was silently ignored. Any `:min`/`:max` set on\na `VcInput` in an app was ignored the same way.\n\nThe `step` prop has the same flaw: it is declared with a default of\n`\"1\"` but was never bound to the input.\n\n## Fix\n- `NATIVE_INPUT_ATTRS` (`min`, `max`, `minlength`, `pattern`,\n`inputmode`) is split off the attrs and bound to the native `<input>`.\nEverything else (`data-test-id`, `id`, `style`, listeners) stays on the\nroot, so automation contracts that read `data-test-id` from the wrapper\nkeep working.\n- `step` is bound to the input **only when given**. Its default changes\nfrom `\"1\"` to none: binding a default of 1 would make every decimal\nvalue of a number input `:invalid`, and the spinner would step by whole\nnumbers. `vc-input.docs.md` is updated to match.\n\nNote: native `min` does not stop a user from *typing* a lower value. It\ndrives the spinner, `:invalid` and form validity. An app that must\nreject a value still validates it. vendor-portal does that for its\nmax-length field in a separate PR.\n\n## Tests (`vc-input.test.ts`)\n- `min`/`max`/`minlength`/`pattern`/`inputmode` are on the input, not on\nthe wrapper.\n- `data-test-id` stays on the wrapper.\n- `step` is on the input when given, and absent otherwise.\n- RED check: with `vc-input.vue` reverted and the tests kept, 2 tests\nfail.\n\nFull framework suite with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`:\n**424 files / 4273 tests passed**. typecheck, eslint and prettier are\nclean.","tree":{"sha":"82b2c91ca7eeba8ef446ce8cad93ebb35211bd83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/82b2c91ca7eeba8ef446ce8cad93ebb35211bd83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19","verification":{"payload":"tree 82b2c91ca7eeba8ef446ce8cad93ebb35211bd83\nparent 673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1791377627 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791377627 +0300\n\nfix(vc-input): put native input attributes on the input, not the wrapper (VM-1833) (#384)\n\n## Problem (VM-1833)\n`VcInput` sets `inheritAttrs: false` and binds every leftover attribute\nto its **root element**. So native input attributes written on the\ncomponent never reached the `<input>`: `min`, `max`, `minlength`,\n`pattern` and `inputmode` landed on the wrapping div and had no effect.\n\nvendor-portal''s configuration section passes `:min=\"1\"` to its\nmax-length field, and it was silently ignored. Any `:min`/`:max` set on\na `VcInput` in an app was ignored the same way.\n\nThe `step` prop has the same flaw: it is declared with a default of\n`\"1\"` but was never bound to the input.\n\n## Fix\n- `NATIVE_INPUT_ATTRS` (`min`, `max`, `minlength`, `pattern`,\n`inputmode`) is split off the attrs and bound to the native `<input>`.\nEverything else (`data-test-id`, `id`, `style`, listeners) stays on the\nroot, so automation contracts that read `data-test-id` from the wrapper\nkeep working.\n- `step` is bound to the input **only when given**. Its default changes\nfrom `\"1\"` to none: binding a default of 1 would make every decimal\nvalue of a number input `:invalid`, and the spinner would step by whole\nnumbers. `vc-input.docs.md` is updated to match.\n\nNote: native `min` does not stop a user from *typing* a lower value. It\ndrives the spinner, `:invalid` and form validity. An app that must\nreject a value still validates it. vendor-portal does that for its\nmax-length field in a separate PR.\n\n## Tests (`vc-input.test.ts`)\n- `min`/`max`/`minlength`/`pattern`/`inputmode` are on the input, not on\nthe wrapper.\n- `data-test-id` stays on the wrapper.\n- `step` is on the input when given, and absent otherwise.\n- RED check: with `vc-input.vue` reverted and the tests kept, 2 tests\nfail.\n\nFull framework suite with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`:\n**424 files / 4273 tests passed**. typecheck, eslint and prettier are\nclean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxkDbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHWIQAA084Hx2DRkyfpISxtBQPItV\n/66QsM9reeCpMxaT1v3r8+6GBqwfRELB+uVrW3UBIIpdWStyGSESG25MYtCD6ghH\nltdg8uSYO2WNMRWlT6qe+EsD3lWh4+sS5zZJDKiPj6KB5tJcQRzgQsfz+2yOSrna\nTFfZs3tVEr7+x8IOxPocFJjdygh6KxilggWRguRo1uusns8qtChDg6ZVeFRbR1AB\nPKZRLMatDGuoib3VfjdPMjH6G7wCV3MbGEhhGcQ6U8ELPij4Hw1Kgz2BSSFBwpe8\nhnvRNOJwe1eciaKAVqnGnLHsW378SymK1wEWA0A5l7Tw7TOkyzmvQSDZnIYin85W\n5+kVJkbfiB2b8Hp13LLIW4IbyP+l39o+3XtrXLO6IJQ+J1hVXMFaFEVIxZ5QjoX8\nkqbfHZDkHAdDH+/BDPk/FDabh65/Ddv9ajpiBFcAs1d/UKnp4cLqNLZLcdlQ4Mtm\nVPOVc7H0eBesUaViy8L8+fPtbWNdxSByeEAUrWO/Mmg80AbT+GkTxKFi2uTCSJwr\ne8guVlCXthvuW4yMogjPTOyD0r3/izuGzedpPxpiMAHi8x2wsUmxUCNd0gzn/z/h\ntDBenBcZQcp5Nlf2RdWsaNq4y6t5igrjuPqr+VrvnNW457MJfhclyEacEmRpKVP3\nEyacvldv6CMFnehOhx3f\n=YiXg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T12:53:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDk2YzI1YmM3N2UyZTk2OTFiNzBhOTMwZTA2MGViM2E4MDA5NjFkMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4","sha":"673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4"}],"sha":"96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/96c25bc77e2e9691b70a930e060eb3a800961d19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:53:36Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:53:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-data-table): leave Space and Enter from cell controls to the controls (VM-1839) (#383)\n\n## Problem (VM-1839)\n`TableRow.vue` handles keys like this:\n\n```vue\n@keydown.enter.prevent=\"isClickable && handleClick(...)\"\n@keydown.space.prevent=\"handleSpacePress($event)\"\n```\n\nKeydowns from any control inside a cell bubble up to the row, and the\nrow called `preventDefault()` on them. As a result:\n- A `VcSwitch` or checkbox in a cell never toggled with **Space**.\nvendor-portal''s product configuration \"Default\" switch is where this was\nfound.\n- **Enter** typed into an input inside a cell also fired the row''s click\nhandler.\n\n## Fix\nBoth handlers get `.self`, so the row reacts only to keys aimed at the\nrow itself. Nothing changes for keyboard users of the row: Space on a\nfocused row still toggles its selection (`space-press`), and Enter still\nclicks it.\n\n## Tests (`TableRow.a11y.test.ts`)\n- Space on the row: `space-press` is emitted and the key is prevented.\n- Space on a checkbox in a cell: not prevented, and no `space-press`.\n- Enter on the row: the row is clicked.\n- Enter in a cell input: the row is not clicked, and the key is not\nprevented.\n\nBefore the fix the two cell-control tests fail; after it, all pass.\n\nFull framework suite with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`:\n**424 files / 4274 tests passed**. typecheck, eslint and prettier are\nclean.\n\n## Verified in a real browser, locally\nvendor-portal was built against this branch (framework packed from it)\nand run against vcmp-qa. Its `configuration-items.spec.ts` now toggles\nthe \"Default\" switch by focus + Space instead of a click:\n\n| Build | Result |\n|---|---|\n| this branch | 6/6 passed; the default is toggled by Space and stored |\n| stock 2.6.3-rc.0 | the keyboard toggle fails: the switch stays\nunchecked after Space |","tree":{"sha":"c4e2f6d4fa95662188d3c1d02508912dd774a2bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/c4e2f6d4fa95662188d3c1d02508912dd774a2bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4","verification":{"payload":"tree c4e2f6d4fa95662188d3c1d02508912dd774a2bb\nparent c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1791377616 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791377616 +0300\n\nfix(vc-data-table): leave Space and Enter from cell controls to the controls (VM-1839) (#383)\n\n## Problem (VM-1839)\n`TableRow.vue` handles keys like this:\n\n```vue\n@keydown.enter.prevent=\"isClickable && handleClick(...)\"\n@keydown.space.prevent=\"handleSpacePress($event)\"\n```\n\nKeydowns from any control inside a cell bubble up to the row, and the\nrow called `preventDefault()` on them. As a result:\n- A `VcSwitch` or checkbox in a cell never toggled with **Space**.\nvendor-portal''s product configuration \"Default\" switch is where this was\nfound.\n- **Enter** typed into an input inside a cell also fired the row''s click\nhandler.\n\n## Fix\nBoth handlers get `.self`, so the row reacts only to keys aimed at the\nrow itself. Nothing changes for keyboard users of the row: Space on a\nfocused row still toggles its selection (`space-press`), and Enter still\nclicks it.\n\n## Tests (`TableRow.a11y.test.ts`)\n- Space on the row: `space-press` is emitted and the key is prevented.\n- Space on a checkbox in a cell: not prevented, and no `space-press`.\n- Enter on the row: the row is clicked.\n- Enter in a cell input: the row is not clicked, and the key is not\nprevented.\n\nBefore the fix the two cell-control tests fail; after it, all pass.\n\nFull framework suite with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`:\n**424 files / 4274 tests passed**. typecheck, eslint and prettier are\nclean.\n\n## Verified in a real browser, locally\nvendor-portal was built against this branch (framework packed from it)\nand run against vcmp-qa. Its `configuration-items.spec.ts` now toggles\nthe \"Default\" switch by focus + Space instead of a click:\n\n| Build | Result |\n|---|---|\n| this branch | 6/6 passed; the default is toggled by Space and stored |\n| stock 2.6.3-rc.0 | the keyboard toggle fails: the switch stays\nunchecked after Space |","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxkDQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7x4QADN+PWbBy/hOm71Evp+ZIpnH\nAqL2X24FCjNmNidKU06oWuXV/s1kWZS11dS9pdj5EvVeKMFj5WwGQWG2XdO49Utx\n5QYq6BXGy9aV6WHUzpc+svq8awsrC/gV5IJXvOIuFM58Tdub4kNMAwuTxShqAgTf\nDHkyG5mR9lYPUKRubIAABopvAuMhPcnSeFNHc+WM9ozBwmP1DSYhwZ5bLvJbJqE9\nJrCO6nHXCkzczrYRfyJgSdMPYPlcG2UB55Ptv4yrM6GwMG1Pd/c0HoklFgFFz89H\n9EP/mUY/yCw2qw4q3dMHi/yp47q/alo7UfVldSxxX1wijbM5WCSbbg06TvyWdyRb\nQ/dRdjFzq4crTlVDHsV+Xt37FYW+aVZu5OpmxVLhK6sbVuXQbe19DRDIaQ99Mycp\nixvG0perOnwLk0YuFN8KvDqERN3o/MlepUqwnEbz6Pd/Pt0BSsVmusOkH2ZV90lX\n55+k9uBsPvOTj5qfz71iJfywCFoNv6NMcvq1byugQslOAjDKoxPHB1MtJn4OWd0U\n0kbGevAMwqoknlWEJ9vqKJD+opZVD+8ObSaTd4SV/zQjBO9Kx0mPGODli1a+g7Mb\n7WWu4Rqx8XrIHVDu7ZKFBcdHh7SzgPbsnnKIe4bGSaYluNsAN4m3dmX5TnWC1S31\nH1sDRWtr1xdCl2YWqJ8d\n=edrG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T12:53:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDY3M2E3MzM4MTdmYTI5MzA5MzVkZTE2MWQxMGIwODk5MmUwYWZjZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54","sha":"c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54"}],"sha":"673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/673a733817fa2930935de161d10b08992e0afcf4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:12:14Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:12:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: expose menu group state and an AssetsManager test id for automation (#382)\n\n## What\nTwo stable hooks that the vendor-portal e2e suite needs. Without them, 7\nof its rows stay blocked.\n\n### 1. Menu groups report their state and identity (`VcMenuGroup`,\n`VcMenuItem`)\n- **`aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` on the default-variant group\nheader.** The `section` variant already had them. The default variant,\nthe one `VcAppMenu` renders for nested navigation, had neither. A\ncollapsed group kept its children in the DOM with no machine-readable\nstate, so assistive technology and automation both saw items that cannot\nbe reached. `VcMenuItem` gets explicit `ariaExpanded` / `ariaControls`\nprops, bound on its `<button>`; attribute fallthrough would land them on\nthe outer wrapper. `aria-expanded=\"false\"` is rendered as a string so a\ncollapsed group keeps the attribute.\n- **`data-group-id` on every `.vc-menu-group` root.** `VcAppMenu` passes\n`group-id`, but `VcMenuGroup` declared `groupId` as a prop, so it never\nreached the DOM. A group''s `data-test-id` mirrors its parent item''s\n`routeId` and can collide with a child''s, which left automation no\nunambiguous way to address a group.\n\n### 2. `AssetsManager` gets a root `data-test-id`\n- `data-test-id=\"assets-manager-blade\"` on the blade root. Every blade\nan app opens carries one; this framework blade had only a per-instance\n`data-blade-id` and a translated title.\n\n## Tests\n- `vc-menu-group.test.ts` / `vc-menu-item.test.ts`: the header''s\n`aria-expanded` flips with the toggle, `aria-controls` points at the\nchildren region, and the group root exposes `data-group-id`.\nMutation-checked: removing the attributes fails 5 tests.\n- `assets-manager.test.ts` (new): the blade root carries the id.\nMutation-checked: removing it fails the test. `defineBlade` is stubbed\nwith `vi.hoisted`, because the framework''s test build does not run the\nblade macro.\n- Full framework suite with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`:\n**424 files / 4270 tests passed**. typecheck, eslint, prettier,\n`check:circular` and `check:layers` are clean.\n\n## Verified end to end, locally\nI built vendor-portal against this branch (the framework was packed from\nit), served it with `vite preview`, and ran the new e2e specs against\nvcmp-qa:\n\n| Spec | This branch | Stock 2.6.3-rc.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5 × open from the sidebar (products, mp-products, team, fulfillment\ncentres, seller profile): collapse the group via its toggle, expand it\nwith a real click, open the item | pass | fail: `[data-group-id]` found\n0 |\n| assets widget opens the assets manager | pass | fail:\n`assets-manager-blade` found 0 |\n| asset removed in the assets manager is gone from the product after\nSave | pass | fail: `assets-manager-blade` found 0 |\n\nThe vendor-portal side is a draft PR that waits for a framework release\ncontaining these changes.","tree":{"sha":"331ea57eecc0657dc374403c062f59d9ca23bee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/331ea57eecc0657dc374403c062f59d9ca23bee6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54","verification":{"payload":"tree 331ea57eecc0657dc374403c062f59d9ca23bee6\nparent 99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1791375134 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791375134 +0300\n\nfix: expose menu group state and an AssetsManager test id for automation (#382)\n\n## What\nTwo stable hooks that the vendor-portal e2e suite needs. Without them, 7\nof its rows stay blocked.\n\n### 1. Menu groups report their state and identity (`VcMenuGroup`,\n`VcMenuItem`)\n- **`aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` on the default-variant group\nheader.** The `section` variant already had them. The default variant,\nthe one `VcAppMenu` renders for nested navigation, had neither. A\ncollapsed group kept its children in the DOM with no machine-readable\nstate, so assistive technology and automation both saw items that cannot\nbe reached. `VcMenuItem` gets explicit `ariaExpanded` / `ariaControls`\nprops, bound on its `<button>`; attribute fallthrough would land them on\nthe outer wrapper. `aria-expanded=\"false\"` is rendered as a string so a\ncollapsed group keeps the attribute.\n- **`data-group-id` on every `.vc-menu-group` root.** `VcAppMenu` passes\n`group-id`, but `VcMenuGroup` declared `groupId` as a prop, so it never\nreached the DOM. A group''s `data-test-id` mirrors its parent item''s\n`routeId` and can collide with a child''s, which left automation no\nunambiguous way to address a group.\n\n### 2. `AssetsManager` gets a root `data-test-id`\n- `data-test-id=\"assets-manager-blade\"` on the blade root. Every blade\nan app opens carries one; this framework blade had only a per-instance\n`data-blade-id` and a translated title.\n\n## Tests\n- `vc-menu-group.test.ts` / `vc-menu-item.test.ts`: the header''s\n`aria-expanded` flips with the toggle, `aria-controls` points at the\nchildren region, and the group root exposes `data-group-id`.\nMutation-checked: removing the attributes fails 5 tests.\n- `assets-manager.test.ts` (new): the blade root carries the id.\nMutation-checked: removing it fails the test. `defineBlade` is stubbed\nwith `vi.hoisted`, because the framework''s test build does not run the\nblade macro.\n- Full framework suite with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`:\n**424 files / 4270 tests passed**. typecheck, eslint, prettier,\n`check:circular` and `check:layers` are clean.\n\n## Verified end to end, locally\nI built vendor-portal against this branch (the framework was packed from\nit), served it with `vite preview`, and ran the new e2e specs against\nvcmp-qa:\n\n| Spec | This branch | Stock 2.6.3-rc.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5 × open from the sidebar (products, mp-products, team, fulfillment\ncentres, seller profile): collapse the group via its toggle, expand it\nwith a real click, open the item | pass | fail: `[data-group-id]` found\n0 |\n| assets widget opens the assets manager | pass | fail:\n`assets-manager-blade` found 0 |\n| asset removed in the assets manager is gone from the product after\nSave | pass | fail: `assets-manager-blade` found 0 |\n\nThe vendor-portal side is a draft PR that waits for a framework release\ncontaining these changes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxjceCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf6EQAFN3IfOAKtS9jIr75V5yJyuA\n0qgm6wVl5KzKAEheAfPlPL4jlJYTKVcXZa0Pvn5ZbSNGOl/0mQTW6b8+7QQ5BVVe\nDKhCWh4rSfjNHFpkttEp0fsroddM2zwz/G61wyqQt7iqPqzQ/WHTEDDWHgTXEYGf\ncqWTOAmibsbFvZhYYMOO7ngiFEy0fG6znuz7uEuIVg1MKl1f9pWlDUoGGGyv4afj\nBhWSr6AgwcNeL5Xm0WvsDTwolzDSaTBLBhizRF2tuOrS3Le5UkKrOXC+kTfdOewu\nKIg8geO1zj2Fenq9nLZYSGTLfkZUKyNVy5ZOgELlCFmr0H3XrpQbRokXswfr70mp\nmwq72L4p3JIhlYzolrrD65suw8sN5oCEID59hppAfnRPayJsS1DfjZLHo37Q2ulh\nf3zjCNkiAMju+KR8vj9Y5hzh3u0YqMkIQLjMh7Tnh6dqvKfUeYVK5N329aDjmbQB\nwdmWT8cDEyNjCQhx9RNs4VpeAiPov9wWw8+QkmDqdNeGpDest+AHlJ9IRg0mMNws\nl3Umczm8lruGWYdE80JiE5lD4R4VqsZliCYof0Z06pQBRIvkvgqDf9LWe7QIeNNG\nsIR8WBV9pvXBLGHKHniNuDGRllfxpyM4SwACWoM0NNeVU6p3vxHu/eT7jAs/s6no\nnmE8vjfJQqEpZzuXt4ZJ\n=4iTd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T12:12:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGM4YmUxMDcwMDU3MWEyMmIzYTFhZDM4OTNmYmI0MTg1MzBlYTNmNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb","sha":"99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb"}],"sha":"c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c8be10700571a22b3a1ad3893fbb418530ea3f54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:58:34Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:58:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): add Remember me to the login form (VM-1822) (#381)\n\n## What (VM-1822)\nAdds \"Remember me\" to the vc-shell login form, as in the platform''s\nAngular admin.\n\n## How it works on the platform\n- The login form sends `rememberMe` to `POST\n/api/platform/security/login`.\n- `SecurityController` passes it to `PasswordSignInAsync(user, password,\nrequest.RememberMe, …)`:\n- `true` → a **persistent** session cookie that survives closing the\nbrowser (sliding, ASP.NET Identity default 14 days);\n  - `false` → a **browser-session** cookie.\n- `LoginRequest.rememberMe` already exists in the generated client, but\nvc-shell never sent it, so every session ended with the browser.\n\nThe OAuth token request is unchanged; the Angular admin does not tie it\nto \"Remember me\" either.\n\n## Changes\n- `useUser.signIn(username, password, rememberMe = false)`: passes the\nflag to `securityClient.login`. `useUserManagement.signIn` gets the same\noptional third parameter, so existing callers are unaffected.\n- `Login.vue`: a `VcCheckbox` \"Remember me\"\n(`data-test-id=\"login-remember-me\"`) between the password and Sign in.\nIt is unchecked by default, as in the platform admin.\n- Locales: `LOGIN.FIELDS.REMEMBER_ME.LABEL` in en (\"Remember me\") and de\n(\"Angemeldet bleiben\").\n- `useUserManagement.docs.md`: the `signIn` signature and the\ncookie-login step.\n\n## Tests\n- `useUser.test.ts`: the platform login gets `rememberMe: false` by\ndefault and `true` when asked.\n- `Login.test.ts`:\n  - the checkbox renders unchecked;\n  - Sign in sends `false` when the box is untouched;\n  - Sign in sends `true` when it is checked.\n- Mutation-checked; each of these fails 2 tests:\n  - dropping the flag from the login request;\n  - dropping it from the form''s `signIn` call;\n  - checking the box by default.\n\n## Verification\n- `yarn typecheck`, eslint, prettier, `check:locales`, `check:circular`,\n`check:layers`: all clean. `docs:lint`: 0 errors; the 6 warnings are in\nunrelated files.\n- Full framework vitest: **421 files / 4222 tests passed**, run with\n`NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`.\n- Without that flag, Node 26 shadows jsdom''s `localStorage`, and ~86\ntests in 10 unrelated files fail the same way on `main`.\n\n## How to check by hand\n1. Sign in with \"Remember me\" checked. DevTools → Application → Cookies:\nthe platform cookie has an **Expires** date. Close and reopen the\nbrowser, and you are still signed in.\n2. Sign in with the box unchecked. The cookie is **Session**, and after\nthe browser restarts you land on Login.\n\n## Note\nThis touches `useUser/index.ts`, `useUser.test.ts` and\n`useUserManagement/index.ts`, which #380 also changes, in different\nplaces. Whichever lands second may need a trivial rebase.","tree":{"sha":"eec74d74912935e00d5484531b61f793844c63f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/eec74d74912935e00d5484531b61f793844c63f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb","verification":{"payload":"tree eec74d74912935e00d5484531b61f793844c63f7\nparent 1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1791367114 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791367114 +0300\n\nfeat(auth): add Remember me to the login form (VM-1822) (#381)\n\n## What (VM-1822)\nAdds \"Remember me\" to the vc-shell login form, as in the platform''s\nAngular admin.\n\n## How it works on the platform\n- The login form sends `rememberMe` to `POST\n/api/platform/security/login`.\n- `SecurityController` passes it to `PasswordSignInAsync(user, password,\nrequest.RememberMe, …)`:\n- `true` → a **persistent** session cookie that survives closing the\nbrowser (sliding, ASP.NET Identity default 14 days);\n  - `false` → a **browser-session** cookie.\n- `LoginRequest.rememberMe` already exists in the generated client, but\nvc-shell never sent it, so every session ended with the browser.\n\nThe OAuth token request is unchanged; the Angular admin does not tie it\nto \"Remember me\" either.\n\n## Changes\n- `useUser.signIn(username, password, rememberMe = false)`: passes the\nflag to `securityClient.login`. `useUserManagement.signIn` gets the same\noptional third parameter, so existing callers are unaffected.\n- `Login.vue`: a `VcCheckbox` \"Remember me\"\n(`data-test-id=\"login-remember-me\"`) between the password and Sign in.\nIt is unchecked by default, as in the platform admin.\n- Locales: `LOGIN.FIELDS.REMEMBER_ME.LABEL` in en (\"Remember me\") and de\n(\"Angemeldet bleiben\").\n- `useUserManagement.docs.md`: the `signIn` signature and the\ncookie-login step.\n\n## Tests\n- `useUser.test.ts`: the platform login gets `rememberMe: false` by\ndefault and `true` when asked.\n- `Login.test.ts`:\n  - the checkbox renders unchecked;\n  - Sign in sends `false` when the box is untouched;\n  - Sign in sends `true` when it is checked.\n- Mutation-checked; each of these fails 2 tests:\n  - dropping the flag from the login request;\n  - dropping it from the form''s `signIn` call;\n  - checking the box by default.\n\n## Verification\n- `yarn typecheck`, eslint, prettier, `check:locales`, `check:circular`,\n`check:layers`: all clean. `docs:lint`: 0 errors; the 6 warnings are in\nunrelated files.\n- Full framework vitest: **421 files / 4222 tests passed**, run with\n`NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage`.\n- Without that flag, Node 26 shadows jsdom''s `localStorage`, and ~86\ntests in 10 unrelated files fail the same way on `main`.\n\n## How to check by hand\n1. Sign in with \"Remember me\" checked. DevTools → Application → Cookies:\nthe platform cookie has an **Expires** date. Close and reopen the\nbrowser, and you are still signed in.\n2. Sign in with the box unchecked. The cookie is **Session**, and after\nthe browser restarts you land on Login.\n\n## Note\nThis touches `useUser/index.ts`, `useUser.test.ts` and\n`useUserManagement/index.ts`, which #380 also changes, in different\nplaces. Whichever lands second may need a trivial rebase.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhfKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq0EQAClcZXukMj3RkVw8Nxm+ZS3N\nWxu2oTxUji1Rw6kmwQYQi5j+4HkzBRCKJkFryDOraSFYaFrdcF8T1KQLEYYPYAy5\nYVl60/VPOFJgDfUtPFW17nu5q04OulBoYby1dg6qwFbLIhUYX9wGwIa4bxf1LQ/2\nmR8xxHvFenzON9isO06yqybAk7o2zvRNM4Wa+2uB3KE3h9b83dGsGceg2dR7SgK+\n2/hvVQjxZzFbxsgSMsNVWiwM959daW/yN7NTgeow01EptXe6C6y/kHp+6/mZKWfK\n3AWxoOJQQnpBkacBr1OFv0W2xCGu/c7ir157ORULzXFIr5TcrM97jg2lx6DGjsrw\n1n1rHWUNz3rtnyChX+FQi4qmbCXJnFevNxmvflpH/efMqpxEaFrjhIeA/zt3kom0\n0XlHebE8D3nZBBcPAkToRM6ogJQF4SzSZqTYuUk3GPX/rSqSAzKAUvIoVRzk4Cys\n15RDQFO0XWMHL98k+Rgj2kRReMTAhw4gioc4lNFJsVgNnOeCLmJKEV3P9ig14dk9\nowZntBudoMrrpncXfydwVFDeP4e7s7a2F2A3d2Jbm1t2ng+Fp6MP/OTUCzpi9pAJ\nPFIazRKLM85VTrOORXGbLlAVQKR0o7m2DTNRxFRGEPIIuFZQuN8Q0lW7xm5ID/IU\nkV4DupG3h88/QQ8oPc2H\n=BkhB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T09:58:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDk5YmVjY2YwNGI4ZDkwNzFjMTVkMzYxYTI3Y2E2ZTVkZGMzOWNiZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30","sha":"1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30"}],"sha":"99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/99beccf04b8d9071c15d361a27ca6e5ddc39cbfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:52:19Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:52:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): send only a definitive ''not signed in'' to Login (VM-1829) (#380)\n\n## Problem (VM-1829)\nOn app start, apps call `useUser().loadUser()`; vendor-portal''s\n`main.ts` does exactly that. `loadUser()` swallowed every\n`getCurrentUser()` error. The root-route guard in `framework/index.ts`\nonly checked `isAuthenticated`, so \"could not load the user\" and \"not\nsigned in\" became the same thing: an empty user.\n\nOne 5xx or a dropped connection on `currentuser` during start was enough\nto send a live session to Login. The vendor-portal e2e suite hit this on\nvcmp-qa: the next API calls with the same cookie answered 200.\n\n## How the platform does it\nThe platform admin UI (`vc-platform`, `wwwroot/js/app`) does not have\nthis bug, and it has no retries either:\n- `currentuser` is `[AllowAnonymous]` (`SecurityController`), so \"not\nsigned in\" is a **200 with no user**, not an error.\n- `authService.fillAuthData()` calls `changeAuth` only on success. A\nfailed `currentuser` changes nothing, broadcasts no `loginStatusChanged`\nand redirects nowhere.\n- Login is reached only on a definitive answer: a 401 from any request\n(the `unauthorized` event), or a 200 with an empty user\n(`loginStatusChanged`). Every other error goes to `httpError` and leaves\nthe session alone.\n\n## Fix: the same three states, made explicit\n`useUser` gets `authState: \"authenticated\" | \"anonymous\" | \"unknown\"`,\nwhich `useUserManagement` also exposes:\n\n| `currentuser` outcome | `authState` |\n|---|---|\n| a user | `authenticated` |\n| 200 with no user, a 401/403, or a sign-out | `anonymous` |\n| no answer yet, a 5xx, or a dropped connection | `unknown`; the user is\nleft as it was |\n\nSo a later failed reload never signs out a session that is already\nauthenticated.\n\nThe root-route guard moves to `core/utilities/authGuard.ts` as a pure\nfunction with injected dependencies, following the `bladeRouterGuard`\npattern, so it can be tested:\n- `authenticated` → let the navigation through.\n- `anonymous` → go to Login, remembering `redirectAfterLogin`, as\nbefore.\n- `unknown` → load the user once more; the call is deduplicated with any\nload already in flight. If there is still no answer, report the new\n`CORE.ERRORS.SESSION_CHECK_FAILED` (en and de) through\n`notification.error` and **let the navigation through**. The user is not\nsent to Login.\n- The navigation is deliberately not cancelled. Cancelling the initial\nnavigation rejects `router.isReady()`, which apps await before\n`app.mount()`. In a manual check the app never mounted, and the global\nerror handler showed an empty toast for the rejected navigation.\n\nAlso, `loadUser()` no longer runs `getAccessToken()`. It used to run it\nalongside `getCurrentUser()` and discard the result. The token''s only\nconsumer, the AI agent''s `tokenGetter`, requests it itself.\n\nNo retries are added. If they are wanted, they belong in the transport\nlayer (see VM-1815), not in one composable.\n\n## Tests\n`useUser.test.ts`, `authState`:\n- `unknown` before any answer.\n- `authenticated` on a user.\n- `anonymous` on an empty user, a 401 and a 403.\n- `unknown` after a 500, a 503 and a dropped connection, with no retry.\n- An authenticated session survives a later 5xx reload.\n- `anonymous` after sign-out.\n- An `isAuthenticationFailure` table.\n\n`authGuard.test.ts`:\n- authenticated passes without a reload.\n- anonymous goes to Login and stores `redirectAfterLogin`.\n- unknown, then authenticated, passes after one load.\n- unknown, then anonymous, goes to Login.\n- unknown, then unknown, reports and lets the navigation through, with\nno Login redirect.\n- Non-root routes are untouched.\n\n**Mutation checks:**\n- Treating any load error as \"not signed in\" makes 4 tests fail.\n- Restoring the old guard, which sends `unknown` to Login, makes the\nguard test fail.\n\n**Manual check** on vendor-portal built against this branch and run\nagainst vcmp-qa, with `currentuser` forced to 500 and to a dropped\nconnection:\n- exactly one error toast, with the session-check text;\n- the app mounts;\n- no Login, and no unhandled rejection.\n\nOnce the request is unblocked, a reload lands in the shell with the\nsession intact. A 401 still goes to Login. On a stock rc.0 build the\nsame 500 and dropped-connection runs end on Login.\n\n## Verification\n- `yarn typecheck`, eslint, prettier, `check:circular`, `check:layers`\nand `check:locales`: all clean.\n- `useUser`, `useUserManagement` and `authGuard` tests: 49 passed.\n- Full framework vitest: 86 failures in 10 files, identical to clean\n`main`. They are the pre-existing Node-26 `localStorage` failures\n(\"localStorage is not available because --localstorage-file was not\nprovided\"); `Login.test.ts` fails the same way on `main`.\n\n## For the reviewer\n- New public surface: `authState` on `useUserManagement()` and the\n`AuthState` type. Both are additive; `isAuthenticated` is unchanged.\n- When the platform cannot answer at start, the app mounts and shows an\nerror notification instead of going to Login. A reload or the next\nnavigation asks again. vendor-portal''s own `App.vue` keeps its loader\nuntil a user is loaded, so in that app the screen is the loader plus the\nnotification.","tree":{"sha":"51fc36793f34ef77bb33ce3b59443e3151fef8d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/51fc36793f34ef77bb33ce3b59443e3151fef8d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30","verification":{"payload":"tree 51fc36793f34ef77bb33ce3b59443e3151fef8d5\nparent d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1791366739 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791366739 +0300\n\nfix(auth): send only a definitive ''not signed in'' to Login (VM-1829) (#380)\n\n## Problem (VM-1829)\nOn app start, apps call `useUser().loadUser()`; vendor-portal''s\n`main.ts` does exactly that. `loadUser()` swallowed every\n`getCurrentUser()` error. The root-route guard in `framework/index.ts`\nonly checked `isAuthenticated`, so \"could not load the user\" and \"not\nsigned in\" became the same thing: an empty user.\n\nOne 5xx or a dropped connection on `currentuser` during start was enough\nto send a live session to Login. The vendor-portal e2e suite hit this on\nvcmp-qa: the next API calls with the same cookie answered 200.\n\n## How the platform does it\nThe platform admin UI (`vc-platform`, `wwwroot/js/app`) does not have\nthis bug, and it has no retries either:\n- `currentuser` is `[AllowAnonymous]` (`SecurityController`), so \"not\nsigned in\" is a **200 with no user**, not an error.\n- `authService.fillAuthData()` calls `changeAuth` only on success. A\nfailed `currentuser` changes nothing, broadcasts no `loginStatusChanged`\nand redirects nowhere.\n- Login is reached only on a definitive answer: a 401 from any request\n(the `unauthorized` event), or a 200 with an empty user\n(`loginStatusChanged`). Every other error goes to `httpError` and leaves\nthe session alone.\n\n## Fix: the same three states, made explicit\n`useUser` gets `authState: \"authenticated\" | \"anonymous\" | \"unknown\"`,\nwhich `useUserManagement` also exposes:\n\n| `currentuser` outcome | `authState` |\n|---|---|\n| a user | `authenticated` |\n| 200 with no user, a 401/403, or a sign-out | `anonymous` |\n| no answer yet, a 5xx, or a dropped connection | `unknown`; the user is\nleft as it was |\n\nSo a later failed reload never signs out a session that is already\nauthenticated.\n\nThe root-route guard moves to `core/utilities/authGuard.ts` as a pure\nfunction with injected dependencies, following the `bladeRouterGuard`\npattern, so it can be tested:\n- `authenticated` → let the navigation through.\n- `anonymous` → go to Login, remembering `redirectAfterLogin`, as\nbefore.\n- `unknown` → load the user once more; the call is deduplicated with any\nload already in flight. If there is still no answer, report the new\n`CORE.ERRORS.SESSION_CHECK_FAILED` (en and de) through\n`notification.error` and **let the navigation through**. The user is not\nsent to Login.\n- The navigation is deliberately not cancelled. Cancelling the initial\nnavigation rejects `router.isReady()`, which apps await before\n`app.mount()`. In a manual check the app never mounted, and the global\nerror handler showed an empty toast for the rejected navigation.\n\nAlso, `loadUser()` no longer runs `getAccessToken()`. It used to run it\nalongside `getCurrentUser()` and discard the result. The token''s only\nconsumer, the AI agent''s `tokenGetter`, requests it itself.\n\nNo retries are added. If they are wanted, they belong in the transport\nlayer (see VM-1815), not in one composable.\n\n## Tests\n`useUser.test.ts`, `authState`:\n- `unknown` before any answer.\n- `authenticated` on a user.\n- `anonymous` on an empty user, a 401 and a 403.\n- `unknown` after a 500, a 503 and a dropped connection, with no retry.\n- An authenticated session survives a later 5xx reload.\n- `anonymous` after sign-out.\n- An `isAuthenticationFailure` table.\n\n`authGuard.test.ts`:\n- authenticated passes without a reload.\n- anonymous goes to Login and stores `redirectAfterLogin`.\n- unknown, then authenticated, passes after one load.\n- unknown, then anonymous, goes to Login.\n- unknown, then unknown, reports and lets the navigation through, with\nno Login redirect.\n- Non-root routes are untouched.\n\n**Mutation checks:**\n- Treating any load error as \"not signed in\" makes 4 tests fail.\n- Restoring the old guard, which sends `unknown` to Login, makes the\nguard test fail.\n\n**Manual check** on vendor-portal built against this branch and run\nagainst vcmp-qa, with `currentuser` forced to 500 and to a dropped\nconnection:\n- exactly one error toast, with the session-check text;\n- the app mounts;\n- no Login, and no unhandled rejection.\n\nOnce the request is unblocked, a reload lands in the shell with the\nsession intact. A 401 still goes to Login. On a stock rc.0 build the\nsame 500 and dropped-connection runs end on Login.\n\n## Verification\n- `yarn typecheck`, eslint, prettier, `check:circular`, `check:layers`\nand `check:locales`: all clean.\n- `useUser`, `useUserManagement` and `authGuard` tests: 49 passed.\n- Full framework vitest: 86 failures in 10 files, identical to clean\n`main`. They are the pre-existing Node-26 `localStorage` failures\n(\"localStorage is not available because --localstorage-file was not\nprovided\"); `Login.test.ts` fails the same way on `main`.\n\n## For the reviewer\n- New public surface: `authState` on `useUserManagement()` and the\n`AuthState` type. Both are additive; `isAuthenticated` is unchanged.\n- When the platform cannot answer at start, the app mounts and shows an\nerror notification instead of going to Login. A reload or the next\nnavigation asks again. vendor-portal''s own `App.vue` keeps its loader\nuntil a user is loaded, so in that app the screen is the loader plus the\nnotification.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhZTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4QMQACnnUSBv8gFqCtos+ou/GHLi\nV18G1f0sM56AbttmC0adXVlkhPFbGTtkdqAiKG5rTaRw9cqkeF3ubd0fX65xahX9\nMzUCWHcYjrBJXfrKt9WSiIaLg3RkUIty2348uj1CZ1tBi2bi9cDOWt/Ud/vSe/hd\nPCMoU5FjbP0ok1u+/nl+13Q1slMqUc28g1gQb9VcwyB5hYwHw/Zifrf3H8ue7g5L\nrW4+eFQ766CFIjiQfzTnhNkYxSG397dlb/NEP8Fq0+hWoPICuI9PD9pdjTEKRoU8\nn4doRpO/TOn9PjNKfgXdEUY5G3D9T1VzujkHplRvVQ0enKvuGkj9OY4v2fkGsQEl\ncun3c+xvELzHqlZ3mWvMRHJ2Q2avBDh+oNKNT8Q00EEgfnuOM8KUAk8OI/cRTi2g\nb26C9E/UiTyjQD7LQcvH53lmP9pxDDHEt/6L38a6/6ghJPW6vqomfirwDDStztu3\nLJUFolXn305AHEt1ZsDEpaJdxA062EuhsO9R390ITOSj16WeiRRBWNQXzGYclWtM\nqhDZ7+RWFEw0wU0G9S1DF9YLsiBtTBkQ94ZiwY7YVyIU5YcVL1mjTjY/OpdLPFLv\nu4ZbXKRRMfdiIB0nlD79oPtL+ylgnSnC4dZc0G6c3oSuA5kg8aWRM5BgwZJGO2R/\n1xasOqlTI97RE+xnvgoU\n=ftkD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T09:52:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDFkMTE2OWZiYTNhYjUyOGJiZjgzNzVhZWMzZTgyZmJhZTYyNTdhMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355","sha":"d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355"}],"sha":"1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/1d1169fba3ab528bbf8375aec3e82fbae6257a30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:51:54Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:51:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-scheduler): stop a double-clicked Save creating two events (VCST-5676) (#379)\n\nFixes all three findings from the 2026-09-23 QA comment on VCST-5676.\n\n## 1. Double-clicking Save created two events\n\nClosing the editor is not instant: the popup runs a leave transition, so\nits Save button stays in the DOM and clickable while it plays. An\nordinary double-click lands the second press in that window, and\n`onEditorSave` emitted again.\n\n`editor.open` is already `false` by then, so that is what the save path\ngates on. `onEditorDelete` had the same hole (two `event-delete` emits\nfor one double-click, not covered by the QA run) and `onQuickSave` is\nguarded for symmetry.\n\nThis also explains why three earlier attempts found nothing: the\nquick-create popover is removed without a transition, so the window does\nnot exist on that path — and that was the path those attempts drove.\n\n## 2. Focus was left on `<body>` when a modal closed\n\nHeadless UI restores focus only when it owns the unmount, which is not\nthe case on the `v-model` path. `usePopup` already repairs this for\nimperative popups; `vc-popup.vue` now does the same for declarative\nones, on `@after-leave` — before that the dialog still holds focus and\n`focusIfLoose` would correctly decline and leave nothing behind it.\n\nMeasured rather than assumed: the opening cell is focused by the click,\nsurvives the save as the same node, and focus was lost on both the save\nand the cancel path, which rules out the re-render.\n\n## 3. Every modal announced itself as \"&lt;title&gt; Close\"\n\nThe Close button sat inside the element `aria-labelledby` points at, so\nits own label was appended to the dialog''s accessible name. It moves to\na header wrapper beside the title. `.vc-popup__title` keeps its own flex\nrow, so a `#header` slot with several children lays out exactly as\nbefore.\n\nThis one is framework-wide — every `VcPopup` was affected, not only the\nscheduler''s editor.\n\n## Verification\n\nMeasured in Chromium with real pointer input (CDP, never\n`element.click()`), on the EditingFlow story, before and after:\n\n| | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| events after a double-clicked Save | **2** | **1** |\n| events after a single Save | 1 | 1 |\n| `document.activeElement` after the modal closes | `BODY` | the day\ncell |\n| dialog accessible name | `New event Close` | `New event` |\n\nOne correction to the report: focus return after the **quick-create\npopover** closes was already working (the cell is focused before and\nafter). Only the modal path lost it.\n\nUnit tests, each with a RED baseline — with the guards reverted the four\nscheduler cases fail and the rest pass; same for the popup focus-restore\ncase:\n\n- `VcScheduler.test.ts` — double Save in create mode, double Save in\nedit mode, double Delete, double quick-create Save\n- `vc-popup.test.ts` — restores the opener after the leave, declines\nwhen something else took focus, Close button outside the naming element\n\nGates: framework unit suite (the 8 files / 84 failures it reports are\nidentical on a clean `origin/main` — `localStorage` undefined in those\nsuites, unrelated), `yarn test:storybook` 95 files / 675 tests green,\ntypecheck, eslint `--max-warnings=0`, stylelint, prettier, `docs:lint` 0\nerrors.","tree":{"sha":"5ec4afde78322881dbd9e0697085706879610e92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/5ec4afde78322881dbd9e0697085706879610e92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ec4afde78322881dbd9e0697085706879610e92\nparent 3924cc573befacfab8d9712d986e85aca4f4cb61\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1791366714 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791366714 +0300\n\nfix(vc-scheduler): stop a double-clicked Save creating two events (VCST-5676) (#379)\n\nFixes all three findings from the 2026-09-23 QA comment on VCST-5676.\n\n## 1. Double-clicking Save created two events\n\nClosing the editor is not instant: the popup runs a leave transition, so\nits Save button stays in the DOM and clickable while it plays. An\nordinary double-click lands the second press in that window, and\n`onEditorSave` emitted again.\n\n`editor.open` is already `false` by then, so that is what the save path\ngates on. `onEditorDelete` had the same hole (two `event-delete` emits\nfor one double-click, not covered by the QA run) and `onQuickSave` is\nguarded for symmetry.\n\nThis also explains why three earlier attempts found nothing: the\nquick-create popover is removed without a transition, so the window does\nnot exist on that path — and that was the path those attempts drove.\n\n## 2. Focus was left on `<body>` when a modal closed\n\nHeadless UI restores focus only when it owns the unmount, which is not\nthe case on the `v-model` path. `usePopup` already repairs this for\nimperative popups; `vc-popup.vue` now does the same for declarative\nones, on `@after-leave` — before that the dialog still holds focus and\n`focusIfLoose` would correctly decline and leave nothing behind it.\n\nMeasured rather than assumed: the opening cell is focused by the click,\nsurvives the save as the same node, and focus was lost on both the save\nand the cancel path, which rules out the re-render.\n\n## 3. Every modal announced itself as \"&lt;title&gt; Close\"\n\nThe Close button sat inside the element `aria-labelledby` points at, so\nits own label was appended to the dialog''s accessible name. It moves to\na header wrapper beside the title. `.vc-popup__title` keeps its own flex\nrow, so a `#header` slot with several children lays out exactly as\nbefore.\n\nThis one is framework-wide — every `VcPopup` was affected, not only the\nscheduler''s editor.\n\n## Verification\n\nMeasured in Chromium with real pointer input (CDP, never\n`element.click()`), on the EditingFlow story, before and after:\n\n| | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| events after a double-clicked Save | **2** | **1** |\n| events after a single Save | 1 | 1 |\n| `document.activeElement` after the modal closes | `BODY` | the day\ncell |\n| dialog accessible name | `New event Close` | `New event` |\n\nOne correction to the report: focus return after the **quick-create\npopover** closes was already working (the cell is focused before and\nafter). Only the modal path lost it.\n\nUnit tests, each with a RED baseline — with the guards reverted the four\nscheduler cases fail and the rest pass; same for the popup focus-restore\ncase:\n\n- `VcScheduler.test.ts` — double Save in create mode, double Save in\nedit mode, double Delete, double quick-create Save\n- `vc-popup.test.ts` — restores the opener after the leave, declines\nwhen something else took focus, Close button outside the naming element\n\nGates: framework unit suite (the 8 files / 84 failures it reports are\nidentical on a clean `origin/main` — `localStorage` undefined in those\nsuites, unrelated), `yarn test:storybook` 95 files / 675 tests green,\ntypecheck, eslint `--max-warnings=0`, stylelint, prettier, `docs:lint` 0\nerrors.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhY6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFYYQAKJQLb81QCwAsxWgXyM4/p2p\nd8NgumHacQoArf41o+PucrXFn0UHgYTnnnw64fV8HaIPQ6r09sRGJBccSGSMVK/N\nPt7umg1ZEGUUa3spN49373UENAozgaMsfh8RoZuxlItAP5F5xE9WoOPUHlzjegXi\nMrQwECuo7PHe/B8mXKd4Z4oKn/oagpPzJ3UAGvl6JHkdf98RZoIkHVhjQasbPEzn\nJ7M6lCp8RAnocK2vH0YOr32UiGNPf7LlC0H6BjUPPbChTSBS3IDS8+r7DPL22eL5\nAGp8aJQhFjFNHb0t8IEC8h3NZKroZFI/1iCSgRBliTFT6aNFB0IHRIoM+fZplzUf\noeZEYjSEvDC0+heO6E2PYR4f/hyah/697ZGg51Xmkp5/zjkohmAheERf5ni+pZNT\nKgiF1vCuAvz3Ppn6AMtTu3WEzHQo7tUryNdSQBCzcYAWfIn7T5YQG74RQxh8fbHv\n+DZ0E1ZkBIFdyu8+Dfoxcuutj5iEx0p9avZsihx7tHuJ6m+jUuFL7hMRuCqI+HIC\nxhcRdXoHO7t2RP54jbC4L8ix9iYRWc8rpME0iYFq//2Ul84/A2eNty4V7Nf75fqP\nukasLX8O29EFicCvd67+0fRPsyX28Ri0nw3md/DTQa3bEDpCvhLbAkK1kkhVNmjg\nmxjOHnj3BMWTKHC+VUbR\n=jOXw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T09:51:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGQxZDhjOGIxMjU4YWIwNWU1MjJhNjlkZmRiZDcxMDlkMGJlZjIzNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/3924cc573befacfab8d9712d986e85aca4f4cb61","sha":"3924cc573befacfab8d9712d986e85aca4f4cb61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3924cc573befacfab8d9712d986e85aca4f4cb61"}],"sha":"d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d1d8c8b1258ab05e522a69dfdbd7109d0bef2355"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3924cc573befacfab8d9712d986e85aca4f4cb61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:51:11Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:51:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-select): keep paging, scroll arrows and the search field right under browser zoom (#378)\n\nThree `VcSelect` defects that only show at a fractional browser zoom.\nReported by QA from a push-messages company picker on vcptcore-qa1:\nscrolling the list stopped after the first page, and the search field\nrendered visibly shorter than the options.\n\n## 1. The list stops loading (`vc-select.vue`)\n\nThe next page loads when the `.vc-select__load-more-trigger` — a 1px\nline after the last option — intersects the viewport with `threshold:\n1`, i.e. fully visible. At a fractional zoom the list scrolled to its\nend still leaves that line a fraction of a pixel past the viewport edge.\nMeasured at 80%: trigger at 884.05–885.05, viewport bottom at 885. A\nfull intersection never happens, so nothing more loads.\n\n75 organizations, wheel-scrolled to the end with the cursor mid-list:\n\n| zoom | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| 100% | 75 | 75 |\n| 90% | 60 | 75 |\n| 80% | **20** | 75 |\n| 67% | **20** | 75 |\n| 50% | 75 | 75 |\n| 110%, 125% | — | 75 |\n\n100% and 50% work today only because the geometry happens to land on\nwhole pixels.\n\nFix: `threshold: 0` — any part of the trigger showing is enough — with\n`rootMargin: \"0px 0px 48px 0px\"` so the next page starts just before the\nend.\n\n## 2. The down arrow stays lit at the end (`useScrollArrows`,\n`SelectDropdown`, `MultivalueDropdown`)\n\n`canScrollDown` and the wheel boundary (`atBottom`, which stops the page\nbehind from scrolling) compared exactly: `Math.ceil(scrollTop) <\nscrollHeight - clientHeight`. `scrollHeight` and `clientHeight` are\nrounded to whole CSS pixels, and the scroll position stops on a whole\n*device* pixel — 1.49 CSS px at 67%. Measured at the end: 90%\n`scrollTop` 1710 vs 1711, 67% 431.34 vs 433. The down arrow stayed\nvisible there and hovering it did nothing.\n\nFix: one `isScrolledToEnd(el)` in `useScrollArrows.ts`, with a CSS pixel\nof slack for the rounding plus one device pixel for the stop. The three\nplaces that held a copy of the comparison now call it.\n\n## 3. The search field gets squeezed (`vc-select.vue`)\n\nThe dropdown is a flex column capped at `max-h-72`; the search input had\n`h-8` but no `shrink-0`. With a long list the column shrinks its items,\nand only the input''s automatic minimum height holds it — which depends\non the browser, OS fonts and zoom. Where that minimum is small (QA''s\nWindows at reduced zoom) the field came out about 16px. With\n`min-height: 0` forced to stand in for such a browser, the field drops\nto 8px today and stays at 32px with `shrink-0`. The scroll buttons\nbeside it already have `shrink-0`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `useScrollArrows.test.ts` — the end-of-list cases at 90% and 67% (the\nmeasured numbers above, with `devicePixelRatio` mocked), plus a table\nfor `isScrolledToEnd`.\n- `vc-select.load-more.test.ts` — the trigger is observed with\n`threshold: 0` and a bottom `rootMargin`. jsdom has no layout, so the\ngeometry itself is covered by the browser runs, not by this test.\n- RED baseline: with the sources reverted and the tests kept, 7 of the\n16 cases fail; with the change, all pass.\n- `npx vitest run` on `vc-select`, `vc-multivalue` and `useScrollArrows`\n— 20 files, 208 tests, green.\n- Full `npx vitest run` in `framework/` — the same 101 failures with and\nwithout this change, identical list. They are environmental\n(`localStorage` under Node 26 + jsdom) and do not touch these\ncomponents.\n- `yarn workspace @vc-shell/framework run check:types` clean; eslint\n`--max-warnings=0` clean on the changed files.\n- Browser: the framework built from this branch, dropped into\n`vc-module-push-messages` on a local platform, Edge via Playwright. The\nzoom table above (8 levels): every level loads all 75 with no\nduplicates, the down arrow is hidden at the end, and the search field\nholds 32px under `min-height: 0`.\n\n## Also checked, no change needed\n\n- `useSelectVisibility` — `threshold: 0.1` on the whole select (≥32px\ntall); fractions of a pixel do not matter there.\n- `VcDataTable` infinite scroll and `AppHubContent` — trigger within\n100px / an offset of the end, so they already have slack.","tree":{"sha":"10cb4cbe2ac2f48fe97836e03419667e045bde89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/10cb4cbe2ac2f48fe97836e03419667e045bde89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/3924cc573befacfab8d9712d986e85aca4f4cb61","verification":{"payload":"tree 10cb4cbe2ac2f48fe97836e03419667e045bde89\nparent 4118dee7f73f845ec3385e79bd33c9e4741fce71\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1791366671 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791366671 +0300\n\nfix(vc-select): keep paging, scroll arrows and the search field right under browser zoom (#378)\n\nThree `VcSelect` defects that only show at a fractional browser zoom.\nReported by QA from a push-messages company picker on vcptcore-qa1:\nscrolling the list stopped after the first page, and the search field\nrendered visibly shorter than the options.\n\n## 1. The list stops loading (`vc-select.vue`)\n\nThe next page loads when the `.vc-select__load-more-trigger` — a 1px\nline after the last option — intersects the viewport with `threshold:\n1`, i.e. fully visible. At a fractional zoom the list scrolled to its\nend still leaves that line a fraction of a pixel past the viewport edge.\nMeasured at 80%: trigger at 884.05–885.05, viewport bottom at 885. A\nfull intersection never happens, so nothing more loads.\n\n75 organizations, wheel-scrolled to the end with the cursor mid-list:\n\n| zoom | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| 100% | 75 | 75 |\n| 90% | 60 | 75 |\n| 80% | **20** | 75 |\n| 67% | **20** | 75 |\n| 50% | 75 | 75 |\n| 110%, 125% | — | 75 |\n\n100% and 50% work today only because the geometry happens to land on\nwhole pixels.\n\nFix: `threshold: 0` — any part of the trigger showing is enough — with\n`rootMargin: \"0px 0px 48px 0px\"` so the next page starts just before the\nend.\n\n## 2. The down arrow stays lit at the end (`useScrollArrows`,\n`SelectDropdown`, `MultivalueDropdown`)\n\n`canScrollDown` and the wheel boundary (`atBottom`, which stops the page\nbehind from scrolling) compared exactly: `Math.ceil(scrollTop) <\nscrollHeight - clientHeight`. `scrollHeight` and `clientHeight` are\nrounded to whole CSS pixels, and the scroll position stops on a whole\n*device* pixel — 1.49 CSS px at 67%. Measured at the end: 90%\n`scrollTop` 1710 vs 1711, 67% 431.34 vs 433. The down arrow stayed\nvisible there and hovering it did nothing.\n\nFix: one `isScrolledToEnd(el)` in `useScrollArrows.ts`, with a CSS pixel\nof slack for the rounding plus one device pixel for the stop. The three\nplaces that held a copy of the comparison now call it.\n\n## 3. The search field gets squeezed (`vc-select.vue`)\n\nThe dropdown is a flex column capped at `max-h-72`; the search input had\n`h-8` but no `shrink-0`. With a long list the column shrinks its items,\nand only the input''s automatic minimum height holds it — which depends\non the browser, OS fonts and zoom. Where that minimum is small (QA''s\nWindows at reduced zoom) the field came out about 16px. With\n`min-height: 0` forced to stand in for such a browser, the field drops\nto 8px today and stays at 32px with `shrink-0`. The scroll buttons\nbeside it already have `shrink-0`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `useScrollArrows.test.ts` — the end-of-list cases at 90% and 67% (the\nmeasured numbers above, with `devicePixelRatio` mocked), plus a table\nfor `isScrolledToEnd`.\n- `vc-select.load-more.test.ts` — the trigger is observed with\n`threshold: 0` and a bottom `rootMargin`. jsdom has no layout, so the\ngeometry itself is covered by the browser runs, not by this test.\n- RED baseline: with the sources reverted and the tests kept, 7 of the\n16 cases fail; with the change, all pass.\n- `npx vitest run` on `vc-select`, `vc-multivalue` and `useScrollArrows`\n— 20 files, 208 tests, green.\n- Full `npx vitest run` in `framework/` — the same 101 failures with and\nwithout this change, identical list. They are environmental\n(`localStorage` under Node 26 + jsdom) and do not touch these\ncomponents.\n- `yarn workspace @vc-shell/framework run check:types` clean; eslint\n`--max-warnings=0` clean on the changed files.\n- Browser: the framework built from this branch, dropped into\n`vc-module-push-messages` on a local platform, Edge via Playwright. The\nzoom table above (8 levels): every level loads all 75 with no\nduplicates, the down arrow is hidden at the end, and the search field\nholds 32px under `min-height: 0`.\n\n## Also checked, no change needed\n\n- `useSelectVisibility` — `threshold: 0.1` on the whole select (≥32px\ntall); fractions of a pixel do not matter there.\n- `VcDataTable` infinite scroll and `AppHubContent` — trigger within\n100px / an offset of the end, so they already have slack.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhYQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGggQAAgNPRTEtS2kuMrGkx41TZt1\n/iw04uTnOC1Y4dklMNidpu1qf+C7ukawgeU/5YIEdDLFqoQkA8g1FgjERIhNpwTT\nRmIYgSJfj2T/G+RT58l96iIo0ckp8rr7aPZZ2YbG564m37mXrPKrWmJ5TdgUYSIq\n8mno3ij/Txrhrxo5/4vR9JaxaJ8q5phCMc7xrn8Xcrujxd9lI7pMFQxW1HLJp6fq\nHtpSCyCCvKyUFQJEPo2WgJCCpCKPLzpc89Cytk35bPCexs0Pw6w5WDL4EDeualjS\nUoDnYUJy3ylUr6SV+dHnd1Ye6B1RvIeoleXcRjDHDGiyAI77Nz1caezo/Sjb7Pwf\nh1PdPxSHWBy6HJgLRT21RaJ9id3UM2H0V95NHpiNSoxvUcZE8UCmvv6VqW7vko51\nq3mrRiRo9hPZKGFIaezgzgIdTnePpgbudYt5m7UDZPCuzKGHP9VYpXcumNy8rSKt\n84BeEsZsjD7jXoXraDuQ8oQOOm6q3Y2kmJOvJacpSl4BrtU4fsI965KRjA49reBN\n65tu3eWzfOSU8vPSaML5VtSGkhn2DZdHmmA9Dl0xWLv6VlrF9VCP/stKmaOBZ/RU\nk1isDGXroEFPxz6QglylN3