ceived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/7a6bd416c4addd9c97017a4b303d9f39bd1c03a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:42:50Z","email":"ci@virtocommerce.com","name":"vc-ci"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:42:50Z","email":"ci@virtocommerce.com","name":"vc-ci"},"message":"release: v2.6.2","tree":{"sha":"3a5aad34efd9ee2a4666bb3dd8b364a0f18b5686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/3a5aad34efd9ee2a4666bb3dd8b364a0f18b5686"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/7a6bd416c4addd9c97017a4b303d9f39bd1c03a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31079468?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vc-ci","id":31079468,"login":"vc-ci","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDc5NDY4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/7a6bd416c4addd9c97017a4b303d9f39bd1c03a6","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDdhNmJkNDE2YzRhZGRkOWM5NzAxN2E0YjMwM2Q5ZjM5YmQxYzAzYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2c6aeace39ff66af59513f2b46cac875518a4487","sha":"2c6aeace39ff66af59513f2b46cac875518a4487","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2c6aeace39ff66af59513f2b46cac875518a4487"}],"sha":"7a6bd416c4addd9c97017a4b303d9f39bd1c03a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/7a6bd416c4addd9c97017a4b303d9f39bd1c03a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2c6aeace39ff66af59513f2b46cac875518a4487/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:39:14Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:39:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: consistent hint size in form fields, refresh VcDataTable selection on reload (#374)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Hint size differed between form fields**\n`VcInput`, `VcTextarea`, `VcDatePicker` and `VcColorInput` applied\n`tw-text-sm` to their hint, overriding the `--hint-font-size` token that\n`VcHint` reads. Their hints were 14px; every other field (`VcSelect`,\n`VcMultivalue`, `VcInputGroup`, checkbox, switch, ...) and every error\nmessage were 12px. The override is gone, so all hints and error messages\nfollow the token (12px) and a theme can change it in one place.\n\n**VcDataTable selection kept stale objects after reload**\nThe selection stored the row objects it was given and matched rows by\nkey. After `reload()` the table received new objects for the same rows,\nso the checkboxes stayed checked while `update:selection` (and\n`selectionChanged` on the legacy adapter) kept emitting the old copies\nwith outdated data. `useTableSelectionV2` now swaps selected rows for\nthe fresh objects whenever `items` change. Selected rows that are not in\nthe new items are kept, so cross-page selection is not lost. While rows\nare selected, each `items` change emits one `update:selection`, even if\nthe content is unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Storybook, 21 form stories with error/validation states: every hint\nand error message computes to 12px.\n- New tests in `useTableSelectionV2.test.ts` (swap, keep rows missing\nfrom the reload) and `useDataTableOrchestrator.test.ts`\n(`update:selection` carries the reloaded data). The swap test and the\norchestrator test fail with the fix disabled.\n- `vitest` for the four form components, vc-hint and vc-data-table;\n`yarn typecheck`; eslint; stylelint.\n\n`useDataTableState.test.ts` fails on this machine with or without these\nchanges (`localStorage` is undefined), so it is unrelated.","tree":{"sha":"a2c9751e3587c5cef14281931faa0d4287350c83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/a2c9751e3587c5cef14281931faa0d4287350c83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/2c6aeace39ff66af59513f2b46cac875518a4487","verification":{"payload":"tree a2c9751e3587c5cef14281931faa0d4287350c83\nparent 71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1790789954 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790789954 +0300\n\nfix: consistent hint size in form fields, refresh VcDataTable selection on reload (#374)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Hint size differed between form fields**\n`VcInput`, `VcTextarea`, `VcDatePicker` and `VcColorInput` applied\n`tw-text-sm` to their hint, overriding the `--hint-font-size` token that\n`VcHint` reads. Their hints were 14px; every other field (`VcSelect`,\n`VcMultivalue`, `VcInputGroup`, checkbox, switch, ...) and every error\nmessage were 12px. The override is gone, so all hints and error messages\nfollow the token (12px) and a theme can change it in one place.\n\n**VcDataTable selection kept stale objects after reload**\nThe selection stored the row objects it was given and matched rows by\nkey. After `reload()` the table received new objects for the same rows,\nso the checkboxes stayed checked while `update:selection` (and\n`selectionChanged` on the legacy adapter) kept emitting the old copies\nwith outdated data. `useTableSelectionV2` now swaps selected rows for\nthe fresh objects whenever `items` change. Selected rows that are not in\nthe new items are kept, so cross-page selection is not lost. While rows\nare selected, each `items` change emits one `update:selection`, even if\nthe content is unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Storybook, 21 form stories with error/validation states: every hint\nand error message computes to 12px.\n- New tests in `useTableSelectionV2.test.ts` (swap, keep rows missing\nfrom the reload) and `useDataTableOrchestrator.test.ts`\n(`update:selection` carries the reloaded data). The swap test and the\norchestrator test fail with the fix disabled.\n- `vitest` for the four form components, vc-hint and vc-data-table;\n`yarn typecheck`; eslint; stylelint.\n\n`useDataTableState.test.ts` fails on this machine with or without these\nchanges (`localStorage` is undefined), so it is unrelated.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvUlCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkLsQAK7pDAOrkXldjX3El4psD7kW\nTh9Gx2SwfepSgwQLVqGbZ+EB13GfbHt/Ov/r8wN44v+5aPysmDmnMovQVk80WN/F\nv3kQs0ocBjyvUcvvuKr8RGmOwKeptCL1u/TzA2Fe84Ph5AIDFzyZyRDR76k3tUoP\nSeySm6eeSTcHYBvcYQydqp2w52sBg1nifv/ep3DIIAaGKjnpaUaVm8UKBjuSM3XW\nLvKweGk6qEn67m6d42Tmfpns7mRyqJH6qLqIOWuWc8hk4gjrmmTLCnSlPxgUrraG\nFrZh3pUGOOEIsHv8e8bVZtV80LnyMl3lfgVt4LRy0T1hb1DJlNwo93oTa/mfoUAv\nH37IUbh0HDtjXhFcC9Tq7AgcVUKxe0bjAFmljX2B9VVEvZoetG9+l7ZBhA0dzD5T\nWDSKdaVIV03EXdrqFCjyKnSUCcMfd+taH7IZ0zJPazWl9AExw34Drf+GJncZSCqb\n1BZShdvujjRa6wZhi7MPqXKzy63QrpPi5ig2yAQzV1urJqgRQikYyI3wfBYAxOZe\nr5jpfLPzB9m8sj5ngUle5vXP48/VdSrcEWtTXAg9tvaRzgCpHhbTghwgYLCFWcx1\npm3vp9lnd/mEGz7VVTBTqjx4+4Y0+C7dwbfoaeyYvxIX387uIfn3MgLzlNiYYazq\nORBUF96780TsQztDaso6\n=JKVz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:39:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2c6aeace39ff66af59513f2b46cac875518a4487","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDJjNmFlYWNlMzlmZjY2YWY1OTUxM2YyYjQ2Y2FjODc1NTE4YTQ0ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e","sha":"71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e"}],"sha":"2c6aeace39ff66af59513f2b46cac875518a4487","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2c6aeace39ff66af59513f2b46cac875518a4487"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31079468?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vc-ci","id":31079468,"login":"vc-ci","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDc5NDY4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:59:12Z","email":"ci@virtocommerce.com","name":"vc-ci"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:59:12Z","email":"ci@virtocommerce.com","name":"vc-ci"},"message":"release: v2.6.1","tree":{"sha":"f0366efa14960d62ecfb333541a6496de5d74862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/f0366efa14960d62ecfb333541a6496de5d74862"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31079468?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vc-ci","id":31079468,"login":"vc-ci","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDc5NDY4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDcxMzY4NzAyZDgwOTU4M2NiNjBjMDZiNGFiOWE2ZGY0MjAzOTYzOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/ce26475280da7e5be90bd96bd23e89a30d2d7146","sha":"ce26475280da7e5be90bd96bd23e89a30d2d7146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ce26475280da7e5be90bd96bd23e89a30d2d7146"}],"sha":"71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/71368702d809583cb60c06b4ab9a6df42039639e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ce26475280da7e5be90bd96bd23e89a30d2d7146/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:53:34Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:53:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): blank shell at 1024px, clipped VcSelect hint, shortcut tooltip delay (#373)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Blank screen at exactly 1024px**\n`$isMobile` was `smaller(\"desktop\")` (< 1024) and `$isDesktop` was\n`greater(\"desktop\")` (> 1024). At 1024px both were false, so `VcApp`\npicked `MobileLayout` while `isMobile` was false, and nothing rendered.\n`$isDesktop` now uses `greaterOrEqual`, so 1024px is desktop.\n`useResponsive.docs.md` updated to match.\n\n**VcSelect hint not visible**\n`.vc-select__field-wrapper` applied both `overflow-x-clip` and\n`truncate`. `truncate` sets `overflow: hidden`, which overrides the clip\nand hides the hint/error block positioned below the field. Replaced\n`truncate` with `whitespace-nowrap`, so the wrapper is `overflow: clip\nvisible`. The hint/error block gets `whitespace-normal` so long hints\nwrap. The error message was clipped the same way and is fixed too.\n\n**Shortcut tooltip delay**\nTooltips that show a keyboard shortcut (blade toolbar buttons, blade\nheader controls, AI panel header controls) now use a 500ms delay\n(`SHORTCUT_TOOLTIP_DELAY`) instead of opening immediately on hover.\n\n**Refactor: one `ShortcutTooltip` component** (separate commit)\nThe blade toolbar, blade header and AI panel header each built the\nshortcut tooltip by hand (seven copies of `VcTooltip` +\n`formatShortcut`/`isMac` + `ShortcutKbd` + a separate\n`aria-keyshortcuts` value). They now use an internal `ShortcutTooltip`\nthat owns placement, delay and formatting and passes `aria` to the\ntrigger through its slot. Not exported.\n\n**Refactor: shared `HeaderControls`** (separate commit)\n`BladeHeader` and `VcAiAgentHeader` rendered the same\nmaximize/restore/close controls but had drifted: only the blade header\nhanded focus to the replacement control after a maximize/restore swap\n(VCST-5812) and gave the buttons a 24px target (WCAG 2.5.8). Both now\nuse a shared `HeaderControls`, so the AI panel header gets both fixes.\nClass names stay `vc-blade-header__controls` / `__button`, so existing\nCSS overrides keep working; `.vc-ai-agent-header__button` / `__controls`\nare gone.\n\n**`ui/components/shared`** (separate commit)\n`ShortcutKbd`, `ShortcutTooltip` and `HeaderControls` live in\n`framework/ui/components/shared/` (one folder per component with its\ntest and `index.ts`, like everywhere else), not in `vc-blade/_internal`:\nthe AI panel header uses them too, and `_internal` belongs to its owning\ncomponent. The folder is not part of any barrel, so none of them are\npublic. `shell/components` was not an option: the layer rules forbid\n`ui/` and `core/` from importing `shell/`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Storybook, `Layout/VcApp` at 1023 / 1024 / 1025px: mobile / desktop /\ndesktop (1024 was blank before).\n- Storybook, `Form/VcSelect` Appearance and CustomMessagingSlots: hint\nand error visible below the field; MultipleSelection chips stay inside\nthe border.\n- Storybook, `Navigation/VcBlade` WithShortcut: toolbar Save and header\nClose tooltips absent at 200ms, shown at 700ms; `aria-keyshortcuts`\nstill set.\n- New AI header test for the focus handoff; it and the existing\nBladeHeader handoff test both fail with the watch disabled.\n- `vitest` for vc-blade (incl. new `ShortcutTooltip.test.ts`),\nvc-select, ai-agent, vc-tooltip, useResponsive; `yarn typecheck`;\nstylelint; `check:layers`; madge.\n\nKnown, not addressed here: a multi-line custom `#error` slot overlaps\ncontent below the select, since only `pb-5` is reserved for the\nabsolutely positioned hint/error block.","tree":{"sha":"53446d1ca6d6d92c3aeb46c11340e20b261f7995","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/53446d1ca6d6d92c3aeb46c11340e20b261f7995"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/ce26475280da7e5be90bd96bd23e89a30d2d7146","verification":{"payload":"tree 53446d1ca6d6d92c3aeb46c11340e20b261f7995\nparent 83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1790679214 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790679214 +0300\n\nfix(ui): blank shell at 1024px, clipped VcSelect hint, shortcut tooltip delay (#373)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Blank screen at exactly 1024px**\n`$isMobile` was `smaller(\"desktop\")` (< 1024) and `$isDesktop` was\n`greater(\"desktop\")` (> 1024). At 1024px both were false, so `VcApp`\npicked `MobileLayout` while `isMobile` was false, and nothing rendered.\n`$isDesktop` now uses `greaterOrEqual`, so 1024px is desktop.\n`useResponsive.docs.md` updated to match.\n\n**VcSelect hint not visible**\n`.vc-select__field-wrapper` applied both `overflow-x-clip` and\n`truncate`. `truncate` sets `overflow: hidden`, which overrides the clip\nand hides the hint/error block positioned below the field. Replaced\n`truncate` with `whitespace-nowrap`, so the wrapper is `overflow: clip\nvisible`. The hint/error block gets `whitespace-normal` so long hints\nwrap. The error message was clipped the same way and is fixed too.\n\n**Shortcut tooltip delay**\nTooltips that show a keyboard shortcut (blade toolbar buttons, blade\nheader controls, AI panel header controls) now use a 500ms delay\n(`SHORTCUT_TOOLTIP_DELAY`) instead of opening immediately on hover.\n\n**Refactor: one `ShortcutTooltip` component** (separate commit)\nThe blade toolbar, blade header and AI panel header each built the\nshortcut tooltip by hand (seven copies of `VcTooltip` +\n`formatShortcut`/`isMac` + `ShortcutKbd` + a separate\n`aria-keyshortcuts` value). They now use an internal `ShortcutTooltip`\nthat owns placement, delay and formatting and passes `aria` to the\ntrigger through its slot. Not exported.\n\n**Refactor: shared `HeaderControls`** (separate commit)\n`BladeHeader` and `VcAiAgentHeader` rendered the same\nmaximize/restore/close controls but had drifted: only the blade header\nhanded focus to the replacement control after a maximize/restore swap\n(VCST-5812) and gave the buttons a 24px target (WCAG 2.5.8). Both now\nuse a shared `HeaderControls`, so the AI panel header gets both fixes.\nClass names stay `vc-blade-header__controls` / `__button`, so existing\nCSS overrides keep working; `.vc-ai-agent-header__button` / `__controls`\nare gone.\n\n**`ui/components/shared`** (separate commit)\n`ShortcutKbd`, `ShortcutTooltip` and `HeaderControls` live in\n`framework/ui/components/shared/` (one folder per component with its\ntest and `index.ts`, like everywhere else), not in `vc-blade/_internal`:\nthe AI panel header uses them too, and `_internal` belongs to its owning\ncomponent. The folder is not part of any barrel, so none of them are\npublic. `shell/components` was not an option: the layer rules forbid\n`ui/` and `core/` from importing `shell/`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Storybook, `Layout/VcApp` at 1023 / 1024 / 1025px: mobile / desktop /\ndesktop (1024 was blank before).\n- Storybook, `Form/VcSelect` Appearance and CustomMessagingSlots: hint\nand error visible below the field; MultipleSelection chips stay inside\nthe border.\n- Storybook, `Navigation/VcBlade` WithShortcut: toolbar Save and header\nClose tooltips absent at 200ms, shown at 700ms; `aria-keyshortcuts`\nstill set.\n- New AI header test for the focus handoff; it and the existing\nBladeHeader handoff test both fail with the watch disabled.\n- `vitest` for vc-blade (incl. new `ShortcutTooltip.test.ts`),\nvc-select, ai-agent, vc-tooltip, useResponsive; `yarn typecheck`;\nstylelint; `check:layers`; madge.\n\nKnown, not addressed here: a multi-line custom `#error` slot overlaps\ncontent below the select, since only `pb-5` is reserved for the\nabsolutely positioned hint/error block.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu5iuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK80QABOmA0pF3i2du7yiLGxTopHG\nCrB7xn5jNA2BMh3SuAw/W+jagc76J49+r/a6MzJjOs+SMnyZDHwx3fcuuLGec69l\nFt5UP05NmiRcUWnReHuUJTBaEFhXyxTuz21JfSV52y9p741R2o0nxR0Be2DY0Rd1\nWceT9MhZcdXwV2v4DjtL6QhnM/05/sJPdx6LtTkEqu+ZmppkmuVxp3yOhl1EaGuc\n+M6SrPQVz88XEx+WLh02hWGzUFLfF/DY4OIUy3YSxKyrl2El682LfJEpa6YfhqrB\nA43AYK2uamEY3nxVCXQxmeFK19QWTTDoJDtZ3wYScsGwPTQRf/7XFCizYprkzyr7\nzS/8L2qkp0rPXcz416aBCVlffR7NJxGMbpDledC2YsL53+2dLOfmEDBiFtmcEcvn\n1tsXuergwGVcJAgRE5+HWqc6mqy5IUB6uBqQAssdwigFPY/H5VpjnDnzxBpxdYof\no6qGUSPt4zD8dlv3lg8cKXpEriZAk/G/98FgFJ4P4nAyXXogmFU+1r4fQm6l1+rX\nG0czKHTFy4rmQHloq7RcsUF0kMm/jFA+WEPN3KpwhdD4ylduOH2ndwygG1qv9khA\n6dtyStiTwLLV7K6PTNxH2gfOuX1hq2j3G7mQ2sUx9LXUXrOiJLrrywRk76WSBnAr\nSDwKCwRo963sQmui7w6P\n=ingp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:53:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/ce26475280da7e5be90bd96bd23e89a30d2d7146","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGNlMjY0NzUyODBkYTdlNWJlOTBiZDk2YmQyM2U4OWEzMGQyZDcxNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146","sha":"83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146"}],"sha":"ce26475280da7e5be90bd96bd23e89a30d2d7146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ce26475280da7e5be90bd96bd23e89a30d2d7146"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:17:07Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:17:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-data-table): label the page range from pageSize (#372)\n\nThe range beside the pagination (\"21–40 of 45\") is wrong whenever the\ntotal does not divide evenly by the page size.\n\n## The defect\n\n`paginationRangeText` rebuilt the page size from the page count:\n\n```ts\nconst pageSize = Math.ceil(total / p.pages);\n```\n\nThat division rounds. 45 rows at 20 a page make 3 pages, and `ceil(45 /\n3)` is 15 — so page 2 was labelled **16–35 of 45** instead of **21–40**,\nand page 3 **31–35** instead of **41–45**. The rows themselves are\nright; only the label is off.\n\nFound in `vc-module-push-messages` (recipients preview, paged through\n`useDataTablePagination`). Present in `2.6.0` and on `main`.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`VcDataTable.vue`** — use the page size the caller already passes, and\nderive it only when it is missing:\n\n```ts\nconst pageSize = p.pageSize ?? Math.ceil(total / p.pages);\n```\n\n`pageSize` is already on `DataTablePagination` and\n`useDataTablePagination` fills it in, so every consumer of the\ncomposable gets the right range with no change on their side.\n\n**`types.ts`** — the `pageSize` comment called it \"informational, for\nfuture ''Showing 1-20 of 500''\". That label exists now; the comment says\nwhat the field is used for and when the fallback is exact.\n\n## Why the tests did not catch it\n\nThe three pagination tests only assert that `.vc-data-table__pagination`\nrenders; nothing read `.vc-data-table__page-info`. They also mount with\n`items: []` and page counts like 5 or 10 with no `totalCount` — and on\nevenly dividing totals the rounding formula happens to give the right\nanswer.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `VcDataTable.test.ts` — two cases added: a middle page (45 rows, 20 a\npage, page 2 → `21–40`) and the shorter last page (page 3 → `41–45`).\nRED baseline taken: with the one-line fix reverted both fail, the other\n14 pass. With it, 16 of 16 pass.\n- Full `npx vitest run` in `framework/` — the same 101 failures with and\nwithout this change, byte-identical list. They are environmental\n(`localStorage` under Node 26 + jsdom: `Cannot read properties of\nundefined (reading ''clear'')`) and do not touch the table.\n- `yarn workspace @vc-shell/framework run check:types` clean; eslint\n`--max-warnings=0` clean on the changed files.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\n`VcTableAdapter` builds its pagination config without `pageSize` and has\nno prop for it, so legacy tables keep the derived value. That needs a\nnew adapter prop and is left for a separate change.","tree":{"sha":"d40c92c4d391734543bf597127b10d57589af369","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/d40c92c4d391734543bf597127b10d57589af369"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146","verification":{"payload":"tree d40c92c4d391734543bf597127b10d57589af369\nparent ef816a9c2202c3a315b73ec396d7a16216c4fe9d\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1790677027 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790677027 +0300\n\nfix(vc-data-table): label the page range from pageSize (#372)\n\nThe range beside the pagination (\"21–40 of 45\") is wrong whenever the\ntotal does not divide evenly by the page size.\n\n## The defect\n\n`paginationRangeText` rebuilt the page size from the page count:\n\n```ts\nconst pageSize = Math.ceil(total / p.pages);\n```\n\nThat division rounds. 45 rows at 20 a page make 3 pages, and `ceil(45 /\n3)` is 15 — so page 2 was labelled **16–35 of 45** instead of **21–40**,\nand page 3 **31–35** instead of **41–45**. The rows themselves are\nright; only the label is off.\n\nFound in `vc-module-push-messages` (recipients preview, paged through\n`useDataTablePagination`). Present in `2.6.0` and on `main`.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`VcDataTable.vue`** — use the page size the caller already passes, and\nderive it only when it is missing:\n\n```ts\nconst pageSize = p.pageSize ?? Math.ceil(total / p.pages);\n```\n\n`pageSize` is already on `DataTablePagination` and\n`useDataTablePagination` fills it in, so every consumer of the\ncomposable gets the right range with no change on their side.\n\n**`types.ts`** — the `pageSize` comment called it \"informational, for\nfuture ''Showing 1-20 of 500''\". That label exists now; the comment says\nwhat the field is used for and when the fallback is exact.\n\n## Why the tests did not catch it\n\nThe three pagination tests only assert that `.vc-data-table__pagination`\nrenders; nothing read `.vc-data-table__page-info`. They also mount with\n`items: []` and page counts like 5 or 10 with no `totalCount` — and on\nevenly dividing totals the rounding formula happens to give the right\nanswer.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `VcDataTable.test.ts` — two cases added: a middle page (45 rows, 20 a\npage, page 2 → `21–40`) and the shorter last page (page 3 → `41–45`).\nRED baseline taken: with the one-line fix reverted both fail, the other\n14 pass. With it, 16 of 16 pass.\n- Full `npx vitest run` in `framework/` — the same 101 failures with and\nwithout this change, byte-identical list. They are environmental\n(`localStorage` under Node 26 + jsdom: `Cannot read properties of\nundefined (reading ''clear'')`) and do not touch the table.\n- `yarn workspace @vc-shell/framework run check:types` clean; eslint\n`--max-warnings=0` clean on the changed files.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\n`VcTableAdapter` builds its pagination config without `pageSize` and has\nno prop for it, so legacy tables keep the derived value. That needs a\nnew adapter prop and is left for a separate change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu5AjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcPwQAFvxziM7njEGz62SFmIb7ULf\nsyHeeRMgMLrGfPF18pGJNXVqM3r+kGnkDlZj9AFPTmgEn40EOLo17mlmt6k3EZ9M\nboSPWmp3F2tnYIWJ7IzikWcnShK+aNM5z4vu+TrDHEwQ1XwVm7U05UKdbi8n9k3d\nwmNEnOD7pDqFBZMVg0ZmP3yDh51d2GOgAeKcPqQB0FA2UFsgpRH2uW+Cw4eyHdVV\nKcv35nR23h872X1BPnzBWBxfajJQGMZbMOJ45qP2y/2m4thjbgS875U41lh5irLg\n4jGxljVkv3DDIz5yRQfqPaAYbTnbLrW6ALqqbiNQSTsOuBM2Ov+X1i0lYtvEEtQ8\nzjA9ej1anVFLtoLW2kSqfWxd5y4abNCJILpzMq58tPfnWhyQolx55JU/QupHMZ3T\nWHJ4D8ZIZK3qWsTezqINHilmoXt3SNT12xqV2QnQddiMX8zXangZV9u6fFTKJPdp\nfvjqQx973h+hPFKsD0v8B+tp3q2LQA+eR0F5U912vQ4H7xHaQGFF042OO02bFukh\nShnPYqtJ5M6g7iTeGhQeCHvKjCWhElRYomg63SDXiNvmFOeCmkQ+9bggHBljztqE\n2ogoZ+57sp9wiRnXXUqZo6nWDTpUEpePuJsn6435kMH6Ji5ffuLsJqv23MZ5Veua\na35rU4npe+KiYzeqzhAD\n=UU7R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:17:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDgzZTQ3ZDI0NDM5NWVmODVjYTA2OWFhYWQ5ODhhNThlNDdiYzYxNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/ef816a9c2202c3a315b73ec396d7a16216c4fe9d","sha":"ef816a9c2202c3a315b73ec396d7a16216c4fe9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ef816a9c2202c3a315b73ec396d7a16216c4fe9d"}],"sha":"83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/83e47d244395ef85ca069aaad988a58e47bc6146"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56427313?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrewEhlo","id":56427313,"login":"AndrewEhlo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDI3MzEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ef816a9c2202c3a315b73ec396d7a16216c4fe9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:37:11Z","email":"56427313+AndrewEhlo@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Andrew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:37:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: use actions and workflows from VirtoCommerce/.github v3.1000.1 (VCST-5414) (#371)\n\nThe actions moved from `vc-github-actions` to `VirtoCommerce/.github`\n(VCST-5414). `vc-github-actions` is frozen: its `@master` refs keep\nworking but no longer get updates.\n\n- Switches every `uses: VirtoCommerce/vc-github-actions/<action>@…` to\n`VirtoCommerce/.github/actions/<action>@v3.1000.1`.\n- Moves reusable workflows (`VirtoCommerce/.github/.github/workflows/*`)\nto `@v3.1000.1` where they exist in that release.\n- Nothing else in the workflows changes: only `uses:` lines are edited.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> CI-only `uses:` pin changes with no application or runtime logic\nmodified; main risk is a mis-pinned action version breaking image\ntagging or Jira key parsing in this workflow.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Updates **Storybook CI** to consume shared GitHub Actions from\n`VirtoCommerce/.github` at tag **v3.1000.1** instead of the legacy\n`VirtoCommerce/vc-github-actions` repo on `@master`.\n> \n> The **Get Image Version** and **Parse Jira Keys from All Commits**\nsteps now point to `VirtoCommerce/.github/actions/get-image-version` and\n`get-jira-keys` respectively. Step inputs, outputs, and the rest of the\nworkflow are unchanged—only the `uses:` references move to the\nmaintained actions package (VCST-5414).\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nc384bbc0777483b640b360607e8a6a1a1ebfde08. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3cb3118693f544457d5507d6933890fac7adf717","url":"http