ubscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/ef816a9c2202c3a315b73ec396d7a16216c4fe9d","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGVmODE2YTljMjIwMmMzYTMxNWI3M2VjMzk2ZDdhMTYyMTZjNGZlOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9977ed6338c9ec068421ba317b4f7df1eeec9f72","sha":"9977ed6338c9ec068421ba317b4f7df1eeec9f72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9977ed6338c9ec068421ba317b4f7df1eeec9f72"}],"sha":"ef816a9c2202c3a315b73ec396d7a16216c4fe9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ef816a9c2202c3a315b73ec396d7a16216c4fe9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9977ed6338c9ec068421ba317b4f7df1eeec9f72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:30:15Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:30:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-blade): give a save a focus target of its own (VCST-5670) (#370)\n\nCloses the last open item on VCST-5670, which QA reopened on 2026-09-02.\n\n## What was left\n\nThe two failures from that run are already fixed and shipped in\n`2.6.0-rc.1`: the `mod+\\` shortcut with focus in the sidebar (#353) and\nself-disabling buttons (#355). Two items were not:\n\n1. **Save had no target of its own.** QA flagged it on both the\n2026-08-26 and 2026-09-02 runs: the blade region''s ref changed on every\nsave (`e10641 → e10809 → e11144`), so the blade remounts and\n`onMounted(focusIfLoose)` picks the loose focus up. That is an accident\nof the consumer''s implementation — the day a blade stops remounting on\nsave, focus lands on `<body>` and nothing reports it.\n2. **Acceptance item 2 — \"the chosen target is documented per\ntransition, so QA can assert it\"** — was only ever half done. Four\ntransitions were written up in ticket comments; the two shortcut paths\nand the popup path were not written down anywhere.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`vc-blade.vue`** — repair loose focus on the load transition itself:\n\n```ts\nwatch(\n  () => Boolean(props.loading),\n  () => focusIfLoose(() => bladeRef.value),\n);\n```\n\nSame shape as the two repairs already in the file. `focusIfLoose`\ndeclines when something live holds focus, so a user mid-edit is never\nyanked.\n\n**`focus.docs.md`** — a table of all eight transitions: target, which\ncode delivers it, and whether it is a repair (declines when focus is\nheld) or a deliberate handoff (moves it because the node is about to be\nunmounted). Plus how to measure one, including why the Tab-once check\nproves nothing where the nav precedes `main` in DOM order.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vc-blade.focus.test.ts` — two cases added. RED baseline taken: with\nthe watch reverted, \"takes focus when the save left it nowhere\" fails\nand the other four still pass.\n- `npx vitest run ui/components/organisms/vc-blade/` — 18 files, 178\ntests, green.\n- Focus-adjacent suites (`focus.test.ts`, `vc-app`, `vc-auth-layout`,\n`usePopup`) — 27 files, 261 tests, green.\n- `yarn typecheck` clean, `yarn docs:lint` 0 errors, eslint\n`--max-warnings=0` clean on the changed files.\n\n## Note for QA\n\nvcmp-dev was serving `2.6.0-rc.0` at the last run. `2.6.0-rc.1`\n(published 2026-09-08 from `cd4eeb6d6`) already carries #353 and #355 —\nverified with `git merge-base --is-ancestor`. This PR is not in any\npublished version yet.","tree":{"sha":"d669fc29981094762efc6af59f7062690364a360","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/d669fc29981094762efc6af59f7062690364a360"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/9977ed6338c9ec068421ba317b4f7df1eeec9f72","verification":{"payload":"tree d669fc29981094762efc6af59f7062690364a360\nparent 581835dae9fdf84a5421026888234ab37d98bc60\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1790173815 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790173815 +0300\n\nfix(vc-blade): give a save a focus target of its own (VCST-5670) (#370)\n\nCloses the last open item on VCST-5670, which QA reopened on 2026-09-02.\n\n## What was left\n\nThe two failures from that run are already fixed and shipped in\n`2.6.0-rc.1`: the `mod+\\` shortcut with focus in the sidebar (#353) and\nself-disabling buttons (#355). Two items were not:\n\n1. **Save had no target of its own.** QA flagged it on both the\n2026-08-26 and 2026-09-02 runs: the blade region''s ref changed on every\nsave (`e10641 → e10809 → e11144`), so the blade remounts and\n`onMounted(focusIfLoose)` picks the loose focus up. That is an accident\nof the consumer''s implementation — the day a blade stops remounting on\nsave, focus lands on `<body>` and nothing reports it.\n2. **Acceptance item 2 — \"the chosen target is documented per\ntransition, so QA can assert it\"** — was only ever half done. Four\ntransitions were written up in ticket comments; the two shortcut paths\nand the popup path were not written down anywhere.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`vc-blade.vue`** — repair loose focus on the load transition itself:\n\n```ts\nwatch(\n  () => Boolean(props.loading),\n  () => focusIfLoose(() => bladeRef.value),\n);\n```\n\nSame shape as the two repairs already in the file. `focusIfLoose`\ndeclines when something live holds focus, so a user mid-edit is never\nyanked.\n\n**`focus.docs.md`** — a table of all eight transitions: target, which\ncode delivers it, and whether it is a repair (declines when focus is\nheld) or a deliberate handoff (moves it because the node is about to be\nunmounted). Plus how to measure one, including why the Tab-once check\nproves nothing where the nav precedes `main` in DOM order.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vc-blade.focus.test.ts` — two cases added. RED baseline taken: with\nthe watch reverted, \"takes focus when the save left it nowhere\" fails\nand the other four still pass.\n- `npx vitest run ui/components/organisms/vc-blade/` — 18 files, 178\ntests, green.\n- Focus-adjacent suites (`focus.test.ts`, `vc-app`, `vc-auth-layout`,\n`usePopup`) — 27 files, 261 tests, green.\n- `yarn typecheck` clean, `yarn docs:lint` 0 errors, eslint\n`--max-warnings=0` clean on the changed files.\n\n## Note for QA\n\nvcmp-dev was serving `2.6.0-rc.0` at the last run. `2.6.0-rc.1`\n(published 2026-09-08 from `cd4eeb6d6`) already carries #353 and #355 —\nverified with `git merge-base --is-ancestor`. This PR is not in any\npublished version yet.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs+J4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAokAQACxVL2p9uwBxRZtwU859CRMO\n3hRBZ5Biw8bNPHQMvIutWev1C9oP2wJt9+mXsCjctUFPgL1x7Chjub/4hse2uLo8\nmP5fdl8T0U/Q3xAQvptsU0HcWZqZapLn0J1NQ3oDVxNIe2mgaEl+1iKFKC8Ygw2H\n7HEfMpPjJrCj/OQEmUj3pVaeWkcJVSFVy35e345GlQnQCJR4t1MN29ZzJcY57Wgs\nnIVdXdVvvxnFfIJejO7FWyistaAcs915j/N9ifpwGGPgXsNIddHa5QuMsD4ScGf2\n1GAkpYiDkaqscoxG