om/users/vc-ci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vc-ci","id":31079468,"login":"vc-ci","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDc5NDY4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/cd4eeb6d68e85266735267e135a4296ce4e8932e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T10:10:58Z","email":"ci@virtocommerce.com","name":"vc-ci"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T10:10:58Z","email":"ci@virtocommerce.com","name":"vc-ci"},"message":"release: v2.6.0-rc.1","tree":{"sha":"dfa4c0d99900e84c958c664f587409466c190f38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/dfa4c0d99900e84c958c664f587409466c190f38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/cd4eeb6d68e85266735267e135a4296ce4e8932e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31079468?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vc-ci","id":31079468,"login":"vc-ci","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDc5NDY4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/cd4eeb6d68e85266735267e135a4296ce4e8932e","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGNkNGVlYjZkNjhlODUyNjY3MzUyNjdlMTM1YTQyOTZjZTRlODkzMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/371aa8ec59e2cd88d583e2686afaea15dcd02aeb","sha":"371aa8ec59e2cd88d583e2686afaea15dcd02aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/371aa8ec59e2cd88d583e2686afaea15dcd02aeb"}],"sha":"cd4eeb6d68e85266735267e135a4296ce4e8932e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/cd4eeb6d68e85266735267e135a4296ce4e8932e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/371aa8ec59e2cd88d583e2686afaea15dcd02aeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:52:03Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:52:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(framework): let consumers own a dynamic property''s label row (VM-1795) (#357)\n\nFramework half of VM-1795. Adds two additive props so a consumer can\nsuppress a form control''s visible label without the field losing its\naccessible name, and fixes the accessible-name gaps that surfaced while\nwiring them up. No user-visible behaviour ships here on its own — the\npopover UI that consumes these props lives in the vendor-portal\nrepository and is a separate PR.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `VcDynamicProperty` gains `hideLabel`. It passes an empty `label` to\nwhichever control the property''s kind selects, while leaving the\nvee-validate `Field` label, the placeholder fallback and `name` intact,\nand forwards the display name to the control as an accessible name. All\n17 control bindings were converted; the `Field` on line 5 deliberately\nkeeps `computedProperty.displayName`.\n- `VcInput`, `VcTextarea`, `VcColorInput`, `VcDatePicker` and\n`VcInputDropdown` gain `ariaLabel`, applied to their own focusable input\nas `!label ? ariaLabel : undefined` — the convention `VcSwitch` and\n`VcRadioButton` already used. This fills a real gap: before this, a\ncontrol rendered without a visible label had no way to be given a name\nat all.\n- `VcDatePicker` needs its own path because the underlying date-picker\nlibrary ignores a plain `aria-label` and reads `ariaLabels.input`; the\nprop is merged into `datePickerOptions.ariaLabels` while preserving any\nkeys a consumer already passed, and the merge does not fire when a\nvisible label exists.\n\n## The contract, and what it deliberately excludes\n\n`hideLabel` guarantees an accessible name for nine control families —\nshort text, long text, number, integer, boolean, datetime, colour,\nmeasure, and the unrecognized-`valueType` fallback. The prop''s JSDoc,\n`vc-dynamic-property.docs.md` and the story argType all enumerate them.\n\nDictionary and multivalue properties are **not** covered, and that is\nstated in the contract rather than papered over: `VcSelect` and\n`VcMultivalue` hand their computed name to the popup listbox, not to the\nfocusable trigger, so a label-less select there has no accessible name.\nThat is `main`''s behaviour, untouched by this branch, and it needs its\nown fix — the blast radius is every label-less select in the product, so\nit does not belong here.\n\n## Fixes found while building this\n\n- `vc-input` / `vc-textarea` briefly fell back to `name` when no\n`ariaLabel` was given. Since `name` defaults to the literal string\n`\"Field\"`, that put `aria-label=\"Field\"` on roughly twenty existing\nlabel-less inputs across the framework — table search headers, column\nfilters, cell editors, the sidebar and the app hub — where they had\npreviously fallen back to their placeholder. Removed; a regression test\nnow pins that a placeholder-only input carries neither `aria-label` nor\n`aria-labelledby`.\n- Six `VcSelect`/`VcMultivalue` branches in `vc-dynamic-property` never\nbound `:name` at all, so their internal `label || name` fallback had\nnothing to fall back to. Added.\n- The `short-text` branch was the only one ignoring an explicit\n`placeholder` prop. Fixed to match its siblings; identity for every\ncaller that passes none.\n\n## Also included\n\n`fix(storybook): drop baseUrl override that broke path alias resolution`\n— `.storybook/tsconfig.json` overrode `baseUrl` to the repo root while\ninheriting `@ui/*` paths from `framework/tsconfig.json`, which\nre-anchored those aliases to a directory that does not exist and made\nESLint''s resolver fail on any framework `.ts` file, blocking the\npre-commit hook. It rides along because every commit here needed a\nworking hook; it is also queued on its own branch, so it can be dropped\non rebase if that merges first.\n\n## Verification\n\n`yarn typecheck`, `yarn lint:check`, `yarn check:locales`, `yarn\ncheck:circular`, `yarn check:layers` — all exit 0. Framework unit tests:\n417 files / 4158 tests. `yarn test:storybook` (the axe accessibility\ngate, every story is a test): 77 files / 618 tests. `yarn docs:lint`: 0\nerrors.\n\nThe Storybook gate matters here specifically because it is the only gate\nthat renders these components for real — it was extended with a\n`HideLabel` story so the new path is covered by axe.\n\nRef VM-1795.","tree":{"sha":"fc7655747e090cb223c92dc96f5f13a080f7f0d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/fc7655747e090cb223c92dc96f5f13a080f7f0d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/371aa8ec59e2cd88d583e2686afaea15dcd02aeb","verification":{"payload":"tree fc7655747e090cb223c92dc96f5f13a080f7f0d3\nparent 76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788861123 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788861123 +0300\n\nfeat(framework): let consumers own a dynamic property''s label row (VM-1795) (#357)\n\nFramework half of VM-1795. Adds two additive props so a consumer can\nsuppress a form control''s visible label without the field losing its\naccessible name, and fixes the accessible-name gaps that surfaced while\nwiring them up. No user-visible behaviour ships here on its own — the\npopover UI that consumes these props lives in the vendor-portal\nrepository and is a separate PR.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `VcDynamicProperty` gains `hideLabel`. It passes an empty `label` to\nwhichever control the property''s kind selects, while leaving the\nvee-validate `Field` label, the placeholder fallback and `name` intact,\nand forwards the display name to the control as an accessible name. All\n17 control bindings were converted; the `Field` on line 5 deliberately\nkeeps `computedProperty.displayName`.\n- `VcInput`, `VcTextarea`, `VcColorInput`, `VcDatePicker` and\n`VcInputDropdown` gain `ariaLabel`, applied to their own focusable input\nas `!label ? ariaLabel : undefined` — the convention `VcSwitch` and\n`VcRadioButton` already used. This fills a real gap: before this, a\ncontrol rendered without a visible label had no way to be given a name\nat all.\n- `VcDatePicker` needs its own path because the underlying date-picker\nlibrary ignores a plain `aria-label` and reads `ariaLabels.input`; the\nprop is merged into `datePickerOptions.ariaLabels` while preserving any\nkeys a consumer already passed, and the merge does not fire when a\nvisible label exists.\n\n## The contract, and what it deliberately excludes\n\n`hideLabel` guarantees an accessible name for nine control families —\nshort text, long text, number, integer, boolean, datetime, colour,\nmeasure, and the unrecognized-`valueType` fallback. The prop''s JSDoc,\n`vc-dynamic-property.docs.md` and the story argType all enumerate them.\n\nDictionary and multivalue properties are **not** covered, and that is\nstated in the contract rather than papered over: `VcSelect` and\n`VcMultivalue` hand their computed name to the popup listbox, not to the\nfocusable trigger, so a label-less select there has no accessible name.\nThat is `main`''s behaviour, untouched by this branch, and it needs its\nown fix — the blast radius is every label-less select in the product, so\nit does not belong here.\n\n## Fixes found while building this\n\n- `vc-input` / `vc-textarea` briefly fell back to `name` when no\n`ariaLabel` was given. Since `name` defaults to the literal string\n`\"Field\"`, that put `aria-label=\"Field\"` on roughly twenty existing\nlabel-less inputs across the framework — table search headers, column\nfilters, cell editors, the sidebar and the app hub — where they had\npreviously fallen back to their placeholder. Removed; a regression test\nnow pins that a placeholder-only input carries neither `aria-label` nor\n`aria-labelledby`.\n- Six `VcSelect`/`VcMultivalue` branches in `vc-dynamic-property` never\nbound `:name` at all, so their internal `label || name` fallback had\nnothing to fall back to. Added.\n- The `short-text` branch was the only one ignoring an explicit\n`placeholder` prop. Fixed to match its siblings; identity for every\ncaller that passes none.\n\n## Also included\n\n`fix(storybook): drop baseUrl override that broke path alias resolution`\n— `.storybook/tsconfig.json` overrode `baseUrl` to the repo root while\ninheriting `@ui/*` paths from `framework/tsconfig.json`, which\nre-anchored those aliases to a directory that does not exist and made\nESLint''s resolver fail on any framework `.ts` file, blocking the\npre-commit hook. It rides along because every commit here needed a\nworking hook; it is also queued on its own branch, so it can be dropped\non rebase if that merges first.\n\n## Verification\n\n`yarn typecheck`, `yarn lint:check`, `yarn check:locales`, `yarn\ncheck:circular`, `yarn check:layers` — all exit 0. Framework unit tests:\n417 files / 4158 tests. `yarn test:storybook` (the axe accessibility\ngate, every story is a test): 77 files / 618 tests. `yarn docs:lint`: 0\nerrors.\n\nThe Storybook gate matters here specifically because it is the only gate\nthat renders these components for real — it was extended with a\n`HideLabel` story so the new path is covered by axe.\n\nRef VM-1795.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn9rDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+KgQAHurxU0n+AePwE33+CuAbpOy\ngXDf53q3VWtP1oVpWwQwYEWH/Cdlq0sdVSpXLGkbnx2JVqrZ/6D3bmhV0QD8e4AP\nE5oXCxE2Rmnh5/WevvMqfs8rDy3eZJ2IWfKjfR/sADi7JTPBirMmn3zsZGeqXNEj\n4EpyloO97HXRSdve0nZ8jFo623m2gm+0MA+0uuzeHIRn6vzLW9uBU5oGrtHhcZLZ\nl6dO1k8jV99CeopLY1SScWMspCgOrNPCxWBNOBzOTsEaATN0d9FJJ1yuewts/jAm\nluH49x6/aGc5HLLefTVBEXgP2BLIxxSr7Mgro4kefAzzwUgNxxKIGyzfybMQyPzp\nVk5pTDdKXNi7McjPC33Dz5OpXyuw/TAw4C7Xa4C2Cu/jgS+/xMe84YIJNV1cz9jb\n87SwIgoTaqhDUd89x1+lwlnzEO9lzo3sQ1jkK/T62idHzhnlHQdovNbgs8EAakbB\n9xMbIh2fAELuWL3bM/uIW7rlJIjUJu6zeonNQTfaMPEP7HGVbCEm9PcS1w1kvPep\nV3IB+kVnbwu5uhlpjlFuLVMW/O1clRyARgAm46M/u+jvJOniDa/xMA84vjqX7JaE\nyO0v2tyU36cEexsIdxO/u8QF1CsA0752hsCx51CdB6uYjz6lzYKrWfsM18sD/iRC\nxZeiVL2pU285VMGp7L2s\n=Ww2/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T09:52:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/371aa8ec59e2cd88d583e2686afaea15dcd02aeb","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDM3MWFhOGVjNTllMmNkODhkNTgzZTI2ODZhZmFlYTE1ZGNkMDJhZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06","sha":"76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06"}],"sha":"371aa8ec59e2cd88d583e2686afaea15dcd02aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/371aa8ec59e2cd88d583e2686afaea15dcd02aeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:05:30Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:05:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(create-vc-app): drop the unknown projectType arg from the init test (#354)\n\n## What\n\nRemoves a single stale argument from\n`cli/create-vc-app/src/commands/init.test.ts`:\n\n```diff\n       const data = buildTemplateData({\n         projectName: \"demo\",\n         packageName: \"demo\",\n-        projectType: \"standalone\",\n         moduleName: \"Orders\",\n```\n\n## Why\n\n`buildTemplateData()` never had a `projectType` option — the template\ndirectory is chosen by the caller''s path\n(`templateRoot/standalone/...`), not by the template data — so the\nobject literal failed TypeScript''s excess property check:\n\n```\nsrc/commands/init.test.ts:470:9 - error TS2353: Object literal may only specify known properties,\nand ''projectType'' does not exist in type ''{ moduleName?: string | undefined; ... }''.\n```\n\nThe key was copy-pasted from `InitOptions` when the EJS-whitespace test\nblock was added in #302; the later Module Federation block in the same\nfile already omits it.\n\nNothing was gating this:\n\n- the root `typecheck` script only runs `@vc-shell/framework`''s\n`check:types`, so `cli/*` is never type-checked in CI;\n- during `yarn build` the error is reported by `vite-plugin-dts`, which\nprints the diagnostic and still exits 0 — the log ends with a green `✓\nbuilt`.\n\nAs a result the diagnostic sat in `main` from #302 onward, across the\nv2.5.0 release.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npx tsc -p src/tsconfig.json --noEmit` in `cli/create-vc-app` — clean\n(this was the only error in the package)\n- `npx vitest run --root cli/create-vc-app --config vitest.config.ts` —\n4 files, 74 tests passed\n- `yarn workspace @vc-shell/create-vc-app run build` — no diagnostics\n\n## Follow-up (not in this PR)\n\nWiring the `cli/*` packages'' `check:types` into the root `yarn check`\nwould keep the next such error from reaching a release unnoticed.","tree":{"sha":"b3769b5c1ce029f5a2152b5fcc3fc2b5bcc6ec8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/b3769b5c1ce029f5a2152b5fcc3fc2b5bcc6ec8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06","verification":{"payload":"tree b3769b5c1ce029f5a2152b5fcc3fc2b5bcc6ec8f\nparent 477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788527130 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788527130 +0300\n\nfix(create-vc-app): drop the unknown projectType arg from the init test (#354)\n\n## What\n\nRemoves a single stale argument from\n`cli/create-vc-app/src/commands/init.test.ts`:\n\n```diff\n       const data = buildTemplateData({\n         projectName: \"demo\",\n         packageName: \"demo\",\n-        projectType: \"standalone\",\n         moduleName: \"Orders\",\n```\n\n## Why\n\n`buildTemplateData()` never had a `projectType` option — the template\ndirectory is chosen by the caller''s path\n(`templateRoot/standalone/...`), not by the template data — so the\nobject literal failed TypeScript''s excess property check:\n\n```\nsrc/commands/init.test.ts:470:9 - error TS2353: Object literal may only specify known properties,\nand ''projectType'' does not exist in type ''{ moduleName?: string | undefined; ... }''.\n```\n\nThe key was copy-pasted from `InitOptions` when the EJS-whitespace test\nblock was added in #302; the later Module Federation block in the same\nfile already omits it.\n\nNothing was gating this:\n\n- the root `typecheck` script only runs `@vc-shell/framework`''s\n`check:types`, so `cli/*` is never type-checked in CI;\n- during `yarn build` the error is reported by `vite-plugin-dts`, which\nprints the diagnostic and still exits 0 — the log ends with a green `✓\nbuilt`.\n\nAs a result the diagnostic sat in `main` from #302 onward, across the\nv2.5.0 release.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npx tsc -p src/tsconfig.json --noEmit` in `cli/create-vc-app` — clean\n(this was the only error in the package)\n- `npx vitest run --root cli/create-vc-app --config vitest.config.ts` —\n4 files, 74 tests passed\n- `yarn workspace @vc-shell/create-vc-app run build` — no diagnostics\n\n## Follow-up (not in this PR)\n\nWiring the `cli/*` packages'' `check:types` into the root `yarn check`\nwould keep the next such error from reaching a release unnoticed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmsIaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzxAQAFEJH2tt07SedyEXkpNuDMz8\nO90TOrklABdNcsQMVmCWT8mLNt0+GWhtSfBuXTJ/gxB0TJFd0/rw5y/VZ+2N98zx\nm0L/3cx2x+/iY2lx/11klZhFuXduDNS/gCStrHfpcm9i3FPGmjFcCJ8Xp4tYTzY1\nXVxdZmmVLnyomDaxxdfIwdFA29fxO9NrmbImekNTsTT3D26p+T0lPFGXt3KP0vk+\n/OAq9uw81MFBgF8GOw30y0VaHJzxwi1AxZnMA3vybKKw9Ysz1TOdoKxDiq1sWkic\nCG8rfyvMSjNUZMESYjwxCA3bjvtdoQnSHGvA+XWx8b7EJDfyjiP1fX9P0zo54BGu\nUqM9aWAJnTCMv2EqmvcFP+wfgvEKNj3by6WJS5kvVWtfgMMZgH22NPzT9G4aGQ1p\nkzLVx4s3xB67QY6L7hu4EJ8pAiEbdFyyyEAbqYj9NLuDZnESnbtHGGPbnkE6p1cx\n3a3EsC7GfV8TsKhRBrks5wYwiDV9qa9pxV82lBMdFjCpbZn6jmjI+gIunvU4j2Ml\nM+6SBhiNZXU6hI60ftgReanhcq6rFMQqfZkNYJzHAc8xIjI967gsZzqILboXIguU\nsakUeKYokyBRXtW/mbrQXsunIGhx/glS4PNbJff0htliQN0b2Qrwl4GZXRUFxl5z\nELI+MjtetfYuJ58ebZn8\n=cOyG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T13:05:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDc2ZTM4ZThlZjk4MGU1MjIyOWZkM2JiNTVmNDQ0ZWI0ZDIwODVkMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594","sha":"477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594"}],"sha":"76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/76e38e8ef980e52229fd3bb55f444eb4d2085d06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:52:08Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:52:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): bring the reported colour-contrast failures up to AA (#356)\n\n### What the 25 violations actually are\n\nMeasured with axe on the running Vendor Portal rather than derived from\nthe source. They come from a few elements, repeated — not 25 independent\nplaces. That matters, because `--neutrals-400` has 46 uses in the\nframework and a blanket swap would have been wrong.\n\n| Element | light | dark | fix | after (light / dark) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| User role label, 11px | 2.41:1 | 3.41:1 | `--neutrals-500` | 4.54 /\n5.09 |\n| Relative timestamps (×7) | 2.52:1 white row · 2.09:1 selected row |\n3.16:1 · 2.83:1 | `--neutrals-600` | 7.81 · 6.49 / 5.76 · 5.16 |\n| Sorted column header | 4.41:1 | passes | `--primary-800` | 5.6 / 8.96\n|\n| Environment banner | 2.79:1 | fails on primary and danger | black\nlabel ink | 6.33–12.33 / 4.56–8.32 |\n\n`--neutrals-600` rather than `-500` for the timestamps because `-500` is\nstill **3.94:1** on the selected-row tint.\n\nThe palette''s own comments already say what these tokens are for: `-400`\nis *\"muted text / disabled\"*, `-500` is *\"secondary text (WCAG AA\n~5:1)\"*. The defect was text reaching for the disabled ink.\n\n### Both themes, from one change\n\nThe first three are **token references, not values**, so each theme\nresolves them against its own scale. The ticket audited Light only; Dark\nhad the same two defects and is fixed by the same swap.\n\n### The environment banner needed more than a swap\n\nIts label was white on every variant — 1.70:1 to 3.32:1 in Light, worst\non amber, and no shade of amber fixes white text. In Dark the\ntheme-following ink already failed on `primary` (4.34) and `danger`\n(3.15) **before any change here**.\n\nSweeping all seven variants in both themes, from the live cascade:\n\n| ink | worst, light | worst, dark |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| white (before) | 1.70 warning | 2.52 warning |\n| `--additional-50` (dark''s value) | — | 3.15 danger |\n| `--neutrals-800` | 3.19 neutral | 2.12 warning |\n| **black** | **6.33 danger** | **4.56 danger** |\n\nBlack is the only ink that clears AA on every accent background, and no\npalette token can carry it: every candidate flips with the theme —\n`--additional-950` is `#000000` in Light but `#ebebeb` in Dark — while\nthese backgrounds stay mid-tone in both. Hence a fixed value, with the\nreasoning in the comment.\n\nThe `neutral` variant, and an unmodified banner which shares its\nbackground, keep the theme-following token: that grey is too dark for\nblack (4.43) and the token passes in both (4.74 / 4.72).\n\n**No background changed** — every variant keeps the colour it was\ndesigned with; only the label moved.\n\n### Not swapped\n\n`--neutrals-400` stays wherever it marks a **disabled or inactive**\ncontrol — WCAG 1.4.3 exempts those, and darkening them would make\ndisabled read as enabled.\n\nThe toolbar''s disabled title was in QA''s list and is **not** fixed here:\naxe flagged it only because the button exposed no disabled state at all,\nso axe could not know the exemption applied.\n[#355](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/pull/355) adds\n`aria-disabled` and the finding disappears — confirmed by elimination,\nsince this PR does not touch that colour.\n\n### Verification\n\nFull axe pass over `#/`, `#/products`, `#/orders` and `#/offers`, both\nthemes:\n\n```\nbefore   light 23 nodes   dark 16 nodes      (colour-contrast; no other rule fires)\nafter    light  0         dark  0\n```\n\nThe last three failures were app code, not framework — the dashboard\nwidget empty states — fixed in\n[vendor-portal#154](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vendor-portal/pull/154).\nWith that and this in, the four routes report zero axe violations of any\nrule in either theme.\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4123 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier and stylelint clean.\n\nOne limit worth stating: the story-level axe gate has `color-contrast`\ndisabled as a documented exception, so nothing in CI keeps this from\ndrifting back.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5862","tree":{"sha":"b3769b5c1ce029f5a2152b5fcc3fc2b5bcc6ec8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/b3769b5c1ce029f5a2152b5fcc3fc2b5bcc6ec8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594","verification":{"payload":"tree b3769b5c1ce029f5a2152b5fcc3fc2b5bcc6ec8f\nparent 8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788526328 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788526328 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): bring the reported colour-contrast failures up to AA (#356)\n\n### What the 25 violations actually are\n\nMeasured with axe on the running Vendor Portal rather than derived from\nthe source. They come from a few elements, repeated — not 25 independent\nplaces. That matters, because `--neutrals-400` has 46 uses in the\nframework and a blanket swap would have been wrong.\n\n| Element | light | dark | fix | after (light / dark) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| User role label, 11px | 2.41:1 | 3.41:1 | `--neutrals-500` | 4.54 /\n5.09 |\n| Relative timestamps (×7) | 2.52:1 white row · 2.09:1 selected row |\n3.16:1 · 2.83:1 | `--neutrals-600` | 7.81 · 6.49 / 5.76 · 5.16 |\n| Sorted column header | 4.41:1 | passes | `--primary-800` | 5.6 / 8.96\n|\n| Environment banner | 2.79:1 | fails on primary and danger | black\nlabel ink | 6.33–12.33 / 4.56–8.32 |\n\n`--neutrals-600` rather than `-500` for the timestamps because `-500` is\nstill **3.94:1** on the selected-row tint.\n\nThe palette''s own comments already say what these tokens are for: `-400`\nis *\"muted text / disabled\"*, `-500` is *\"secondary text (WCAG AA\n~5:1)\"*. The defect was text reaching for the disabled ink.\n\n### Both themes, from one change\n\nThe first three are **token references, not values**, so each theme\nresolves them against its own scale. The ticket audited Light only; Dark\nhad the same two defects and is fixed by the same swap.\n\n### The environment banner needed more than a swap\n\nIts label was white on every variant — 1.70:1 to 3.32:1 in Light, worst\non amber, and no shade of amber fixes white text. In Dark the\ntheme-following ink already failed on `primary` (4.34) and `danger`\n(3.15) **before any change here**.\n\nSweeping all seven variants in both themes, from the live cascade:\n\n| ink | worst, light | worst, dark |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| white (before) | 1.70 warning | 2.52 warning |\n| `--additional-50` (dark''s value) | — | 3.15 danger |\n| `--neutrals-800` | 3.19 neutral | 2.12 warning |\n| **black** | **6.33 danger** | **4.56 danger** |\n\nBlack is the only ink that clears AA on every accent background, and no\npalette token can carry it: every candidate flips with the theme —\n`--additional-950` is `#000000` in Light but `#ebebeb` in Dark — while\nthese backgrounds stay mid-tone in both. Hence a fixed value, with the\nreasoning in the comment.\n\nThe `neutral` variant, and an unmodified banner which shares its\nbackground, keep the theme-following token: that grey is too dark for\nblack (4.43) and the token passes in both (4.74 / 4.72).\n\n**No background changed** — every variant keeps the colour it was\ndesigned with; only the label moved.\n\n### Not swapped\n\n`--neutrals-400` stays wherever it marks a **disabled or inactive**\ncontrol — WCAG 1.4.3 exempts those, and darkening them would make\ndisabled read as enabled.\n\nThe toolbar''s disabled title was in QA''s list and is **not** fixed here:\naxe flagged it only because the button exposed no disabled state at all,\nso axe could not know the exemption applied.\n[#355](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/pull/355) adds\n`aria-disabled` and the finding disappears — confirmed by elimination,\nsince this PR does not touch that colour.\n\n### Verification\n\nFull axe pass over `#/`, `#/products`, `#/orders` and `#/offers`, both\nthemes:\n\n```\nbefore   light 23 nodes   dark 16 nodes      (colour-contrast; no other rule fires)\nafter    light  0         dark  0\n```\n\nThe last three failures were app code, not framework — the dashboard\nwidget empty states — fixed in\n[vendor-portal#154](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vendor-portal/pull/154).\nWith that and this in, the four routes report zero axe violations of any\nrule in either theme.\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4123 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier and stylelint clean.\n\nOne limit worth stating: the story-level axe gate has `color-contrast`\ndisabled as a documented exception, so nothing in CI keeps this from\ndrifting back.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5862","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmr74CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiVgQAD7BZDvZX9y+mbOMD/wxggQi\nUjlf3y0FqJGPj1VimLlrxK3aWswofQSqCKpaxNlz47Tu2rt1sJQZPFgmWOCQ1AHi\njqdf6BKwNqZDEe76lJT4mdB/X/JROCypAMG1+1m5GgmPBgFL2eUCKlSDuT/mIBy1\nLVfLQWXcXCXDbusQnDgXO61E7SixmUldz+n5wf8Xf+W4LcHeHehSaAq9lATbWYUB\nn+z095c5EA7sOs1NSMwjePo87TOcXV00YDSCv2MJPzadVog4lMVyha8yi/hPa0yS\niu1TiCiUCzQ21AYBkmoxFN19R/lulSdMJ9i0x1sNL8PZUL8W0ix2mpTs69Yj48UW\nAywVsPOd+O6HWN5I8DFWn+2SqtpRApRBAy3jRVH8I5Lyx0RqLfpGydTXrOMCEO0I\nhAqJn/iND82NDe/7DjgU266ez9hDTEV362ypI6grp6/LtsJEqc2JpQW5VP2ckRNL\nxWvk3up/m7HyDRN7FILCnJDo41uA3+77COzdgbRCw/7ZfDbiyhDhbXfBuBxlSJJO\n+r3AjsQMOVzFnzAa1KcZe93m3R/+HSMFE1cmL0YxwTWrQGBjfUMji+Slvlh1ryth\nB8p3xHPp8vwOGhm//+zb+A0l0NULIoH5ff0zKZvUxJGnmnnBgzwZ0JW6/74JxYJq\nLsoE34ayTzeIbdZqUqYY\n=tasq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T12:52:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDQ3N2NiNTI5OTAwYzlkYjQ1MDQ3MTBkNTJhYjA5OGViODQwNDc1OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2","sha":"8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2"}],"sha":"477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/477cb529900c9db4504710d52ab098eb84047594"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:51:46Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:51:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): make blade-toolbar buttons announce that they are unavailable (#355)\n\nA disabled blade-toolbar button carried its state **only** in a CSS\nmodifier class — no `disabled`, no `aria-disabled`:\n\n```html\n<button class=\"vc-blade-toolbar-base-button vc-blade-toolbar-base-button--disabled\" data-test-id=\"save\">\n```\n\nSo assistive tech was told these were ordinary actionable buttons while\nthey were inert, and a keyboard user tabbed onto a control that does\nnothing with no reason given. WCAG 4.1.2.\n\n### Fix\n\n`aria-disabled` rather than the native attribute, so the control stays\nreachable. In a toolbar a keyboard user should be able to find a button\nand be told it is unavailable, rather than have it disappear from the\ntab order — the same choice #347 made for a focused self-disabling\nbutton. `handleClick` already refuses, so pressing it does nothing.\n\nTwo things the ticket did not mention, found while fixing:\n\n- The button''s **own in-flight click** used the same class and was\nequally silent. It now announces too, and clears when the handler\nsettles.\n- `ToolbarCircleButton` delegates to this component, so it is covered by\nthe same change. `ToolbarMobile` already sets the native attribute and\nan `aria-label`, and is untouched.\n\n### Tests\n\nFive cases: announced when disabled, silent when actionable, still in\nthe tab order while disabled, the in-flight state, and the shortcut\nvariant — which renders a **separate** `<button>` inside a tooltip\nwrapper and would otherwise have been missed. Reverting the fix fails\nthree of the five.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4128 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` and\nprettier clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5861","tree":{"sha":"d5c033afaef406446de57bda3f80a59e82112285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/d5c033afaef406446de57bda3f80a59e82112285"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2","verification":{"payload":"tree d5c033afaef406446de57bda3f80a59e82112285\nparent 741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788526306 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788526306 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): make blade-toolbar buttons announce that they are unavailable (#355)\n\nA disabled blade-toolbar button carried its state **only** in a CSS\nmodifier class — no `disabled`, no `aria-disabled`:\n\n```html\n<button class=\"vc-blade-toolbar-base-button vc-blade-toolbar-base-button--disabled\" data-test-id=\"save\">\n```\n\nSo assistive tech was told these were ordinary actionable buttons while\nthey were inert, and a keyboard user tabbed onto a control that does\nnothing with no reason given. WCAG 4.1.2.\n\n### Fix\n\n`aria-disabled` rather than the native attribute, so the control stays\nreachable. In a toolbar a keyboard user should be able to find a button\nand be told it is unavailable, rather than have it disappear from the\ntab order — the same choice #347 made for a focused self-disabling\nbutton. `handleClick` already refuses, so pressing it does nothing.\n\nTwo things the ticket did not mention, found while fixing:\n\n- The button''s **own in-flight click** used the same class and was\nequally silent. It now announces too, and clears when the handler\nsettles.\n- `ToolbarCircleButton` delegates to this component, so it is covered by\nthe same change. `ToolbarMobile` already sets the native attribute and\nan `aria-label`, and is untouched.\n\n### Tests\n\nFive cases: announced when disabled, silent when actionable, still in\nthe tab order while disabled, the in-flight state, and the shortcut\nvariant — which renders a **separate** `<button>` inside a tooltip\nwrapper and would otherwise have been missed. Reverting the fix fails\nthree of the five.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4128 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` and\nprettier clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5861","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmr7iCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArrgQAGYva9CUHdafSdUg90x9GtiR\noXm4TeqlSzTBaz3TNrjDj2E/S1Hs+nU5B3pAZy5N2XTEx2JQhDGYeSOgXDv4vaZ1\n0iCPTd/7Oi2uW6Lvj9a1E9cWrkZKQdRKh6df/4loLMFozbrgTYg1Qsx2vnDU5D7o\nzVgS74mRvTEbtbQT41ytpChXMWiD5pXfu/HJ/+oRK9vJIi5TagXPsX8n2HfL8BXA\nfp17OgAuOyqh7RkLA1WmNI9OXGeM3+djEAemjJdC9NvsNNUMaGqO6x7elMKkplVc\nV47hOj2OxofxKnf465hoCbl+HX+3B3RJma7l/79T37t31yxWCL+OYzGZ2aMtxXDK\nTOMS0L6RON6F6tJF8qYNzQh8UmTpOHmWHAUzEogJ6xQRhgzpAdYqsINQ+sP6ROVW\nZ01KsvCZNDSFIbPq3BW1a+z6HZAFdk6HS03oTo/WxiIXYsukt9EpEZCSj0f+uE8b\nYy1iOgfv4llV/L922ABYZhLvuigtICjx30AnYF1a5gFq/5AvNakulw3Np0MHRkFh\nbsiAvkM23UfWybNuN1+7CdKJ9/DCA5Pao7Dk7Vi5YSjvFAd8C0cuDyQzjnsyMrtO\noGumrRLN2+pQmHU1h4G9K5clqDrGLPW0/S3U4nnPp8MnHc/1xSQ+GuVTKo94vGP/\nwrL2VpyyCPSUQw/jjERB\n=c93g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T12:51:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDhmNWM1NGY0MzQ5NjgzYTgyZmU0ODU1N2Y1ZGEwNDYxODQ0NzU2ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377","sha":"741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377"}],"sha":"8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/8f5c54f4349683a82fe48557f5da0461844756f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:51:36Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:51:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): rescue focus when maximizing a blade inerts the region holding it (#353)\n\nReported by QA against 2.6.0-rc.0 on the environment, reopening\nVCST-5670.\n\n`Ctrl/Cmd+\\` with focus in the sidebar maximizes the blade, the nav goes\n`inert`, and focus lands on `<body>` — 3/3, from three different origin\ncontrols. Restoring does not recover it, so the keyboard user is\nstranded rather than momentarily displaced.\n\n### Attribution: not #344\n\nThe ticket suggests #344''s watch as the cause. It is not — reproduced on\na tree that **predates** #344:\n\n```\nafter maximize (maximized blades: 1): <body>\nafter restore:                        <body>\n```\n\n#344''s guard asks \"is focus inside *my* header controls\", not \"does\nanything hold focus\", and it declines correctly here: handing focus\nbetween the two expand controls is its job, a general rescue is not. The\ngap arrived with the inert work in #306, released in 2.5.0.\n\n### Fix, in two parts\n\n**The blade repairs loose focus onto itself when its maximized state\nchanges.** Focus that is still somewhere live is left alone, which keeps\nthe header''s handoff in charge of its own case.\n\n**`focusIfLoose` now counts focus inside an `[inert]` subtree as\nloose.** The first part alone did not work: the repair runs after the\nDOM patch, but the browser blurs the inert node later still, so the\ncheck saw the sidebar control apparently focused and declined — exactly\nthe ordering QA described. Delaying the check would have been a guess\nabout when the blur lands; asking whether the element sits inside an\ninert subtree is a fact about the element. It is unreachable and about\nto be dropped either way.\n\n### Live A/B, on the running app\n\n| focus origin | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| sidebar → maximize | `<body>` | the maximized blade |\n| sidebar → restore | `<body>` | the blade |\n| expand control → maximize | `Restore` | `Restore` — handoff still wins\n|\n| expand control → restore | `Maximize` | `Maximize` |\n\n### Tests\n\nThree cases on the blade: takes focus when maximizing left it nowhere,\nrecovers on restore, and leaves focus alone when something still holds\nit. Reverting the watch fails the first two.\n\nOne trap worth recording: the first version of the maximize test passed\n**without** the fix, on the blade''s mount-time repair rather than on the\nwatcher. It now lets the mount settle and asserts focus is still on the\norigin before triggering, so it measures the watcher.\n\njsdom does not blur on `inert` any more than it does on `disabled`, so\nthe tests blur the origin themselves and assert what the blade owns —\nrepairing focus that is already loose. The browser half is the A/B\nabove.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4126 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier and madge clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5859","tree":{"sha":"f85910560c7edec751a3f82df9b45801012aeaac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/f85910560c7edec751a3f82df9b45801012aeaac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377","verification":{"payload":"tree f85910560c7edec751a3f82df9b45801012aeaac\nparent bf43467775961364acd1377960ba7ef655f34b39\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788526296 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788526296 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): rescue focus when maximizing a blade inerts the region holding it (#353)\n\nReported by QA against 2.6.0-rc.0 on the environment, reopening\nVCST-5670.\n\n`Ctrl/Cmd+\\` with focus in the sidebar maximizes the blade, the nav goes\n`inert`, and focus lands on `<body>` — 3/3, from three different origin\ncontrols. Restoring does not recover it, so the keyboard user is\nstranded rather than momentarily displaced.\n\n### Attribution: not #344\n\nThe ticket suggests #344''s watch as the cause. It is not — reproduced on\na tree that **predates** #344:\n\n```\nafter maximize (maximized blades: 1): <body>\nafter restore:                        <body>\n```\n\n#344''s guard asks \"is focus inside *my* header controls\", not \"does\nanything hold focus\", and it declines correctly here: handing focus\nbetween the two expand controls is its job, a general rescue is not. The\ngap arrived with the inert work in #306, released in 2.5.0.\n\n### Fix, in two parts\n\n**The blade repairs loose focus onto itself when its maximized state\nchanges.** Focus that is still somewhere live is left alone, which keeps\nthe header''s handoff in charge of its own case.\n\n**`focusIfLoose` now counts focus inside an `[inert]` subtree as\nloose.** The first part alone did not work: the repair runs after the\nDOM patch, but the browser blurs the inert node later still, so the\ncheck saw the sidebar control apparently focused and declined — exactly\nthe ordering QA described. Delaying the check would have been a guess\nabout when the blur lands; asking whether the element sits inside an\ninert subtree is a fact about the element. It is unreachable and about\nto be dropped either way.\n\n### Live A/B, on the running app\n\n| focus origin | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| sidebar → maximize | `<body>` | the maximized blade |\n| sidebar → restore | `<body>` | the blade |\n| expand control → maximize | `Restore` | `Restore` — handoff still wins\n|\n| expand control → restore | `Maximize` | `Maximize` |\n\n### Tests\n\nThree cases on the blade: takes focus when maximizing left it nowhere,\nrecovers on restore, and leaves focus alone when something still holds\nit. Reverting the watch fails the first two.\n\nOne trap worth recording: the first version of the maximize test passed\n**without** the fix, on the blade''s mount-time repair rather than on the\nwatcher. It now lets the mount settle and asserts focus is still on the\norigin before triggering, so it measures the watcher.\n\njsdom does not blur on `inert` any more than it does on `disabled`, so\nthe tests blur the origin themselves and assert what the blade owns —\nrepairing focus that is already loose. The browser half is the A/B\nabove.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4126 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier and madge clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5859","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmr7YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAggIQAJOai+5LK/14Q/SdnWC+weId\njPfP3QfCGJBROzB5FmIDiBtcaQG28AcyvRWjxDbmEtT+bQ6ljpbxCYxJv6P6xrI4\nzxDEI5ELjCXw1ei8w8oL7tFDYeONeV1NHvb8wKNwKbgNOB3vUXow3kwHtSVzpJhc\nZ7PFV7H6OpfpxIQUHEBlbdbBGj0VUJbFONhzVpuS0cNfBqEXzR+ClM8Szt03Y7zj\nrtDaQQxwgFAffNBRZWvKJjviOvmP1vpIb5lx2IlUiA7WMGx69miFciiRkIoSdiku\n7GkQ4+VURhHABABoZYUmJCQJ6U0FtzrlikJOa6XD7nMT5YyzeR6ZzeDVP18A0nyE\nHG61cAwvsoHQ59hbBXMnS1g4Uo9cYZkIb/Tl3hmdqCalVehtNM4GeGzFd8hXUWO0\no3BdyqHC5HsjWap+pj2K2s4713d52Hz+0KIYqg3WpsWGVIwQuw7GPObzX5/V+TdP\nA757lKHUShbsVIbxORxJ7CoJKOJ3MtuSqMA8q0qK+O22cGxnVzqCmLGV4WbCqXvM\n9EP/TaB77QGRupFPCZifUzQTmN24nowvDkh2kWB82NrfdEKEzqgUS9gb7weuqLba\nGv6PoZRKODUQdqhEg7tGfWNgs8FwMGWmCX9fGrUSEEcIBMDc+Re9/lztyCgOcYMk\nNk3GG0mOFuVa/1/UFSVl\n=D7Xe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T12:51:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDc0MTgzNDg5MGViMmQ3NjVmMjgwNDA4ZTU3MTliNGUwN2Y1MDUzNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/bf43467775961364acd1377960ba7ef655f34b39","sha":"bf43467775961364acd1377960ba7ef655f34b39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/bf43467775961364acd1377960ba7ef655f34b39"}],"sha":"741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/741834890eb2d765f280408e5719b4e07f505377"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/bf43467775961364acd1377960ba7ef655f34b39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:50:58Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:50:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-blade): keep skeletons up when a second load starts before a paint (#352)\n\nReported from the 2.6.0-rc.0 test deployment: in Orders the skeletons\nswitch off before the real load finishes.\n\n### What actually happens\n\n`VcBlade` closes its \"content has rendered\" latch on the falling edge of\n`loading`. A page that loads in two steps drops the flag between them,\nand nothing has rendered at that point — so the second, real fetch shows\na **busy overlay over an empty blade** instead of skeletons.\n\nThe order details blade does exactly that on mount: `await\nsearchStateMachines(...)` and then `await loadOrder(...)`, both feeding\nthe same `useLoading(...)` OR.\n\nTraced live against the running app, sampling the blade''s own markers:\n\n| | skeletons | overlay over an empty blade | content |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| before | 70–657ms | **657–1015ms** — the entire order request | 1038ms\n|\n| after | 70–1000ms — the whole load | none | 1028ms |\n\n### Fix\n\nConfirm the latch across a frame. If a new load starts before the\nbrowser paints, the user never saw content, so the latch stays open and\nthe next load still gets skeletons. The gap between the two loads\nmeasures under 8ms — comfortably inside one frame.\n\n`VcDataTable` latches on `items.length > 0` — content actually arriving\n— which is why it never had this. `VcBlade`''s comment claims the \"same\ntwo-state treatment\", but it substituted a loading-edge proxy for the\ncontent check. A blade cannot see content generically, so a painted\nframe is the closest honest proxy for \"the user saw something\".\n\n### Tests\n\nFirst tests for this latch at all — #330 shipped it stating \"No test\ncovers the overlay or the latch reset. Verified in the browser only\",\nwhich is why this reached a release candidate.\n\nThree cases: an overlay for a load that follows a completed one,\nskeletons kept when a second load starts before a paint, and the reset\nwhen the blade switches to a different entity. Reverting the frame\nconfirmation fails exactly the middle one.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4126 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier, stylelint and madge clean. Behaviour A/B''d in Chrome against\nthe running Vendor Portal, table above.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.","tree":{"sha":"5f30ef30386fa6ae73324b68c62d886122718737","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/5f30ef30386fa6ae73324b68c62d886122718737"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/bf43467775961364acd1377960ba7ef655f34b39","verification":{"payload":"tree 5f30ef30386fa6ae73324b68c62d886122718737\nparent cb6379d0f51a6858624a5c10f0258b229314acfa\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788526258 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788526258 +0300\n\nfix(vc-blade): keep skeletons up when a second load starts before a paint (#352)\n\nReported from the 2.6.0-rc.0 test deployment: in Orders the skeletons\nswitch off before the real load finishes.\n\n### What actually happens\n\n`VcBlade` closes its \"content has rendered\" latch on the falling edge of\n`loading`. A page that loads in two steps drops the flag between them,\nand nothing has rendered at that point — so the second, real fetch shows\na **busy overlay over an empty blade** instead of skeletons.\n\nThe order details blade does exactly that on mount: `await\nsearchStateMachines(...)` and then `await loadOrder(...)`, both feeding\nthe same `useLoading(...)` OR.\n\nTraced live against the running app, sampling the blade''s own markers:\n\n| | skeletons | overlay over an empty blade | content |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| before | 70–657ms | **657–1015ms** — the entire order request | 1038ms\n|\n| after | 70–1000ms — the whole load | none | 1028ms |\n\n### Fix\n\nConfirm the latch across a frame. If a new load starts before the\nbrowser paints, the user never saw content, so the latch stays open and\nthe next load still gets skeletons. The gap between the two loads\nmeasures under 8ms — comfortably inside one frame.\n\n`VcDataTable` latches on `items.length > 0` — content actually arriving\n— which is why it never had this. `VcBlade`''s comment claims the \"same\ntwo-state treatment\", but it substituted a loading-edge proxy for the\ncontent check. A blade cannot see content generically, so a painted\nframe is the closest honest proxy for \"the user saw something\".\n\n### Tests\n\nFirst tests for this latch at all — #330 shipped it stating \"No test\ncovers the overlay or the latch reset. Verified in the browser only\",\nwhich is why this reached a release candidate.\n\nThree cases: an overlay for a load that follows a completed one,\nskeletons kept when a second load starts before a paint, and the reset\nwhen the blade switches to a different entity. Reverting the frame\nconfirmation fails exactly the middle one.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4126 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier, stylelint and madge clean. Behaviour A/B''d in Chrome against\nthe running Vendor Portal, table above.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmr6yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIDgQAGUJWTAHw/+lM+lL7WSs723K\nb4D+DBfaB8XML4B8DfeTtO+e6gzlGm5gKTN5MpasT6u71RLRUKCXiqgpgTevNnan\n24FZRS00N4sb6xp+viAttwUJSwL+h39gOhz++7oo/h3TuYoZ5te3zp/mO4oavAQH\n7yxaNspV2zU++nSejCtsSGvu5qIkxL0NV3vrUyYRV0RemBW8TOpSoUfXucGFd2fm\nWInyF3BbPN9pc2s6UIfUOzl6BHN6p6PZ1Emi6Ld+RQ1F1JwJZXbMdrtfgqzX4F74\nozQ0AZPMXgkdg3VQgykilxOEG3jPlKcfFbCCFiOcJ6QPN28/UblUzkAimaeCfdHA\npqBy5AgfC7nTeL6sFkWHYoJcFLtP+QvceyXJHgggq2wxTMuUXb6VMKEOLVGjsz5L\n8P5wnD1kF+EGz+XylWeA9Tdq2C4d1/Iilu1AbKU03dT3E6Kwhc0jk42PsKYEQJKk\n1DLFW81Up8QeKdTxIKXR1HVIAO+gb7Q8ad+gdL0bN1axOcohLQCZTyJK2K6iA205\nlAVq+Gzz8G2ahtBq6DxTLYURScH9WY/eGd2ZTSW08tUyIn5F4wJmF4Fm3p1x0mwJ\nIJYnghZ9C8RDMmAnmSmCJyNToeen35EjIW8bmPOgx/qfrVHK4S6roRXqyuDTHJ4w\nQaCcOOWSzPUf7ZWDU4S9\n=NrUl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T12:50:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":1986444