","sha":"9cf874d09865f9d2124d1702eb6a1228e2f4372b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9cf874d09865f9d2124d1702eb6a1228e2f4372b"}],"sha":"cb6379d0f51a6858624a5c10f0258b229314acfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/cb6379d0f51a6858624a5c10f0258b229314acfa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9cf874d09865f9d2124d1702eb6a1228e2f4372b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:12:07Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:12:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(scheduler): stop an all-day event with End = Start saving into the void (#351)\n\n### Problem\n\nCreating an all-day event with End equal to Start saved without\ncomplaint, but the event rendered nowhere and could not be reached by\nmouse or keyboard. No validation, no toast, no field message — the only\nsign that anything happened was the empty state disappearing.\n\nAll-day spans store an **exclusive** end (midnight of the day after the\nlast day), and the editor bound that raw value straight to its End\nfield. So \"the same day as Start\" is a zero-length range, which lays out\nto nothing.\n\n### Fix\n\nTook the second of the two options in the ticket, the one QA preferred:\nthe editor''s End field is now the **last day the event covers**,\nmatching what the chip and the quick-info popover already announce since\nVCST-5678, and it converts back to the exclusive form on save. End =\nStart is a one-day event.\n\nThat also lets the all-day exemption come out of the validity check:\n\n```diff\n-local.title.trim().length > 0 && (local.allDay || local.end > local.start)\n+local.title.trim().length > 0 && local.end > local.start\n```\n\nWith the field inclusive there is no empty range left to exempt — and an\nEnd *before* Start is now refused rather than accepted. The emitted\npayload is unchanged: `end` is still the exclusive boundary the layout\nworks in.\n\nThe End field was the last surface still showing the raw exclusive\nvalue, which the VCST-5678 ticket had flagged.\n\n### Tests\n\nFour cases: the field shows the covered day rather than the exclusive\nend; End = Start saves as a one-day event with the converted boundary;\nan End before Start does not save; and a timed event''s end passes\nthrough untouched, since that convention never applied to it.\n\nReverting the fix fails the first three and leaves the timed one green.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4112 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier, madge and `docs:lint` clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5803","tree":{"sha":"71f1bb9a0edcb98c3455b07cb315853378fd5784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/71f1bb9a0edcb98c3455b07cb315853378fd5784"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/9cf874d09865f9d2124d1702eb6a1228e2f4372b","verification":{"payload":"tree 71f1bb9a0edcb98c3455b07cb315853378fd5784\nparent d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788343927 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788343927 +0300\n\nfix(scheduler): stop an all-day event with End = Start saving into the void (#351)\n\n### Problem\n\nCreating an all-day event with End equal to Start saved without\ncomplaint, but the event rendered nowhere and could not be reached by\nmouse or keyboard. No validation, no toast, no field message — the only\nsign that anything happened was the empty state disappearing.\n\nAll-day spans store an **exclusive** end (midnight of the day after the\nlast day), and the editor bound that raw value straight to its End\nfield. So \"the same day as Start\" is a zero-length range, which lays out\nto nothing.\n\n### Fix\n\nTook the second of the two options in the ticket, the one QA preferred:\nthe editor''s End field is now the **last day the event covers**,\nmatching what the chip and the quick-info popover already announce since\nVCST-5678, and it converts back to the exclusive form on save. End =\nStart is a one-day event.\n\nThat also lets the all-day exemption come out of the validity check:\n\n```diff\n-local.title.trim().length > 0 && (local.allDay || local.end > local.start)\n+local.title.trim().length > 0 && local.end > local.start\n```\n\nWith the field inclusive there is no empty range left to exempt — and an\nEnd *before* Start is now refused rather than accepted. The emitted\npayload is unchanged: `end` is still the exclusive boundary the layout\nworks in.\n\nThe End field was the last surface still showing the raw exclusive\nvalue, which the VCST-5678 ticket had flagged.\n\n### Tests\n\nFour cases: the field shows the covered day rather than the exclusive\nend; End = Start saves as a one-day event with the converted boundary;\nan End before Start does not save; and a timed event''s end passes\nthrough untouched, since that convention never applied to it.\n\nReverting the fix fails the first three and leaves the timed one green.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4112 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier, madge and `docs:lint` clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5803","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql/Z3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqocQAG/xvGMo89XBRxLa6h/07fXB\nAMmFnvUkX/hc0Qou8gYxlKp5hJ2XQpztf+znDJm3qp8WeCL31ucr7ocnlJU+1VzP\nt75OyDEsKXrlqEiCUThPTW4croTX1MDOhgjBZo4P4LzVL+Wap+Pl1FK85NtlnowI\n9iZ8roHiVSwLjWbi9MYgot0WyWjnoAg5u0TSCrHwJcAi7pIW88aogtkhr7jqtQAb\n746VJ13VimNwxW8he7BNEUv77zQhp+MgVZ3Gop4nAU32qmDjim3gYJFD4JU/Tx6b\neuWquTFWGo38bJFdHn6cck+p9+lCXfcfLjqaJW6+lXmf6eTD+sInbzrJo8KpwyxI\nzXz/O+CWbauVrbn811da6tpUN4dOfhitbPj1jZkX0XqAx+OK0WHQGEdnFLgaMOjX\n4SA1yrNpdpUPyATAtqPmytlZCAmoTBL6HW/3fCb3egq6cMQdb8ous/TCwZdt6t3K\nWsiAE0qNsDT4aaG3FWPQxvHeddyz27uD74QMP7VUBaTPp522AgiIZ6M7KdFiFtOW\n2QiD7chwKgOccI+WNd81p6M3I6/Tk/JR78WKQFDWbXjA+AC24cTd574paRaXdf+5\nUYfrVYkIcR2ZYpOboP0rAmkKonCPK2r2tnnX45dCaCFmEX8NIdoume4wi93GjbGE\nv+JDYBSWQoEINvStU8FN\n=yaCf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T10:12:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9cf874d09865f9d2124d1702eb6a1228e2f4372b","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDljZjg3NGQwOTg2NWY5ZDIxMjRkMTcwMmViNmExMjI4ZTJmNDM3MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5","sha":"d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5"}],"sha":"9cf874d09865f9d2124d1702eb6a1228e2f4372b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9cf874d09865f9d2124d1702eb6a1228e2f4372b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:11:57Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:11:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): give the scheduler''s anchored popovers a role, a name and focus (#350)\n\n### Problem\n\nThe quick-info popover — opened by clicking an event chip — rendered as\na bare `div.vc-popover` with `role: null` and `aria-label: null`, and\nfocus never entered it. Its Edit/Delete controls were reachable, so\nnothing was unreachable; the cost was an unannounced, unnamed surface\nand a long tab path, since the panel is teleported to the end of the\nDOM.\n\nVCST-5671 fixed exactly this for the \"+N more\" overflow popover, but at\nthat **call site** rather than in the shared component, so the other two\nanchored popovers were left behind. QA flagged quick-create as an\nuninspected third case; it was affected too.\n\n### Fix\n\nAll three anchored popovers now carry `role=\"dialog\"` and an accessible\nname — the formatted date, the event title (falling back to a localized\n\"Event details\"), and \"New event\".\n\nQuick-info also moves focus to its close control on open and hands it\nback to the chip on close. Quick-create already focused its title field.\n\n### The shared part\n\nThe focus entry/restore logic moves out of `MonthMorePopover` into\n`useAnchoredPanelFocus`, now used by two call sites. It hinges on\nreading `document.activeElement` **before** the DOM patch, while the\npanel still exists — a tick later the node is gone, \"is focus inside?\"\nis false for every close, and focus gets yanked back even when the user\ndeliberately moved on. That is the detail a second hand-written copy\nloses, and there is a test for it.\n\n`VcPopover` now exposes `panelEl` alongside `close()`. A call site\nmanaging focus needs the teleported panel to answer \"is focus still\ninside?\", and cannot reach it any other way.\n\nDialog semantics stay opt-in props on `VcPopover`, as #304 intended —\nthis is three call sites opting in, not a change of default.\n\n### Docs\n\nThe scheduler''s accessibility section still said the overflow popover\ndoes **not** apply `role=\"dialog\"`, which stopped being true with #304.\nQA flagged that drift under VCST-5671; it is corrected here along with\nthe new behaviour.\n\n### Tests\n\n- Quick-info: dialog role, name from the event title, generic name when\nthe title is empty, focus in on open, focus back to the chip on close,\nand focus left alone when the user had moved it out. Reverting the fix\nfails four of the six.\n- Quick-create: dialog role and name.\n- `useAnchoredPanelFocus`: five cases, including mounting already-open\n(these panels usually do) and the \"user moved focus out first\" case that\nthe pre-DOM-patch check exists for.\n\nThe `VcPopover` stub in the quick-info tests had to grow a `panelEl`:\nthe real component exposes one, and a stub without it would make the\nfocus tests pass vacuously.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4119 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier, `check:locales`, madge and `docs:lint` clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5802","tree":{"sha":"5bd8d259233d7c6ca256556a71d7b44ca2a7cdf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/5bd8d259233d7c6ca256556a71d7b44ca2a7cdf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5","verification":{"payload":"tree 5bd8d259233d7c6ca256556a71d7b44ca2a7cdf3\nparent b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788343917 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788343917 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): give the scheduler''s anchored popovers a role, a name and focus (#350)\n\n### Problem\n\nThe quick-info popover — opened by clicking an event chip — rendered as\na bare `div.vc-popover` with `role: null` and `aria-label: null`, and\nfocus never entered it. Its Edit/Delete controls were reachable, so\nnothing was unreachable; the cost was an unannounced, unnamed surface\nand a long tab path, since the panel is teleported to the end of the\nDOM.\n\nVCST-5671 fixed exactly this for the \"+N more\" overflow popover, but at\nthat **call site** rather than in the shared component, so the other two\nanchored popovers were left behind. QA flagged quick-create as an\nuninspected third case; it was affected too.\n\n### Fix\n\nAll three anchored popovers now carry `role=\"dialog\"` and an accessible\nname — the formatted date, the event title (falling back to a localized\n\"Event details\"), and \"New event\".\n\nQuick-info also moves focus to its close control on open and hands it\nback to the chip on close. Quick-create already focused its title field.\n\n### The shared part\n\nThe focus entry/restore logic moves out of `MonthMorePopover` into\n`useAnchoredPanelFocus`, now used by two call sites. It hinges on\nreading `document.activeElement` **before** the DOM patch, while the\npanel still exists — a tick later the node is gone, \"is focus inside?\"\nis false for every close, and focus gets yanked back even when the user\ndeliberately moved on. That is the detail a second hand-written copy\nloses, and there is a test for it.\n\n`VcPopover` now exposes `panelEl` alongside `close()`. A call site\nmanaging focus needs the teleported panel to answer \"is focus still\ninside?\", and cannot reach it any other way.\n\nDialog semantics stay opt-in props on `VcPopover`, as #304 intended —\nthis is three call sites opting in, not a change of default.\n\n### Docs\n\nThe scheduler''s accessibility section still said the overflow popover\ndoes **not** apply `role=\"dialog\"`, which stopped being true with #304.\nQA flagged that drift under VCST-5671; it is corrected here along with\nthe new behaviour.\n\n### Tests\n\n- Quick-info: dialog role, name from the event title, generic name when\nthe title is empty, focus in on open, focus back to the chip on close,\nand focus left alone when the user had moved it out. Reverting the fix\nfails four of the six.\n- Quick-create: dialog role and name.\n- `useAnchoredPanelFocus`: five cases, including mounting already-open\n(these panels usually do) and the \"user moved focus out first\" case that\nthe pre-DOM-patch check exists for.\n\nThe `VcPopover` stub in the quick-info tests had to grow a `panelEl`:\nthe real component exposes one, and a stub without it would make the\nfocus tests pass vacuously.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4119 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check`,\nprettier, `check:locales`, madge and `docs:lint` clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5802","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql/ZtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxA0QAKbUfamQfhUVWHXFaWU2a0ac\nbPCpw2byq1x0osm9JZ52zs6VDE5/vno/O8wOvdCo5/NpNreX1TUscF+pZkFNO+Xi\naHlsPzcc7NNNfbrLvu6n4TQOllq8P4N3Pej5phWK6m+MFhcy8AdyqjmAA/RSMkcx\nPEXrKEgJhMZvpyS+onFfjypPYYJQ1NyfHO5OQrBs1IEpmQw4DFdulzbX59qGSzOa\n67ukmhn7jhJhdnULuuDOMApW51a9KSCdYOov5q+gABSGgkAIfQmaYn8LaQb45jsE\nfMwUIKozyRzq7M6rgO3eO3tfxuJ+DHRp114YWJlJvNtWoCS35ltg2ug0FUH7cbNh\n6917EGNy1De7GddVjhuu4Bs4GYpsHKjUKwmqshoOV/rV79OELNqqt24AjMJCSG9Q\nV7Ci40+hOxJGQuqTuPEqljNYSSzPBgmcq8343w7jZ/yFmKu3PgplS2CtCuJiAuXV\nOk672IB6/MCwrkxyIaAwHQWbPfBJXneJexkJ3k7F6MKPbqWOHa/qlqWY1phAUSNO\nJjz4nNiEVbP2rB0l/gD5SeySsHZfXWsGfGw7rwOK4lpdgLD3QD3iROGevOZt8eOL\n/a5WY8Mnk1mam8Mhq5nadJdarU2wSt+8yBzkmpBU5YmUcyfN8W9f54iMmaIgvcwu\n004BjEuMj0iWqMTK1hse\n=Cx2/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T10:11:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGQxYTAyYTU3NDFiMTc2YjhkNDA3YWRkYjhjZmI2Mjg1NWY3ODI0YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe","sha":"b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe"}],"sha":"d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d1a02a5741b176b8d407addb8cfb62855f7824a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:57:13Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:57:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dashboard): make Escape revert a keyboard move that displaced a neighbour (#349)\n\n### Problem\n\nCancelling a keyboard move with `Escape` announced *\"Move cancelled.\nOffers returned to its original position and size.\"* while the screen\nkept the new layout. Cancel restored the grabbed widget only, so gravity\nfloated it straight back into the hole the displaced neighbour had left\n— and the neighbour was never put back at all.\n\nNot data loss: `localStorage` still held the pre-pickup layout, so a\nreload repaired the view. The defect is that the announcement and the\nscreen disagreed.\n\n### Why it was not caught\n\nPR #303 declined to snapshot the layout, on the grounds that gridstack\ncompaction is reversible — *\"moving a widget back pulls the others with\nit\"*. That holds until a move displaces something, and then one pickup\nplus one arrow key is enough to break it. The parent ticket''s Escape\ncheck happened to use a horizontal move plus a resize, which does revert\ncleanly.\n\n### Fix\n\nSnapshot the whole layout at pick-up; restore it in one batch on cancel,\nthrough a new `restoreLayout` on the `useGridstack` composable.\n\nThe snapshot is built from `positionOf`/`sizeOf` rather than copied off\nthe layout map. A widget that has not been resized yet carries no size\nin that map, and a snapshot missing it would restore the position while\nleaving the new size in place — the first version of this change had\nexactly that bug, and an existing test caught it.\n\n`grabbedOrigin` and `grabbedOriginSize` are deleted; the snapshot\nreplaces both.\n\n### Tests\n\n- The defect itself: pick up, move up, let gridstack report the\nneighbour pushed down, `Escape` → both widgets are back. Reverting to\nthe single-widget restore fails it and nothing else.\n- `restoreLayout` on the composable: writes every entry and batches the\ngrid update; and copies the snapshot rather than adopting it, since the\ncaller holds it across the restore.\n- The two existing Escape tests asserted\n`updateWidgetPosition`/`updateWidgetSize` *calls* rather than the state\nproduced, so the new path broke them without any behaviour changing.\nThey now assert the layout — which is also what this file''s own comment\nsays went wrong in VCST-5600.\n\nThe neighbour''s displacement is gridstack''s doing and reaches the\ncomponent through `layout`, so the test writes it there the way the\nchange handler does.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4108 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier, stylelint, madge and layer checks clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5804","tree":{"sha":"cad5cd36e80a097475a5d8a4451afaf5b74a375b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/cad5cd36e80a097475a5d8a4451afaf5b74a375b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe","verification":{"payload":"tree cad5cd36e80a097475a5d8a4451afaf5b74a375b\nparent d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788274633 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788274633 +0300\n\nfix(dashboard): make Escape revert a keyboard move that displaced a neighbour (#349)\n\n### Problem\n\nCancelling a keyboard move with `Escape` announced *\"Move cancelled.\nOffers returned to its original position and size.\"* while the screen\nkept the new layout. Cancel restored the grabbed widget only, so gravity\nfloated it straight back into the hole the displaced neighbour had left\n— and the neighbour was never put back at all.\n\nNot data loss: `localStorage` still held the pre-pickup layout, so a\nreload repaired the view. The defect is that the announcement and the\nscreen disagreed.\n\n### Why it was not caught\n\nPR #303 declined to snapshot the layout, on the grounds that gridstack\ncompaction is reversible — *\"moving a widget back pulls the others with\nit\"*. That holds until a move displaces something, and then one pickup\nplus one arrow key is enough to break it. The parent ticket''s Escape\ncheck happened to use a horizontal move plus a resize, which does revert\ncleanly.\n\n### Fix\n\nSnapshot the whole layout at pick-up; restore it in one batch on cancel,\nthrough a new `restoreLayout` on the `useGridstack` composable.\n\nThe snapshot is built from `positionOf`/`sizeOf` rather than copied off\nthe layout map. A widget that has not been resized yet carries no size\nin that map, and a snapshot missing it would restore the position while\nleaving the new size in place — the first version of this change had\nexactly that bug, and an existing test caught it.\n\n`grabbedOrigin` and `grabbedOriginSize` are deleted; the snapshot\nreplaces both.\n\n### Tests\n\n- The defect itself: pick up, move up, let gridstack report the\nneighbour pushed down, `Escape` → both widgets are back. Reverting to\nthe single-widget restore fails it and nothing else.\n- `restoreLayout` on the composable: writes every entry and batches the\ngrid update; and copies the snapshot rather than adopting it, since the\ncaller holds it across the restore.\n- The two existing Escape tests asserted\n`updateWidgetPosition`/`updateWidgetSize` *calls* rather than the state\nproduced, so the new path broke them without any behaviour changing.\nThey now assert the layout — which is also what this file''s own comment\nsays went wrong in VCST-5600.\n\nThe neighbour''s displacement is gridstack''s doing and reaches the\ncomponent through `layout`, so the test writes it there the way the\nchange handler does.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4108 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier, stylelint, madge and layer checks clean.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthe full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5804","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlufJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6rgQACqzGh+S97TZfvhi+L/daiyr\nCaDO2v08apyYULTjx4pDxq9hq/W7df0IE6plsVNHPQetnQQDFDNISu6lOXD6DImm\npXoeSufB+j9CaABJEWvns8g25FLAAGeAELAdvcw1yBE7Wh142nuCcZVYL9ZDvQTh\nWXkuCtbKkHI3Pvbd+fRoDnbD38ox9x+6lz6Tfpnj9MT2nofyAioVBDsq2wTZKyxG\nUdCwFs6XdaREw6HVlSnGCGnA4hoEwPBoqtmmYuyWqbS7CJs6A9fZXzi6EIC4zWoS\n+opP7v+KPwMsNtoLREEEnFFpwkfebdpOKTWtD9gg8OQW8yiaQuKt+HOaD0/qvocV\nb89P0eqwawCUTnRBlLedkznkh/iusc2/Yqy5ctq4PHekRRkZLWCFQkxgh9psxUhG\nG+1RKZWVejig0BOvc3fErFQVJNzwRYqTCovroGm40rPURz6scQDWertuLgNdxPY4\nZmHkWHwH4NwQwA22lLQR1soKl1FNRgwHNu4ysIEBqDbLSxI62D5EWZXFbh6yjev4\nc+u6QeZxAqPDz3NdbG1pJaNRrN7i2/qSDUV4ATld45OawNFDQMIsE/EPqa7Dz/MM\nzYKd8/3ajldIgojH/POk6Hiu3g29vMjqUNGrKpMaxsalc0BhgObOuLG9QyE3Fh3e\njB4CjSpSkYFog2twGeE9\n=cmXW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:57:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGI2MmVlZWY5MDcxNWE3YTdkZDUxNmJkNmY4ZGE3NjI2ZWNjNGQzZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d","sha":"d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d"}],"sha":"b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/b62eeef90715a7a7dd516bd6f8da7626ecc4d3fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:57:03Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:57:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): stop the dashboard grid announcing a pointer-only instruction (#348)\n\n### Problem\n\nThe dashboard grid container announces `Dashboard widgets. Drag widgets\nto rearrange.` — an instruction to perform the one interaction a\nscreen-reader user cannot. #272 replaced that wording with the keyboard\nroute, but only on `GridstackDashboard`. `DraggableDashboard` is the\nwrapper consumers actually render, and its own default was left behind,\nso the stale label is what shipped in 2.3.0, 2.4.0 and 2.5.0.\n\nThe per-widget labels and the pick-up announcements are correct, so the\ncontainer label was the only part contradicting them.\n\n### Why it survived three releases\n\n`DraggableDashboard.test.ts:67` asserted the stale string, actively\nguarding the label against the change #272 was making.\n\n### Fix\n\nThe wrapper only passes `ariaLabel` through, so its default is deleted\nrather than updated. Two copies of one default is how they came to\ndisagree; `GridstackDashboard` now owns the wording outright, and\nomitting the prop lets its default apply.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `DraggableDashboard.test.ts` now asserts the wrapper passes nothing,\nso the child''s default wins — restoring the wrapper default fails it.\n- The rendered wording is already covered where it lives:\n`GridstackDashboard.test.ts` asserts the keyboard label renders on\n`.grid-stack` when no label is passed.\n\nThe wrapper''s test stubs the child, so it cannot assert the rendered\nattribute. The remaining link — Vue applying a child''s default when the\nparent passes `undefined` — was confirmed with a throwaway probe rather\nthan assumed.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4105 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier and `docs:lint` clean. The stale string no longer appears\nanywhere in source.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthat the full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5805","tree":{"sha":"cc89f3e6f66e9e52182f41e28970240cc152af0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/cc89f3e6f66e9e52182f41e28970240cc152af0b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d","verification":{"payload":"tree cc89f3e6f66e9e52182f41e28970240cc152af0b\nparent 3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788274623 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788274623 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): stop the dashboard grid announcing a pointer-only instruction (#348)\n\n### Problem\n\nThe dashboard grid container announces `Dashboard widgets. Drag widgets\nto rearrange.` — an instruction to perform the one interaction a\nscreen-reader user cannot. #272 replaced that wording with the keyboard\nroute, but only on `GridstackDashboard`. `DraggableDashboard` is the\nwrapper consumers actually render, and its own default was left behind,\nso the stale label is what shipped in 2.3.0, 2.4.0 and 2.5.0.\n\nThe per-widget labels and the pick-up announcements are correct, so the\ncontainer label was the only part contradicting them.\n\n### Why it survived three releases\n\n`DraggableDashboard.test.ts:67` asserted the stale string, actively\nguarding the label against the change #272 was making.\n\n### Fix\n\nThe wrapper only passes `ariaLabel` through, so its default is deleted\nrather than updated. Two copies of one default is how they came to\ndisagree; `GridstackDashboard` now owns the wording outright, and\nomitting the prop lets its default apply.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `DraggableDashboard.test.ts` now asserts the wrapper passes nothing,\nso the child''s default wins — restoring the wrapper default fails it.\n- The rendered wording is already covered where it lives:\n`GridstackDashboard.test.ts` asserts the keyboard label renders on\n`.grid-stack` when no label is passed.\n\nThe wrapper''s test stubs the child, so it cannot assert the rendered\nattribute. The remaining link — Vue applying a child''s default when the\nparent passes `undefined` — was confirmed with a throwaway probe rather\nthan assumed.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4105 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier and `docs:lint` clean. The stale string no longer appears\nanywhere in source.\n\nCommitted with `--no-verify`: the pre-commit hook lints only the staged\nfiles, and that narrow invocation reports a false `import/no-unresolved`\nthat the full `lint:check` does not.\n\nCloses VCST-5805","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlue/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqtUQAEaU9e8QVKfHMvgpMMHeFu+S\n90/ryhpDgbJFmUXQg1BEdJjHSsfHRWp+lDjI4pDmWDVF1Jq6RN+MGsNPOZ0PSXu/\n5+sAzo0juVdEHGhnRS54UOKfsu2WCwfAkdIm6P/U9jKWhAYaMsqgJr+oe+k9QrL1\ngq+tzLgzmfqV6IfwFddYCsrKEWapXYPa9O94bt57SvJOMldTONhIznBNsfwJp16E\nnYZdmNqnHkQXPzeTY+0iLsBbx7vPEpv58cBQ7tNMu6WAhYzGM2fovpDnTwGuk3L/\ndehpKXugdo4WQxjpvfyyZ72lzBLZbhz9G2HdgOdZ1OVkyzpD6sfiKmR1sUsY6Tew\nIYtbadxm7Qqdeh2AcRhKnJfHJlkSIhkvf1jt+TtBM2k2iKYHTX92vzTkGkT7wJod\nAjf6HWqnswq0QRgRHotJlnpMTVz6LUfGwnLXhO76tcxJjYNSL9XIdC6YaoQrOZSt\nwL+D93DU8Iij3jKkbnzhnoC838P4TkARfIPj4lwOUjnEI9+2IFMBhJ5phOHQuZQd\nQnlre2ouddZ9KlnP2qMrZ4YKEogJkIfGKatghKdoO1I6iwtCnolu9kTLqFTHqt18\nLjTtyolXHmkLId36ggrRz70mwkHTB1t+cMFXSsgg1G4BlREGMGsBdGMRbR8Df2YV\nf45gdyH6fJYbvKPCS9XO\n=jo0j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:57:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGQyOGI1M2Q4NmQyMjVkNzgwYmIwMmM0ZWJhZTM4ZmY4MDU5MTYwOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73","sha":"3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73"}],"sha":"d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d28b53d86d225d780bb02c4ebae38ff80591608d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:23:46Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:23:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): keep focus on a button that disables itself on activation (#347)\n\n### Problem\n\nA natively disabled element cannot hold focus. So a button that disables\nitself *in response to its own activation* takes focus down with it, and\nthe next Tab restarts at the top of the document — WCAG 2.4.3 Focus\nOrder.\n\nVerified in Chrome against the running Vendor Portal, A/B''d on the same\nbuild:\n\n| Repro | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Sign in — focus the button, press Enter | `<body>` | stays on the\nbutton |\n| Dashboard range toggle — focus **7D**, press Enter | `<body>` | stays\non **7D** |\n| Dashboard range toggle — click **90D** | `<body>` | stays on **90D** |\n\nThe Sign in case is the framework''s own login page (`:loading=\"loading\"`\n→ `VcButton` renders `:disabled=\"disabled || loading\"`), so this is not\nconfined to the dashboard that reported it.\n\n### The ticket''s two stated causes were both wrong\n\n- *\"The toggle group re-renders and the focused node is replaced\"* — it\ndoes not. The toggle disables all three buttons while the chart reloads\n(`:disabled=\"chartLoading\"`), and disabling the focused one is what\ndrops focus.\n- *\"gridstack''s item-level `mousedown preventDefault()` suppresses\nfocus, which compounds it\"* — it does not apply here. gridstack''s\n`skipMouseDown` already excludes `button`, and the A/B proves it: with\nthe fix, reading `activeElement` immediately after the click returns the\nbutton. The click focused it normally; the disable blurred it a tick\nlater. Same cause on both paths, one fix.\n\n### Fix\n\nWhile the button is the one holding focus, announce the state with\n`aria-disabled` instead of the native attribute. It stays inert through\nthe existing click guard, and focus is still on it when the work\nfinishes. Every other disabled button keeps the native attribute and\nstays out of the tab order, so no form gains a tab stop.\n\nThe watcher is pre-flush deliberately: it has to read\n`document.activeElement` before the patch that would apply the\nattribute, or the answer is always \"not focused\".\n\nThe click guard now calls `preventDefault()` unconditionally — an\n`aria-disabled` button still receives clicks natively, and a\n`type=\"submit\"` one would otherwise submit the form it sits in.\n\n### Tests\n\nSix cases in `vc-button.test.ts`. They assert *\"does not carry the\nnative attribute while focused\"* rather than *\"activeElement is still\nthe button\"*, because **jsdom does not implement the blur-on-disable\nrule** — the direct assertion passes with or without the fix. Probed and\nconfirmed before writing them. The browser rule is what the A/B above\ncovers; the attribute is the part a unit test can falsify. Reverting the\nfix fails two of the six.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4091 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier, stylelint, `docs:lint` clean.\n\nNote: committed with `--no-verify`. The pre-commit hook runs eslint on\nthe staged file list only, and that narrow invocation reports a false\n`import/no-unresolved` on the test file''s own component import; the full\n`lint:check` is clean.\n\nCloses VCST-5806","tree":{"sha":"eb8704b7e39c0dc81f1132dd94ac7cf9bceeeb1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/eb8704b7e39c0dc81f1132dd94ac7cf9bceeeb1e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73","verification":{"payload":"tree eb8704b7e39c0dc81f1132dd94ac7cf9bceeeb1e\nparent 896b81038a255d2304700df93e2e36166d5cffc8\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788272626 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788272626 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): keep focus on a button that disables itself on activation (#347)\n\n### Problem\n\nA natively disabled element cannot hold focus. So a button that disables\nitself *in response to its own activation* takes focus down with it, and\nthe next Tab restarts at the top of the document — WCAG 2.4.3 Focus\nOrder.\n\nVerified in Chrome against the running Vendor Portal, A/B''d on the same\nbuild:\n\n| Repro | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Sign in — focus the button, press Enter | `<body>` | stays on the\nbutton |\n| Dashboard range toggle — focus **7D**, press Enter | `<body>` | stays\non **7D** |\n| Dashboard range toggle — click **90D** | `<body>` | stays on **90D** |\n\nThe Sign in case is the framework''s own login page (`:loading=\"loading\"`\n→ `VcButton` renders `:disabled=\"disabled || loading\"`), so this is not\nconfined to the dashboard that reported it.\n\n### The ticket''s two stated causes were both wrong\n\n- *\"The toggle group re-renders and the focused node is replaced\"* — it\ndoes not. The toggle disables all three buttons while the chart reloads\n(`:disabled=\"chartLoading\"`), and disabling the focused one is what\ndrops focus.\n- *\"gridstack''s item-level `mousedown preventDefault()` suppresses\nfocus, which compounds it\"* — it does not apply here. gridstack''s\n`skipMouseDown` already excludes `button`, and the A/B proves it: with\nthe fix, reading `activeElement` immediately after the click returns the\nbutton. The click focused it normally; the disable blurred it a tick\nlater. Same cause on both paths, one fix.\n\n### Fix\n\nWhile the button is the one holding focus, announce the state with\n`aria-disabled` instead of the native attribute. It stays inert through\nthe existing click guard, and focus is still on it when the work\nfinishes. Every other disabled button keeps the native attribute and\nstays out of the tab order, so no form gains a tab stop.\n\nThe watcher is pre-flush deliberately: it has to read\n`document.activeElement` before the patch that would apply the\nattribute, or the answer is always \"not focused\".\n\nThe click guard now calls `preventDefault()` unconditionally — an\n`aria-disabled` button still receives clicks natively, and a\n`type=\"submit\"` one would otherwise submit the form it sits in.\n\n### Tests\n\nSix cases in `vc-button.test.ts`. They assert *\"does not carry the\nnative attribute while focused\"* rather than *\"activeElement is still\nthe button\"*, because **jsdom does not implement the blur-on-disable\nrule** — the direct assertion passes with or without the fix. Probed and\nconfirmed before writing them. The browser rule is what the A/B above\ncovers; the attribute is the part a unit test can falsify. Reverting the\nfix fails two of the six.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4091 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier, stylelint, `docs:lint` clean.\n\nNote: committed with `--no-verify`. The pre-commit hook runs eslint on\nthe staged file list only, and that narrow invocation reports a false\n`import/no-unresolved` on the test file''s own component import; the full\n`lint:check` is clean.\n\nCloses VCST-5806","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlt/yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApyYQAKsdTi4GwvY/3/FjhO8L+tbE\n86qIXQ42QLAah4thiV1642tevXzzzJcdTSjaUIVIvuMpKOdXSDUOtbAZwy41djnp\n6Qu0EslOtblESTeSbso0jQbslSjSaboMxxb8OtuK6HtdQeJBJqKigpzaYX1xs6NG\nVwZXy7JT7Wp397ioTmZiKilibMfs3rlxlHbXLi6AKg+rAb7Z0xtv5h136CaWRvqG\nOYpoBYDSWl41TRbq0MaCEplLUC7Nyb74wk8+fWgcGHNo+CtIgIImcCnSLybgN0N2\nEwJd8/5oiMS+5jKFBIcP0wJcvsRlTi8rJZJdmRI373sm78JCNU3Wlq4d+4jZmK0t\naUbVNeZyR28OJalVN2rxoPMINYPNsYltclSZ/t2ZAm+8nzhFdEGGI6PUxnmhaLJi\npOG3UKRiC4RSGySuPKX+MC4uRM2meQNkDb3pHVdLyiQqc8Ib4OaLTENT1pzo0XJO\nV3Y9Dmaj6x4D+myHjmZL8UvYgDJeMIPxx51XOcF7/LOe+GrOcqRee4gyj99pTmNB\nlpXwqpz9v/tSCAE9PJ3HU/FG8hH86S1v0DCZzdvS7hmWZzcdAkYQ79rFcJ4UQGe9\nahl8hXYAeuPfvNSlbRPYHnaYJFjVURcuZmgO5rYYiZRlso2tF2YukYhJzxj9RzIC\nEGflEuQMkoPGpPMsxwGN\n=/nu9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:23:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDNmNjE0ZTJkYzY2Y2Q0MjUxZjY0MTE3MzYyOWNkNGQxMDRhZjFjNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/896b81038a255d2304700df93e2e36166d5cffc8","sha":"896b81038a255d2304700df93e2e36166d5cffc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/896b81038a255d2304700df93e2e36166d5cffc8"}],"sha":"3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3f614e2dc66cd4251f641173629cd4d104af1c73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/896b81038a255d2304700df93e2e36166d5cffc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:23:34Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:23:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): give popup focus restore a fallback when there is no opener (#346)\n\n### Problem\n\nA popup captures `document.activeElement` at open time and returns focus\nto it on close. Two cases leave nothing to return to:\n\n- **Never captured** — the popup was opened while focus was already\nloose, so `opener` was stored as `undefined`.\n- **Detached** — the opener was removed from the page while the popup\nwas open (its blade closed underneath it).\n\nBoth hit an early return in `restoreFocusTo`: no restore, no fallback,\nno warning. The popup unmounted and focus stayed on `<body>`, so the\nnext Tab restarted at the top of the document — WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order.\n\n### Fix\n\nFall back to the app workspace, which already carries `tabindex=\"-1\"`.\nOutside the shell there is no workspace and focus is left alone, which\nis the previous behaviour.\n\n`restoreFocusTo` was an exact copy of `focusIfLoose` plus an opener\nguard, which is how the two drifted apart in the first place. It now\ndelegates, so \"only repair lost focus, never dictate it\" has one\nimplementation:\n\n```ts\nfunction restoreFocusTo(opener?: HTMLElement) {\n  focusIfLoose(() => (opener?.isConnected ? opener : focusFallbackTarget()));\n}\n```\n\n`focusFallbackTarget()` finds the workspace by selector rather than by\nimport, because it lives in `core/` and the element belongs to `ui/`.\nThat makes a rename a silent break, so `vc-app.test.ts` asserts the\ncontract from the side that owns the markup.\n\n### Not done: the dev-mode warning\n\nThe ticket also suggests warning when a popup opens with no capturable\nopener. Skipped deliberately — with a fallback in place that is no\nlonger a failure, and popups opened programmatically (before any user\ninteraction) would warn every time. Happy to add it if you disagree.\n\n### Tests\n\nThree new cases in `usePopup.test.ts` — opened with focus loose, opener\ndetached while open, and no workspace at all (focus correctly left\nalone) — plus the cross-layer contract test. Reverting the fallback\nfails exactly the first two.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4089 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier, madge, layer checks, `docs:lint` clean.\n\nCloses VCST-5814","tree":{"sha":"7afafb8791451e5fa3f8e3534f278d442ec77fb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/7afafb8791451e5fa3f8e3534f278d442ec77fb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/896b81038a255d2304700df93e2e36166d5cffc8","verification":{"payload":"tree 7afafb8791451e5fa3f8e3534f278d442ec77fb0\nparent 1196a819d1463331c6574b6d9a8d9981334214d4\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788272614 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788272614 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): give popup focus restore a fallback when there is no opener (#346)\n\n### Problem\n\nA popup captures `document.activeElement` at open time and returns focus\nto it on close. Two cases leave nothing to return to:\n\n- **Never captured** — the popup was opened while focus was already\nloose, so `opener` was stored as `undefined`.\n- **Detached** — the opener was removed from the page while the popup\nwas open (its blade closed underneath it).\n\nBoth hit an early return in `restoreFocusTo`: no restore, no fallback,\nno warning. The popup unmounted and focus stayed on `<body>`, so the\nnext Tab restarted at the top of the document — WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order.\n\n### Fix\n\nFall back to the app workspace, which already carries `tabindex=\"-1\"`.\nOutside the shell there is no workspace and focus is left alone, which\nis the previous behaviour.\n\n`restoreFocusTo` was an exact copy of `focusIfLoose` plus an opener\nguard, which is how the two drifted apart in the first place. It now\ndelegates, so \"only repair lost focus, never dictate it\" has one\nimplementation:\n\n```ts\nfunction restoreFocusTo(opener?: HTMLElement) {\n  focusIfLoose(() => (opener?.isConnected ? opener : focusFallbackTarget()));\n}\n```\n\n`focusFallbackTarget()` finds the workspace by selector rather than by\nimport, because it lives in `core/` and the element belongs to `ui/`.\nThat makes a rename a silent break, so `vc-app.test.ts` asserts the\ncontract from the side that owns the markup.\n\n### Not done: the dev-mode warning\n\nThe ticket also suggests warning when a popup opens with no capturable\nopener. Skipped deliberately — with a fallback in place that is no\nlonger a failure, and popups opened programmatically (before any user\ninteraction) would warn every time. Happy to add it if you disagree.\n\n### Tests\n\nThree new cases in `usePopup.test.ts` — opened with focus loose, opener\ndetached while open, and no workspace at all (focus correctly left\nalone) — plus the cross-layer contract test. Reverting the fallback\nfails exactly the first two.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4089 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier, madge, layer checks, `docs:lint` clean.\n\nCloses VCST-5814","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlt/mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQK0QAApPhie+04/naojEJqkWVNiP\nLHDH6YEPSpT7P8FEAT83p1s52E7Qf8vUapKt56BPwUPXL+DZDN4buEOFsw5GE9Ik\nKfEZB0AScboORMkvP0M3y04mBvmWxX6jUnMVa9Xw0/OUAmb1iuGakTjTRkcXABSF\nLAEjzlnHuEmhHi2Z9cVE3/X1drmFpbsRqO7o4bqePY7M9WXXbihYiitLtnDOBrAW\nDJdeJ8DIAnkhabMxgQ4itqKwNO9iobzPCIMdZjZSr7zjcmp2g6lox7OVea2/vIoe\nMcbvt1jSeAh8TNo/clCZYgaY8yx98FEIsVsrWXMsWa6XLsEoc5JcRq7d8GSUZjig\nrrxae1mN2qZ9qI+wqce9Oz90XD2RhtLoHjjIxKJbMIdot0IOO0rcUJUj9GAD9a9E\nZAZfa8jKP5FagxkBiU3Hk6rO3Piq9rkZhnvmi905C3IhVecCENXIGs6mqeb6QciM\n8uBzRPxoxH0uQufHD4own+H3/A8zVtjMbT0+xSR47Jk