url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/1196a819d1463331c6574b6d9a8d9981334214d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:22:59Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:22:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): hide teleported popovers behind a maximized blade (#345)\n\n### Problem\n\nThe app hub and the notification panel both teleport out of the `<nav>`\nthat carries the covering state, so they land as siblings of it rather\nthan descendants — and `inert` does not cross a `Teleport`. Maximizing a\nblade left both panels in the tab order and in the accessibility tree,\nreachable behind content that was supposed to be covering them.\n\n`VcSidebar` and `VcAiAgentPanel` already got this treatment in #306;\nthese two were missed because their teleport hides the relationship.\n\n### Fix\n\n- `VcPopover` gets an `inert` prop rendered on its teleported root. It\nhas to be a prop: a fallthrough attribute never reaches the real root\nthrough the `Teleport`.\n- `AppHubPopover` forwards it to the `VcPopover` it wraps.\n- `DesktopLayout` passes the covering state to both panels explicitly.\n\n`MobileLayout` renders neither panel, so it needs nothing.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `vc-popover.test.ts` — the panel carries `inert` when covered; the\nattribute is absent otherwise (`inert=\"false\"` is still inert in HTML,\nso absence is the assertion).\n- `DesktopLayout.test.ts` — the layout tells both panels they are\ncovered. This is the assertion that matches the defect: the panels were\nfine, the layout never told them.\n\nRemoving either binding fails exactly these tests.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4090 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier, stylelint, madge, layer checks, `docs:lint` clean.\n\nCloses VCST-5815","tree":{"sha":"8d05c8c5fc5b7e0e3901877f1160d226aac3556a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/8d05c8c5fc5b7e0e3901877f1160d226aac3556a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/1196a819d1463331c6574b6d9a8d9981334214d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d05c8c5fc5b7e0e3901877f1160d226aac3556a\nparent 83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788272579 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788272579 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): hide teleported popovers behind a maximized blade (#345)\n\n### Problem\n\nThe app hub and the notification panel both teleport out of the `<nav>`\nthat carries the covering state, so they land as siblings of it rather\nthan descendants — and `inert` does not cross a `Teleport`. Maximizing a\nblade left both panels in the tab order and in the accessibility tree,\nreachable behind content that was supposed to be covering them.\n\n`VcSidebar` and `VcAiAgentPanel` already got this treatment in #306;\nthese two were missed because their teleport hides the relationship.\n\n### Fix\n\n- `VcPopover` gets an `inert` prop rendered on its teleported root. It\nhas to be a prop: a fallthrough attribute never reaches the real root\nthrough the `Teleport`.\n- `AppHubPopover` forwards it to the `VcPopover` it wraps.\n- `DesktopLayout` passes the covering state to both panels explicitly.\n\n`MobileLayout` renders neither panel, so it needs nothing.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `vc-popover.test.ts` — the panel carries `inert` when covered; the\nattribute is absent otherwise (`inert=\"false\"` is still inert in HTML,\nso absence is the assertion).\n- `DesktopLayout.test.ts` — the layout tells both panels they are\ncovered. This is the assertion that matches the defect: the panels were\nfine, the layout never told them.\n\nRemoving either binding fails exactly these tests.\n\n### Verification\n\n`vue-tsc` clean · `vitest run` 4090 passed, exit 0 · `lint:check` clean\n· prettier, stylelint, madge, layer checks, `docs:lint` clean.\n\nCloses VCST-5815","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlt/DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATbUQAGCTcV9PZCOdHuV4SMUa32KS\n1RmXV8yDDXcm53cvwYF6T5YMK4W9CqGoVvkwtO0JO/WETskWPxDZ8NGsaeQiwH2s\nYmUEYgRflYBSFF1J02+1f8cWaMFxEBbWQyYaWHXtshFb2fHlQ6aVxCKIw9DfyPQQ\nR3eGPDfXm84XAaI3C8F5G4mRWZVTu/PhDwLUVzBucFd/hFhWJ5kh+ouatLQa99wO\n6FxmtzApxlOzeS3/2loYGte6qOgLT4qHh3XnQd6fLW0NjC3iiLZbpOYJssnkrLbc\nxCozdkWPrkotCwv1IMeglXVpfqvyqYxee1G5nV6QaXka+DaU/Fx0YzIgGZM0MY8l\n7+qDLVE9MuE72uHq2OZtt6bBm2bK75oYQQTG0jzxWarfutg5fvkrHvrFm6Df0FvI\n/tiXH97p3+MyFz5ZlxRe+ld6ukNGLnzcuQV7DMUYxM23a6ueGdZAP3Knx1Xyrrbx\nXEqKT8+nJsraJhKyG4NlN2PcTqoMuSuY27h7JEMiXYQhUGcpbPRRQyNnaUSSBkX5\n5a1ByRFZFnhIca3Dj0Km1px7m9M6MPx6jGNBB1J38m006B2bDc5ynu1BalHYeOm1\nKPRDwU6RMCEGPmvPub4RoCwiNh7HXKZT+BumF85BCn0Ng1DjXuAylTEHzm7BCEtI\nwCsCyAe8vO/7YuGmVsrT\n=V8o1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:23:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/1196a819d1463331c6574b6d9a8d9981334214d4","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDExOTZhODE5ZDE0NjMzMzFjNjU3NGI2ZDlhOGQ5OTgxMzM0MjE0ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7","sha":"83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7"}],"sha":"1196a819d1463331c6574b6d9a8d9981334214d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/1196a819d1463331c6574b6d9a8d9981334214d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:22:41Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:22:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(blade-header): hand off expand focus on the state change, not the click (VCST-5812) (#344)\n\nFixes VCST-5812, the one condition that reopened VCST-5670.\n\n## What QA found\n\nNine conditions, eight passed. The failure: `Ctrl + \\` with focus on the\nexpand control lands on `<body>`, reproducibly, in both directions —\nwhile the same action via the header button correctly hands focus to the\nreplacement control.\n\nTheir diagnosis was right, and confirmed here against the source:\n`keepFocusOnExpandControl()` is reachable only from\n`onExpand`/`onCollapse` in `BladeHeader.vue`. The shortcut is dispatched\nin `shortcut-dispatch.ts:133` and calls `deps.toggleMaximized(bladeId)`\non the blade stack — it never reaches the header at all.\n\n## Change\n\nThe mistake was hooking the handoff to a *handler*. It is the **swap**\nthat loses the focused node, not the click, so the handoff now watches\nthe state that drives the swap:\n\n```ts\nwatch(() => renderingState?.value?.maximized, () => keepFocusOnExpandControl());\n```\n\nBoth entry points are covered by one mechanism, and a third would be\ntoo. `onExpand`/`onCollapse` go back to just emitting.\n\nTwo details that are load-bearing and easy to lose:\n\n- **Default `pre` flush.** The guard inside `keepFocusOnExpandControl`\nasks whether focus is still inside the header controls, which is only\ntrue while the control the user activated is still mounted. A `post`\nflush would run after the swap, find focus already on `<body>`, and\ndecline.\n- The existing `requestAnimationFrame` still does the actual focusing,\nafter the patch. That part is unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\nTwo, driving the state from outside the component exactly as the\nshortcut does — a mutable `maximized` ref flipped without touching the\nheader:\n\n- focus moves to the replacement control\n- focus is left alone when it sits outside the header, so a mouse user\nwho clicked elsewhere is not interrupted\n\nRestoring the handler-driven form fails the first one. That is the\ndiscriminating check: the old code passes every test that drives the\nheader''s own button, which is why this survived the previous round.\n\n## Verification\n\n414 files, 4087 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`, the full-glob\n`lint:check --max-warnings=0` and prettier clean.\n\nNot measured in a live browser here: reproducing it needs the chord\npressed with focus on the control, and QA has a documented recipe and\nscreenshots on VCST-5670. Worth re-running theirs against a build with\nthis change.\n\n## Notes for the parent ticket\n\nTwo observations in the QA report worth keeping, neither addressed here:\n\n- **Save passes by accident.** That path is untouched by #286; saving\n*remounts* the blade, so `vc-blade.vue`''s `onMounted(focusIfLoose)`\ncatches the loose focus. It would regress silently if the blade ever\nstopped remounting on save.\n- **The failure''s severity is genuinely Low.** Chrome keeps the\nsequential-focus starting point at the removed node, so Tab still\nreaches the replacement. That is engine-specific and does nothing for a\nscreen reader, so it remains a real 2.4.3 failure.","tree":{"sha":"4aacbf790faec890bb1a7167808eedf5a08920de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/4aacbf790faec890bb1a7167808eedf5a08920de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7","verification":{"payload":"tree 4aacbf790faec890bb1a7167808eedf5a08920de\nparent 87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788272561 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788272561 +0300\n\nfix(blade-header): hand off expand focus on the state change, not the click (VCST-5812) (#344)\n\nFixes VCST-5812, the one condition that reopened VCST-5670.\n\n## What QA found\n\nNine conditions, eight passed. The failure: `Ctrl + \\` with focus on the\nexpand control lands on `<body>`, reproducibly, in both directions —\nwhile the same action via the header button correctly hands focus to the\nreplacement control.\n\nTheir diagnosis was right, and confirmed here against the source:\n`keepFocusOnExpandControl()` is reachable only from\n`onExpand`/`onCollapse` in `BladeHeader.vue`. The shortcut is dispatched\nin `shortcut-dispatch.ts:133` and calls `deps.toggleMaximized(bladeId)`\non the blade stack — it never reaches the header at all.\n\n## Change\n\nThe mistake was hooking the handoff to a *handler*. It is the **swap**\nthat loses the focused node, not the click, so the handoff now watches\nthe state that drives the swap:\n\n```ts\nwatch(() => renderingState?.value?.maximized, () => keepFocusOnExpandControl());\n```\n\nBoth entry points are covered by one mechanism, and a third would be\ntoo. `onExpand`/`onCollapse` go back to just emitting.\n\nTwo details that are load-bearing and easy to lose:\n\n- **Default `pre` flush.** The guard inside `keepFocusOnExpandControl`\nasks whether focus is still inside the header controls, which is only\ntrue while the control the user activated is still mounted. A `post`\nflush would run after the swap, find focus already on `<body>`, and\ndecline.\n- The existing `requestAnimationFrame` still does the actual focusing,\nafter the patch. That part is unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\nTwo, driving the state from outside the component exactly as the\nshortcut does — a mutable `maximized` ref flipped without touching the\nheader:\n\n- focus moves to the replacement control\n- focus is left alone when it sits outside the header, so a mouse user\nwho clicked elsewhere is not interrupted\n\nRestoring the handler-driven form fails the first one. That is the\ndiscriminating check: the old code passes every test that drives the\nheader''s own button, which is why this survived the previous round.\n\n## Verification\n\n414 files, 4087 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`, the full-glob\n`lint:check --max-warnings=0` and prettier clean.\n\nNot measured in a live browser here: reproducing it needs the chord\npressed with focus on the control, and QA has a documented recipe and\nscreenshots on VCST-5670. Worth re-running theirs against a build with\nthis change.\n\n## Notes for the parent ticket\n\nTwo observations in the QA report worth keeping, neither addressed here:\n\n- **Save passes by accident.** That path is untouched by #286; saving\n*remounts* the blade, so `vc-blade.vue`''s `onMounted(focusIfLoose)`\ncatches the loose focus. It would regress silently if the blade ever\nstopped remounting on save.\n- **The failure''s severity is genuinely Low.** Chrome keeps the\nsequential-focus starting point at the removed node, so Tab still\nreaches the replacement. That is engine-specific and does nothing for a\nscreen reader, so it remains a real 2.4.3 failure.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlt+xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlCwQAA0Lu47aIKAT3PGdf5d5Ff5X\n8YQh017D7FOGHunNqdPIiH+pyX+sMBcrsQdL0kmNYxYj6+ig6o8T7sj+yexkQmTW\n8Nb8FZ2nUePkU3aYdSmP+YOpEpd2Fth2Je6WJkRGcOcetRm3XNpQURi5lXUIWlQn\nB41Sb5TxtyXYuTxEDzrKjUirv0WjXUy6MNgdpVfFHl4Hxh0q2hCoU9zkGnba9ITj\n/Tyd6xn1COkkxgPLmK/fHsjtNhWbM+E8KcZdI77PVZo6ueKdZP84roFepItg7Tlk\nWVs/2YtrD8zhWwgSDwVzsXHcBWK0gtVrRLM0Ua5w6/Ozly622EFRELIbVYEwXvt9\nGJy+vUc4HoQVhPPmuts0nmUOT15jGWQ1NceAfZ8aa1PN6gGzhfKBAw6RJ1qS4Uss\nx4FCgWh1EdKk5Zm237hpimQzdtFYNCFytCj8QLkHht/YREr8+NZaWiNepaGuto54\nctMs4oQb+txraKB3loqiJBdktYGrkGwX5W+8b6aaNiAC/Ff80rFwSa0EkzuFjc/q\nH6uZ6czihN7rGoE1L9USDJddeHux+7A6CwAA7ECzTvACw4nqtLJGNyXCB4WK/ZUQ\nkObcRJdGgiu0Z7DRk5lRnSY9WU9d1VzieEJvRfIYlCDBOc7ncBqAERjLVeUayWqg\nanzO9TBPUP/nL0VTzGaR\n=u7QO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:22:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDgzY2E5MTVjMjMyNzcwMjQ2ZGZkMGI3OGYwNTIzZWIxODcwM2U3ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892","sha":"87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892"}],"sha":"83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/83ca915c232770246dfd0b78f0523eb18703e7e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:22:29Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:22:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-auth-layout): give the unauthenticated pages a focus target (VCST-5813) (#343)\n\nFixes VCST-5813.\n\n## Why the existing repair could not reach this\n\nVCST-5670 (#286) added a route watcher in `vc-app.vue`:\n\n```ts\nwatch(() => route.fullPath, () => focusIfLoose(() => workspaceRef.value));\n```\n\nSigning out cannot be repaired from there. `/login` and the shell are\n**sibling routes**, so logging out unmounts `vc-app` entirely and the\nwatcher goes with it. Even if it survived, `workspaceRef` points at\n`<main v-if=\"isAuthenticated\">`, so the target would be null and\n`focusIfLoose` would decline — correctly, since focusing a detached node\nis worse than not focusing at all.\n\nThe ticket reached the same conclusion independently; this confirms it\nagainst the source rather than restating it.\n\n## Change\n\nThe target has to belong to the *arriving* context, not the departing\none.\n\n`vc-auth-layout` is the root of every unauthenticated page — sign-in,\nforgot password, reset password, invitation, and the forced password\nchange — and its root element is already a `<main>`, the same shape as\nthe workspace. It now carries `tabindex=\"-1\"` and the same `onMounted(()\n=> focusIfLoose(...))` repair that each blade already performs for\nitself.\n\nFive pages, one repair. The ticket asked only for the login page; the\nother four arrive by the same kind of transition and had the same gap.\n\n## Tests\n\nThree, on the layout:\n\n- it takes focus when focus is loose on mount\n- it declines when something already holds focus — this repairs lost\nfocus, it does not dictate focus, so a page that autofocuses its first\nfield keeps it\n- the root is focusable without becoming a tab stop (`tabindex=\"-1\"`)\n\nOne detail worth knowing for anyone extending these: the first test\nneeds `attachTo: document.body`. `focusIfLoose` refuses a target that is\nnot connected, which is precisely what makes it safe, so a detached\nmount silently passes for the wrong reason.\n\nRemoving the `onMounted` line fails that test.\n\n## Verification\n\n414 files, 4088 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`, the full-glob\n`lint:check --max-warnings=0`, prettier and stylelint all clean.\n\n## Related\n\nPart of a cluster of four focus-order defects: VCST-5670 and VCST-5632\n(reopened), this one, and VCST-5806 (dashboard range toggle). VCST-5806\nhas a different cause — a control re-rendering under its own focus — and\nis not addressed here.","tree":{"sha":"8162f87a38eb73d9ed03a2ecce03bc1fc877b29e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/8162f87a38eb73d9ed03a2ecce03bc1fc877b29e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892","verification":{"payload":"tree 8162f87a38eb73d9ed03a2ecce03bc1fc877b29e\nparent 2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788272549 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788272549 +0300\n\nfix(vc-auth-layout): give the unauthenticated pages a focus target (VCST-5813) (#343)\n\nFixes VCST-5813.\n\n## Why the existing repair could not reach this\n\nVCST-5670 (#286) added a route watcher in `vc-app.vue`:\n\n```ts\nwatch(() => route.fullPath, () => focusIfLoose(() => workspaceRef.value));\n```\n\nSigning out cannot be repaired from there. `/login` and the shell are\n**sibling routes**, so logging out unmounts `vc-app` entirely and the\nwatcher goes with it. Even if it survived, `workspaceRef` points at\n`<main v-if=\"isAuthenticated\">`, so the target would be null and\n`focusIfLoose` would decline — correctly, since focusing a detached node\nis worse than not focusing at all.\n\nThe ticket reached the same conclusion independently; this confirms it\nagainst the source rather than restating it.\n\n## Change\n\nThe target has to belong to the *arriving* context, not the departing\none.\n\n`vc-auth-layout` is the root of every unauthenticated page — sign-in,\nforgot password, reset password, invitation, and the forced password\nchange — and its root element is already a `<main>`, the same shape as\nthe workspace. It now carries `tabindex=\"-1\"` and the same `onMounted(()\n=> focusIfLoose(...))` repair that each blade already performs for\nitself.\n\nFive pages, one repair. The ticket asked only for the login page; the\nother four arrive by the same kind of transition and had the same gap.\n\n## Tests\n\nThree, on the layout:\n\n- it takes focus when focus is loose on mount\n- it declines when something already holds focus — this repairs lost\nfocus, it does not dictate focus, so a page that autofocuses its first\nfield keeps it\n- the root is focusable without becoming a tab stop (`tabindex=\"-1\"`)\n\nOne detail worth knowing for anyone extending these: the first test\nneeds `attachTo: document.body`. `focusIfLoose` refuses a target that is\nnot connected, which is precisely what makes it safe, so a detached\nmount silently passes for the wrong reason.\n\nRemoving the `onMounted` line fails that test.\n\n## Verification\n\n414 files, 4088 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`, the full-glob\n`lint:check --max-warnings=0`, prettier and stylelint all clean.\n\n## Related\n\nPart of a cluster of four focus-order defects: VCST-5670 and VCST-5632\n(reopened), this one, and VCST-5806 (dashboard range toggle). VCST-5806\nhas a different cause — a control re-rendering under its own focus — and\nis not addressed here.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlt+lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe6oQACEDhcR/h2r3abgPXspiTvKc\n4KlN8WJNzljnaLaB0/0u+kgUuuC4hWMX8Z6HEuxCGxx83eyADWtAE3qdtxxZiKb3\nvVOGRu6bFmrwJja0P1tr/axu7qIWFRzgaEb2jTPcdWOO9Gmdz4h292X3BJJ0a1h8\n0xwyYWq6hl4FOo0xfKta158QAcbeY3qbl0RYtSSQzi/Z49mQH4gBbhBZWMPI7nhm\nSi0qtxQS5KMu53QqE4plQfKasbpBiyPRt04Xym6m7zyAHlvZ8gOdvpB5DzBzeDd6\nHggmKQc0/bJvTYKJIrF5u4aokvXZG3aqkEqsyt7LUbUYH8XbA42Ydk5wOdrGx4Cq\ncDb1Ui5jCOUotemaFR+6TfOfepbzvGiPEvyU9Ixizu4uez1V2wd+5s+R6+JPcPrY\nHMYLLZPipOfLkm/y24nR7Uzq5326Vl6w1DlTf38x6TcHSOyaVSvrJP9I4fbz3lLs\nKF3HyJ7kAXiVrp64tkBrDD4Yd1UrQZrAPYnT/iwr6j7+oadMOvt9OrFJau1QrFwH\nufLtzxAVkaJaWAwkD5yJReKWtEEy/5iSgaR2xwA9thqkpmI7YFrDcPRE10PblO2/\nt96e3miCr+pm3JWpP4WarTWtzlobLu4kST2+8XG5sCTgbNESkFtFuSGKIITMzAIV\nO6z/9Iwe6EJksptSxlCA\n=Z80X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:22:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDg3YjRiYzA5YzIwNTA4MTJiMmJjYmNkYzdhM2YyZWIzNDdlYWE4OTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4","sha":"2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4"}],"sha":"87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/87b4bc09c2050812b2bcbcdc7a3f2eb347eaa892"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:31:25Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:31:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-dynamic-property): pick the control the value strategy agrees with (VM-1774) (#342)\n\nFixes VM-1774, scoped down from what the ticket proposed — see the last\nsection.\n\n## The defect\n\nWhich control to render was decided twice, in two different orders.\n\n```ts\n// vc-dynamic-property.vue, first of sixteen ordered conditions\nv-if=\"valueType !== ''Color'' && dictionary && !multivalue\"   // dictionary VcSelect\n\n// strategies/index.ts, resolveStrategy\nif (isMeasureProperty(property)) return measureStrategy;    // Measure wins here\n```\n\nThe template tested `dictionary` first; `resolveStrategy` tests\n`Measure` first. So a **Measure property carrying a dictionary**\nrendered the dictionary `VcSelect`, while its value was read and written\nby `measureStrategy`:\n\n| | reads | writes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `measureStrategy` | `values[0].value` | `{ value, unitOfMeasureId }` |\n| `dictionaryStrategy` | `values[0].valueId` | dictionary items by\n`valueId` |\n\nDifferent fields. The select showed nothing as selected, stored no\ndictionary reference, and **the unit could not be set at all** — the\nunit dropdown belongs to the measure control, which never rendered.\n`Boolean` with a dictionary diverged the same way.\n\nConsumers are real: `PropertyGroup.vue` and `PropertyGroupOffers.vue` in\nthe vendor portal.\n\n## Four more, found by writing the table\n\n`Number`, `Integer`, `LongText` and `DateTime` with a **multivalue**\ndictionary rendered a plain input while `resolveStrategy` routed their\nvalues through `dictionaryStrategy`, again by `valueId`. The old chain\nhad a dictionary control for the single-value case and for multivalue\n`ShortText` only.\n\nThe multivalue-dictionary markup is a generic `VcMultivalue` bound to\ndictionary items — nothing `ShortText`-specific about it — so the other\nfour now reach it.\n\n## Change\n\n`resolveControlKind(property)` makes the decision once, in the same\nprecedence as `resolveStrategy`. The strategy is the data contract —\nnon-UI code reads through it — so the control follows the strategy\nrather than the reverse.\n\nThe sixteen branches keep their markup exactly; only their conditions\nnow read from the shared decision.\n\nA final `v-else` was added. `valueType` is `string | undefined`, not a\nunion, so the platform can send a type this component has never heard\nof; the chain had no fallback and rendered a labelled field with **no\ncontrol at all**.\n\n## What this deliberately does not do\n\n- **No `registerPropertyControl()`.** The ticket asks for it; it has no\ncaller, and a public export cannot be withdrawn before the next major.\nSame trap that closed VM-1764.\n- **No collapse into one `<component :is>`.** The `Measure` branch\ncarries a scoped slot for its unit button, so a single dynamic component\nneeds per-case slot machinery. The ticket treats this as mechanical; it\nis not. Sixteen branches is a fair complaint, but it is not what was\nbroken.\n\nBoth are worth revisiting when something asks for them.\n\n## Tests\n\nTwenty-two, over `valueType × multivalue × dictionary`. The load-bearing\none asserts the invariant that would have caught all six defects:\n**every control must belong to the strategy that reads its value.**\n\nReinstating the old precedence in `resolveControlKind` fails exactly\nfour of them, naming `Measure` and `Boolean` with a dictionary.\n\n## Verification\n\n414 files, 4078 tests passing (4010 before). `vue-tsc --noEmit`, the\nfull-glob `lint:check --max-warnings=0` and prettier all clean. Existing\ndynamic-property component and composable tests (43) pass unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"18c952923d180cbe510cd60d2ffbeb4aa4c3afdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/18c952923d180cbe510cd60d2ffbeb4aa4c3afdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4","verification":{"payload":"tree 18c952923d180cbe510cd60d2ffbeb4aa4c3afdc\nparent d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788247885 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788247885 +0300\n\nfix(vc-dynamic-property): pick the control the value strategy agrees with (VM-1774) (#342)\n\nFixes VM-1774, scoped down from what the ticket proposed — see the last\nsection.\n\n## The defect\n\nWhich control to render was decided twice, in two different orders.\n\n```ts\n// vc-dynamic-property.vue, first of sixteen ordered conditions\nv-if=\"valueType !== ''Color'' && dictionary && !multivalue\"   // dictionary VcSelect\n\n// strategies/index.ts, resolveStrategy\nif (isMeasureProperty(property)) return measureStrategy;    // Measure wins here\n```\n\nThe template tested `dictionary` first; `resolveStrategy` tests\n`Measure` first. So a **Measure property carrying a dictionary**\nrendered the dictionary `VcSelect`, while its value was read and written\nby `measureStrategy`:\n\n| | reads | writes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `measureStrategy` | `values[0].value` | `{ value, unitOfMeasureId }` |\n| `dictionaryStrategy` | `values[0].valueId` | dictionary items by\n`valueId` |\n\nDifferent fields. The select showed nothing as selected, stored no\ndictionary reference, and **the unit could not be set at all** — the\nunit dropdown belongs to the measure control, which never rendered.\n`Boolean` with a dictionary diverged the same way.\n\nConsumers are real: `PropertyGroup.vue` and `PropertyGroupOffers.vue` in\nthe vendor portal.\n\n## Four more, found by writing the table\n\n`Number`, `Integer`, `LongText` and `DateTime` with a **multivalue**\ndictionary rendered a plain input while `resolveStrategy` routed their\nvalues through `dictionaryStrategy`, again by `valueId`. The old chain\nhad a dictionary control for the single-value case and for multivalue\n`ShortText` only.\n\nThe multivalue-dictionary markup is a generic `VcMultivalue` bound to\ndictionary items — nothing `ShortText`-specific about it — so the other\nfour now reach it.\n\n## Change\n\n`resolveControlKind(property)` makes the decision once, in the same\nprecedence as `resolveStrategy`. The strategy is the data contract —\nnon-UI code reads through it — so the control follows the strategy\nrather than the reverse.\n\nThe sixteen branches keep their markup exactly; only their conditions\nnow read from the shared decision.\n\nA final `v-else` was added. `valueType` is `string | undefined`, not a\nunion, so the platform can send a type this component has never heard\nof; the chain had no fallback and rendered a labelled field with **no\ncontrol at all**.\n\n## What this deliberately does not do\n\n- **No `registerPropertyControl()`.** The ticket asks for it; it has no\ncaller, and a public export cannot be withdrawn before the next major.\nSame trap that closed VM-1764.\n- **No collapse into one `<component :is>`.** The `Measure` branch\ncarries a scoped slot for its unit button, so a single dynamic component\nneeds per-case slot machinery. The ticket treats this as mechanical; it\nis not. Sixteen branches is a fair complaint, but it is not what was\nbroken.\n\nBoth are worth revisiting when something asks for them.\n\n## Tests\n\nTwenty-two, over `valueType × multivalue × dictionary`. The load-bearing\none asserts the invariant that would have caught all six defects:\n**every control must belong to the strategy that reads its value.**\n\nReinstating the old precedence in `resolveControlKind` fails exactly\nfour of them, naming `Measure` and `Boolean` with a dictionary.\n\n## Verification\n\n414 files, 4078 tests passing (4010 before). `vue-tsc --noEmit`, the\nfull-glob `lint:check --max-warnings=0` and prettier all clean. Existing\ndynamic-property component and composable tests (43) pass unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqln9NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZLwQAIx/sCUFJmUAgLotMqV2qTl3\nCNZyiLPvWu6RDQOujFYHZXpNc5f4Qll61LpdEUPFnMIWnCk55UhkkRHyaf1Gw4Ao\n+aSyuEB9+ZPFH5fESjmqSVhd4Am0SpvwwfsuQj5SS3tGVwdigY85yYvv08vGORDp\nppSP+abUScCd7/kwFgiV5FQBrwcELps5jw2uehtU3PrSRX+VLjgrdV+Mk8IksEnr\nl8dnyWjbAH4tnGeZK01/RAch0rFwXihN8xITntOVwWkTl4k8RTPrDAezYzoTKJPF\nBZ/N5Alyoh2eU/GxKLKaHKf/S+q3Q6Wnb7yYqimRhQNm8W9RFw9jVXe0ewVry3gM\n1xxKqF0tFLVwMLggvt5ajOdjf5czuu5TqC5daf8jqClYFtlfP9MGW4eflEM2G7Al\ninE6alQI78wjr4yhxnD5Sn448qzdQcHkI1M8eI74I6DeOLL3AYQkZ92TlyPwdQFU\nPJG/nj/LpdahHos8sM6gUzL0DHnx7NAO7M0Bax403vYXiVhDlP9iw+sT6+9/NwK8\noh9Va1qcB7+dZK+nW0l4rwixLiXf3pA/WdtGsdlwoR4xWkDU4Yt4ST26+9SjmlSf\n2Xqp/7D0FDDLflzj49NS0wIlUyA3FGqLfkSxjnPpfCzN+xKc1gAFIeq7G7wXfxaJ\nEzdRgUQx5qgM98wSe4YQ\n=DKDk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T07:31:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDJmM2U4MTAzYjVjZDg3YWE4OWRmYTQ1MTA1NzgwZDJmOGZlZWEyZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5","sha":"d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5"}],"sha":"2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2f3e8103b5cd87aa89dfa45105780d2f8feea2f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:31:09Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:31:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(create-vc-app): use latest() in the scaffolded list (#340)\n\nFollows #337 and depends on #339.\n\n#337 put the stale-response guard into the scaffolded list, spelled out\nas `begin` / `try` / `isCurrent` / `finally` / `complete`. That is eight\nlines of bookkeeping wrapped around one assignment, and it is the first\ncode a new module author reads.\n\nWith `latest()` in the framework (#339) the template can show the short\nform:\n\n```ts\n// const result = await search.latest(\n//   apiClient.search({ ... }),\n// );\n// if (!result) return; // a newer search superseded this one\n// data.value = result.results ?? [];\n```\n\nSame protection, three lines, and nothing for the author to forget — the\n`finally` that releases `pending` now lives in the framework rather than\nin every generated module.\n\n## Note on the eslint directive\n\n`search` is referenced only from the commented-out example call, so it\ncarries the same `eslint-disable-next-line\n@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` the template already uses for\n`query`. In #337 it did not need one, because `search.begin()` was live\ncode.\n\nConfirmed the hard way: rendering the template without the directive\nreports `''search'' is assigned a value but never used`. A `.ejs` cannot\nbe linted, so the check is to render it and run the real gates over the\noutput — `eslint --max-warnings=0` and `prettier --check` both clean\nwith the directive, and the eslint one fails without it.\n\n74 scaffolder tests pass unchanged.\n\n## Merge order\n\nAfter #339, or the generated code references a method the installed\nframework does not have.","tree":{"sha":"7c1fa66bdedceacb861f25bbf90fd671819c3020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/7c1fa66bdedceacb861f25bbf90fd671819c3020"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c1fa66bdedceacb861f25bbf90fd671819c3020\nparent 2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788247869 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788247869 +0300\n\nfix(create-vc-app): use latest() in the scaffolded list (#340)\n\nFollows #337 and depends on #339.\n\n#337 put the stale-response guard into the scaffolded list, spelled out\nas `begin` / `try` / `isCurrent` / `finally` / `complete`. That is eight\nlines of bookkeeping wrapped around one assignment, and it is the first\ncode a new module author reads.\n\nWith `latest()` in the framework (#339) the template can show the short\nform:\n\n```ts\n// const result = await search.latest(\n//   apiClient.search({ ... }),\n// );\n// if (!result) return; // a newer search superseded this one\n// data.value = result.results ?? [];\n```\n\nSame protection, three lines, and nothing for the author to forget — the\n`finally` that releases `pending` now lives in the framework rather than\nin every generated module.\n\n## Note on the eslint directive\n\n`search` is referenced only from the commented-out example call, so it\ncarries the same `eslint-disable-next-line\n@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` the template already uses for\n`query`. In #337 it did not need one, because `search.begin()` was live\ncode.\n\nConfirmed the hard way: rendering the template without the directive\nreports `''search'' is assigned a value but never used`. A `.ejs` cannot\nbe linted, so the check is to render it and run the real gates over the\noutput — `eslint --max-warnings=0` and `prettier --check` both clean\nwith the directive, and the eslint one fails without it.\n\n74 scaffolder tests pass unchanged.\n\n## Merge order\n\nAfter #339, or the generated code references a method the installed\nframework does not have.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqln89CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtbIQAANX/j/wG08Pj31cKJ9wNR45\ngT2rbv1DlBkjIucAml16K5I5xGyrLUFmLsYsTpwPolkzyPeSmRdX87IZeyQXDo1Z\nUY530VpU7BeXnqGHO7opCfuMSpFGOlXMOHmI1+gvTUsNw44muJFJIc1ngOoSn292\nka/CFJC78mWdUonoNznr4BEOnZc7mjD/hSGxWhmJwz1kadxWXFfsu0oTs4ZOKtoG\ncTLLgjzuqUcR7dCXZ68a8reZOuytKsntKv3vJTEn41emPuXAP6AhU52yODFexGjT\n/rH/4hgErAvHE2Gq30yACgKotUQQpjQdnc5lwFvRrqrC3UVW7kl2rWdIyxVfzPBe\nb+wNOd8lNq0iVtZ9ZUICYaywnZzHAk39prZABqru1hTfp9KwNzZEy7N7uHAcTtaD\nk3wbfejH/guFeJld/3Cs6gDLF/qnXj9unPuCryCfovuvONCNJj0ws+uGBLbFnvWm\nSu65XR945eNwuITfXFD864tEI+pR7fw7ljC32fOe3jydxd4qIZuadqDbW4vfFShs\npGmeMWvcIe+TAH7qydEMdiNE4DKITJJ8Q2d6LKe0KilqYon07zQik+i2Amcj38tf\nGFfqlGIaXSP549CUJC17i3ORFPmTrWlvKHekERBkIrOHt/ebZ11IHpZcFirZ+GXK\nPCXJjdLAfvXnTtwUber6\n=3CLU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T07:31:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGQ5ODQ5NGRhM2RjYjY0NWExYmU4YjE0ZWRlMjdiMDJmMzQ2YWQyYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584","sha":"2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584"}],"sha":"d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d98494da3dcb645a1be8b14ede27b02f346ad2c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:30:55Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:30:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(useLatestRequest): add latest(), so callers stop writing the bookkeeping (#339)\n\nPrompted by review of vendor-portal#151: the pattern it applied eight\ntimes is unpleasant enough that it should not be the recommended one.\n\n## The problem with the current shape\n\nGuarding a single assignment costs eight lines:\n\n```ts\nconst request = search.begin();\ntry {\n  const result = await client.searchProducts(criteria);\n  if (!request.isCurrent()) return;\n  searchResult.value = result;\n} finally {\n  request.complete();\n}\n```\n\nTwo of those are the easiest thing in the pattern to get wrong. A\nmissing `finally` leaves `pending` stuck true after a throw; a missing\n`complete()` leaves it stuck true always. Neither fails loudly — the\nscreen just keeps a spinner nobody can clear.\n\n## Change\n\n```ts\nconst result = await search.latest(client.searchProducts(criteria));\nif (!result) return;\nsearchResult.value = result;\n```\n\n`latest()` marks the request as the newest, releases it when it settles\n— including on a throw — and resolves to `undefined` if a newer request\nstarted meanwhile.\n\nWhat has to stay in the caller is the check between the await and the\nassignment: that is the only place it can go, since the framework does\nnot own the function doing the awaiting. What did not have to stay is\neverything around it.\n\n## `begin()` is unchanged\n\nStill exported, still the same behaviour, for the two cases `latest()`\ncannot serve:\n\n- the request and the check living in different functions\n- a result that is legitimately `undefined` — `latest()` uses\n`undefined` to mean superseded, so it cannot express that one\n\nDocumented on both, so the choice is visible at the point of use.\n\n## Tests\n\nSeven, against a deferred promise the test settles by hand:\n\n- the result of an unsuperseded request passes through\n- a superseded request resolves to `undefined`\n- `pending` stays true when a superseded request finishes, and clears\nwhen the newest one does\n- a rejection propagates rather than being swallowed\n- `pending` clears when the request rejects — the missing-`finally` bug,\nnow impossible for callers to reintroduce\n- supersession through `invalidate()`\n- supersession through the owning scope stopping\n\n## Verification\n\n413 files, 4010 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`, `lint:check\n--max-warnings=0`, prettier and `docs-sync lint` (0 errors) all clean.\n\nOne note for anyone verifying locally: running eslint on a narrow glob\ninside a git worktree that has no `node_modules` reports spurious\n`import/no-unresolved` errors on files the change never touched. The\nfull-project glob against a checkout with dependencies is the honest\nrun.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\nvendor-portal#151 will be rewritten onto this before merging — eight\ncomposables drop from eight lines each to three. The `create-vc-app`\nlist template (#337) gets the same treatment.","tree":{"sha":"7cc7c237e1930eeea6fbb0f75f3ecfa868feb151","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/7cc7c237e1930eeea6fbb0f75f3ecfa868feb151"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584","verification":{"payload":"tree 7cc7c237e1930eeea6fbb0f75f3ecfa868feb151\nparent d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788247855 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788247855 +0300\n\nfeat(useLatestRequest): add latest(), so callers stop writing the bookkeeping (#339)\n\nPrompted by review of vendor-portal#151: the pattern it applied eight\ntimes is unpleasant enough that it should not be the recommended one.\n\n## The problem with the current shape\n\nGuarding a single assignment costs eight lines:\n\n```ts\nconst request = search.begin();\ntry {\n  const result = await client.searchProducts(criteria);\n  if (!request.isCurrent()) return;\n  searchResult.value = result;\n} finally {\n  request.complete();\n}\n```\n\nTwo of those are the easiest thing in the pattern to get wrong. A\nmissing `finally` leaves `pending` stuck true after a throw; a missing\n`complete()` leaves it stuck true always. Neither fails loudly — the\nscreen just keeps a spinner nobody can clear.\n\n## Change\n\n```ts\nconst result = await search.latest(client.searchProducts(criteria));\nif (!result) return;\nsearchResult.value = result;\n```\n\n`latest()` marks the request as the newest, releases it when it settles\n— including on a throw — and resolves to `undefined` if a newer request\nstarted meanwhile.\n\nWhat has to stay in the caller is the check between the await and the\nassignment: that is the only place it can go, since the framework does\nnot own the function doing the awaiting. What did not have to stay is\neverything around it.\n\n## `begin()` is unchanged\n\nStill exported, still the same behaviour, for the two cases `latest()`\ncannot serve:\n\n- the request and the check living in different functions\n- a result that is legitimately `undefined` — `latest()` uses\n`undefined` to mean superseded, so it cannot express that one\n\nDocumented on both, so the choice is visible at the point of use.\n\n## Tests\n\nSeven, against a deferred promise the test settles by hand:\n\n- the result of an unsuperseded request passes through\n- a superseded request resolves to `undefined`\n- `pending` stays true when a superseded request finishes, and clears\nwhen the newest one does\n- a rejection propagates rather than being swallowed\n- `pending` clears when the request rejects — the missing-`finally` bug,\nnow impossible for callers to reintroduce\n- supersession through `invalidate()`\n- supersession through the owning scope stopping\n\n## Verification\n\n413 files, 4010 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`, `lint:check\n--max-warnings=0`, prettier and `docs-sync lint` (0 errors) all clean.\n\nOne note for anyone verifying locally: running eslint on a narrow glob\ninside a git worktree that has no `node_modules` reports spurious\n`import/no-unresolved` errors on files the change never touched. The\nfull-project glob against a checkout with dependencies is the honest\nrun.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\nvendor-portal#151 will be rewritten onto this before merging — eight\ncomposables drop from eight lines each to three. The `create-vc-app`\nlist template (#337) gets the same treatment.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqln8vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxs8QAKshzlRY/RND0Jrkoo1sWguq\nE/DSGDFwJOCkhqfP1YsPLTmoRsWWgsDvX98xs0xnLaEE4+eso4nw5yLalD5Dngin\naqFCYuGJ4fPbO2r1LXWgclGUZj2QRDeGx6p1zOnd0ikufPXyYaNvLsb0N85t7lYv\ncxvEZO521QlInB8lAPzdJR8coHWCt1hhbYdEdfMEIdX/Bw8hJtMYY2H2f8eYYSrN\nnh+in/wOT4/JqfqNVx5m9SAd+0/tdGXulgG2bOfP09ZpWBK+HlACmAVsVZI1vZWU\nnGXh6dTcNyAmQYOyJIr393KRkmGjMsYj+6qPA9Sza5imjjGrXvuwXuU1HgTgmd23\nnB2qhHiAPegK6DkUogcjQtv4Lkgl2J4978oCBnrelaffgHjvSmwUwMkeS5Id1HpX\nGmMGfmka6Q3oQ1n3ttT41yFxCOBNyfBqRSZLnp8EbkjNUlLgez99swyzuXy37nnJ\n6Wpb5CnutfFR4tUEVOGSmDWVBNxtdVOdWrkMd2lrD+uuA7zTYO78d4Lag1Oln7VN\na1IS4xS8zqffU7oo46Ye03iW9+i8xgBRUBjENej9TbH5bnM3XzinVW3oN2uoSb+m\n5tIwBAqLbawlHdVCN5YNR2/TuvnNWvCbZDS0WGpaQYT0V3ywWmHt0ap+Vyd4Wn//\nvgBi7QheK2McX4OUpZxU\n=HWgP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T07:30:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDJmYTczYjczMzlhZjY1NDk0ZDExZTM0YmJmODQxZjcwOGZkZjQ1ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30","sha":"d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30"}],"sha":"2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2fa73b7339af65494d11e34bbf841f708fdf4584"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:27:03Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:27:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(create-vc-app): drop an unknown property, and let the gate see it (#341)\n\n## The error\n\n`buildTemplateData` accepts no `projectType`. Passing one is an excess\nproperty on an object literal:\n\n```\nsrc/commands/init.test.ts(470,9): error TS2353: Object literal may only specify known\nproperties, and ''projectType'' does not exist in type ''{ moduleName?: string | undefined; ... }''\n```\n\nThe three sibling calls in the same file do not pass it, so it was a\nstray in one place rather than an API that changed.\n\n## Why nothing caught it\n\nThe root `typecheck` script ran only the framework''s:\n\n```json\n\"typecheck\": \"yarn workspace @vc-shell/framework run check:types\"\n```\n\n`create-vc-app` has its own `check:types` and nothing invoked it. So a\ntype error could sit in the CLI indefinitely, surfacing at best as a\nnon-fatal build diagnostic.\n\n## Change\n\nThe property is removed, and the root script runs create-vc-app''s\n`check:types` as well.\n\nThat is the whole cost of covering it. `create-vc-app` is the only CLI\npackage with the script, and it is clean once this one line goes —\nchecked before widening the gate, so this does not land a red build.\n\n## Verification\n\n`yarn typecheck` passes. Reverting just the test line makes it fail with\nthe TS2353 above, which it did not do before this change — the gate now\nsees the package it was blind to.\n\n74 scaffolder tests pass unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"602e6d81243e329cc6d518343baa7a17dc691aca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/602e6d81243e329cc6d518343baa7a17dc691aca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30","verification":{"payload":"tree 602e6d81243e329cc6d518343baa7a17dc691aca\nparent 07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788247623 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788247623 +0300\n\nfix(create-vc-app): drop an unknown property, and let the gate see it (#341)\n\n## The error\n\n`buildTemplateData` accepts no `projectType`. Passing one is an excess\nproperty on an object literal:\n\n```\nsrc/commands/init.test.ts(470,9): error TS2353: Object literal may only specify known\nproperties, and ''projectType'' does not exist in type ''{ moduleName?: string | undefined; ... }''\n```\n\nThe three sibling calls in the same file do not pass it, so it was a\nstray in one place rather than an API that changed.\n\n## Why nothing caught it\n\nThe root `typecheck` script ran only the framework''s:\n\n```json\n\"typecheck\": \"yarn workspace @vc-shell/framework run check:types\"\n```\n\n`create-vc-app` has its own `check:types` and nothing invoked it. So a\ntype error could sit in the CLI indefinitely, surfacing at best as a\nnon-fatal build diagnostic.\n\n## Change\n\nThe property is removed, and the root script runs create-vc-app''s\n`check:types` as well.\n\nThat is the whole cost of covering it. `create-vc-app` is the only CLI\npackage with the script, and it is clean once this one line goes —\nchecked before widening the gate, so this does not land a red build.\n\n## Verification\n\n`yarn typecheck` passes. Reverting just the test line makes it fail with\nthe TS2353 above, which it did not do before this change — the gate now\nsees the package it was blind to.\n\n74 scaffolder tests pass unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqln5HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtxoQAKvnUE+o+NNlBRpD43mn7S9m\nwvi/IhTMVN6IOLvBoMmoNcU5p8XMjX4opeWW8O/kkrlsl31hdMokfAcjindJK2Vr\n8Jcl6q09mC5UG3Jhir3hNt6w85PhYWJ02IE+29P7N1y1h3cWrg59XY6ydA0GEZaX\nfPZi4oQRju2h3nDqxTE2l5IfWCYV+LqLNceYSrpBnFMNrKWaU4tE+FU528Lvi/4b\n9/QIabDCSqYL/l9VnI3M1EfbbD2JYzzm7pi96KZDGli9AcDdWUDFm/OvUXv1Lp/9\npoDU48UmwkxxQzCz7vbKEYGgqOdlr3eZagpfIxJ4rDOk2Ez3kzkFx6BVQjpDAuuP\nRGcoJW7Xitt9V27kR+eGAQ3Hfe4E1a0bWpa9OTYcWyzsu7ceUW7txVO87lO35k6g\nOWzjFOehE3rvgKOR89jMTXKaWF5VHA1OxmBS62YM+aDQNhTLo9XfipTdp4TYFfUo\n92R2OSCGzu7sW26LXQsEcklNLhDjHXUP8cAAgMt+R622bhHSjL/jpun0GNUdTATX\nXKmRP48L6xmX9qEbilEx6lkiSIHfCtHWlNngxYuvXgQEOZ0gNwWbXQ4eStzPAVn/\nZi7ukuxtppehWQQXyCtgG9ybI8SFZsumYBR8kLDXmwTG4HSqj4fypS8clldT/Wx/\nvMJxm46tKrUtdsnDZA19\n=ZxKe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T07:27:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGQyNTIxOWI3NGE5ZTg3ZWRhZWZjNGZiYjgxZWIxYjlhMDVmYzZmMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363","sha":"07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363"}],"sha":"d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d25219b74a9e87edaefc4fbb81eb1b9a05fc6f30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:20:02Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:20:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-editor): connect the error message to the editable region (VM-1782) (#338)\n\nFixes VM-1782.\n\n## The defect\n\n`VcEditor` rendered its validation error in a `VcHint` with no `id`, and\nnever set `aria-describedby` on the editable region. A screen reader\nuser was told the field was invalid and never told why — the message was\non screen and unreachable.\n\nIt also checked `!!errorMessage` locally rather than the shared\n`invalid`, so an editor inside an invalid `InputGroup` looked fine to\nassistive technology.\n\n## Change\n\n`VcEditor` now takes `errorId`, `invalid` and `ariaDescribedBy` from\n`useFormField`, like the other ten controls: the id goes on the hint,\nthe reference goes on the editable region.\n\nTwo details worth review:\n\n**Tiptap takes `editorProps.attributes` once at creation.** The\nattributes moved into a computed that is pushed back through\n`setOptions` when it changes — an error appearing after mount has to\nreach the node tiptap already rendered. The previous static object also\nmeant `aria-label` never followed a label change.\n\n**`aria-describedby` is withheld in fullscreen.** The error element is\n`v-if=\"errorMessage && !isFullscreen\"`, so in fullscreen there is\nnothing to point at, and a dangling reference is worse than none.\n\n## Tests\n\n**Editor a11y** (8) — in their own file, because `vc-editor.test.ts`\nmocks `useEditor` to `{ value: null }`, which leaves nothing to carry\nARIA attributes. One trap worth noting for anyone extending them: the\nmock has to return a real `shallowRef`. A plain `{ value }` is not\nunwrapped by the template, so the toolbar receives the wrapper instead\nof the editor and dies on `editor.isActive is not a function`.\n\nCovered: the region named as a multiline textbox; the reference pointing\nat the element that actually holds the message; nothing described while\nvalid; `aria-invalid` on the region rather than only the wrapper; the\nreference appearing when an error arrives after mount and disappearing\nwhen it clears; group-level invalid adopted; group `describedBy` ids\nadopted.\n\n**Cross-control contract** (34) — the invariant the ticket asked for.\nEvery component calling `useFormField` must reference its description,\ncarry an error id, and take invalid from the shared computed.\n\nIt reads sources rather than mounting a dozen components. Mount tests\nassert the rendered result more directly, but each control needs its own\nprops, stubs and providers, and the drift being guarded against is\nexactly the kind a per-component suite misses — nobody writes the test\nfor the control they forgot about.\n\n## Verification\n\nReverting only `vc-editor.vue` and keeping both suites fails seven\ntests.\n\nFull framework suite: 413 files, 4003 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`,\nthe full-glob `lint:check --max-warnings=0`, prettier and stylelint all\nclean.\n\n## Found while surveying, not fixed here\n\nSixteen components are typed with `IFormFieldProps`; eleven call\n`useFormField` and all eleven are compliant. Of the five that do not:\n\n- `VcInputCurrency` → `VcInputDropdown` → `VcInput`, `VcCheckboxGroup`\nand `VcRadioGroup` wrap `VcInputGroup` plus compliant children. These\ninherit correct behaviour and are legitimately out of scope.\n- **`VcRating` delegates to `VcIcon`, `VcLabel` and `VcSkeleton` only**\n— no compliant child, no `useFormField`. That is the same defect as this\none, in a different control. Worth its own ticket; it is not folded in\nhere because it is a different component with its own risk.","tree":{"sha":"90b8602ad546b3a33e3fb2300a5bd8ba0dd533a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/90b8602ad546b3a33e3fb2300a5bd8ba0dd533a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363","verification":{"payload":"tree 90b8602ad546b3a33e3fb2300a5bd8ba0dd533a2\nparent c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788193202 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788193202 +0300\n\nfix(vc-editor): connect the error message to the editable region (VM-1782) (#338)\n\nFixes VM-1782.\n\n## The defect\n\n`VcEditor` rendered its validation error in a `VcHint` with no `id`, and\nnever set `aria-describedby` on the editable region. A screen reader\nuser was told the field was invalid and never told why — the message was\non screen and unreachable.\n\nIt also checked `!!errorMessage` locally rather than the shared\n`invalid`, so an editor inside an invalid `InputGroup` looked fine to\nassistive technology.\n\n## Change\n\n`VcEditor` now takes `errorId`, `invalid` and `ariaDescribedBy` from\n`useFormField`, like the other ten controls: the id goes on the hint,\nthe reference goes on the editable region.\n\nTwo details worth review:\n\n**Tiptap takes `editorProps.attributes` once at creation.** The\nattributes moved into a computed that is pushed back through\n`setOptions` when it changes — an error appearing after mount has to\nreach the node tiptap already rendered. The previous static object also\nmeant `aria-label` never followed a label change.\n\n**`aria-describedby` is withheld in fullscreen.** The error element is\n`v-if=\"errorMessage && !isFullscreen\"`, so in fullscreen there is\nnothing to point at, and a dangling reference is worse than none.\n\n## Tests\n\n**Editor a11y** (8) — in their own file, because `vc-editor.test.ts`\nmocks `useEditor` to `{ value: null }`, which leaves nothing to carry\nARIA attributes. One trap worth noting for anyone extending them: the\nmock has to return a real `shallowRef`. A plain `{ value }` is not\nunwrapped by the template, so the toolbar receives the wrapper instead\nof the editor and dies on `editor.isActive is not a function`.\n\nCovered: the region named as a multiline textbox; the reference pointing\nat the element that actually holds the message; nothing described while\nvalid; `aria-invalid` on the region rather than only the wrapper; the\nreference appearing when an error arrives after mount and disappearing\nwhen it clears; group-level invalid adopted; group `describedBy` ids\nadopted.\n\n**Cross-control contract** (34) — the invariant the ticket asked for.\nEvery component calling `useFormField` must reference its description,\ncarry an error id, and take invalid from the shared computed.\n\nIt reads sources rather than mounting a dozen components. Mount tests\nassert the rendered result more directly, but each control needs its own\nprops, stubs and providers, and the drift being guarded against is\nexactly the kind a per-component suite misses — nobody writes the test\nfor the control they forgot about.\n\n## Verification\n\nReverting only `vc-editor.vue` and keeping both suites fails seven\ntests.\n\nFull framework suite: 413 files, 4003 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`,\nthe full-glob `lint:check --max-warnings=0`, prettier and stylelint all\nclean.\n\n## Found while surveying, not fixed here\n\nSixteen components are typed with `IFormFieldProps`; eleven call\n`useFormField` and all eleven are compliant. Of the five that do not:\n\n- `VcInputCurrency` → `VcInputDropdown` → `VcInput`, `VcCheckboxGroup`\nand `VcRadioGroup` wrap `VcInputGroup` plus compliant children. These\ninherit correct behaviour and are legitimately out of scope.\n- **`VcRating` delegates to `VcIcon`, `VcLabel` and `VcSkeleton` only**\n— no compliant child, no `useFormField`. That is the same defect as this\none, in a different control. Worth its own ticket; it is not folded in\nhere because it is a different component with its own risk.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlamyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkC0QAIsUARoA/U4rlzUEzHcV8Gds\nYW+Td0cVwXh5pADMzTEfGJpRO07omzVfh45PsYAMlo5Ksu+Y3I0zPsCAWePtASY4\nyruIkv/B0I+90OiLKZ6ichdx0TCqubMkp6XnMi+lzqi2aoxCRUe3jKG+Kzrj1JSD\nfifhI9vdXpmHXeId7lmTGxCl5UzQYI5APPQDzO23dW/NQQhR4liJTiZRCDWkleYM\nOcgi/Gs/gDWN8ZVELILnlCSyKeLjF7EZ2il4HUvzsBQ7r2JAcssDOs3uizQAqHj4\nKiUnkY8hf5JLqZQhzvEZVpRKYm2NTjCG+T10O0oa88F5vsGBAgfpg4a7mBQmpVwk\nnXuq5n7QYOfHoq3NDmWlKUZQ9ROtLliSLjQsrqD/nJwT8MEqX+ooFRw0sle27Cyv\nStkpeYeexOVzkyDmzXQZzV38FpNPxUpFj/ZGCRZLuFgkslQSefWVACGre9cJGVPH\nx0ioEIIrpChD2+hdV9fxWJz4l8r0uVSDCTGJTbl1Vr1MOzgQ/x09iR+dvEC7dVZp\niwQ0v4TcLHpFq6ywR2fJU7stpxpqrT30Ov8jH5M4CA7UofSuqOOtF0CF7Vz/evq2\nJJxhG6DsvheLXsM58qvoA0whf3yTnNlu2gJIwi1we3Ssdg4WSQ2UMH//ZVJ4qYve\n+/82uLyihxeTw1qX8YG4\n=ltso\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T16:20:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDA3ZTJjNWVjMTFkMmE2YzU4YzczYjg3YjI4YzA2OWRjMzllZGUzNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11","sha":"c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11"}],"sha":"07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/07e2c5ec11d2a6c58c73b87b28c069dc39ede363"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:57:08Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:57:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(create-vc-app): guard the scaffolded list against a stale response (#337)\n\nFound while assessing VM-1765, which was cancelled as too invasive. This\nis the part of it that costs almost nothing and reaches every project.\n\n## The defect\n\nThe generated list page searches as you type, debounced at 300ms:\n\n```ts\nwatch([sortExpression, searchValue, () => pagination.skip], debounce(load, 300));\n```\n\nand the composable assigns unconditionally:\n\n```ts\n// data.value = result.results ?? [];\n```\n\nWhen the server takes longer than the debounce, two searches are in\nflight and whichever *answers* last wins — not whichever *started* last.\nThe list ends up showing results for a keyword the user has already\nmoved past.\n\nEvery module generated from this template starts with that, in every\nproject using the CLI.\n\n## Why the framework cannot fix it anywhere else\n\nThe guard has to sit between the `await` and the assignment — inside the\nfunction the module author writes. The framework does not own that\nfunction, so it cannot insert the check for existing code. A template is\nthe one place where it does own it.\n\n`useLatestRequest` exists for exactly this and shipped in #300. It has\nzero callers anywhere in this repo, and the scaffold was not one either\n— the tool most likely to spread the correct pattern was spreading the\nwrong one.\n\n## Change\n\n`useLatestRequest` in the scaffolded `useList`, with the `isCurrent()`\ncheck placed on the commented-out example call so it is read and kept\nwhen that call is filled in.\n\nThe page template needed nothing: it already passes `stateKey`,\ndebounces, and resets to page 1 on a new keyword.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe rendered output is Prettier-clean. `useLatestRequest` is exported\nfrom `@core/composables` alongside `useAsync` and `useLoading`, which\nthis template already imports through `@vc-shell/framework`, so it\nresolves by the same path.\n\n74 scaffolder tests pass unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"ef8c55c3981fb852372e332337b3827a468e7e9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/ef8c55c3981fb852372e332337b3827a468e7e9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11","verification":{"payload":"tree ef8c55c3981fb852372e332337b3827a468e7e9f\nparent 6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788191828 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788191828 +0300\n\nfix(create-vc-app): guard the scaffolded list against a stale response (#337)\n\nFound while assessing VM-1765, which was cancelled as too invasive. This\nis the part of it that costs almost nothing and reaches every project.\n\n## The defect\n\nThe generated list page searches as you type, debounced at 300ms:\n\n```ts\nwatch([sortExpression, searchValue, () => pagination.skip], debounce(load, 300));\n```\n\nand the composable assigns unconditionally:\n\n```ts\n// data.value = result.results ?? [];\n```\n\nWhen the server takes longer than the debounce, two searches are in\nflight and whichever *answers* last wins — not whichever *started* last.\nThe list ends up showing results for a keyword the user has already\nmoved past.\n\nEvery module generated from this template starts with that, in every\nproject using the CLI.\n\n## Why the framework cannot fix it anywhere else\n\nThe guard has to sit between the `await` and the assignment — inside the\nfunction the module author writes. The framework does not own that\nfunction, so it cannot insert the check for existing code. A template is\nthe one place where it does own it.\n\n`useLatestRequest` exists for exactly this and shipped in #300. It has\nzero callers anywhere in this repo, and the scaffold was not one either\n— the tool most likely to spread the correct pattern was spreading the\nwrong one.\n\n## Change\n\n`useLatestRequest` in the scaffolded `useList`, with the `isCurrent()`\ncheck placed on the commented-out example call so it is read and kept\nwhen that call is filled in.\n\nThe page template needed nothing: it already passes `stateKey`,\ndebounces, and resets to page 1 on a new keyword.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe rendered output is Prettier-clean. `useLatestRequest` is exported\nfrom `@core/composables` alongside `useAsync` and `useLoading`, which\nthis template already imports through `@vc-shell/framework`, so it\nresolves by the same path.\n\n74 scaffolder tests pass unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlaRUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoigQAEWo7EypVlZ+0WD5rVCfHiTI\n/mIG5T9Lvxp1sA96HOJZj001ZG6sKp6nx8DeCdciwxTPxWFiaDG0ic7d1Rep8hao\nydOgyIwRlWLawdbA0qmJWO4dgsvxJIpSO2bQOs4tLBp9b8HBU4Y5Lv2DYCHVvQX1\nGXx9qyfqMIVWqsbAxA6kJTh9JFxmzAmrQdxOqdN9v8kfTZsSIh0j+IfDo/VXZ69i\nDJq4TSOtTH//IlhQjEaPiB1Z4xAap2jeiwxzhIWsK0JckMOZg7+1cLPWapmWXCRT\nxvx60Dsw/tfXo2UxexkqBe4PaCe0vPe/6joJm/NEQ+4Suq90G0zFetfSRBM1l8OG\nMyyh3fTEB052VnhTsY5Srry8nxNyxMc7G4+A5ToJdB8KcvgYaCL+3D1XFWUj2ceN\nZd98ntumGunMkcoQd7OlsXE0A5hhTa5d3eUdYy4Ek9TMxyvdusXcwC1F/N7XsSge\nIdQ0zDI8iQGwO/rJeD/iSLx7Wzcof8Zyv/vxhmzJ+RmpG8bOjtrJEkqgOoMLHwqL\nC94Dxz21SOqjuXKJ+NaX+lW0/Zaq0IY5quwXX7U5CujnkjvCj91lrroRs4d8MRO7\nK7QogtwFBHXw5ky5I7jjQLhmdzTx+6iHwx9gQTMk+enexgrgScLdOT2GYLwSS1g5\n2oSJWWbP4ZH0LDR7cm42\n=5l5z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T15:57:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGMzY2UxNTlkZDBmNjIyODgwNGRlODY3MDliNDdlZmJhMzIwNjVlMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992","sha":"6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992"}],"sha":"c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c3ce159dd0f6228804de86709b47efba32065e11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:28:17Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:28:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(composables): deprecate useModificationTracker in favour of useBladeForm (VM-1767) (#336)\n\nCloses VM-1767, but not the way the ticket proposed.\n\n## What the ticket asked for\n\nOne shared `semanticEqual` in `core/utilities`, plus an opt-in `isEqual`\noption on both `useBladeForm` and `useModificationTracker`, because \"the\nsame payload can be reported dirty by one and clean by the other\".\n\n## What is actually true\n\nThe divergence is real:\n\n```ts\n// useBladeForm/index.ts:16-21 — [] counts as empty\nif (isEmptyPrimitive(a) && Array.isArray(b) && b.length === 0) return true;\n\n// useModificationTracker/index.ts:14-19 — the customizer only fires when both\n// are empty primitives, so [] vs undefined falls through to lodash isEqual → false\n```\n\nThe symptom is not. `useModificationTracker` has **no callers** — not in\nthe framework, not in the reference app. The only references anywhere\nare the barrel export at `core/composables/index.ts:30` and prose in\nthree docs pages. `useBladeForm` mentions it twice, in comments, saying\nwhat it does differently.\n\nSo there is no form on which the two can disagree. The ticket''s scenario\n— \"a form that uses both\" — cannot be constructed.\n\n## Why that is, and what it means\n\n`useBladeForm` was built to replace the `useForm` +\n`useModificationTracker` + `useBeforeUnload` combination; its own\ndocumentation opens by saying so. `cli/migrate` already carries a\ndiagnostic transform, `use-blade-form`, that finds that combination and\nflags it for the move.\n\nThe succession is done in practice and only the label was missing.\nAdding a shared comparator and an option on both sides would mean\nmaintaining new public surface for code nothing calls.\n\n## Change\n\n`@deprecated` on the composable, pointing at `useBladeForm`, and a\nmatching admonition in its docs page.\n\nThe comparator is deliberately left as it is. Aligning it would move the\ndirty flag for any consumer outside this repo still using it — a\nbehavioural change delivered to people who are simultaneously being told\nto migrate away. Not worth it.\n\n## Verification\n\nDeprecation only. The export, its behaviour and its 12 tests are\nunchanged and still pass. `vue-tsc --noEmit`, `eslint --max-warnings=0`\nover the framework, prettier and `docs-sync lint` (0 errors) all clean.","tree":{"sha":"9d7623e1da546c9153a0d76a064c46245bb30198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/9d7623e1da546c9153a0d76a064c46245bb30198"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d7623e1da546c9153a0d76a064c46245bb30198\nparent 5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788190097 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788190097 +0300\n\nrefactor(composables): deprecate useModificationTracker in favour of useBladeForm (VM-1767) (#336)\n\nCloses VM-1767, but not the way the ticket proposed.\n\n## What the ticket asked for\n\nOne shared `semanticEqual` in `core/utilities`, plus an opt-in `isEqual`\noption on both `useBladeForm` and `useModificationTracker`, because \"the\nsame payload can be reported dirty by one and clean by the other\".\n\n## What is actually true\n\nThe divergence is real:\n\n```ts\n// useBladeForm/index.ts:16-21 — [] counts as empty\nif (isEmptyPrimitive(a) && Array.isArray(b) && b.length === 0) return true;\n\n// useModificationTracker/index.ts:14-19 — the customizer only fires when both\n// are empty primitives, so [] vs undefined falls through to lodash isEqual → false\n```\n\nThe symptom is not. `useModificationTracker` has **no callers** — not in\nthe framework, not in the reference app. The only references anywhere\nare the barrel export at `core/composables/index.ts:30` and prose in\nthree docs pages. `useBladeForm` mentions it twice, in comments, saying\nwhat it does differently.\n\nSo there is no form on which the two can disagree. The ticket''s scenario\n— \"a form that uses both\" — cannot be constructed.\n\n## Why that is, and what it means\n\n`useBladeForm` was built to replace the `useForm` +\n`useModificationTracker` + `useBeforeUnload` combination; its own\ndocumentation opens by saying so. `cli/migrate` already carries a\ndiagnostic transform, `use-blade-form`, that finds that combination and\nflags it for the move.\n\nThe succession is done in practice and only the label was missing.\nAdding a shared comparator and an option on both sides would mean\nmaintaining new public surface for code nothing calls.\n\n## Change\n\n`@deprecated` on the composable, pointing at `useBladeForm`, and a\nmatching admonition in its docs page.\n\nThe comparator is deliberately left as it is. Aligning it would move the\ndirty flag for any consumer outside this repo still using it — a\nbehavioural change delivered to people who are simultaneously being told\nto migrate away. Not worth it.\n\n## Verification\n\nDeprecation only. The export, its behaviour and its 12 tests are\nunchanged and still pass. `vue-tsc --noEmit`, `eslint --max-warnings=0`\nover the framework, prettier and `docs-sync lint` (0 errors) all clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlZ2RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxWoQABU1jdKgct1WdBOFiHYFkJMm\n5w5T4IFP2K9y7Lt/ZzCm+76owFW2kGf2KMvAOMkLg5Nnv0rOPrnsGOeyEL3pd0a2\nTjjOZQjWZ+AbyMwVJNl0gvVPS2Sz8UKtB4ReIgFqMGz6U+rzcXVbUkXYtq6j0K7R\ncnabovkvsVIAihOREe8iEokv5ghOfjRD37tXGapnGli4SG/BsUvXMzwKF6y8W0g7\nvCYuvvZDPw+3Kk7DFxI8Vyuf4ZDskuHAwjsMf+AZltPKEE71XhS8LO2JcQvX85L6\nHHA/+V6kPo8jpn7EFTXnwo+SSHre3mi9Wu1pXU3VoSmYvH4sguiZ2OU0L67MAJ4q\nehGr/TJ9Hjail20eBXYRZdYdsXqeFNCl9l1v4uGYDqHlZOHGP2FjTdgbqMyS4/8z\nN+BjhA540K3Kn17TE4MUhpFviqHpZaz8Z3EgRavk/OsDLMu7NIERtqwHzXFVvdDg\nOwNfXXCxrOvHBNMy9GQdGcVAwNKYM9S3XdNGaeQ3Wopixr8IdltIj2DI7Tq6S0pA\n/Qq8P5wlcMfofe0xp1xuKDC20JvwAhNtDsPC3oW872rupmvE9VtThMZhw+f76aqr\n83fdlorTzSoV/aKuZJD7PrAuVRCeCnvipV7jINYQhx85LizDXpMcnZ6KzDTQVmec\nw5ToEQgOgk0oK/S48jXq\n=/XHH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T15:28:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDY4MDllNmEwOWNkZGY0ZTkxYjZmN2FmNTVjNTFmNmExYzcyY2E5OTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791","sha":"5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791"}],"sha":"6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/6809e6a09cddf4e91b6f7af55c51f6a1c72ca992"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:19:28Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:19:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(interceptors): cover the external cancellation path (#335)\n\nSalvaged from #334, which was closed as speculative. This half is not:\nit covers code that already exists and ships today.\n\n## What was untested\n\nThe interceptor creates its own `AbortController` to enforce the\n30-second timeout, and links the caller''s signal to it so that a caller\nabort reaches the request actually in flight — which is not the caller''s\nrequest object, but the one the interceptor issued.\n\n```ts\nconst externalSignal = init?.signal;\nconst abortFromExternal = () => controller.abort();\nif (externalSignal?.aborted) {\n  abortFromExternal();\n} else if (externalSignal) {\n  externalSignal.addEventListener(\"abort\", abortFromExternal, { once: true });\n}\n```\n\n`grep ''signal\\|abort''` over `interceptors.test.ts` returned nothing.\nThis shares a controller with the timeout that every API call in the app\ndepends on.\n\n## Four cases\n\n- the interceptor passes a signal of its own to the underlying fetch\n- a caller abort propagates to the in-flight request\n- an already-aborted caller signal aborts immediately rather than being\nignored\n- an external abort surfaces as itself, not relabelled as \"Request timed\nout\"\n\n## Verification\n\nTests only — no source change in this PR.\n\nA passing test against unchanged code proves nothing on its own, so the\nlinking block was removed as a mutation: two of the four fail. The\nremaining two cover the interceptor''s own signal and the\nabort-vs-timeout distinction, which that mutation does not affect.\n\nFull interceptor suite: 27 passing. Prettier clean.","tree":{"sha":"c8ede1ba1850cef19dd17731f66aee63b7547103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/c8ede1ba1850cef19dd17731f66aee63b7547103"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791","verification":{"payload":"tree c8ede1ba1850cef19dd17731f66aee63b7547103\nparent e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788189568 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788189568 +0300\n\ntest(interceptors): cover the external cancellation path (#335)\n\nSalvaged from #334, which was closed as speculative. This half is not:\nit covers code that already exists and ships today.\n\n## What was untested\n\nThe interceptor creates its own `AbortController` to enforce the\n30-second timeout, and links the caller''s signal to it so that a caller\nabort reaches the request actually in flight — which is not the caller''s\nrequest object, but the one the interceptor issued.\n\n```ts\nconst externalSignal = init?.signal;\nconst abortFromExternal = () => controller.abort();\nif (externalSignal?.aborted) {\n  abortFromExternal();\n} else if (externalSignal) {\n  externalSignal.addEventListener(\"abort\", abortFromExternal, { once: true });\n}\n```\n\n`grep ''signal\\|abort''` over `interceptors.test.ts` returned nothing.\nThis shares a controller with the timeout that every API call in the app\ndepends on.\n\n## Four cases\n\n- the interceptor passes a signal of its own to the underlying fetch\n- a caller abort propagates to the in-flight request\n- an already-aborted caller signal aborts immediately rather than being\nignored\n- an external abort surfaces as itself, not relabelled as \"Request timed\nout\"\n\n## Verification\n\nTests only — no source change in this PR.\n\nA passing test against unchanged code proves nothing on its own, so the\nlinking block was removed as a mutation: two of the four fail. The\nremaining two cover the interceptor''s own signal and the\nabort-vs-timeout distinction, which that mutation does not affect.\n\nFull interceptor suite: 27 passing. Prettier clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlZuACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVHwQAF0f5jlPO1Ig/04GZ5DNCPs9\niVwUlBfW7w4Jk1I86A9CYYgPNh9fFT2mWiOxfbJnsq4pmOTU322ANi+BjDKH2mgy\nvBlJowYWnKHT9T6KAe7rAUP9QEQ3JMRVjIMezxlLlhNfamxSPyI3Yr26rVmtdXue\nt/l2gYClt9a4wGfGOdl5RbEXLDhHRuPTgAi1vUzW2GtL1yYeRi4QbJLq20x9XwGV\neBKvZW0QtjeDwcWmWV/Ix6YjGTsjo/ZkMxuOTdHHjLcnbViqCYm2KxLpMyYfHaPQ\nXr1edl5VmrC7TMS6uzwcybExCTRJzKWN0ACeXG1aYijcKg5FHMP/nUvdWGOTxRMD\nB/hrQfWhHJCFiRhcQBqw5XXvWuT8bkB824JxKc6haNKyHDA5XS8iQf6270jN25Wq\nZNnBACV5PSZqn/sFYbRQtmf8uggMaxx5tbPt48jOkSyi26919jr31Ie4pPIdHOeU\nnNsC2rlY0W0MHW9nr+W9IeEbKDit11tEFAzWEuoESFZkKQehT9YRejlkPcgMfKZP\nvlTD6zvMYGUOWER+bK1TBHtYk8cTHVo4Zd8oeoO00zci+cTnNOWc5IWBoq4NO0BK\nCbJKu5hjUY0aSVAGXaxR94IcybA8odiFh7CQdgmlYHn/3JPNAJzqsliDJqewaCYN\ngyO4kesIPs0MXnx5ttTN\n=nksU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T15:19:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDVhOTBkYzU3OTQ2ODdjMDEwNTc5Y2NlNTJkM2Y2NzljNmJmNmM3OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0","sha":"e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0"}],"sha":"5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5a90dc5794687c010579cce52d3f679c6bf6c791"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:55:33Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:55:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(assets): one upload transport for useAssets and useAssetsManager (VM-1766) (#332)\n\nFixes VM-1766.\n\n## Problem\n\n`uploadSingleFile` and `processBatched` existed in both `useAssets` and\n`useAssetsManager`: the POST, the `sortOrder` assignment, the URL decode\nand the batch loop, written twice. One endpoint with two places to\nchange it — adding retry or upload progress would mean doing it twice\nand keeping the copies in step by hand.\n\nNeither path had a single test.\n\n## Change\n\n`uploadAssets(files, { uploadPath, startingSortOrder, concurrency })`\nowns the transport. Both composables call it; their return surfaces are\nunchanged, and they still differ in the only way that ever mattered —\nwho owns the resulting array. `useAssets` drops from 154 to 87 lines,\n`useAssetsManager` from 205 to 141.\n\n## The copies were not identical\n\nThe ticket describes them as duplicated line for line. They were not:\n`useAssetsManager` stripped a leading slash from the upload path and\n`useAssets` did not.\n\n```\nuploadPath = \"/catalog/images\"\n  useAssets (old)       : /api/assets?folderUrl=//catalog/images\n  useAssetsManager (old): /api/assets?folderUrl=/catalog/images\n  shared transport      : /api/assets?folderUrl=/catalog/images\n```\n\nThe shared transport normalises, so `useAssets` picks up the fix.\n`useAssets` is already `@deprecated`, and a double slash in `folderUrl`\nis not behaviour worth preserving, but it is a behavioural change rather\nthan a pure extraction and is called out here for that reason.\n\n## Tests\n\nNine, against a mocked `fetch`, where there were none:\n\n- every file posted to the folder URL, results in order\n- a leading slash in the upload path\n- `sortOrder` continuing from the last existing item, and its `0`\ndefault\n- the URL decoded (`/a/my%20file%20(1).png` → `/a/my file (1).png`)\n- the local file size winning over whatever the endpoint reports\n- no more than `concurrency` requests in flight, asserted by counting\noverlaps\n- a file the endpoint answers with nothing dropped, the rest kept\n- an empty list returning `[]` without calling the endpoint\n\n## Verification\n\n- `useAssets` + `useAssetsManager`: 3 files, 47 tests passing (38\nexisting, 9 new).\n- Full framework suite: 409 files, 3939 tests passing.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`, eslint `--max-warnings=0`, prettier: all exit 0.\n\nA revert-and-watch-it-fail proof is vacuous here — the transport is new\ncode, so removing it fails on the import rather than on behaviour. The\nmeaningful evidence is that both composables'' existing tests still pass\nagainst the shared implementation, plus the path comparison above.\n\n## Note\n\nCI on this repo is currently failing for every PR before any step runs —\njobs complete in about two seconds with no runner assigned and an empty\nstep list, which is an Actions minutes or spending limit rather than\nanything in the diff. The results above are local.","tree":{"sha":"4dc9d8116ae4a2838bed80cf7032eb3abe0a1a00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/4dc9d8116ae4a2838bed80cf7032eb3abe0a1a00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0","verification":{"payload":"tree 4dc9d8116ae4a2838bed80cf7032eb3abe0a1a00\nparent e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788184533 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788184533 +0300\n\nrefactor(assets): one upload transport for useAssets and useAssetsManager (VM-1766) (#332)\n\nFixes VM-1766.\n\n## Problem\n\n`uploadSingleFile` and `processBatched` existed in both `useAssets` and\n`useAssetsManager`: the POST, the `sortOrder` assignment, the URL decode\nand the batch loop, written twice. One endpoint with two places to\nchange it — adding retry or upload progress would mean doing it twice\nand keeping the copies in step by hand.\n\nNeither path had a single test.\n\n## Change\n\n`uploadAssets(files, { uploadPath, startingSortOrder, concurrency })`\nowns the transport. Both composables call it; their return surfaces are\nunchanged, and they still differ in the only way that ever mattered —\nwho owns the resulting array. `useAssets` drops from 154 to 87 lines,\n`useAssetsManager` from 205 to 141.\n\n## The copies were not identical\n\nThe ticket describes them as duplicated line for line. They were not:\n`useAssetsManager` stripped a leading slash from the upload path and\n`useAssets` did not.\n\n```\nuploadPath = \"/catalog/images\"\n  useAssets (old)       : /api/assets?folderUrl=//catalog/images\n  useAssetsManager (old): /api/assets?folderUrl=/catalog/images\n  shared transport      : /api/assets?folderUrl=/catalog/images\n```\n\nThe shared transport normalises, so `useAssets` picks up the fix.\n`useAssets` is already `@deprecated`, and a double slash in `folderUrl`\nis not behaviour worth preserving, but it is a behavioural change rather\nthan a pure extraction and is called out here for that reason.\n\n## Tests\n\nNine, against a mocked `fetch`, where there were none:\n\n- every file posted to the folder URL, results in order\n- a leading slash in the upload path\n- `sortOrder` continuing from the last existing item, and its `0`\ndefault\n- the URL decoded (`/a/my%20file%20(1).png` → `/a/my file (1).png`)\n- the local file size winning over whatever the endpoint reports\n- no more than `concurrency` requests in flight, asserted by counting\noverlaps\n- a file the endpoint answers with nothing dropped, the rest kept\n- an empty list returning `[]` without calling the endpoint\n\n## Verification\n\n- `useAssets` + `useAssetsManager`: 3 files, 47 tests passing (38\nexisting, 9 new).\n- Full framework suite: 409 files, 3939 tests passing.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`, eslint `--max-warnings=0`, prettier: all exit 0.\n\nA revert-and-watch-it-fail proof is vacuous here — the transport is new\ncode, so removing it fails on the import rather than on behaviour. The\nmeaningful evidence is that both composables'' existing tests still pass\nagainst the shared implementation, plus the path comparison above.\n\n## Note\n\nCI on this repo is currently failing for every PR before any step runs —\njobs complete in about two seconds with no runner assigned and an empty\nstep list, which is an Actions minutes or spending limit rather than\nanything in the diff. The results above are local.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlYfVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3SIQABI0psbB3YGTvI7OShqTq8l7\nfl4bqyrGVFD9Y4JneFPzs4DCG8h2uoNInRUxBRe6NU/ygleqnh3gXfiHXikITauP\nFRb8VRVt/AbWR5lgsc9XPOqxlHYjULDyU50smBTowF0V9PBYnySBQdFg9A7KlFDQ\nCORgUNHByjx6uBF/HTznUViHjTbGVKzN+v8dciqSePbO9ScWK1H0GQubU29jqnYk\nXLIxAo+X0Teoy0rH4AZeWbX8ZsPKf29telgu5v5T3rQLx6t8c2T7Fpc6HVpo3J+D\nAi0/v/hppTeKpCFHo+EHtX7ZgU1fMKczYyPZ+INsFUazFRIIIlxfX/cgatvChOSX\nNzPUIpawHqWvzZKudnNzbvnr55EpotbNDfZawY76YD9IhTtHT2qvcL0qN4SZcrWx\nOkTeSGLRVuXYWsYGQuRnqrsPha1IXvvblLBkbfswWGOatvj0oD/fmd+NuHRUfZBh\nwlrZ9nz+K4fGE6Bqk5WxXkQxoZfF3/MtPcHoBequLZB8opA95CTJD9i6Fl6gGiOU\nqKhdt6AIQ7ctZ6NZa5HuvYog7fDaWeZ3oJOh5wOIjELTSesv4AG+VpJ2NjC1iDDa\nUEoCqC5wu2cmjUYbvErTb2A/mfINZNdT4GG5tgXLQ7KvWU04lOWKOD71MiMM2BZM\nCMYnkf1tIhSLqkbfufvO\n=INQa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T13:55:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGU4Y2E3NDkxMTRkY2U2YjcyZWQwM2VkY2UxY2UyYmZkYWIwNGJmYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f","sha":"e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f"}],"sha":"e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e8ca749114dce6b72ed03edce1ce2bfdab04bfc0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:55:25Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:55:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(blade-navigation): one root-route resolver, and correct a stale comment (VM-1762) (#331)\n\nFixes VM-1762. The ticket asked for one URL codec because encode and\ndecode were said to disagree about depth. They do not — see \"What the\nticket got wrong\" below. What was actually left in this area is a\nduplicated root-route resolver, one copy of which still carries a bug\nthe other had fixed, and a comment describing a hazard that no longer\nexists.\n\n## The bug\n\n`navigateToMainRoute` and the legacy adapter''s `goToRoot` each resolved\nthe root route independently. VM-1777 fixed the adapter''s copy; this one\nwas missed:\n\n```ts\nconst mainRoute = routes.find((r) => r.meta?.root);\nconst mainRouteAlias = routes.find((r) => r.aliasOf?.path === mainRoute?.path) ?? mainRoute;\n```\n\nWith no route declaring `meta.root`, `mainRoute` is `undefined`, so the\nsecond predicate reads `r.aliasOf?.path === undefined` — true for every\nroute without an alias. `find` returns whatever was registered first.\n\nDemonstrated against a two-route table with no `meta.root`:\n\n```\nold resolves to: Login\nnew resolves to: undefined\n```\n\nThis is not a corner nobody reaches: `navigateToMainRoute` is the\nfallback `restoreFromUrl` uses when a URL names an unknown workspace, is\nnot a workspace, or is not permitted — the path a user takes by\nfollowing a stale or mistyped link. In an app without a `meta.root`\nroute, \"go home\" sent them to the login screen.\n\nBoth call sites now use `resolveMainRoute`, which returns `undefined`\nwhen there is no root route instead of guessing.\n\n## The stale comment\n\n`restoreFromUrl`''s idempotency check said it was there because \"the\nblade was opened programmatically and syncUrlPush just triggered the\nguard\". That hazard is gone: the stack owns URL sync and\n`plugin-v2.ts:111` wraps the whole guard in\n`RouterUrlSink.suppressWhile`, so a restore cannot re-enter through the\nstack''s own writes.\n\nThe check still earns its place for a different reason, which the\ncomment now states: the guard runs on every catch-all navigation,\nincluding a back/forward onto a URL the stack already matches, and\n`openBlade` — unlike `openWorkspace` — has no same-target no-op, so\nremoving it would stack a duplicate child.\n\n## What the ticket got wrong\n\nChecked against the source before starting; each of these is now false:\n\n| Ticket | Reality |\n| --- | --- |\n| \"`buildUrlFromStack` serialises a stack of any depth\" | It emits the\nworkspace plus the last visible child, and nothing deeper — symmetric\nwith `parseBladeUrl` |\n| \"two different `getTenantPrefix` implementations with different\nsemantics\" | One, `urlSync.ts:121`. The second went with the URL-sync\nconsolidation |\n| \"restoring from a URL stops at two levels\" — framed as a defect | Two\nblades in the URL is the intended design, confirmed with the product\nowner |\n\nBecause the depth mismatch does not exist, there is nothing for a new\ncodec to reconcile, and `ParsedBladeUrl` / `parseBladeUrl` are left\nalone rather than wrapped in deprecated shims.\n\nThe `onMounted`/`nextTick` reconcile pass in\n`vc-blade-navigation-new.vue` also stays. It is not compensating for a\ncodec asymmetry: it clears query params belonging to blades that a\ntwo-level URL could not restore, which is a consequence of the intended\ndesign and would need a different change to remove.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `navigateToMainRoute.test.ts`: 5 cases covering the root route,\nits alias, the no-root case, and both navigate paths.\n- `core/blade-navigation` +\n`core/composables/useBladeNavigationAdapter`: 15 files, 238 tests\npassing.\n- Full framework suite: 409 files, 3935 tests passing.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`, eslint `--max-warnings=0`, prettier: all exit 0.\n- Regression proof: with `navigateToMainRoute.ts` reverted to\n`origin/main` and the tests kept, 4 of 5 fail. Most of those fail\nbecause `resolveMainRoute` did not exist yet, so the behavioural\ndifference is shown separately by the table above rather than resting on\nthat count alone.","tree":{"sha":"ccafb201972b6586299f732d204f92e9c4777241","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/ccafb201972b6586299f732d204f92e9c4777241"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f","verification":{"payload":"tree ccafb201972b6586299f732d204f92e9c4777241\nparent 68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788184525 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788184525 +0300\n\nrefactor(blade-navigation): one root-route resolver, and correct a stale comment (VM-1762) (#331)\n\nFixes VM-1762. The ticket asked for one URL codec because encode and\ndecode were said to disagree about depth. They do not — see \"What the\nticket got wrong\" below. What was actually left in this area is a\nduplicated root-route resolver, one copy of which still carries a bug\nthe other had fixed, and a comment describing a hazard that no longer\nexists.\n\n## The bug\n\n`navigateToMainRoute` and the legacy adapter''s `goToRoot` each resolved\nthe root route independently. VM-1777 fixed the adapter''s copy; this one\nwas missed:\n\n```ts\nconst mainRoute = routes.find((r) => r.meta?.root);\nconst mainRouteAlias = routes.find((r) => r.aliasOf?.path === mainRoute?.path) ?? mainRoute;\n```\n\nWith no route declaring `meta.root`, `mainRoute` is `undefined`, so the\nsecond predicate reads `r.aliasOf?.path === undefined` — true for every\nroute without an alias. `find` returns whatever was registered first.\n\nDemonstrated against a two-route table with no `meta.root`:\n\n```\nold resolves to: Login\nnew resolves to: undefined\n```\n\nThis is not a corner nobody reaches: `navigateToMainRoute` is the\nfallback `restoreFromUrl` uses when a URL names an unknown workspace, is\nnot a workspace, or is not permitted — the path a user takes by\nfollowing a stale or mistyped link. In an app without a `meta.root`\nroute, \"go home\" sent them to the login screen.\n\nBoth call sites now use `resolveMainRoute`, which returns `undefined`\nwhen there is no root route instead of guessing.\n\n## The stale comment\n\n`restoreFromUrl`''s idempotency check said it was there because \"the\nblade was opened programmatically and syncUrlPush just triggered the\nguard\". That hazard is gone: the stack owns URL sync and\n`plugin-v2.ts:111` wraps the whole guard in\n`RouterUrlSink.suppressWhile`, so a restore cannot re-enter through the\nstack''s own writes.\n\nThe check still earns its place for a different reason, which the\ncomment now states: the guard runs on every catch-all navigation,\nincluding a back/forward onto a URL the stack already matches, and\n`openBlade` — unlike `openWorkspace` — has no same-target no-op, so\nremoving it would stack a duplicate child.\n\n## What the ticket got wrong\n\nChecked against the source before starting; each of these is now false:\n\n| Ticket | Reality |\n| --- | --- |\n| \"`buildUrlFromStack` serialises a stack of any depth\" | It emits the\nworkspace plus the last visible child, and nothing deeper — symmetric\nwith `parseBladeUrl` |\n| \"two different `getTenantPrefix` implementations with different\nsemantics\" | One, `urlSync.ts:121`. The second went with the URL-sync\nconsolidation |\n| \"restoring from a URL stops at two levels\" — framed as a defect | Two\nblades in the URL is the intended design, confirmed with the product\nowner |\n\nBecause the depth mismatch does not exist, there is nothing for a new\ncodec to reconcile, and `ParsedBladeUrl` / `parseBladeUrl` are left\nalone rather than wrapped in deprecated shims.\n\nThe `onMounted`/`nextTick` reconcile pass in\n`vc-blade-navigation-new.vue` also stays. It is not compensating for a\ncodec asymmetry: it clears query params belonging to blades that a\ntwo-level URL could not restore, which is a consequence of the intended\ndesign and would need a different change to remove.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `navigateToMainRoute.test.ts`: 5 cases covering the root route,\nits alias, the no-root case, and both navigate paths.\n- `core/blade-navigation` +\n`core/composables/useBladeNavigationAdapter`: 15 files, 238 tests\npassing.\n- Full framework suite: 409 files, 3935 tests passing.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`, eslint `--max-warnings=0`, prettier: all exit 0.\n- Regression proof: with `navigateToMainRoute.ts` reverted to\n`origin/main` and the tests kept, 4 of 5 fail. Most of those fail\nbecause `resolveMainRoute` did not exist yet, so the behavioural\ndifference is shown separately by the table above rather than resting on\nthat count alone.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlYfNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvycQAHKCZGLlcvWAg8lD6hToj2w7\nDrDvzMaPb9iX9jiz0xA+dYwEULJ9mOAOVgIzS7CkqpxHNLNZFXD3IpvoxYpo+25Q\n+VEoeZ4QVdFxZ9a553Qu7uct331Acbk2hQxT6mr/Ur3u9rhiN7CxciQuciT52+8a\nr8tqJEr9lcWFjhz1jwPMPAMeAeTYy7r0sdhW398nYUWp54EZNEycjVSHzuXW3LMV\ndchlb7GwiNrZJncQBOCbstNm2VhXfd3kJIyF+MIhfjVj9BZr0NP3pyFp/TKKbrRN\n6A5F2+Dd6giiuDyHXfZqSAWg7co/x+goYXt8vJuQt3/dsNG30cL4kILdlenth2/c\nucr9kBL8Yr4ugYErXtKIzkp4nU1WwY3IRa+UBvSXVVyoksJS0uT53bF7ci4+iq9K\nxXbwJVO9oMo0x2mDX3DxsHbKq/3doueD7XICYEvC09TokCjmxUZE2DhzEn/dgldV\nZ4gpSNPlap6pEVUdcKYgmxRfoXbYslZInRHqmza1t+xQzERJwMkqVQRauDp6abam\no2/g+j/0Hkvy2yluhvVmtQ26M48HkJvZzSYFTADKISjX9hneHQGzpAJiJ+MRnfM2\nOQO4p17a6Zk4ahL64I6CW0NVxM/y5JGBn2lz7U1SKALJcoiZcsmdcXtGjVMnRpQX\nR6S9QgeF08a7cmxpJ87+\n=aote\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T13:55:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGU5YTNmMWQ0MjUxMTMyZTAyMTRkYjRhNGM0NzdlMTI4ZDQ4NTkxMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b","sha":"68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b"}],"sha":"e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e9a3f1d4251132e0214db4a4c477e128d485912f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:52:30Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:52:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): sign out on a 401 that arrives outside /api/ (#333)\n\nReported from a real session on vcmp-dev: an old tab whose cookie had\nexpired stayed logged in. Data would not load, the blade showed \"An\nunexpected server error occurred\", and the console filled with 401s\nevery five seconds. No redirect to login ever happened.\n\n## Why nothing signed the user out\n\nTwo independent gaps had to line up, and they did.\n\n**The 401 was never looked at.** The interceptor scopes itself to the\nplatform API before it inspects anything:\n\n```ts\n// core/interceptors/index.ts\nreturn url.origin === window.location.origin && url.pathname.startsWith(\"/api/\");\n```\n\nSignalR negotiates against `/pushNotificationHub`, which is not under\n`/api/`, so that request returned unexamined. It was the only\nunambiguous \"the cookie is dead\" signal in the whole log.\n\n**The request that was looked at said 403.**\n`/api/vcmp/seller/products/search` answered 403, which `sessionDied`\ndeliberately excludes — authenticated-but-unauthorized is not an expired\nsession, and signing someone out because one endpoint refused them would\nbe wrong. That exclusion stays.\n\nSo the request that said 401 was never inspected, and the request that\nwas inspected never said 401.\n\n## Change\n\n**Split the two scopes.** Timeout, offline refusal and slow-request\ntracking are hardening for the platform API and stay scoped to `/api/`.\nSession death is not: the cookie is global, so any same-origin 401 now\ncounts. The 401 still reaches the caller unchanged.\n\nThe login-page heuristic stays API-only. An endpoint under `/api/` has\nno business returning a rendered login page; a non-API same-origin\nrequest may serve HTML perfectly legitimately, and failing those would\nbreak ordinary page loads.\n\n**Stop the retry loop.** `signalR/index.ts` retried a rejected negotiate\nevery 5 seconds unconditionally — the five-second cadence visible in the\nreport. Without a fresh cookie that answer cannot change, so it now\ngives up on a 401 and backs off exponentially (5s → 60s cap) on anything\nelse. A pending retry is cancelled on sign-out instead of outliving it,\nand a fresh sign-in restarts from the base delay.\n\n## Tests\n\nNeither path had a single test — `grep ''signal\\|abort''\ninterceptors.test.ts` returned nothing, and `signalR/` had no test file\nat all. Thirteen added.\n\nInterceptor: the hub 401 signs out; it acts once across the hub''s\nretries; the 401 still reaches the caller; a cross-origin 401 is left\nalone; no timeout is applied to hub requests; a redirected HTML response\noutside `/api/` is not treated as expiry; nothing happens while signed\nout.\n\nSignalR: gives up on 401; retries other failures; backs off rather than\nusing a fixed interval; caps the backoff; cancels a pending retry on\nsign-out; restarts from the base delay after a fresh sign-in.\n\n## Localisation\n\nThe messages this code shows the user were hardcoded English in a\nframework the apps localise. They now live in the locale files as\n`CORE.ERRORS.SESSION_EXPIRED`, `CORE.ERRORS.NETWORK_UNAVAILABLE` and\n`CORE.ERRORS.REQUEST_TIMED_OUT` (en and de), read through\n`i18n.global.t` — the same non-component access `useTheme`, `modularity`\nand the validation rules already use, so no new pattern and no layer\nviolation.\n\nThe demo-mode warning in the same file is deliberately left as it is: it\nfires only under `__DEMO_MODE__` and tells a developer to add\n`APP_PLATFORM_URL` to their `.env`. That is setup instruction for\nwhoever is building the app, not end-user copy.\n\n## Verification\n\nReverting only the two source files, keeping the tests, fails exactly\nseven:\n\n```\n× signs out on a 401 from the notification hub\n× acts once when the hub retries against the same dead session\n× stops retrying once negotiate answers 401\n× backs off instead of retrying at a fixed interval\n× caps the backoff\n× does not reconnect after sign-out cancels a pending retry\n× starts a fresh sign-in from the base delay\n```\n\nFull framework suite: 409 files, 3943 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`,\neslint `--max-warnings=0`, prettier, `check:locales`, `check:layers` and\nthe circular-dependency check all exit 0.\n\n## Worth raising with the backend\n\nThe same dead session produced a 401 on the hub and a 403 on the API. If\na session has expired the API should answer 401; answering 403 makes it\nimpossible for a client to distinguish expiry from a genuine permission\ndenial on one resource. This PR closes the reported symptom regardless —\nthe hub 401 arrives within seconds of load — but the API''s status code\nlooks wrong and is worth a separate ticket.\n\n## Note\n\nCI on this repo is currently failing for every PR before any step runs —\njobs finish in about two seconds with no runner assigned. The results\nabove are local.","tree":{"sha":"977ba7be814865368be651038ab17c9277517e24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/977ba7be814865368be651038ab17c9277517e24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b","verification":{"payload":"tree 977ba7be814865368be651038ab17c9277517e24\nparent 6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1788184350 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788184350 +0300\n\nfix(auth): sign out on a 401 that arrives outside /api/ (#333)\n\nReported from a real session on vcmp-dev: an old tab whose cookie had\nexpired stayed logged in. Data would not load, the blade showed \"An\nunexpected server error occurred\", and the console filled with 401s\nevery five seconds. No redirect to login ever happened.\n\n## Why nothing signed the user out\n\nTwo independent gaps had to line up, and they did.\n\n**The 401 was never looked at.** The interceptor scopes itself to the\nplatform API before it inspects anything:\n\n```ts\n// core/interceptors/index.ts\nreturn url.origin === window.location.origin && url.pathname.startsWith(\"/api/\");\n```\n\nSignalR negotiates against `/pushNotificationHub`, which is not under\n`/api/`, so that request returned unexamined. It was the only\nunambiguous \"the cookie is dead\" signal in the whole log.\n\n**The request that was looked at said 403.**\n`/api/vcmp/seller/products/search` answered 403, which `sessionDied`\ndeliberately excludes — authenticated-but-unauthorized is not an expired\nsession, and signing someone out because one endpoint refused them would\nbe wrong. That exclusion stays.\n\nSo the request that said 401 was never inspected, and the request that\nwas inspected never said 401.\n\n## Change\n\n**Split the two scopes.** Timeout, offline refusal and slow-request\ntracking are hardening for the platform API and stay scoped to `/api/`.\nSession death is not: the cookie is global, so any same-origin 401 now\ncounts. The 401 still reaches the caller unchanged.\n\nThe login-page heuristic stays API-only. An endpoint under `/api/` has\nno business returning a rendered login page; a non-API same-origin\nrequest may serve HTML perfectly legitimately, and failing those would\nbreak ordinary page loads.\n\n**Stop the retry loop.** `signalR/index.ts` retried a rejected negotiate\nevery 5 seconds unconditionally — the five-second cadence visible in the\nreport. Without a fresh cookie that answer cannot change, so it now\ngives up on a 401 and backs off exponentially (5s → 60s cap) on anything\nelse. A pending retry is cancelled on sign-out instead of outliving it,\nand a fresh sign-in restarts from the base delay.\n\n## Tests\n\nNeither path had a single test — `grep ''signal\\|abort''\ninterceptors.test.ts` returned nothing, and `signalR/` had no test file\nat all. Thirteen added.\n\nInterceptor: the hub 401 signs out; it acts once across the hub''s\nretries; the 401 still reaches the caller; a cross-origin 401 is left\nalone; no timeout is applied to hub requests; a redirected HTML response\noutside `/api/` is not treated as expiry; nothing happens while signed\nout.\n\nSignalR: gives up on 401; retries other failures; backs off rather than\nusing a fixed interval; caps the backoff; cancels a pending retry on\nsign-out; restarts from the base delay after a fresh sign-in.\n\n## Localisation\n\nThe messages this code shows the user were hardcoded English in a\nframework the apps localise. They now live in the locale files as\n`CORE.ERRORS.SESSION_EXPIRED`, `CORE.ERRORS.NETWORK_UNAVAILABLE` and\n`CORE.ERRORS.REQUEST_TIMED_OUT` (en and de), read through\n`i18n.global.t` — the same non-component access `useTheme`, `modularity`\nand the validation rules already use, so no new pattern and no layer\nviolation.\n\nThe demo-mode warning in the same file is deliberately left as it is: it\nfires only under `__DEMO_MODE__` and tells a developer to add\n`APP_PLATFORM_URL` to their `.env`. That is setup instruction for\nwhoever is building the app, not end-user copy.\n\n## Verification\n\nReverting only the two source files, keeping the tests, fails exactly\nseven:\n\n```\n× signs out on a 401 from the notification hub\n× acts once when the hub retries against the same dead session\n× stops retrying once negotiate answers 401\n× backs off instead of retrying at a fixed interval\n× caps the backoff\n× does not reconnect after sign-out cancels a pending retry\n× starts a fresh sign-in from the base delay\n```\n\nFull framework suite: 409 files, 3943 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`,\neslint `--max-warnings=0`, prettier, `check:locales`, `check:layers` and\nthe circular-dependency check all exit 0.\n\n## Worth raising with the backend\n\nThe same dead session produced a 401 on the hub and a 403 on the API. If\na session has expired the API should answer 401; answering 403 makes it\nimpossible for a client to distinguish expiry from a genuine permission\ndenial on one resource. This PR closes the reported symptom regardless —\nthe hub 401 arrives within seconds of load — but the API''s status code\nlooks wrong and is worth a separate ticket.\n\n## Note\n\nCI on this repo is currently failing for every PR before any step runs —\njobs finish in about two seconds with no runner assigned. The results\nabove are local.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlYceCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVhQQAJVEg7YnfPiSg/+ay1wvLZto\npTRFBoQXN6PH8jMpWAWXguv6NlkoopIAs4wrOgM966YWDb6X2Sy64rYjQKm+v2zf\nKsVwQJaps64RmoTKDWeXgli/Fz49R34cDwWWUThYqhqg1jUPerHgC3qRfy7Csdd8\nH4tb5nIhPKcxJOVAXMKFP1muptKlgfk4r3NZ2OL+vM9pwtZRT1SgacQjCuvnvwzM\n+BAATjx2VixP6tMEhSesj5CSPR8GuVMnHy00r36pX/trvS1gp35ZxYuINMpYYLP1\nff8lGDlUYCHweq9n07pNPH/XNeTiYawJwi5H3/rtONpJ27xasDS2kbsOeteW2gMw\nRj2Z82JmaRXPi8KkdA0bvkXA16i4AYU0VDEG0vrnBnvWxbWiX3DZjvxgY3Nb4VTg\nP5tXsSV97ZOOswnqgIHuyzT56hvT3P5rGEDvYLOGC9xw5KAMYnUULhI//qw1xsYb\npjDPrnH4DiHawtcJoqReAcQnAJurGkPLBX/qvwvMeKm/nl8jjFqhwaFMSe/UHdgd\nKla0kmt/ixx4EKEtpAU78hbTwAKMW6xa0r2YriykPmgj8VIIITWlsLdgFMXJefmz\nIdFnOAvP0uJzBlktSrb3RjoSmxnkW2LW9lZkOrjEMa2qxfocG7i5pLYalWXPvyg5\nKTN5Mw4zGNivn2uI2pSK\n=jVh/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T13:52:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDY4MjUwYWI0MjliZWRmMjhjMGEzZDAyMDk4ZmE4OTIwN2EwZDcwN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e","sha":"6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e"}],"sha":"68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/68250ab429bedf28c0a3d02098fa89207a0d707b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:01:31Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:01:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-blade): show an overlay once content exists, skeletons only before it (#330)\n\nBlade skeletons have been unreliable since v2.5.0: they disappear a\nsecond into a load, and never appear at all on a blade whose entity\nchanges in place.\n\n## Cause\n\n`c0b07007d` (#301) replaced `computed(() => Boolean(props.loading))`\nwith a latch that treats \"not loading\" as \"content has rendered\". Its\ngoal was right — a save raises `loading`, every field swaps itself for a\nskeleton, the focused control is unmounted and focus falls to `<body>`,\nso the next Tab restarts at the top of the document (VCST-5670, WCAG\n2.4.3 Focus Order).\n\nThe problem is what happens after the latch closes: **nothing is shown\nat all**. And it closes early, because a blade composes `loading` from\nseveral independent requests — `ProductDetailsBase.vue:4` ORs five — and\na real gap between two of them looks exactly like the load finishing:\n\n```\nt=49ms    loading=true   skeleton=true\nt=1258ms  loading=true   skeleton=FALSE   latch closed, nothing shown\nt=2480ms  loading=false  skeleton=false\n```\n\n1.2 seconds of loading with no indication of any kind.\n\n## Change\n\n`VcDataTable` has had the right shape all along\n(`VcDataTable.vue:667-680`): a skeleton for content that has never\nrendered, and a plain overlay for every load after that. The blade now\ndoes the same.\n\n```ts\nconst showSkeleton    = computed(() => Boolean(props.loading) && !hasLoadedOnce.value);\nconst showBusyOverlay = computed(() => Boolean(props.loading) &&  hasLoadedOnce.value);\n```\n\nThe second state is what makes the latch safe. An early close now costs\nan overlay instead of skeletons, rather than costing all feedback — so\nthe exact failure above becomes invisible to the user. It also covers\nthe save case by construction: once content exists the blade overlays\nrather than replaces, nothing is unmounted, and focus stays where the\nuser left it.\n\nThe overlay blocks the pointer and does nothing else. Measured directly\nin the browser: removing a node, `display:none` and `inert` on an\nancestor all move `document.activeElement` to `<body>` identically.\nCovering is the only technique that preserves focus and the element''s\nvalue.\n\n`hasLoadedOnce` resets when `bladeDescriptor.param` changes, so a\ndifferent entity in the same blade instance gets its skeleton back.\n\n`useBladeSkeleton` and its test are deleted.\n\n## Measured, after\n\nLoad:\n\n```\nt=62ms    loading=true   skeleton=true   overlay=false\nt=890ms   loading=true   skeleton=false  overlay=true\nt=1890ms  loading=false  skeleton=false  overlay=false\n\nframes with loading and no indication: 0\n```\n\nSave, with the caret in a text field:\n\n```\nbefore   focus INPUT.vc-input__input  overlay=false  aria-busy=absent\nt=25ms   focus INPUT.vc-input__input  overlay=true   aria-busy=true\nt=925ms  focus DIV.vc-blade           overlay=false  aria-busy=absent\n\nskeleton rendered during the save: never\nfocus held in the input while loading: yes\nfocus reached <body>: never\n```\n\n## Scope\n\nNo new props. No changes in consuming apps. `Props.loading` keeps its\nmeaning; the blade just stops throwing away the \"already have content\"\ncase.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ui/components/organisms/vc-blade`: 16 files, 163 tests passing.\n- Full framework suite: 408 files, 3930 tests passing.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`, eslint `--max-warnings=0`, prettier, stylelint:\nall exit 0.\n- Live checks above ran against vendor-portal linked to this source with\nyarn `portal:`.\n\n## Known gaps, for the reviewer\n\n- **No test covers the overlay or the latch reset.** Verified in the\nbrowser only. A mount test asserting skeleton-then-overlay, the reset on\n`param` change, and that a focused input keeps focus is the obvious next\ncommit.\n- **Teleported layers.** Select and dropdown panels render through\n`<teleport>` (`SelectDropdown.vue:2`), so they sit outside the blade\nroot and outside the overlay. A dropdown open during a save is not\ncovered.\n- **`VcSkeleton` announces itself** — `role=\"status\"` plus an sr-only\nlabel (`vc-skeleton.vue:9`). About twenty render at once during a load,\nso a screen reader hears twenty status messages where one would do.\nPre-existing, worth its own fix.\n\n## Follow-ups, not here\n\n`_internal/BladeContentSkeleton.vue` has had no production importer\nsince `89d328529` (April 2026), which removed it from the template and\ndistributed the skeleton decision to ~24 controls through\n`BladeLoadingKey`.\n\nPR #329 removed `getCurrentInstance` from `useBladeSkeleton`; this PR\ndeletes that file, so #329 should be closed as superseded.","tree":{"sha":"0299f006c31ffaa70a180e449ee44115b1e6536d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/0299f006c31ffaa70a180e449ee44115b1e6536d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e","verification":{"payload":"tree 0299f006c31ffaa70a180e449ee44115b1e6536d\nparent e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787929291 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787929291 +0300\n\nfix(vc-blade): show an overlay once content exists, skeletons only before it (#330)\n\nBlade skeletons have been unreliable since v2.5.0: they disappear a\nsecond into a load, and never appear at all on a blade whose entity\nchanges in place.\n\n## Cause\n\n`c0b07007d` (#301) replaced `computed(() => Boolean(props.loading))`\nwith a latch that treats \"not loading\" as \"content has rendered\". Its\ngoal was right — a save raises `loading`, every field swaps itself for a\nskeleton, the focused control is unmounted and focus falls to `<body>`,\nso the next Tab restarts at the top of the document (VCST-5670, WCAG\n2.4.3 Focus Order).\n\nThe problem is what happens after the latch closes: **nothing is shown\nat all**. And it closes early, because a blade composes `loading` from\nseveral independent requests — `ProductDetailsBase.vue:4` ORs five — and\na real gap between two of them looks exactly like the load finishing:\n\n```\nt=49ms    loading=true   skeleton=true\nt=1258ms  loading=true   skeleton=FALSE   latch closed, nothing shown\nt=2480ms  loading=false  skeleton=false\n```\n\n1.2 seconds of loading with no indication of any kind.\n\n## Change\n\n`VcDataTable` has had the right shape all along\n(`VcDataTable.vue:667-680`): a skeleton for content that has never\nrendered, and a plain overlay for every load after that. The blade now\ndoes the same.\n\n```ts\nconst showSkeleton    = computed(() => Boolean(props.loading) && !hasLoadedOnce.value);\nconst showBusyOverlay = computed(() => Boolean(props.loading) &&  hasLoadedOnce.value);\n```\n\nThe second state is what makes the latch safe. An early close now costs\nan overlay instead of skeletons, rather than costing all feedback — so\nthe exact failure above becomes invisible to the user. It also covers\nthe save case by construction: once content exists the blade overlays\nrather than replaces, nothing is unmounted, and focus stays where the\nuser left it.\n\nThe overlay blocks the pointer and does nothing else. Measured directly\nin the browser: removing a node, `display:none` and `inert` on an\nancestor all move `document.activeElement` to `<body>` identically.\nCovering is the only technique that preserves focus and the element''s\nvalue.\n\n`hasLoadedOnce` resets when `bladeDescriptor.param` changes, so a\ndifferent entity in the same blade instance gets its skeleton back.\n\n`useBladeSkeleton` and its test are deleted.\n\n## Measured, after\n\nLoad:\n\n```\nt=62ms    loading=true   skeleton=true   overlay=false\nt=890ms   loading=true   skeleton=false  overlay=true\nt=1890ms  loading=false  skeleton=false  overlay=false\n\nframes with loading and no indication: 0\n```\n\nSave, with the caret in a text field:\n\n```\nbefore   focus INPUT.vc-input__input  overlay=false  aria-busy=absent\nt=25ms   focus INPUT.vc-input__input  overlay=true   aria-busy=true\nt=925ms  focus DIV.vc-blade           overlay=false  aria-busy=absent\n\nskeleton rendered during the save: never\nfocus held in the input while loading: yes\nfocus reached <body>: never\n```\n\n## Scope\n\nNo new props. No changes in consuming apps. `Props.loading` keeps its\nmeaning; the blade just stops throwing away the \"already have content\"\ncase.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ui/components/organisms/vc-blade`: 16 files, 163 tests passing.\n- Full framework suite: 408 files, 3930 tests passing.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`, eslint `--max-warnings=0`, prettier, stylelint:\nall exit 0.\n- Live checks above ran against vendor-portal linked to this source with\nyarn `portal:`.\n\n## Known gaps, for the reviewer\n\n- **No test covers the overlay or the latch reset.** Verified in the\nbrowser only. A mount test asserting skeleton-then-overlay, the reset on\n`param` change, and that a focused input keeps focus is the obvious next\ncommit.\n- **Teleported layers.** Select and dropdown panels render through\n`<teleport>` (`SelectDropdown.vue:2`), so they sit outside the blade\nroot and outside the overlay. A dropdown open during a save is not\ncovered.\n- **`VcSkeleton` announces itself** — `role=\"status\"` plus an sr-only\nlabel (`vc-skeleton.vue:9`). About twenty render at once during a load,\nso a screen reader hears twenty status messages where one would do.\nPre-existing, worth its own fix.\n\n## Follow-ups, not here\n\n`_internal/BladeContentSkeleton.vue` has had no production importer\nsince `89d328529` (April 2026), which removed it from the template and\ndistributed the skeleton decision to ~24 controls through\n`BladeLoadingKey`.\n\nPR #329 removed `getCurrentInstance` from `useBladeSkeleton`; this PR\ndeletes that file, so #329 should be closed as superseded.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkaLLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiZQQAD5VHEN4iiVbml3zuCTPO387\n6OwGiBuvE8PCzxJWG0xXNo4oS7bjCmzoSu3vB0PnfMUQw0HjNTQUjEaK/I7a9IAh\n/s1YdRLJtqFFziHz+g92eY2zikjyIkPHArNI3gIZHBQDRdyWMunEfzSsHsz2ibmm\nd8vVG0uWLCfITbJp3WNBAJtPbluk2OFua0aEy0d5UP9nMtXpsInNXhu0YDWOriJH\n8HSzYpE6Y6zjpIBjJXRCnPeh1+GTMyfUr4WxniL0z9pwYt2fSbgnG+xtT2JoxKIu\nAwyFw4PWS+YJnwcnCOUpj3IIJbNWjywCXlwCZXWROpe4PuqMT0rsiyhqvKOf6wpy\nzKOxLvjb8+c0SImZrfVp8ecsrE070MuyRHiLLlILAPHqXwYuatR3iQKaQhLSvte5\nCxAz2h/I6jxg90wxekNn4CMidNrrZnDxeHhqFklAr+q4zYbiJgpn7cmJ9hwHQZ9t\nHvfRsG7jnCQyNnq+9k1FSAYc8coV8FlWqsJkzpKIb2mzx2yX+Krwt+0GnN9vLYxf\nhupKUXhgJyaquwg8qegvTUur3UUAGzsfCjWQPbZDzTLkGecW/gbWCyLWXVNv4BCH\ntdSZ8+ZzVDcPve03rVBvSNxhmuMa6rmubPIb/0KVLOHFyvBzwa7AcV4BpMuf1uJh\nAOsvWsKzEV+akQvXtHLb\n=mkUv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T15:01:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDZiZGM0MmI1NzQ4NWQ4NTdjYjFkOWMzOTQ4OWU2ZjJiYjBhY2IxNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9","sha":"e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9"}],"sha":"6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/6bdc42b57485d857cb1d9c39489e6f2bb0acb16e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T12:10:01Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T12:10:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-blade): arm the skeleton latch after mount so the first load shows skeletons (#328)\n\nBlade skeletons have not rendered since v2.5.0. Reported from the\ndeployed dev environment and reproduced locally.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`c0b07007d` — \"fix(a11y): stop blade loading from unmounting the control\nthat has focus (#301)\", 2026-08-18, first tag `v2.5.0` — replaced\n\n```ts\nconst showSkeleton = computed(() => Boolean(props.loading));\n```\n\nwith `useBladeSkeleton(...)` in `vc-blade.vue`. That composable ends its\n`immediate: true` watcher with `if (!loading) hasRenderedContent.value =\ntrue`, and the watcher runs **synchronously during VcBlade''s setup**.\n\nAt that instant `loading` is false in every real blade, because the\nfetch starts in the **parent page''s** `onMounted` and a child completes\nsetup before the parent''s hook runs. So the latch recorded \"content has\nrendered\" before anything had been requested, and `isLoading() &&\n!hasRenderedContent` stayed false forever for that entity context —\nwhich never changes for a detail blade, so nothing ever reset it.\n\nThis is \"never renders\", not \"renders too briefly\": there is no frame in\nwhich the skeleton exists.\n\nThe value is provided as `BladeLoadingKey` and consumed by 25 components\n— every form control plus VcDataTable and VcScheduler — as well as\nBladeHeader and BladeToolbar. `VcDataTable`''s own `hasLoadedOnce` latch\nis separate and correct, which is why table skeleton rows still worked\nwhile the surrounding blade showed none.\n\n## Change\n\nArm the latch on the first post-mount flush rather than during setup:\n\n```ts\nif (getCurrentInstance()) onMounted(() => void nextTick(arm));\nelse void nextTick(arm);\n```\n\n`nextTick` is load-bearing — VcBlade''s own `onMounted` fires *before*\nthe parent page''s, so arming there lands in the same wrong place. The\n`getCurrentInstance()` branch keeps the composable usable outside a\ncomponent, where `onMounted` would only warn and never fire.\n\nThe accessibility guarantee from #301 is untouched: once content has\nrendered, a save or delete does not swap the focused control for a\nskeleton (WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order). That case is asserted directly.\n\n## Why the old tests passed\n\nThey called the composable as a plain function, so they could not\nobserve the parent/child mount ordering that causes the bug — and one of\nthem pinned the broken behaviour as intended:\n\n```ts\nit(\"never shows the skeleton for a blade that starts with its content ready\", async () => {\n  const loading = ref(false);          // the exact production sequence\n  const skeleton = useBladeSkeleton(() => loading.value);\n  loading.value = true;\n  await nextTick();\n  expect(skeleton.value).toBe(false);  // asserts the defect\n});\n```\n\nThe false assumption is in the name: in a real blade `loading === false`\nat setup means the fetch has not started, not that content is ready. The\nother four began from `loading = ref(true)`, a state no blade is ever in\nat setup.\n\nThe tests now mount a child inside a parent that raises `loading` in its\nown `onMounted` — the shape that reproduces the ordering. Cases covered:\nfirst load shows the skeleton; it clears when loading finishes; a later\nsave does **not** bring it back; an in-place entity switch re-arms it; a\nblade already loading at mount still shows it; and the non-component\npath still latches.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vc-blade` suite: 17 files, 169 tests passing.\n- Full framework suite: 409 files, 3936 tests passing.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit` clean; eslint `--max-warnings=0` and prettier clean\non both changed files.\n- Regression proof: reverting only `useBladeSkeleton.ts` to\n`origin/main` while keeping the tests fails **exactly one** — \"shows the\nskeleton on the first load, when the parent starts fetching after mount\"\n(1 failed / 5 passed). That single test is the one that mounts a real\nparent; every other assertion holds either way, which is precisely why\nthe regression shipped.\n\nNot verified: a live run in vendor-portal. The mechanism is reproduced\nin a test that fails without the fix, which is the stronger check, but a\nvisual confirmation on a product or offer blade is worth doing before\nrelease.\n\n## Follow-up, not in this PR\n\n`_internal/BladeContentSkeleton.vue` has had no production importer\nsince `89d328529` (April 2026), which removed `<BladeContentSkeleton\nv-if=\"showSkeleton\" />` from the template. Only its own test and a stub\nin `vc-blade.a11y.test.ts` reference it. It is a deletion candidate, but\nremoving it here would mix an unrelated cleanup into a regression fix.","tree":{"sha":"62ad8efb495c7c7466ff7b2a630d8c737857d2f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/62ad8efb495c7c7466ff7b2a630d8c737857d2f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9","verification":{"payload":"tree 62ad8efb495c7c7466ff7b2a630d8c737857d2f5\nparent bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787832601 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787832601 +0300\n\nfix(vc-blade): arm the skeleton latch after mount so the first load shows skeletons (#328)\n\nBlade skeletons have not rendered since v2.5.0. Reported from the\ndeployed dev environment and reproduced locally.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`c0b07007d` — \"fix(a11y): stop blade loading from unmounting the control\nthat has focus (#301)\", 2026-08-18, first tag `v2.5.0` — replaced\n\n```ts\nconst showSkeleton = computed(() => Boolean(props.loading));\n```\n\nwith `useBladeSkeleton(...)` in `vc-blade.vue`. That composable ends its\n`immediate: true` watcher with `if (!loading) hasRenderedContent.value =\ntrue`, and the watcher runs **synchronously during VcBlade''s setup**.\n\nAt that instant `loading` is false in every real blade, because the\nfetch starts in the **parent page''s** `onMounted` and a child completes\nsetup before the parent''s hook runs. So the latch recorded \"content has\nrendered\" before anything had been requested, and `isLoading() &&\n!hasRenderedContent` stayed false forever for that entity context —\nwhich never changes for a detail blade, so nothing ever reset it.\n\nThis is \"never renders\", not \"renders too briefly\": there is no frame in\nwhich the skeleton exists.\n\nThe value is provided as `BladeLoadingKey` and consumed by 25 components\n— every form control plus VcDataTable and VcScheduler — as well as\nBladeHeader and BladeToolbar. `VcDataTable`''s own `hasLoadedOnce` latch\nis separate and correct, which is why table skeleton rows still worked\nwhile the surrounding blade showed none.\n\n## Change\n\nArm the latch on the first post-mount flush rather than during setup:\n\n```ts\nif (getCurrentInstance()) onMounted(() => void nextTick(arm));\nelse void nextTick(arm);\n```\n\n`nextTick` is load-bearing — VcBlade''s own `onMounted` fires *before*\nthe parent page''s, so arming there lands in the same wrong place. The\n`getCurrentInstance()` branch keeps the composable usable outside a\ncomponent, where `onMounted` would only warn and never fire.\n\nThe accessibility guarantee from #301 is untouched: once content has\nrendered, a save or delete does not swap the focused control for a\nskeleton (WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order). That case is asserted directly.\n\n## Why the old tests passed\n\nThey called the composable as a plain function, so they could not\nobserve the parent/child mount ordering that causes the bug — and one of\nthem pinned the broken behaviour as intended:\n\n```ts\nit(\"never shows the skeleton for a blade that starts with its content ready\", async () => {\n  const loading = ref(false);          // the exact production sequence\n  const skeleton = useBladeSkeleton(() => loading.value);\n  loading.value = true;\n  await nextTick();\n  expect(skeleton.value).toBe(false);  // asserts the defect\n});\n```\n\nThe false assumption is in the name: in a real blade `loading === false`\nat setup means the fetch has not started, not that content is ready. The\nother four began from `loading = ref(true)`, a state no blade is ever in\nat setup.\n\nThe tests now mount a child inside a parent that raises `loading` in its\nown `onMounted` — the shape that reproduces the ordering. Cases covered:\nfirst load shows the skeleton; it clears when loading finishes; a later\nsave does **not** bring it back; an in-place entity switch re-arms it; a\nblade already loading at mount still shows it; and the non-component\npath still latches.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vc-blade` suite: 17 files, 169 tests passing.\n- Full framework suite: 409 files, 3936 tests passing.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit` clean; eslint `--max-warnings=0` and prettier clean\non both changed files.\n- Regression proof: reverting only `useBladeSkeleton.ts` to\n`origin/main` while keeping the tests fails **exactly one** — \"shows the\nskeleton on the first load, when the parent starts fetching after mount\"\n(1 failed / 5 passed). That single test is the one that mounts a real\nparent; every other assertion holds either way, which is precisely why\nthe regression shipped.\n\nNot verified: a live run in vendor-portal. The mechanism is reproduced\nin a test that fails without the fix, which is the stronger check, but a\nvisual confirmation on a product or offer blade is worth doing before\nrelease.\n\n## Follow-up, not in this PR\n\n`_internal/BladeContentSkeleton.vue` has had no production importer\nsince `89d328529` (April 2026), which removed `<BladeContentSkeleton\nv-if=\"showSkeleton\" />` from the template. Only its own test and a stub\nin `vc-blade.a11y.test.ts` reference it. It is a deletion candidate, but\nremoving it here would mix an unrelated cleanup into a regression fix.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkCkZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtXUQAE/bR8a4UeDTwk8zVlq1tRb5\nILZizIoDtqBixdyJEFoHdEe72wxUXSkIOjNy3ArKJLOAc1WudOSlW/8qI9IVtnsE\ny/1gf0jQ+siY8opdH0XlEwhhU3leGjX6jaBxrFeVLpjwM/YzqCoY+v0Vkoh7iG5P\nGUpcdxuUlGo5Bx2bD6yZE52VNLLGrZ1NbMnKs/4CfWr+9kWd39FP4tkUzaTfFLNJ\n9li7xtCBASUAh1XZvuDjeKyiXsWSpfq6eHq35rcdABfwSpPBlBlls7bULMaLemVy\nkq8CdqNuK/BuSlRDsPLGirhkzhNIZC+S7tScyarbvhLn+SObMDh8wXAMAbpSmkGR\nqrkvW6vuUgKWSgl/zLMfHeNRN5CqWnsMum+EMuMkQi9FacTb6/e7TykLQWeB8mfN\nC7sQj2efMiS+0hXK8yGkEDC+nr5KN6aith6wrBqkbJD6SaPLSoadKAIFObWikKNM\nyZxtaM0rm7sGFsSBNRRVetRhCfls5zKeRRsgzLUjk0/zGSiZ0z8VKAPCXUM8NUyR\nM1tPeo2SIsL85oVtyUwqW6yaJlO2gE8ST7cuI2gCa2cdcUG+m+sfNHasOXApXqbU\n+d21OzWA0c8wo8LmyTTPiAJVT134uHU9vlw79X574kzHHEx23t3JQN9ou/WxPZeA\nNpGqRossDnzUhjWBsTqW\n=glvS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T12:10:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGU5ZTI5YWEwZTY0ZWM0NTdiOTAzMDQwZGRjYjNlZWIwZTczZTkwZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa","sha":"bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa"}],"sha":"e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/e9e29aa0e64ec457b903040ddcb3eeb0e73e90f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T11:39:15Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T11:39:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(blade-navigation): derive breadcrumbs from the blade stack (VM-1763) (#326)\n\n## Why\n\nThe breadcrumb trail is a pure function of the blade stack, but it was\nrouted through the `useBreadcrumbs` store. `vc-blade-navigation-new.vue`\ncleared and rebuilt that store on every stack change (a `watchDebounced`\nover `blades`), so none of the store''s push/remove/trim/dedup protocol\never actually ran — and the rebuild carried two defects:\n\n- crumbs were keyed by **visible index**, so getting back to the real\nblade needed an off-by-one bridge (`visibleBlades[visibleIndex + 1]`);\n- crumb text came from `descriptor.name` (the registered component\nname), ignoring the title a blade sets through `setBladeTitle`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `IBladeStack` gains `trailFor(bladeId): Breadcrumbs[]` — the visible\nancestors of that blade, outermost first, each with the **real blade\nid** and `title ?? name`. It reads `blades`, so it stays reactive when\ncalled inside a computed. A crumb''s `clickHandler` calls\n`closeChildren(id)`, which closes everything opened after that blade\n(and syncs the URL, as any close does).\n- `VcBladeSlot` reads the trail from the stack. Its `breadcrumbs` prop\nis kept and marked `@deprecated`; it is ignored whenever the stack\nprovides a trail.\n- The rebuild watcher, the index bridge, and the `useBreadcrumbs` wiring\nare gone from `vc-blade-navigation-new.vue`. The mobile back button gets\nits trail from `trailFor` too.\n- `useBreadcrumbs` is **untouched** — apps use it standalone, outside\nblades.\n\nThe change to `IBladeStack` is purely additive: `trailFor` is a new\nmember, no existing member changed shape.\n\n## Breadcrumb titles that change\n\nNo story or unit-test snapshot contains a stack-derived breadcrumb\ntitle, so nothing in the test suite changes text. The stack-derived\ntrail only exists at runtime inside `VcBladeNavigation`, and the\nexisting tests around it either mock `useBreadcrumbs` with an empty list\nor assert structure, not labels. The `VcBreadcrumbs` stories drive\n`useBreadcrumbs` directly with their own literal titles and are\nunaffected.\n\nAt runtime, every crumb whose blade sets a title now shows that title\ninstead of the component name. In this repo''s own blades:\n\n| Blade | Crumb before | Crumb after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `AssetsManager` | `AssetsManager` | its header title —\n`options.title`, else the localized `ASSETS_MANAGER.TITLE` |\n| `AssetsDetails` | `AssetsDetails` | `options.asset.name` (falls back\nto `AssetsDetails` when the asset has no name) |\n\nConsuming apps see the same substitution for every blade that passes a\n`title` to `VcBlade` (in the vendor portal: `Order #1042` in place of\n`OrderDetails`, and so on). A blade that sets no title keeps showing its\ncomponent name, exactly as before.\n\nTwo further behaviour differences, both fixes rather than regressions:\n\n- a blade hidden by `coverCurrentBlade` no longer contributes a crumb\n*and* no longer shifts the trail — the old code built crumbs from\nvisible blades but sliced them by the index in the full stack, so a\nhidden blade made the trail one crumb too long;\n- crumbs carry real blade ids, so a click resolves to a blade directly\ninstead of through the `+1` index arithmetic.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `useBladeStack.test.ts` — new `trailFor` block: ancestor order with\nreal ids, `setBladeTitle` winning over `name`, empty trail for the\nworkspace and unknown ids, a blade hidden by `coverCurrentBlade` being\nskipped, and a crumb click closing everything after it.\n- `vc-blade-slot.test.ts` — the slot takes the stack trail and ignores\nthe deprecated prop.\n\nTargeted suite `core/blade-navigation` +\n`shell/_internal/blade-navigation`: 18 files, 223 tests passing. Full\nframework suite: 409 files, 3935 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`,\neslint (`--max-warnings=0`), prettier, `check-layer-violations`, and a\n`madge --circular` pass over both touched trees are clean.\n\nRegression proof: with only the four source files reverted to\n`origin/main` and the tests kept, the targeted suite fails 6 / passes\n217 — the five `trailFor` tests error with `stack.trailFor is not a\nfunction`, and the slot test fails on the deprecated prop leaking\nthrough (`expected [{ id: ''0'', title: ''TestBlade'' }] to deeply equal [{\nid: ''blade-0'', title: ''All orders'' }]`). Restored, it is 223 / 223\nagain.","tree":{"sha":"26d887f5fa46b4ac5315529dc66e09603f6427df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/26d887f5fa46b4ac5315529dc66e09603f6427df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa","verification":{"payload":"tree 26d887f5fa46b4ac5315529dc66e09603f6427df\nparent 883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787830755 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787830755 +0300\n\nrefactor(blade-navigation): derive breadcrumbs from the blade stack (VM-1763) (#326)\n\n## Why\n\nThe breadcrumb trail is a pure function of the blade stack, but it was\nrouted through the `useBreadcrumbs` store. `vc-blade-navigation-new.vue`\ncleared and rebuilt that store on every stack change (a `watchDebounced`\nover `blades`), so none of the store''s push/remove/trim/dedup protocol\never actually ran — and the rebuild carried two defects:\n\n- crumbs were keyed by **visible index**, so getting back to the real\nblade needed an off-by-one bridge (`visibleBlades[visibleIndex + 1]`);\n- crumb text came from `descriptor.name` (the registered component\nname), ignoring the title a blade sets through `setBladeTitle`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `IBladeStack` gains `trailFor(bladeId): Breadcrumbs[]` — the visible\nancestors of that blade, outermost first, each with the **real blade\nid** and `title ?? name`. It reads `blades`, so it stays reactive when\ncalled inside a computed. A crumb''s `clickHandler` calls\n`closeChildren(id)`, which closes everything opened after that blade\n(and syncs the URL, as any close does).\n- `VcBladeSlot` reads the trail from the stack. Its `breadcrumbs` prop\nis kept and marked `@deprecated`; it is ignored whenever the stack\nprovides a trail.\n- The rebuild watcher, the index bridge, and the `useBreadcrumbs` wiring\nare gone from `vc-blade-navigation-new.vue`. The mobile back button gets\nits trail from `trailFor` too.\n- `useBreadcrumbs` is **untouched** — apps use it standalone, outside\nblades.\n\nThe change to `IBladeStack` is purely additive: `trailFor` is a new\nmember, no existing member changed shape.\n\n## Breadcrumb titles that change\n\nNo story or unit-test snapshot contains a stack-derived breadcrumb\ntitle, so nothing in the test suite changes text. The stack-derived\ntrail only exists at runtime inside `VcBladeNavigation`, and the\nexisting tests around it either mock `useBreadcrumbs` with an empty list\nor assert structure, not labels. The `VcBreadcrumbs` stories drive\n`useBreadcrumbs` directly with their own literal titles and are\nunaffected.\n\nAt runtime, every crumb whose blade sets a title now shows that title\ninstead of the component name. In this repo''s own blades:\n\n| Blade | Crumb before | Crumb after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `AssetsManager` | `AssetsManager` | its header title —\n`options.title`, else the localized `ASSETS_MANAGER.TITLE` |\n| `AssetsDetails` | `AssetsDetails` | `options.asset.name` (falls back\nto `AssetsDetails` when the asset has no name) |\n\nConsuming apps see the same substitution for every blade that passes a\n`title` to `VcBlade` (in the vendor portal: `Order #1042` in place of\n`OrderDetails`, and so on). A blade that sets no title keeps showing its\ncomponent name, exactly as before.\n\nTwo further behaviour differences, both fixes rather than regressions:\n\n- a blade hidden by `coverCurrentBlade` no longer contributes a crumb\n*and* no longer shifts the trail — the old code built crumbs from\nvisible blades but sliced them by the index in the full stack, so a\nhidden blade made the trail one crumb too long;\n- crumbs carry real blade ids, so a click resolves to a blade directly\ninstead of through the `+1` index arithmetic.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `useBladeStack.test.ts` — new `trailFor` block: ancestor order with\nreal ids, `setBladeTitle` winning over `name`, empty trail for the\nworkspace and unknown ids, a blade hidden by `coverCurrentBlade` being\nskipped, and a crumb click closing everything after it.\n- `vc-blade-slot.test.ts` — the slot takes the stack trail and ignores\nthe deprecated prop.\n\nTargeted suite `core/blade-navigation` +\n`shell/_internal/blade-navigation`: 18 files, 223 tests passing. Full\nframework suite: 409 files, 3935 tests passing. `vue-tsc --noEmit`,\neslint (`--max-warnings=0`), prettier, `check-layer-violations`, and a\n`madge --circular` pass over both touched trees are clean.\n\nRegression proof: with only the four source files reverted to\n`origin/main` and the tests kept, the targeted suite fails 6 / passes\n217 — the five `trailFor` tests error with `stack.trailFor is not a\nfunction`, and the slot test fails on the deprecated prop leaking\nthrough (`expected [{ id: ''0'', title: ''TestBlade'' }] to deeply equal [{\nid: ''blade-0'', title: ''All orders'' }]`). Restored, it is 223 / 223\nagain.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkCHjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANY8QAG9Ejzf3tihYKAcU4zDQog4P\nnQeQyK7YwEFTPh2aR+4/OSeUvfUs8tajnGusjn/yEZxG2Uw8YMeJZmPT0arhgVLO\nD5eRsIzFaTTT+FpXUXpQxWHjvkf+UUjhkxOKAF4/W/Fuzf4GiPWtrHrpntH1nFcK\nl7EE6tn6WBGxKFrhqzaPKYELaJqwuuen4eM1/6QfKe8DlTiOkm5mBdOC64Sk75cJ\njAwSQNkQs511gGMHOW5pKkRnf2JtjFSgRRuHwDv5+v9jmaQrzvWrHX0kfqwx0Z1/\n5HuZzBWWmErPz/y+5n79TTEzUmLzbbvmALng9+cojQy0A9jN08whsYnz0/ihSnP4\n/wlUFEgVZiKOLyhqWrFM9J/95HiC+AkHD7GrITwTZwj8qGgE5JWff51dy0RANycT\nr8kyGMHxKfcM7QutthZhBCdcXF3SoSnjp4G44Tp9/9Ng2OGoSuJr3FtP6vV92kdM\n2d2Msohh031jzGmeEph3224bGJorZDR8Qcclih8xOA+B74pMPhgZgKUNEV1pmsTK\nnACx9+kEJwxzhP96N7y5/df4jrr+aRHYFGy8Ez3RIHv56a0mJR27BEkfWQB4efsK\nnVIiyRAocduoHi14+qR3ANEWgTxQSmzB1g7/uLiyVCyzLghzvwkrblAJS3svlLpW\nI2lGog8Ui7Ic1PsPkQw8\n=k1zl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T11:39:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGJiYzlkYjY1YWZmODRmYzRlMTA3NGZhYzM2ZTY2ZDBiODc0Njk5ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79","sha":"883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79"}],"sha":"bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/bbc9db65aff84fc4e1074fac36e66d0b874699fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T11:27:04Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T11:27:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vite-config): decide the framework source alias from resolution, not layout (#327)\n\n## Problem\n\n`getApplicationConfiguration` aliased `@vc-shell/framework` — and every\nsubpath — to the checked-out source whenever\n`../../framework/package.json` existed:\n\n```ts\nconst isMonorepo = fs.existsSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), \"./../../framework/package.json\"));\n```\n\nApps under `apps/` are **not** workspaces. They are linked to the local\npackages with yarn `portal:` by `scripts/setup-app.ts`, and an app\nliving inside the repo may deliberately depend on a published build — a\nPR preview package, or a specific release being bisected. The layout\ntest cannot tell those two situations apart, and it always answered\n\"source\".\n\nThe alias could not be overridden from the app either.\n`configs/vite-config/src/index.ts:52` merges as `[...baseAlias,\n...optionAlias]`, and `@rollup/plugin-alias` takes the first match, so\nanything an app adds is dead weight behind the built-in entries.\n\nThe result is silent and expensive: `apps/vendor-portal/package.json`\npinned `@vc-shell/framework` to a PR preview build, `yarn install`\nfetched it, `require.resolve` from the app pointed at it — and the\nbrowser still loaded `@fs/…/vc-shell/framework/index.ts`. A whole\ndebugging session ran against the working tree while appearing to test\nthe pinned package, and reinstalling `node_modules` changed nothing\nbecause the package was never consulted.\n\n## Change\n\nDecide from what the app''s own dependency actually resolves to:\n\n```ts\nconst resolved = path.dirname(fs.realpathSync(require.resolve(\"@vc-shell/framework/package.json\")));\nreturn resolved === fs.realpathSync(frameworkSourceDir);\n```\n\n`portal:` produces a symlink into the source tree, so a linked app\nresolves to `<repo>/framework` and keeps the aliases; an app pinning a\npublished version resolves into its own `node_modules` and gets the\npackage. `./package.json` is exported by both the source and the\npublished manifests, so the probe works either way.\n\n`APP_FRAMEWORK_SOURCE=true|false` forces either side. If resolution\nthrows — dependencies not installed yet — the old layout answer stands,\nso nobody loses their aliases mid-setup.\n\n## Verification\n\nDetection, exercised directly against the five cases:\n\n| Case | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| vendor-portal pinning `2.5.0-pr326.40af648` | `false` — package wins |\n| `portal:` symlink to `<repo>/framework` (simulated) | `true` — source\nwins |\n| `APP_FRAMEWORK_SOURCE=true` | `true` |\n| `APP_FRAMEWORK_SOURCE=false` | `false` |\n| app outside the monorepo | `false` |\n\nEnd to end, loading the rebuilt config with the portal as cwd:\n\n- default: `alias entries: (none)` — vite resolves the pinned package\nnormally\n- `APP_FRAMEWORK_SOURCE=true`: all 14 alias entries present, unchanged\nfrom today\n\nNot verified: a live dev-server run. Vite reads its config once at\nstartup and does not watch the config''s transitive dependencies, so\npicking this up needs a restart — I did not restart the running server.\nThe config object itself was inspected after a real rebuild, which is\nthe same object vite would consume.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo behaviour change for a `portal:`-linked app, which is how every app\nin `apps/` is set up by `scripts/setup-app.ts`. The only apps that\nchange are those pinning a published version, and for them the current\nbehaviour is the bug.\n\nvendor-portal imports only public entry points — `@vc-shell/framework`,\n`/ui`, `/ai-agent`, `/extensions` — and no internal aliases (`@core`,\n`@shell`, `@ui`): zero matches. All four are in the published package''s\n`exports`, so dropping the aliases resolves cleanly.","tree":{"sha":"e1a68bede499b5ad708f57bc7da61cbf55cb476d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/e1a68bede499b5ad708f57bc7da61cbf55cb476d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79","verification":{"payload":"tree e1a68bede499b5ad708f57bc7da61cbf55cb476d\nparent dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787830024 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787830024 +0300\n\nfix(vite-config): decide the framework source alias from resolution, not layout (#327)\n\n## Problem\n\n`getApplicationConfiguration` aliased `@vc-shell/framework` — and every\nsubpath — to the checked-out source whenever\n`../../framework/package.json` existed:\n\n```ts\nconst isMonorepo = fs.existsSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), \"./../../framework/package.json\"));\n```\n\nApps under `apps/` are **not** workspaces. They are linked to the local\npackages with yarn `portal:` by `scripts/setup-app.ts`, and an app\nliving inside the repo may deliberately depend on a published build — a\nPR preview package, or a specific release being bisected. The layout\ntest cannot tell those two situations apart, and it always answered\n\"source\".\n\nThe alias could not be overridden from the app either.\n`configs/vite-config/src/index.ts:52` merges as `[...baseAlias,\n...optionAlias]`, and `@rollup/plugin-alias` takes the first match, so\nanything an app adds is dead weight behind the built-in entries.\n\nThe result is silent and expensive: `apps/vendor-portal/package.json`\npinned `@vc-shell/framework` to a PR preview build, `yarn install`\nfetched it, `require.resolve` from the app pointed at it — and the\nbrowser still loaded `@fs/…/vc-shell/framework/index.ts`. A whole\ndebugging session ran against the working tree while appearing to test\nthe pinned package, and reinstalling `node_modules` changed nothing\nbecause the package was never consulted.\n\n## Change\n\nDecide from what the app''s own dependency actually resolves to:\n\n```ts\nconst resolved = path.dirname(fs.realpathSync(require.resolve(\"@vc-shell/framework/package.json\")));\nreturn resolved === fs.realpathSync(frameworkSourceDir);\n```\n\n`portal:` produces a symlink into the source tree, so a linked app\nresolves to `<repo>/framework` and keeps the aliases; an app pinning a\npublished version resolves into its own `node_modules` and gets the\npackage. `./package.json` is exported by both the source and the\npublished manifests, so the probe works either way.\n\n`APP_FRAMEWORK_SOURCE=true|false` forces either side. If resolution\nthrows — dependencies not installed yet — the old layout answer stands,\nso nobody loses their aliases mid-setup.\n\n## Verification\n\nDetection, exercised directly against the five cases:\n\n| Case | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| vendor-portal pinning `2.5.0-pr326.40af648` | `false` — package wins |\n| `portal:` symlink to `<repo>/framework` (simulated) | `true` — source\nwins |\n| `APP_FRAMEWORK_SOURCE=true` | `true` |\n| `APP_FRAMEWORK_SOURCE=false` | `false` |\n| app outside the monorepo | `false` |\n\nEnd to end, loading the rebuilt config with the portal as cwd:\n\n- default: `alias entries: (none)` — vite resolves the pinned package\nnormally\n- `APP_FRAMEWORK_SOURCE=true`: all 14 alias entries present, unchanged\nfrom today\n\nNot verified: a live dev-server run. Vite reads its config once at\nstartup and does not watch the config''s transitive dependencies, so\npicking this up needs a restart — I did not restart the running server.\nThe config object itself was inspected after a real rebuild, which is\nthe same object vite would consume.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo behaviour change for a `portal:`-linked app, which is how every app\nin `apps/` is set up by `scripts/setup-app.ts`. The only apps that\nchange are those pinning a published version, and for them the current\nbehaviour is the bug.\n\nvendor-portal imports only public entry points — `@vc-shell/framework`,\n`/ui`, `/ai-agent`, `/extensions` — and no internal aliases (`@core`,\n`@shell`, `@ui`): zero matches. All four are in the published package''s\n`exports`, so dropping the aliases resolves cleanly.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkB8ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ40QAElDsFnfEmTxv6W8mkRxfdvB\nQkHQ6us89Kmtp5WZcgA08XvMcInVZx/XTwRmMlSUe2eWiy42GQ3xwDAofZ4yEgI5\nAl6wgPdP1+tUvfTewHG3gKg9VIf3OPOSSWoCWlFSCIaaShSHQ5jg/yFzoyUUS9ts\niAb0CQBjiHJOtR0IFWfvB86LbLfagC5zsaM99QmnE1+83vvW4KPxvDRwM2yWcje+\n/8mInOAuf8tJNbNwODTks4lQyvMD9Hae3Er/E4hldSSGRLTpd5/7EOO7EyD/nxn6\nNoUvz3cBrgG6jA8oo3lIL/3UAA8ZGM9QUXmQCT08NuKcmR/ITwKmEPdZeHQVDMXL\nAmZDIU21G937PxEMX0DKpbwlbbk9i9UHgZeFJQW35ag/51YLNsY4bJy9QIZnm7GW\nsGJP2fay0IEe3OcYK1gtUAiUAgTaOW/G19Ihq8lWXsp+r8kzMKdkKv7z7dNEa57B\nr+ijVmNrPdAzitKb+Xkfg5EkcJsXEcQIr+RXn0SXOu53QdpxGyUU10foY7hgiQfT\nljM8D7AYIInjll7yoZAg/3YrzW7vucPRK12eYhFvdsqzUyvlxTIbF28mtib6QRy8\n0iXinZw5ZzbDnAQ70JjdfcrA1a1d+RR7ju856nGFer7R6J25FWXxmDGIbw4ppJAS\nizQ9EJlXU9mWjsYdhByt\n=BJSw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T11:27:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDg4M2NhNGJkZjM2MjQ3NzUwNzY1OTYwMGFlOTA4M2I3YTE5OTliNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1","sha":"dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1"}],"sha":"883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/883ca4bdf362477507659600ae9083b7a1999b79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:35:45Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:35:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(blade-navigation): sync the URL only after a mutation that happened (VM-1784) (#325)\n\nVM-1777 established the rule that the blade stack writes the URL only\nafter a mutation that actually took place, but applied it to\n`openWorkspace` and `closeBlade` only, because the other sites were not\non that ticket''s list. The file then stated two different rules with\nnothing to explain the difference.\n\n## The named defect\n\nWhen a child blade''s `onBeforeClose` guard prevents the open,\n`_openBlade` returns without touching the stack, yet `openBlade` still\ncalled `_syncOpened(\"push\")`. The sink resolves the location from the\nstack, so what got pushed was the *existing* blade''s URL — history grew\na duplicate entry for a navigation that did not happen. Press Back and\nnothing moves.\n\n## The rule, applied uniformly\n\n`_openBlade`, `_replaceCurrentBlade`, `_coverCurrentBlade` and\n`_closeChildren` now report whether they mutated the stack, exactly as\n`_openWorkspace` already did, and their public wrappers gate the sync on\nthat.\n\n| Sync site | No-op path | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `openWorkspace` | same workspace re-opened; permission denied |\nalready gated on `_openWorkspace`''s boolean (VM-1777) | unchanged |\n| `openBlade` | a child''s `onBeforeClose` guard prevents the open |\nalways pushed — pushed the existing blade''s location | pushes only when\na blade was opened |\n| `replaceCurrentBlade` | a guard on a blade after the active one\nprevents the replace | always replaced | replaces only when the blade\nwas replaced |\n| `coverCurrentBlade` | a guard on a blade after the active one prevents\nthe cover | always pushed | pushes only when the covering blade was\nopened |\n| `closeBlade` | unknown id; the workspace blade, which cannot be\nclosed; a guard prevents the close | already gated on `CloseOutcome ===\n\"closed\"` (VM-1777) | unchanged |\n| `closeChildren` | unknown parent id; parent has no children; a guard\nprevents the close | **always** replaced, on all three | replaces only\nwhen children were actually closed |\n\nPaths that throw (`Blade ''<name>'' not found in registry`, no active\nblade, parent not in the stack) never reached the sync before and still\ndo not.\n\n`closeChildren` was the widest of these: it rewrote the URL for an\nunknown parent id and for a parent with no children at all — the two\ncases in which nothing anywhere had changed.\n\nOn `replaceCurrentBlade` and `coverCurrentBlade` the guard branch is\ncurrently unreachable through the public API: the only writer of\n`visible: false` is `_coverCurrentBlade`, which always appends a visible\ndescriptor straight after it, so the last blade in the stack is always\nvisible and `activeBlade` is always the last element — `bladesToClose`\nthere is always empty. The branch exists in the code, so it is gated for\nthe sake of one rule instead of two, but it is not a live defect today\nand there is no test for it, because a test would have to fabricate the\nstate through `_restoreStack`.\n\n## Public API\n\nNo public signature changed. `openBlade`, `replaceCurrentBlade`,\n`coverCurrentBlade` and `closeChildren` all keep `Promise<void>`;\n`closeBlade` keeps its `prevented` boolean. The richer result lives on\nthe private `_`-prefixed function, as `CloseOutcome` and\n`_openWorkspace`''s boolean already did.\n`framework/core/blade-navigation/types/index.ts` is untouched.\n\n## Tests\n\n`useBladeStack.url.test.ts`: the case that pinned the old behaviour,\n`\"openBlade still pushes when a child guard prevented the open\"`, is\nflipped to `\"openBlade records nothing when a child guard prevented the\nopen\"`, and the comment that argued for the push is gone. The three\n`closeChildren` cases that asserted an unconditional `replace` are\nrewritten as no-op cases and moved into the \"actions that changed\nnothing leave the history alone\" block. One case added: after the guard\nstops preventing, the same open pushes exactly once.\n\n- Targeted (`core/blade-navigation`,\n`core/composables/useBladeNavigationAdapter`): 14 files, 228 tests, all\npass.\n- Full framework suite: 409 files, 3929 tests, all pass.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`, `eslint --max-warnings=0` and `prettier --check`\non both changed files: clean.\n\nRegression proof — with the test changes kept and `useBladeStack.ts`\nreverted to `origin/main`, `useBladeStack.url.test.ts` fails **5 of\n25**: the flipped `openBlade` case, the new push-once case, and the\nthree `closeChildren` cases. With the fix, 25 of 25 pass.","tree":{"sha":"9705f3b535d338bbdaf459dfa1947b138f3c669a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/9705f3b535d338bbdaf459dfa1947b138f3c669a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1","verification":{"payload":"tree 9705f3b535d338bbdaf459dfa1947b138f3c669a\nparent 3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787823345 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787823345 +0300\n\nfix(blade-navigation): sync the URL only after a mutation that happened (VM-1784) (#325)\n\nVM-1777 established the rule that the blade stack writes the URL only\nafter a mutation that actually took place, but applied it to\n`openWorkspace` and `closeBlade` only, because the other sites were not\non that ticket''s list. The file then stated two different rules with\nnothing to explain the difference.\n\n## The named defect\n\nWhen a child blade''s `onBeforeClose` guard prevents the open,\n`_openBlade` returns without touching the stack, yet `openBlade` still\ncalled `_syncOpened(\"push\")`. The sink resolves the location from the\nstack, so what got pushed was the *existing* blade''s URL — history grew\na duplicate entry for a navigation that did not happen. Press Back and\nnothing moves.\n\n## The rule, applied uniformly\n\n`_openBlade`, `_replaceCurrentBlade`, `_coverCurrentBlade` and\n`_closeChildren` now report whether they mutated the stack, exactly as\n`_openWorkspace` already did, and their public wrappers gate the sync on\nthat.\n\n| Sync site | No-op path | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `openWorkspace` | same workspace re-opened; permission denied |\nalready gated on `_openWorkspace`''s boolean (VM-1777) | unchanged |\n| `openBlade` | a child''s `onBeforeClose` guard prevents the open |\nalways pushed — pushed the existing blade''s location | pushes only when\na blade was opened |\n| `replaceCurrentBlade` | a guard on a blade after the active one\nprevents the replace | always replaced | replaces only when the blade\nwas replaced |\n| `coverCurrentBlade` | a guard on a blade after the active one prevents\nthe cover | always pushed | pushes only when the covering blade was\nopened |\n| `closeBlade` | unknown id; the workspace blade, which cannot be\nclosed; a guard prevents the close | already gated on `CloseOutcome ===\n\"closed\"` (VM-1777) | unchanged |\n| `closeChildren` | unknown parent id; parent has no children; a guard\nprevents the close | **always** replaced, on all three | replaces only\nwhen children were actually closed |\n\nPaths that throw (`Blade ''<name>'' not found in registry`, no active\nblade, parent not in the stack) never reached the sync before and still\ndo not.\n\n`closeChildren` was the widest of these: it rewrote the URL for an\nunknown parent id and for a parent with no children at all — the two\ncases in which nothing anywhere had changed.\n\nOn `replaceCurrentBlade` and `coverCurrentBlade` the guard branch is\ncurrently unreachable through the public API: the only writer of\n`visible: false` is `_coverCurrentBlade`, which always appends a visible\ndescriptor straight after it, so the last blade in the stack is always\nvisible and `activeBlade` is always the last element — `bladesToClose`\nthere is always empty. The branch exists in the code, so it is gated for\nthe sake of one rule instead of two, but it is not a live defect today\nand there is no test for it, because a test would have to fabricate the\nstate through `_restoreStack`.\n\n## Public API\n\nNo public signature changed. `openBlade`, `replaceCurrentBlade`,\n`coverCurrentBlade` and `closeChildren` all keep `Promise<void>`;\n`closeBlade` keeps its `prevented` boolean. The richer result lives on\nthe private `_`-prefixed function, as `CloseOutcome` and\n`_openWorkspace`''s boolean already did.\n`framework/core/blade-navigation/types/index.ts` is untouched.\n\n## Tests\n\n`useBladeStack.url.test.ts`: the case that pinned the old behaviour,\n`\"openBlade still pushes when a child guard prevented the open\"`, is\nflipped to `\"openBlade records nothing when a child guard prevented the\nopen\"`, and the comment that argued for the push is gone. The three\n`closeChildren` cases that asserted an unconditional `replace` are\nrewritten as no-op cases and moved into the \"actions that changed\nnothing leave the history alone\" block. One case added: after the guard\nstops preventing, the same open pushes exactly once.\n\n- Targeted (`core/blade-navigation`,\n`core/composables/useBladeNavigationAdapter`): 14 files, 228 tests, all\npass.\n- Full framework suite: 409 files, 3929 tests, all pass.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`, `eslint --max-warnings=0` and `prettier --check`\non both changed files: clean.\n\nRegression proof — with the test changes kept and `useBladeStack.ts`\nreverted to `origin/main`, `useBladeStack.url.test.ts` fails **5 of\n25**: the flipped `openBlade` case, the new push-once case, and the\nthree `closeChildren` cases. With the fix, 25 of 25 pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkATxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhUEQAFgATENEoyBF/xVV+35PSCq7\nK4ZL4YM+4+ssOVxZ5IkMCAClSOOW1YJ77RuxQxVOkARNvSdZop1Ue9BAbQQHRG+/\nTcEQpx9Cotp9dZfBvS7f1NiOsNVccSmaHthH41Pt4CoijuJ8aPtlpYVgr0t724Jd\nIcFG73rn7lQ9Y802DGEcRJ9hC7nV6Q25Xu3Hx75MHZMlzRSC4XVKoTGtxKzdMz8O\nyJmAL6uGaQmGIVAl9kFLoLruwNToSCs/eIk/ajaT/w0uERLMcjyE1j9IBS4kFvcq\nzatnsdlHkFwd0qTKudUQFEEn/J6F6u6wXFPIq/wTGhNGdiNL2EPltQD9AEYeCFyB\ne18nfGcd/qWL63LCOSm/kD709ufyiH9e9XpwFPEgCOibwt77JVjbb+XFtsqwBh9N\n5sT/znyUYQepmgcvGDwjbJg5XcAtNOSo43oOFw+0Z3lOwDCXVE2hS21ZviVSO+Hf\nsNVilrEesof8t49lmff/MrYQwCkfd/FZtloQFxJK0XaYcmIpGWApuUToJ11hOTCC\nqmM8usFmthjntamn4pUTF7vi461ri9UqkBhE2xhwmlYKlcan73XE0VjP/D6c3Wib\nhn5buh74oe0YtSQiIWe1DtNjxSen49J+IrCILKTVTKm+niMcuqFEdqR8C86vYbON\nmKVzpl8kaM9DG4yJ8DOw\n=im4d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T09:35:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGRmYzdiYzEyMTE5MTJiZjA5MjFlMDYwNzViMGM5NzFlOGIxYmI4ZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda","sha":"3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda"}],"sha":"dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/dfc7bc1211912bf0921e06075b0c971e8b1bb8f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:35:18Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:35:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: always run the required jobs and gate on one aggregate check (#324)\n\nTwo defects in how branch protection is wired to CI. Both come from the\nsame cause: protection points at individual jobs that live inside a\npath-filtered workflow.\n\n## Problem 1 — a PR touching only certain files wedges forever\n\n`ci.yml` carried a top-level `paths:` filter on both triggers. It\nproduces `static-checks` and `test`, which the `main` ruleset requires.\nA workflow filtered out by `paths` does not run, so those checks never\nreport — and a required check that never reports does not let the PR\nmerge without CI, it leaves it waiting indefinitely.\n\n**52 tracked files matched none of the old patterns.** Among them:\n\n```\n.storybook/decorators.ts, .storybook/preview.ts, .storybook/advanced-docgen.mjs\nvitest.config.ts, vitest.config.storybook.ts\nscripts/*.ts\ncommitlint.config.ts, .release-it.cjs, .editorconfig, .madgerc\n.husky/pre-commit, .husky/commit-msg\n.github/CODEOWNERS\n.gitattributes\n```\n\nA PR editing only `.storybook/preview.ts` — which is where the axe rule\nconfiguration lives — could not be merged at all.\n\n**Fix:** the filter is gone. CI now runs on every pull request, and on\npushes to `main` and `dev`. The cost is CI on doc-only PRs; the previous\nPR removed the duplicate `feat/**` push trigger, so the total run count\nis roughly where it was.\n\n## Problem 2 — the job that actually executes story code gates nothing\n\nThe ruleset requires `static-checks`, `test` and `lint`. It does **not**\nrequire `storybook-tests`, and by its own comment that job is \"the only\ngate that executes story code — typecheck excludes `*.stories.ts`,\nESLint sees nothing wrong in an unimported identifier, and\nstorybook-build only compiles\". It is also the only job running axe. So\na change that breaks stories or introduces accessibility regressions\ncould merge with everything green that the ruleset looks at.\n\n**Fix:** a new `ci-gate` job.\n\n```yaml\nci-gate:\n  if: always()\n  needs: [static-checks, test, storybook-tests, storybook-build]\n```\n\nIt fails unless every job it needs either succeeded or was skipped, and\nbecause of `if: always()` it reports on every event rather than\nvanishing when a dependency fails. A skipped job counts as a pass\ndeliberately: `storybook-build` is pull-request only, and all four skip\non a `release:` commit.\n\nPointing protection at one aggregate rather than at each job also means\nadding, renaming or splitting a job stops being a ruleset change. The\ntrade-off is that the `needs` list is now load-bearing — a job dropped\nfrom it silently stops gating — which the comment in the file says out\nloud.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The workflow parses, and the parsed structure is what it should be:\njobs `static-checks, test, storybook, storybook-tests, storybook-build,\nci-gate`; triggers `workflow_dispatch, pull_request, push`; `ci-gate`\nwith `if: always()` and the four `needs`.\n- `prettier --check` on the file passes.\n- `actionlint` was **not** run — it is not installed in this\nenvironment.\n- The gate''s shell logic was exercised directly against every outcome\ncombination:\n\n| `needs` results | gate |\n|---|---|\n| all success | PASS |\n| push, `storybook-build` skipped | PASS |\n| `release:` commit, all four skipped | PASS |\n| `test` failure | FAIL — `test=failure` |\n| `storybook-tests` failure | FAIL — `storybook-tests=failure` |\n| `static-checks` cancelled | FAIL — `static-checks=cancelled` |\n\nThe fifth row is the point of the change: today that combination merges.\n\n## Follow-up, not in this PR\n\nThis PR does not change the ruleset, so `static-checks` and `test` stay\nthe required contexts and `ci-gate` is advisory until someone switches\nit. Once `ci-gate` has reported on `main`, the required set should\nbecome `ci-gate` plus `pr-title`, and `static-checks`, `test` and `lint`\nshould come off it.\n\nThat also unblocks renaming the two jobs currently both named `lint` —\n`pr-title.yml` validates the PR title, `docs-lint.yml` runs `docs-sync\nlint` and is itself path-filtered, and both report into one required\ncontext. Renaming them while `lint` is required would wedge every open\nPR, so the ruleset change has to come first. `docs-lint` must never be\nmade required in its present form for the same reason as problem 1.","tree":{"sha":"6f4c48c35cfa9e6c10b0620a1c6d08233b823122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/6f4c48c35cfa9e6c10b0620a1c6d08233b823122"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f4c48c35cfa9e6c10b0620a1c6d08233b823122\nparent 7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787819718 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787819718 +0300\n\nci: always run the required jobs and gate on one aggregate check (#324)\n\nTwo defects in how branch protection is wired to CI. Both come from the\nsame cause: protection points at individual jobs that live inside a\npath-filtered workflow.\n\n## Problem 1 — a PR touching only certain files wedges forever\n\n`ci.yml` carried a top-level `paths:` filter on both triggers. It\nproduces `static-checks` and `test`, which the `main` ruleset requires.\nA workflow filtered out by `paths` does not run, so those checks never\nreport — and a required check that never reports does not let the PR\nmerge without CI, it leaves it waiting indefinitely.\n\n**52 tracked files matched none of the old patterns.** Among them:\n\n```\n.storybook/decorators.ts, .storybook/preview.ts, .storybook/advanced-docgen.mjs\nvitest.config.ts, vitest.config.storybook.ts\nscripts/*.ts\ncommitlint.config.ts, .release-it.cjs, .editorconfig, .madgerc\n.husky/pre-commit, .husky/commit-msg\n.github/CODEOWNERS\n.gitattributes\n```\n\nA PR editing only `.storybook/preview.ts` — which is where the axe rule\nconfiguration lives — could not be merged at all.\n\n**Fix:** the filter is gone. CI now runs on every pull request, and on\npushes to `main` and `dev`. The cost is CI on doc-only PRs; the previous\nPR removed the duplicate `feat/**` push trigger, so the total run count\nis roughly where it was.\n\n## Problem 2 — the job that actually executes story code gates nothing\n\nThe ruleset requires `static-checks`, `test` and `lint`. It does **not**\nrequire `storybook-tests`, and by its own comment that job is \"the only\ngate that executes story code — typecheck excludes `*.stories.ts`,\nESLint sees nothing wrong in an unimported identifier, and\nstorybook-build only compiles\". It is also the only job running axe. So\na change that breaks stories or introduces accessibility regressions\ncould merge with everything green that the ruleset looks at.\n\n**Fix:** a new `ci-gate` job.\n\n```yaml\nci-gate:\n  if: always()\n  needs: [static-checks, test, storybook-tests, storybook-build]\n```\n\nIt fails unless every job it needs either succeeded or was skipped, and\nbecause of `if: always()` it reports on every event rather than\nvanishing when a dependency fails. A skipped job counts as a pass\ndeliberately: `storybook-build` is pull-request only, and all four skip\non a `release:` commit.\n\nPointing protection at one aggregate rather than at each job also means\nadding, renaming or splitting a job stops being a ruleset change. The\ntrade-off is that the `needs` list is now load-bearing — a job dropped\nfrom it silently stops gating — which the comment in the file says out\nloud.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The workflow parses, and the parsed structure is what it should be:\njobs `static-checks, test, storybook, storybook-tests, storybook-build,\nci-gate`; triggers `workflow_dispatch, pull_request, push`; `ci-gate`\nwith `if: always()` and the four `needs`.\n- `prettier --check` on the file passes.\n- `actionlint` was **not** run — it is not installed in this\nenvironment.\n- The gate''s shell logic was exercised directly against every outcome\ncombination:\n\n| `needs` results | gate |\n|---|---|\n| all success | PASS |\n| push, `storybook-build` skipped | PASS |\n| `release:` commit, all four skipped | PASS |\n| `test` failure | FAIL — `test=failure` |\n| `storybook-tests` failure | FAIL — `storybook-tests=failure` |\n| `static-checks` cancelled | FAIL — `static-checks=cancelled` |\n\nThe fifth row is the point of the change: today that combination merges.\n\n## Follow-up, not in this PR\n\nThis PR does not change the ruleset, so `static-checks` and `test` stay\nthe required contexts and `ci-gate` is advisory until someone switches\nit. Once `ci-gate` has reported on `main`, the required set should\nbecome `ci-gate` plus `pr-title`, and `static-checks`, `test` and `lint`\nshould come off it.\n\nThat also unblocks renaming the two jobs currently both named `lint` —\n`pr-title.yml` validates the PR title, `docs-lint.yml` runs `docs-sync\nlint` and is itself path-filtered, and both report into one required\ncontext. Renaming them while `lint` is required would wedge every open\nPR, so the ruleset change has to come first. `docs-lint` must never be\nmade required in its present form for the same reason as problem 1.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj/bGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAak8QAKG4d7zPF0FnciAMAt3ixJBX\n+1KlugVzNSrcGoADvX7kfS0CJqG26y1mfBqG/Ww+Jct17JeplLmeQBrp/mV3kxZ+\nfDV6bEAXJvxOWwrQ/Ne6eW25iIIIRECxSJj0eo5fLNvgVeX+jwWELps3zRwWxRWW\njTyTFQlU6W4waBqQ9FReEwWZsRVyi2HWoaJCRNEW0N/qlXoQRW6Yi65KGJgsUui4\nZO/V+O4K2aCpdz1ilsSa7aQueNJnm0njYfvM+9B/Z52jEyPultbGY5oBzxVee/Xh\ngThB2mJoeOeJKrayl0jfYDVn+54x8hfNEUDg929Yo1RGcvFJwR09sQHWf/a8F7MQ\ndGJzxuwxdf7xR5IU2goEWcwG5UHbw5zHmrikWzVffWwKdHCHhOHETgQ1E1F3ZTSq\nV4dGrMkuptuEvEQBYguAkBA4VeHwQnDbAHl2wPzH6Bxzb5BFt+wfNkyy1ZtrXvec\nVyG5Qq9oySHBZ91TEC5jhGZtJYOR+P3iwLXAReEpJca+Ew0jD4xSGcVy8qH0GBhm\nqofLYg/bme7Aah/bcIM5PJFTWoMEcsX66eIHMtlIkE8yM6ZC88DG63tzeh2m9uDN\nLZXGr2nsuASm34NyiKU6idDxh7Xx0BWUUEwkn6uspHHKT0zKKdGVVTIPQL+BdJ/B\n+Lc05TRgoXjF88SQu+DX\n=N85X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T08:35:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDNmNTNkMmYwN2IzY2MyZjEzNjdlMDliNTdhM2U0NzFhOWE2MWViZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8","sha":"7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8"}],"sha":"3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3f53d2f07b3cc2f1367e09b57a3e471a9a61ebda"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:47:57Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:47:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: normalise line endings to LF (VM-1778) (#323)\n\nFixes VM-1778. Line endings only — no source content changes.\n\n## Why\n\n300 tracked files were stored with CRLF while everything around them was\nLF. There was no `.gitattributes`, and `.prettierrc` set `endOfLine:\n\"auto\"`, which tells Prettier to keep whatever a file already has.\nNothing normalised the endings and nothing reported the inconsistency:\n`format:check`, `lint:check` and CI all passed either way.\n\nThe cost is invisible until review. Any tool that round-trips a file as\ntext rather than bytes rewrites every line, and the change passes every\ngate. It happened twice in one day: a 15-line edit became a 267-line\ndiff, and in PR #313 a genuine `+702/−27` was reported by git as\n`+817/−142` because one test file flipped to LF. 115 phantom deletions\nmade a test-only PR look like it had rewritten existing tests. A\nreviewer who does not know to pass `--ignore-cr-at-eol` either wastes\ntime or approves a diff they did not really read.\n\n## Change\n\nThree parts:\n\n1. **`.gitattributes`** — `* text=auto eol=lf`, so text files are stored\nand checked out with LF on every platform. `eol=lf` rather than bare\n`text=auto` because a Windows checkout under `text=auto` keeps CRLF in\nthe working tree, which is exactly what the Prettier setting below would\nthen fight with. `*.png`, `*.jpg`, `*.ico` are declared `binary`;\nauto-detection already leaves them alone, and the explicit rule keeps a\nfuture `text=` rule from reaching them.\n2. **`.prettierrc`** — `endOfLine` from `\"auto\"` to `\"lf\"`, so\n`format:check` now fails on drift instead of accepting it.\n3. **`git add --renormalize .`** — 320 files, of which 300 changed from\nCRLF to LF.\n\nNothing requires CRLF in this repo: there are no `.bat`, `.cmd` or\n`.ps1` files.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Content is untouched.** `git diff --cached --ignore-cr-at-eol` over\nthe renormalisation, excluding the two config files, is **empty**. Only\nline endings changed, in every one of the 300 files.\n- **No CRLF left.** `git ls-files --eol` reports zero `w/crlf` and zero\n`i/crlf` entries; `file(1)` over all tracked files reports zero CRLF.\n- `prettier --check` over `framework`, `cli`, `configs`, `packages`: all\nmatched files use Prettier code style.\n- `vitest run` in `framework/`: **409 files passed / 409, 3928 tests\npassed / 3928**.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`: exit 0, no diagnostics.\n- `eslint --max-warnings=0` over `framework`, `cli`, `configs`,\n`packages`: exit 0.\n- **The trap itself is gone.** A scripted text-mode round-trip edit of\none comment line in `useBladeNavigationAdapter/index.ts` now produces `1\nfile changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)`. Before this change the\nsame edit rewrote the whole file.\n\n## After merging: existing clones need one command\n\n`--renormalize` rewrites the index, not the files on disk, so a clone\nthat already exists keeps CRLF in its working tree and will start\nfailing `format:check` locally. Refresh it once:\n\n```\ngit rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard\n```\n\nFresh clones and CI checkouts are unaffected — they get LF from\n`.gitattributes` directly.\n\n## Timing\n\nDeliberately landed with no other branches in flight. A renormalisation\nconflicts with every concurrent branch in every file it touches, because\ngit sees a full-file replacement rather than a targeted edit. At the\ntime of opening this PR there were no other open PRs, and the only other\nremote branches were `feat/response` (last commit 2024-04-25) and\n`feat/vc-data-table-single-load-restore` (2026-06-18), both stale with\nno PR.","tree":{"sha":"70cafa8241eed9e7318aca6953a84a7fe6f8f54e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/70cafa8241eed9e7318aca6953a84a7fe6f8f54e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 70cafa8241eed9e7318aca6953a84a7fe6f8f54e\nparent b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787770077 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787770077 +0300\n\nchore: normalise line endings to LF (VM-1778) (#323)\n\nFixes VM-1778. Line endings only — no source content changes.\n\n## Why\n\n300 tracked files were stored with CRLF while everything around them was\nLF. There was no `.gitattributes`, and `.prettierrc` set `endOfLine:\n\"auto\"`, which tells Prettier to keep whatever a file already has.\nNothing normalised the endings and nothing reported the inconsistency:\n`format:check`, `lint:check` and CI all passed either way.\n\nThe cost is invisible until review. Any tool that round-trips a file as\ntext rather than bytes rewrites every line, and the change passes every\ngate. It happened twice in one day: a 15-line edit became a 267-line\ndiff, and in PR #313 a genuine `+702/−27` was reported by git as\n`+817/−142` because one test file flipped to LF. 115 phantom deletions\nmade a test-only PR look like it had rewritten existing tests. A\nreviewer who does not know to pass `--ignore-cr-at-eol` either wastes\ntime or approves a diff they did not really read.\n\n## Change\n\nThree parts:\n\n1. **`.gitattributes`** — `* text=auto eol=lf`, so text files are stored\nand checked out with LF on every platform. `eol=lf` rather than bare\n`text=auto` because a Windows checkout under `text=auto` keeps CRLF in\nthe working tree, which is exactly what the Prettier setting below would\nthen fight with. `*.png`, `*.jpg`, `*.ico` are declared `binary`;\nauto-detection already leaves them alone, and the explicit rule keeps a\nfuture `text=` rule from reaching them.\n2. **`.prettierrc`** — `endOfLine` from `\"auto\"` to `\"lf\"`, so\n`format:check` now fails on drift instead of accepting it.\n3. **`git add --renormalize .`** — 320 files, of which 300 changed from\nCRLF to LF.\n\nNothing requires CRLF in this repo: there are no `.bat`, `.cmd` or\n`.ps1` files.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Content is untouched.** `git diff --cached --ignore-cr-at-eol` over\nthe renormalisation, excluding the two config files, is **empty**. Only\nline endings changed, in every one of the 300 files.\n- **No CRLF left.** `git ls-files --eol` reports zero `w/crlf` and zero\n`i/crlf` entries; `file(1)` over all tracked files reports zero CRLF.\n- `prettier --check` over `framework`, `cli`, `configs`, `packages`: all\nmatched files use Prettier code style.\n- `vitest run` in `framework/`: **409 files passed / 409, 3928 tests\npassed / 3928**.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`: exit 0, no diagnostics.\n- `eslint --max-warnings=0` over `framework`, `cli`, `configs`,\n`packages`: exit 0.\n- **The trap itself is gone.** A scripted text-mode round-trip edit of\none comment line in `useBladeNavigationAdapter/index.ts` now produces `1\nfile changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)`. Before this change the\nsame edit rewrote the whole file.\n\n## After merging: existing clones need one command\n\n`--renormalize` rewrites the index, not the files on disk, so a clone\nthat already exists keeps CRLF in its working tree and will start\nfailing `format:check` locally. Refresh it once:\n\n```\ngit rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard\n```\n\nFresh clones and CI checkouts are unaffected — they get LF from\n`.gitattributes` directly.\n\n## Timing\n\nDeliberately landed with no other branches in flight. A renormalisation\nconflicts with every concurrent branch in every file it touches, because\ngit sees a full-file replacement rather than a targeted edit. At the\ntime of opening this PR there were no other open PRs, and the only other\nremote branches were `feat/response` (last commit 2024-04-25) and\n`feat/vc-data-table-single-load-restore` (2026-06-18), both stale with\nno PR.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjzTdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1woQAJERtbNPHJ8zPLWvmBl5rP6N\nz0Axf6cfClQqro9Zcra/Zv0jbKLacYxe6NZnsE5sJOvjDtsxvgRUiHXomj8P3lfl\na5MSDS6k8sI3sGa3EaYDmfbRt5qJ/enzEhqviCcPsuEe/ITvce2m3BiH/zH0f9c6\ndp9dKnoijv2hklJev7vADXKsTOb0Y72sGlfujXq4n9jTjIyC0ajqP48gsqxpcpPD\nekf0ek9Jld0DGugUZDUeUe1JKAT6GWLKsnJNBIkQ6DsJQUos+TD8QwgsKr5L4bcN\nmFwu22bZa8M5lTx2J3ivX/tr1YoSn5lpwsU82UTv0YU4e/mk5xL/Qtor4XeyUBRf\ne8HowWH6h9bBK2JkYeyFnoFJhsuxqjClRqjOw56i5gJKhqbb/VUQ5unHngP4B0+J\nYjBUNTv5CZ8iVFRVJ1CqLOc9VjOMT/PRDgbX7VEoJ1HRiA/ZbxbzeyCcYPi6AryP\nXEHwuGjruJo24SqrhY8cOP8QZ2XErd/FxT0WG6rjPa4I8wDYbP8K6bEvZmBUF7NN\nV4qyzL5f0zLlz8g+QECtHt0d+PdfqqCVwDYOYphZig8o+xP2Uca6C9JDJHNPgTe4\ni9EHThy9EwK8qR0uoXvObyGbU+QkA9LZCDk/jb0Erbq7qx5CXYw6yNyAR65/0sPd\nBvZOWAMN2vRW34tSVrX7\n=y4dp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T18:47:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDdlZmZhMDQzYTVmZWU5ZjI2MDFjMTRmNzQ4MmFkNzk3YzIyYzMzZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217","sha":"b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217"}],"sha":"7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/7effa043a5fee9f2601c14f7482ad797c22c33e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:34:19Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:34:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(blade-navigation): correct five URL and query defects in the legacy adapter (VM-1777) (#321)\n\nFive defects in the legacy blade navigation adapter and in the blade\nstack''s URL sync paths. No public signature changed:\n`IUseBladeNavigation` and `IBladeStack` are untouched, and `closeBlade`\nstill returns the same \"prevented\" boolean.\n\n## 1. `goToRoot()` returned the first registered route when no route\ndeclares `meta.root`\n\n`routes.find((r) => r.aliasOf?.path === mainRoute?.path)` degenerated to\n`r.aliasOf?.path === undefined` when `mainRoute` was undefined, which is\ntrue for every alias-less route. `find` therefore returned `routes[0]`,\n`|| mainRoute` never ran, and the tenant-prefix fallback below was\nunreachable — an app with no root route navigated \"home\" to whatever\nregistered first, e.g. Login.\n\nThe alias lookup now only runs once `mainRoute` is known, so the\ntenant-prefixed path fallback is reachable again.\n\n## 2. `closeBlade` rewrote the URL for a close that never happened\n\n`_closeBlade` returned `false` for three distinct outcomes — closed,\nrefused because it is the workspace blade, and blade id not in the stack\n— so the caller read every refusal as a successful close and issued a\n`history.replace`.\n\nInternally `_closeBlade` now returns `\"closed\" | \"prevented\" |\n\"refused\"`; the URL is written only for `\"closed\"`. The public\n`closeBlade` collapses that back to the legacy boolean (`true` only for\n`\"prevented\"`).\n\n## 3. `setNavigationQuery` destroyed other workspaces'' query state, and\n`getNavigationQuery` coerced strings to numbers\n\n`getNavigationQuery` filters by `${prefix}_`, so several workspaces\nholding state in the hash at once is clearly intended — but\n`setNavigationQuery` built a fresh query object and replaced the entire\nquery string, dropping every foreign namespace on the next write. It now\nreads the existing hash, deletes only its own namespace''s keys and\nwrites the rest back untouched.\n\nOn the read side every value went through `Number()` and was kept unless\n`NaN`. `Number(\"\")` is 0, `\"007\"` became 7 and `\"1e3\"` became 1000.\nValues are now converted only when the conversion is reversible\n(`String(Number(v)) === v`), so plain integers still read back as\nnumbers while `\"\"`, `\"007\"` and `\"1e3\"` stay text.\n\n## 4. `setNavigationQuery` corrupted values containing `&` or `=`\n\nThe built query string was wrapped in `decodeURIComponent`, undoing the\npercent-encoding `URLSearchParams` had just applied:\n\n```\nsetNavigationQuery({ keyword: \"a&b\", note: \"x=1\" })\n  URLSearchParams builds:   /offers?offers_keyword=a%26b&offers_note=x%3D1\n  after decodeURIComponent: /offers?offers_keyword=a&b&offers_note=x=1\n  reads back as:            { keyword: \"a\", note: \"x=1\" } plus a stray b= parameter\n```\n\n`decodeURIComponent` is gone; the encoding is preserved and the round\ntrip is exact.\n\n## 5. Re-opening the current workspace pushed a history entry for a\nnavigation that did not happen\n\n`_openWorkspace` early-returns when the requested workspace is already\nopen (and when permission is denied), but the unconditional\n`_syncOpened(\"push\")` after it still ran. Clicking the same top-level\nmenu item twice grew browser history. `_openWorkspace` now reports\nwhether it opened anything and the push is gated on that.\n\n## Tests\n\nEach defect has a regression test that fails before the fix and passes\nafter — 13 assertions in total across `useBladeStack.url.test.ts` and\n`useBladeNavigationAdapter.test.ts`. Defect 4 is pinned by an exact\nround trip of `\"a&b\"` and `\"x=1\"`. Tests added in VM-1760 that pinned\ndefects 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 as current behaviour now assert the corrected\nbehaviour, and their explanatory comments are gone.\n\nFull framework suite: 409 files, 3928 tests, all green. Typecheck and\nlint clean.\n\n## Note\n\n`openBlade` still pushes when a child `onBeforeClose` guard prevents the\nopen — the same class of defect as 2 and 5, on a path the ticket did not\nlist. Left as is and flagged for a follow-up rather than widened into\nthis fix.","tree":{"sha":"5ff1d595e9d0ae4363d45d51d19e7fd40811658c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/5ff1d595e9d0ae4363d45d51d19e7fd40811658c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ff1d595e9d0ae4363d45d51d19e7fd40811658c\nparent 0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787769259 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787769259 +0300\n\nfix(blade-navigation): correct five URL and query defects in the legacy adapter (VM-1777) (#321)\n\nFive defects in the legacy blade navigation adapter and in the blade\nstack''s URL sync paths. No public signature changed:\n`IUseBladeNavigation` and `IBladeStack` are untouched, and `closeBlade`\nstill returns the same \"prevented\" boolean.\n\n## 1. `goToRoot()` returned the first registered route when no route\ndeclares `meta.root`\n\n`routes.find((r) => r.aliasOf?.path === mainRoute?.path)` degenerated to\n`r.aliasOf?.path === undefined` when `mainRoute` was undefined, which is\ntrue for every alias-less route. `find` therefore returned `routes[0]`,\n`|| mainRoute` never ran, and the tenant-prefix fallback below was\nunreachable — an app with no root route navigated \"home\" to whatever\nregistered first, e.g. Login.\n\nThe alias lookup now only runs once `mainRoute` is known, so the\ntenant-prefixed path fallback is reachable again.\n\n## 2. `closeBlade` rewrote the URL for a close that never happened\n\n`_closeBlade` returned `false` for three distinct outcomes — closed,\nrefused because it is the workspace blade, and blade id not in the stack\n— so the caller read every refusal as a successful close and issued a\n`history.replace`.\n\nInternally `_closeBlade` now returns `\"closed\" | \"prevented\" |\n\"refused\"`; the URL is written only for `\"closed\"`. The public\n`closeBlade` collapses that back to the legacy boolean (`true` only for\n`\"prevented\"`).\n\n## 3. `setNavigationQuery` destroyed other workspaces'' query state, and\n`getNavigationQuery` coerced strings to numbers\n\n`getNavigationQuery` filters by `${prefix}_`, so several workspaces\nholding state in the hash at once is clearly intended — but\n`setNavigationQuery` built a fresh query object and replaced the entire\nquery string, dropping every foreign namespace on the next write. It now\nreads the existing hash, deletes only its own namespace''s keys and\nwrites the rest back untouched.\n\nOn the read side every value went through `Number()` and was kept unless\n`NaN`. `Number(\"\")` is 0, `\"007\"` became 7 and `\"1e3\"` became 1000.\nValues are now converted only when the conversion is reversible\n(`String(Number(v)) === v`), so plain integers still read back as\nnumbers while `\"\"`, `\"007\"` and `\"1e3\"` stay text.\n\n## 4. `setNavigationQuery` corrupted values containing `&` or `=`\n\nThe built query string was wrapped in `decodeURIComponent`, undoing the\npercent-encoding `URLSearchParams` had just applied:\n\n```\nsetNavigationQuery({ keyword: \"a&b\", note: \"x=1\" })\n  URLSearchParams builds:   /offers?offers_keyword=a%26b&offers_note=x%3D1\n  after decodeURIComponent: /offers?offers_keyword=a&b&offers_note=x=1\n  reads back as:            { keyword: \"a\", note: \"x=1\" } plus a stray b= parameter\n```\n\n`decodeURIComponent` is gone; the encoding is preserved and the round\ntrip is exact.\n\n## 5. Re-opening the current workspace pushed a history entry for a\nnavigation that did not happen\n\n`_openWorkspace` early-returns when the requested workspace is already\nopen (and when permission is denied), but the unconditional\n`_syncOpened(\"push\")` after it still ran. Clicking the same top-level\nmenu item twice grew browser history. `_openWorkspace` now reports\nwhether it opened anything and the push is gated on that.\n\n## Tests\n\nEach defect has a regression test that fails before the fix and passes\nafter — 13 assertions in total across `useBladeStack.url.test.ts` and\n`useBladeNavigationAdapter.test.ts`. Defect 4 is pinned by an exact\nround trip of `\"a&b\"` and `\"x=1\"`. Tests added in VM-1760 that pinned\ndefects 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 as current behaviour now assert the corrected\nbehaviour, and their explanatory comments are gone.\n\nFull framework suite: 409 files, 3928 tests, all green. Typecheck and\nlint clean.\n\n## Note\n\n`openBlade` still pushes when a child `onBeforeClose` guard prevents the\nopen — the same class of defect as 2 and 5, on a path the ticket did not\nlist. Left as is and flagged for a follow-up rather than widened into\nthis fix.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjzGrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2CYQAGf01IUeMaciqi9G8iYvP+9w\nrZNmdXZvGXmYkdeeE0l+H46VGZLbgFeffJhwH/yU2rKg49ylHmdqBZ/7YwLOrccf\nRi7IrfzuTF3+zd6K3JI8qovdCJcCWc/BE8z1ll01m+AP2B5xUAyE9Z5yN/FqW/+b\niLQeUaw45WCDyj2AIXNwzdZwhU7rF3WOGfK7Wf9/1CUjF2liUx8x6NSuQc1SGyxp\nni47xU/sYIOdgOAUR1oa86Ig26mUNvdtYTiST74HLYxU+rzMedR2f10TqH9vr8Ce\n0GvGl7AkqqXRngE2z5Vr7cxjJSm+lAscj8R/6jkCbdEWK/QRnCJZfiIYKQK9qUG3\nXl1M330/ca9jYdhLK5PmWCB5JFAtSQ+NSEFAWWahORtX1MG2vU8YlVh0+Aix5h5R\nXT0UMf5Dty+M1BjK7C05yTMYiXGde/XEfr7JS2WQ6yHL7gIH3bNGW1aSPOPhX6BU\n9IoT7JsLDJc+QLysQ9DIYK+1Q8hVP6bYmnLXDvZ1+s3uZc5aV3NXTxsmbUkH3Oww\nREUZ/6LzT00ZWxT1s3DlK/ZVliZehWhGyyzD6FFvS1P2cAAilSWoGBX6Mk+sFMZp\nAES2q9uXzOZf6dAy9sBy8cWTBdiB/zPyXAgQsxOQPsV7K1nR2ZwJqM5yznAY2nLw\nT8h3wJm/XX8oF6SJmOZZ\n=aFj9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T18:34:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGIwOGUzOTI1MGJkOTI4NDJjYmZjYjlkNmRmZTdkODM4MDkyNTkyMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f","sha":"0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f"}],"sha":"b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/b08e39250bd92842cbfcb9d6dfe7d83809259217"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:34:01Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:34:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: run CI once per commit and stop cancelling trunk runs (VM-1783) (#322)\n\nFixes VM-1783. Changes **when** CI runs, never what it checks. No job,\nstep, or check name is touched — the diff is three hunks: the header\ncomment, the `push` branch list, and the `concurrency` block.\n\n## Problem 1 — a `feat/**` branch with an open PR ran CI twice\n\n`pull_request` and `push` both fired for the same commit. The\nconcurrency guard could not merge them: `github.ref` is\n`refs/heads/feat/<name>` for the push and `refs/pull/<n>/merge` for the\npull_request, so the two runs landed in different groups and neither\ncancelled the other.\n\nObserved on PR #318, commit `0bb1c8982`: two runs. The push run failed\nwith `[vitest] Browser connection was closed while running tests` after\n602 of 605 tests passed; the pull_request run passed the same commit.\nDouble runner minutes, doubled flake exposure, and a red cross on a\ngreen PR.\n\n**Fix:** dropped `feat/**` from the `push` trigger, leaving `main` and\n`dev`. Topic branches are already covered by `pull_request`.\n\n**Trade-off, stated explicitly:** a `feat/**` branch with *no* PR open\nnow gets no CI until a PR exists. The merge gate is unaffected —\nprotection evaluates the checks on the `pull_request` run, which still\nruns. This is the only behavioural loss in the PR.\n\n## Problem 2 — on trunk, an older commit''s run could cancel a newer one\n\n`cancel-in-progress: true` assumes runs are created in commit order.\nGitHub does not guarantee that.\n\nObserved 2026-08-26: PR #319 merged 15:05:46, PR #318 merged 15:05:51.\nGitHub created the run for `05e37006b` (newer, and main HEAD) at\n15:06:01, then created the run for `5896c2f18` (older) at 15:08:36. Both\nhashed to `ci-refs/heads/main`, so the later-created run for the *older*\ncommit cancelled the in-progress run for the *newer* one. Main HEAD was\nleft unverified, and a cancelled run reports as `failure`.\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```yaml\ngroup: ci-${{ github.event_name == ''pull_request'' && github.ref || github.sha }}\ncancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == ''pull_request'' }}\n```\n\nWhy this shape rather than only flipping `cancel-in-progress` to `${{\ngithub.event_name == ''pull_request'' }}` and leaving the group alone:\nturning cancellation off is not sufficient on its own. With a shared\ntrunk group, a third run arriving while a second is *pending* still gets\nthe second one cancelled — GitHub cancels previously-pending runs in a\ngroup, not just in-progress ones. Two merges 5 seconds apart is already\nthe observed pattern, so three is realistic. Giving trunk a group per\ncommit removes the shared group entirely: every trunk commit gets its\nown run, never cancelled, never queued behind another. PRs keep the old,\ncorrect behaviour — one run per PR, a new push supersedes the previous\none.\n\n## Event / job / concurrency-group matrix\n\nThis is **reasoning about the YAML**, not measurement — see the\nverification note below. `H` = the\n`!startsWith(github.event.head_commit.message, ''release:'')` guard.\n\n| Event | Triggered? | Jobs that run | Jobs skipped | Concurrency group\n| `cancel-in-progress` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `pull_request` (paths match) | yes | `static-checks`, `test`,\n`storybook-tests`, `storybook-build` | `storybook` |\n`ci-refs/pull/<n>/merge` | `true` |\n| `push` to `main` | yes | `static-checks`, `test`, `storybook-tests` (H\ntrue), `storybook` | `storybook-build` | `ci-<sha>` | `false` |\n| `push` to `main`, `release:` commit | yes | `storybook` only |\n`static-checks`, `test`, `storybook-tests`, `storybook-build` |\n`ci-<sha>` | `false` |\n| `push` to `dev` | yes | `static-checks`, `test`, `storybook-tests` |\n`storybook`, `storybook-build` | `ci-<sha>` | `false` |\n| `push` to `feat/**` **with** an open PR | **no** (was: yes → 2 runs) |\none run, from `pull_request` | — | — | — |\n| `push` to `feat/**` **without** a PR | **no** (was: yes) | no CI until\na PR is opened | — | — | — |\n| `workflow_dispatch` | yes | `static-checks`, `test`, `storybook-tests`\n| `storybook`, `storybook-build` | `ci-<sha>` | `false` |\n\n`H` is true for `pull_request` and `workflow_dispatch` because neither\nevent carries `head_commit`, so the guard only ever suppresses jobs on a\n`release:` push to trunk — unchanged from before.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `actionlint` v1.7.7 on `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: clean, exit 0.\n(Repo-wide it reports 7 pre-existing findings in `storybook-ci.yml`\nabout secrets not declared under `workflow_call` — untouched by this\nPR.)\n- Every claim in the rewritten header comment was checked against the\nfile itself: the `push` branch list is `main`, `dev`; `pull_request` and\n`workflow_dispatch` are both declared; `cancel-in-progress` resolves to\nfalse for everything except `pull_request`. The comment deliberately\nasserts nothing about which checks are required — that lives in the\nbranch ruleset, not in this file, and would go stale here.\n- **The live trigger check could not be made.** GitHub Actions was in a\nmajor outage across this work: runs stuck in `queued`, and workflow runs\nnot created at all for some PRs. Any run count or conclusion observed in\nthat window is an artefact of the outage rather than evidence about the\ntriggers, so none is reported here. Trigger and cancellation behaviour\non trunk is in any case only fully observable after merge; the matrix\nabove is the argument, and `actionlint` plus the header audit cover what\nis checkable statically.\n\n\n## Review notes\n\nTwo consequences checked against the live repo state, added during\nreview.\n\n**The stated trade-off costs nothing today.** Two `feat/**` branches\nexist on the remote and neither has an open PR: `feat/response` (last\ncommit 2024-04-25) and `feat/vc-data-table-single-load-restore` (last\ncommit 2026-06-18). Both are stale, so no active branch loses a CI\nsignal when this lands.\n\n**The `storybook` job''s `feat/redesign` clause becomes unreachable.**\nIts condition is `github.event_name == ''push'' && (github.ref ==\n''refs/heads/main'' || github.ref == ''refs/heads/feat/redesign'')`. With\n`feat/**` gone from the push trigger, a push to `feat/redesign` no\nlonger starts this workflow at all, so the second half of that condition\ncan never be true. Nothing is lost: `git ls-remote` shows\n`feat/redesign` does not exist on the remote and it has no run history.\nThe clause was already dead; it is now structurally unreachable too.\nLeft in place deliberately — removing it is unrelated to this change and\nbelongs in a separate cleanup.","tree":{"sha":"e24d8183005e670d3e5c1ce6864cef4ba6aa8ae9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/e24d8183005e670d3e5c1ce6864cef4ba6aa8ae9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f","verification":{"payload":"tree e24d8183005e670d3e5c1ce6864cef4ba6aa8ae9\nparent 05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787769241 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787769241 +0300\n\nci: run CI once per commit and stop cancelling trunk runs (VM-1783) (#322)\n\nFixes VM-1783. Changes **when** CI runs, never what it checks. No job,\nstep, or check name is touched — the diff is three hunks: the header\ncomment, the `push` branch list, and the `concurrency` block.\n\n## Problem 1 — a `feat/**` branch with an open PR ran CI twice\n\n`pull_request` and `push` both fired for the same commit. The\nconcurrency guard could not merge them: `github.ref` is\n`refs/heads/feat/<name>` for the push and `refs/pull/<n>/merge` for the\npull_request, so the two runs landed in different groups and neither\ncancelled the other.\n\nObserved on PR #318, commit `0bb1c8982`: two runs. The push run failed\nwith `[vitest] Browser connection was closed while running tests` after\n602 of 605 tests passed; the pull_request run passed the same commit.\nDouble runner minutes, doubled flake exposure, and a red cross on a\ngreen PR.\n\n**Fix:** dropped `feat/**` from the `push` trigger, leaving `main` and\n`dev`. Topic branches are already covered by `pull_request`.\n\n**Trade-off, stated explicitly:** a `feat/**` branch with *no* PR open\nnow gets no CI until a PR exists. The merge gate is unaffected —\nprotection evaluates the checks on the `pull_request` run, which still\nruns. This is the only behavioural loss in the PR.\n\n## Problem 2 — on trunk, an older commit''s run could cancel a newer one\n\n`cancel-in-progress: true` assumes runs are created in commit order.\nGitHub does not guarantee that.\n\nObserved 2026-08-26: PR #319 merged 15:05:46, PR #318 merged 15:05:51.\nGitHub created the run for `05e37006b` (newer, and main HEAD) at\n15:06:01, then created the run for `5896c2f18` (older) at 15:08:36. Both\nhashed to `ci-refs/heads/main`, so the later-created run for the *older*\ncommit cancelled the in-progress run for the *newer* one. Main HEAD was\nleft unverified, and a cancelled run reports as `failure`.\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```yaml\ngroup: ci-${{ github.event_name == ''pull_request'' && github.ref || github.sha }}\ncancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == ''pull_request'' }}\n```\n\nWhy this shape rather than only flipping `cancel-in-progress` to `${{\ngithub.event_name == ''pull_request'' }}` and leaving the group alone:\nturning cancellation off is not sufficient on its own. With a shared\ntrunk group, a third run arriving while a second is *pending* still gets\nthe second one cancelled — GitHub cancels previously-pending runs in a\ngroup, not just in-progress ones. Two merges 5 seconds apart is already\nthe observed pattern, so three is realistic. Giving trunk a group per\ncommit removes the shared group entirely: every trunk commit gets its\nown run, never cancelled, never queued behind another. PRs keep the old,\ncorrect behaviour — one run per PR, a new push supersedes the previous\none.\n\n## Event / job / concurrency-group matrix\n\nThis is **reasoning about the YAML**, not measurement — see the\nverification note below. `H` = the\n`!startsWith(github.event.head_commit.message, ''release:'')` guard.\n\n| Event | Triggered? | Jobs that run | Jobs skipped | Concurrency group\n| `cancel-in-progress` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `pull_request` (paths match) | yes | `static-checks`, `test`,\n`storybook-tests`, `storybook-build` | `storybook` |\n`ci-refs/pull/<n>/merge` | `true` |\n| `push` to `main` | yes | `static-checks`, `test`, `storybook-tests` (H\ntrue), `storybook` | `storybook-build` | `ci-<sha>` | `false` |\n| `push` to `main`, `release:` commit | yes | `storybook` only |\n`static-checks`, `test`, `storybook-tests`, `storybook-build` |\n`ci-<sha>` | `false` |\n| `push` to `dev` | yes | `static-checks`, `test`, `storybook-tests` |\n`storybook`, `storybook-build` | `ci-<sha>` | `false` |\n| `push` to `feat/**` **with** an open PR | **no** (was: yes → 2 runs) |\none run, from `pull_request` | — | — | — |\n| `push` to `feat/**` **without** a PR | **no** (was: yes) | no CI until\na PR is opened | — | — | — |\n| `workflow_dispatch` | yes | `static-checks`, `test`, `storybook-tests`\n| `storybook`, `storybook-build` | `ci-<sha>` | `false` |\n\n`H` is true for `pull_request` and `workflow_dispatch` because neither\nevent carries `head_commit`, so the guard only ever suppresses jobs on a\n`release:` push to trunk — unchanged from before.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `actionlint` v1.7.7 on `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: clean, exit 0.\n(Repo-wide it reports 7 pre-existing findings in `storybook-ci.yml`\nabout secrets not declared under `workflow_call` — untouched by this\nPR.)\n- Every claim in the rewritten header comment was checked against the\nfile itself: the `push` branch list is `main`, `dev`; `pull_request` and\n`workflow_dispatch` are both declared; `cancel-in-progress` resolves to\nfalse for everything except `pull_request`. The comment deliberately\nasserts nothing about which checks are required — that lives in the\nbranch ruleset, not in this file, and would go stale here.\n- **The live trigger check could not be made.** GitHub Actions was in a\nmajor outage across this work: runs stuck in `queued`, and workflow runs\nnot created at all for some PRs. Any run count or conclusion observed in\nthat window is an artefact of the outage rather than evidence about the\ntriggers, so none is reported here. Trigger and cancellation behaviour\non trunk is in any case only fully observable after merge; the matrix\nabove is the argument, and `actionlint` plus the header audit cover what\nis checkable statically.\n\n\n## Review notes\n\nTwo consequences checked against the live repo state, added during\nreview.\n\n**The stated trade-off costs nothing today.** Two `feat/**` branches\nexist on the remote and neither has an open PR: `feat/response` (last\ncommit 2024-04-25) and `feat/vc-data-table-single-load-restore` (last\ncommit 2026-06-18). Both are stale, so no active branch loses a CI\nsignal when this lands.\n\n**The `storybook` job''s `feat/redesign` clause becomes unreachable.**\nIts condition is `github.event_name == ''push'' && (github.ref ==\n''refs/heads/main'' || github.ref == ''refs/heads/feat/redesign'')`. With\n`feat/**` gone from the push trigger, a push to `feat/redesign` no\nlonger starts this workflow at all, so the second half of that condition\ncan never be true. Nothing is lost: `git ls-remote` shows\n`feat/redesign` does not exist on the remote and it has no run history.\nThe clause was already dead; it is now structurally unreachable too.\nLeft in place deliberately — removing it is unrelated to this change and\nbelongs in a separate cleanup.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjzGZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1acQAGhhhUS5ir+0S9BQBJ5GgGGJ\nhGkAw4uAvdORIj/FfYwW0ZYnXY2991ASdn/xaTB9Pm/Z2veG0HWRsf8d/wCB9Rxd\n76/x3CyeDbQfqGlkX4yFIMjqKA57bfHRx4oRbBKsKtcTFSAGJGQVqzC0ZM24692U\nYUfFLYy4vqBvgvi2QPZHJR4qHnCCMmNtRcfilHAktp7U9+V/Q5NlofI/LmXrvhQJ\ncGvqoMZkTAMZi4YuPkyNhJLWR5/7o11KVkHUHqooaAdyhsStmA7h5ehtOP3nQMqU\n8l6VmJZ/5cuIBtz2L0vaiH+JHh5BxojxH3OGxQF6vmW6O5L1QrwWF+U6ER26zH5J\n3wzWx7rgc4GNOpqT83EskiLiw2AA1mSSDLb0alsIDII5GyF70aGAkaQuKrB/kdw4\nTM96dyLoI/ayy6AqbGlseXYVeX2UBk04DlZaBAfD59M7T3ptwykBnmyiBZwpt6FY\nu7NbexbDUGi5ZDpyFDS9KbI8H/B3ZQ4p2D5XrCkbIjqadzS9AY995ID0sJIOjpTS\nX4lfCEVul2Bbvk/sXT6ObQeTjAbs6mtQOh4zYGarnuIcm8wYYj8wilMtJJBhk4Q2\n6QFeM2a5xKiAHgvdbZBf2vSsJ/q9xszdmNtPG/pv4wllYB9v5HDGucKxXRn5N9a9\nAsEg503NhuquimHrtBi4\n=8qIu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T18:34:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDBmMjg4OTI1ZDIwODBiNDhjNmVhYWY3NWYwYzAxMTMwNzgzYTMwN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1","sha":"05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1"}],"sha":"0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/0f288925d2080b48c6eaaf75f0c01130783a307f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T15:05:51Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T15:05:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(create-vc-app): add an opt-in Module Federation option (VM-1757) (#318)\n\n## Problem\n\nA scaffolded standalone app cannot host remote modules. Three pieces\nwere missing together, so adding any one alone would not build:\n\n1. `@vc-shell/mf-host` absent from\n`cli/create-vc-app/src/templates/standalone/_package.json.ejs`\n2. `cli/create-vc-app/src/templates/standalone/vite.config.mts.ejs` did\nnot apply `mfHostConfig()`\n3. `cli/create-vc-app/src/templates/standalone/src/main.ts.ejs` never\ncalled `registerRemoteModules(app, { router, appName })` before mount\n\nThere was also no flag or prompt for it, so it was not opt-in either. A\nteam that scaffolds an app and then wants to load a remote module has to\nreverse-engineer the wiring from the reference app.\n\n## Change\n\nA `moduleFederation` option threaded through the same path as the\nexisting `aiAgent`, `dashboard` and `mocks` options — a\n`--module-federation` CLI flag, an interactive prompt, and a default of\noff. All three template pieces are conditional on it.\n\nOpt-in, not on by default: teams that do not need Module Federation keep\na minimal scaffold, and neither the dependency nor the Vite plugin is\nforced on every new app. The prompt is suppressed for `dynamic-module`\n(the remote side), the same way `tenantRoutes` / `aiAgent` / `dashboard`\nare.\n\n| File | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/types.ts` | `ProjectOptions.moduleFederation`,\n`CLIArgs[\"module-federation\"]` |\n| `src/index.ts` | `mri` boolean flag + `--help` line |\n| `src/commands/init.ts` | non-interactive default, interactive confirm,\noptions assembly |\n| `src/engine/helpers.ts` | `buildTemplateData` passthrough → EJS local\n|\n| `templates/standalone/_package.json.ejs` | conditional\n`@vc-shell/mf-host` dependency |\n| `templates/standalone/vite.config.mts.ejs` | conditional\n`mfHostConfig()` spread |\n| `templates/standalone/src/main.ts.ejs` | conditional import +\n`registerRemoteModules()` before mount |\n| `cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/vc-app.md` | the flag added to the three\nplaces the sibling flags are listed |\n\nGenerated with the option on:\n\n```ts\n// vite.config.mts\nimport { getApplicationConfiguration } from \"@vc-shell/config-generator\";\nimport { mfHostConfig } from \"@vc-shell/mf-host/vite\";\n\nexport default getApplicationConfiguration({\n  ...mfHostConfig(),\n  // Add you extra Vite configuration here\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// src/main.ts — before router.isReady() and mount\nregisterRemoteModules(app, { router, appName: \"my-app\" });\n```\n\n`preserveSymlinks` is deliberately not part of the template:\n`scripts/setup-app.ts` injects it for the local portal flow, it is not a\nModule Federation requirement.\n\n## Release-script fix included\n\nMaking the dependency conditional puts an EJS control tag at object\nlevel in `_package.json.ejs`, so the template is no longer valid JSON.\n`updateBoilerplatePkgVersions` in `scripts/utils.ts` read it with\n`readJsonSync` and wrote it back with `JSON.stringify` — that would have\nthrown on the next version bump (`runAfterBump` calls it with no\ntry/catch) and, had it parsed, silently deleted the conditional and\nhard-coded the dependency into every scaffold.\n\nIt now patches dependency versions line by line, scoped to\n`dependencies` / `devDependencies` blocks, leaving every other byte\nuntouched. Scoping matters: `lint-staged` is both a dev dependency and a\nscript name, and a whole-file rewrite would corrupt the script. Two\nregression tests cover both cases.\n\n## Verification\n\n### Output with the option off is unchanged\n\nA full-flag scaffold produced by `origin/main`''s scaffolder and by this\nbranch''s, into equally named directories:\n\n```\n$ diff -r cmp/a/demo-app cmp/b/demo-app\nIDENTICAL — off variant output unchanged\n```\n\n(`--type standalone --module-name Orders --dashboard --mocks --ai-agent\n--tenant-routes`)\n\n### Repository gates\n\n```\n$ yarn typecheck\nEXIT=0\n\n$ yarn lint:check\nEXIT=0\n\n$ yarn format:check\nChecking formatting...\nAll matched files use Prettier code style!\nEXIT=0\n\n$ cd cli/create-vc-app && npx vitest run --config vitest.config.ts\n Test Files  4 passed (4)\n      Tests  74 passed (74)\n   Duration  2.80s\n\n$ cd cli/migrate && npx vitest run\n Test Files  45 passed (45)\n      Tests  243 passed (243)\n   Duration  802ms\n\n$ yarn test\n Test Files  1 failed | 483 passed (484)\n      Tests  4445 passed (4445)\n```\n\nThe single root-suite failure is `VcScheduler.style.test.ts`, which\nresolves `assets/styles/theme/colors.scss` against `process.cwd()` and\ntherefore fails in any git worktree. Pre-existing, unrelated to this\nchange.\n\nNew tests:\n\n- `init.test.ts` — the option on emits the import, the\n`registerRemoteModules` call before `router.isReady()` and mount, the\n`mfHostConfig()` spread and the dependency; the option off emits none of\nthem.\n- `init.test.ts` — three new Prettier-clean combos (`module-federation`\nalone, with a module, and folded into the existing all-flags combo).\n- `init.test.ts` — a raw-render suite over `main.ts.ejs`,\n`vite.config.mts.ejs` and `_package.json.ejs` for both flag states. The\n`formatGenerated` Prettier pass can mask template whitespace bugs, so\nthis asserts the unformatted render. Falsified by reverting `<%_ … _%>`\nto `<% … %>` in one template — both cases fail as expected.\n- `helpers.test.ts` — the `moduleFederation` passthrough and its\ndefault.\n- `cli/migrate/tests/scripts/utils.test.ts` — a template carrying EJS\ncontrol tags keeps them across a version bump; a package name that is\nalso a script key is rewritten only inside the dependency blocks.\n\n### Generated projects\n\nTwo apps scaffolded from the built CLI, a module added to each with\n`add-module`, then each project''s own gates. `@vc-shell/*` deps were\nrewired to `portal:` paths against this branch''s build, matching what\n`scripts/setup-app.ts` does for `apps/`.\n\n```\n$ node dist/index.js mf-off --type standalone --module-name Orders --dashboard\n$ node dist/index.js mf-on  --type standalone --module-name Orders --dashboard --module-federation\n$ (cd each && node dist/index.js add-module reviews)\n\nmf-off: type-check=0 lint=0 build=0\nmf-on:  type-check=0 lint=0 build=0\n```\n\n```\n$ cd mf-off && yarn build\nBuilding application mf-off v.0.0.0 ...\nvite v6.4.3 building for production...\n✓ 282 modules transformed.\ndist/index.html                    6.24 kB │ gzip: 1.23 kB\ndist/index18468.js                 2.60 kB │ gzip: 0.73 kB\n✓ built in 3.21s\n\n$ cd mf-on && yarn build\nBuilding application mf-on v.0.0.0 ...\nvite v6.4.3 building for production...\n✓ 998 modules transformed.\ndist/index.html                             8.86 kB │ gzip: 1.41 kB\ndist/app-vendor-vc-shell-mf-host61928.js    3.71 kB │ gzip: 1.56 kB\ndist/index61928.js                          3.81 kB │ gzip: 0.90 kB\n✓ built in 4.68s\n```\n\nThe MF runtime is present only in the `mf-on` bundle —\n`app-vendor-vc-shell-mf-host*.js`, `module-federation-error-codes*.js`,\nand the `/api/apps/` manifest endpoint. None of them appear in `mf-off`.\n\nBoth `type-check` and `lint` were falsified before being trusted: a\ndeliberate type error and a deliberate unused variable each surfaced,\nand disappeared again on restore.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Loading an actual remote module needs a platform backend serving\n`/api/apps/<appName>/manifest`, so end-to-end remote loading was not\nexercised here. What is verified is that the runtime is wired, bundled,\nand reaches the manifest fetch.\n- Under the local `portal:` flow only, `@vc-shell/mf-host` cannot\nresolve its `\"@vc-shell/mf-config\": \"workspace:*\"` dependency outside\nthe monorepo; the scratch project needed a `resolutions` override.\nPublished packages are unaffected — Yarn rewrites `workspace:*` to a\nreal version on publish — so nothing in the scaffold changes because of\nit. Worth knowing if anyone runs `yarn setup:apps` against an MF-enabled\napp.\n- `cli/create-vc-app`''s own `check:types` reports one pre-existing error\n(`init.test.ts` passes `projectType` to `buildTemplateData`, which does\nnot accept it). Present on `main` too, at the same call site; left alone\nas unrelated.","tree":{"sha":"4114dac609359664ad717e334ca840ebbfbaa1d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/4114dac609359664ad717e334ca840ebbfbaa1d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1","verification":{"payload":"tree 4114dac609359664ad717e334ca840ebbfbaa1d7\nparent 5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787756751 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787756751 +0300\n\nfeat(create-vc-app): add an opt-in Module Federation option (VM-1757) (#318)\n\n## Problem\n\nA scaffolded standalone app cannot host remote modules. Three pieces\nwere missing together, so adding any one alone would not build:\n\n1. `@vc-shell/mf-host` absent from\n`cli/create-vc-app/src/templates/standalone/_package.json.ejs`\n2. `cli/create-vc-app/src/templates/standalone/vite.config.mts.ejs` did\nnot apply `mfHostConfig()`\n3. `cli/create-vc-app/src/templates/standalone/src/main.ts.ejs` never\ncalled `registerRemoteModules(app, { router, appName })` before mount\n\nThere was also no flag or prompt for it, so it was not opt-in either. A\nteam that scaffolds an app and then wants to load a remote module has to\nreverse-engineer the wiring from the reference app.\n\n## Change\n\nA `moduleFederation` option threaded through the same path as the\nexisting `aiAgent`, `dashboard` and `mocks` options — a\n`--module-federation` CLI flag, an interactive prompt, and a default of\noff. All three template pieces are conditional on it.\n\nOpt-in, not on by default: teams that do not need Module Federation keep\na minimal scaffold, and neither the dependency nor the Vite plugin is\nforced on every new app. The prompt is suppressed for `dynamic-module`\n(the remote side), the same way `tenantRoutes` / `aiAgent` / `dashboard`\nare.\n\n| File | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/types.ts` | `ProjectOptions.moduleFederation`,\n`CLIArgs[\"module-federation\"]` |\n| `src/index.ts` | `mri` boolean flag + `--help` line |\n| `src/commands/init.ts` | non-interactive default, interactive confirm,\noptions assembly |\n| `src/engine/helpers.ts` | `buildTemplateData` passthrough → EJS local\n|\n| `templates/standalone/_package.json.ejs` | conditional\n`@vc-shell/mf-host` dependency |\n| `templates/standalone/vite.config.mts.ejs` | conditional\n`mfHostConfig()` spread |\n| `templates/standalone/src/main.ts.ejs` | conditional import +\n`registerRemoteModules()` before mount |\n| `cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/vc-app.md` | the flag added to the three\nplaces the sibling flags are listed |\n\nGenerated with the option on:\n\n```ts\n// vite.config.mts\nimport { getApplicationConfiguration } from \"@vc-shell/config-generator\";\nimport { mfHostConfig } from \"@vc-shell/mf-host/vite\";\n\nexport default getApplicationConfiguration({\n  ...mfHostConfig(),\n  // Add you extra Vite configuration here\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// src/main.ts — before router.isReady() and mount\nregisterRemoteModules(app, { router, appName: \"my-app\" });\n```\n\n`preserveSymlinks` is deliberately not part of the template:\n`scripts/setup-app.ts` injects it for the local portal flow, it is not a\nModule Federation requirement.\n\n## Release-script fix included\n\nMaking the dependency conditional puts an EJS control tag at object\nlevel in `_package.json.ejs`, so the template is no longer valid JSON.\n`updateBoilerplatePkgVersions` in `scripts/utils.ts` read it with\n`readJsonSync` and wrote it back with `JSON.stringify` — that would have\nthrown on the next version bump (`runAfterBump` calls it with no\ntry/catch) and, had it parsed, silently deleted the conditional and\nhard-coded the dependency into every scaffold.\n\nIt now patches dependency versions line by line, scoped to\n`dependencies` / `devDependencies` blocks, leaving every other byte\nuntouched. Scoping matters: `lint-staged` is both a dev dependency and a\nscript name, and a whole-file rewrite would corrupt the script. Two\nregression tests cover both cases.\n\n## Verification\n\n### Output with the option off is unchanged\n\nA full-flag scaffold produced by `origin/main`''s scaffolder and by this\nbranch''s, into equally named directories:\n\n```\n$ diff -r cmp/a/demo-app cmp/b/demo-app\nIDENTICAL — off variant output unchanged\n```\n\n(`--type standalone --module-name Orders --dashboard --mocks --ai-agent\n--tenant-routes`)\n\n### Repository gates\n\n```\n$ yarn typecheck\nEXIT=0\n\n$ yarn lint:check\nEXIT=0\n\n$ yarn format:check\nChecking formatting...\nAll matched files use Prettier code style!\nEXIT=0\n\n$ cd cli/create-vc-app && npx vitest run --config vitest.config.ts\n Test Files  4 passed (4)\n      Tests  74 passed (74)\n   Duration  2.80s\n\n$ cd cli/migrate && npx vitest run\n Test Files  45 passed (45)\n      Tests  243 passed (243)\n   Duration  802ms\n\n$ yarn test\n Test Files  1 failed | 483 passed (484)\n      Tests  4445 passed (4445)\n```\n\nThe single root-suite failure is `VcScheduler.style.test.ts`, which\nresolves `assets/styles/theme/colors.scss` against `process.cwd()` and\ntherefore fails in any git worktree. Pre-existing, unrelated to this\nchange.\n\nNew tests:\n\n- `init.test.ts` — the option on emits the import, the\n`registerRemoteModules` call before `router.isReady()` and mount, the\n`mfHostConfig()` spread and the dependency; the option off emits none of\nthem.\n- `init.test.ts` — three new Prettier-clean combos (`module-federation`\nalone, with a module, and folded into the existing all-flags combo).\n- `init.test.ts` — a raw-render suite over `main.ts.ejs`,\n`vite.config.mts.ejs` and `_package.json.ejs` for both flag states. The\n`formatGenerated` Prettier pass can mask template whitespace bugs, so\nthis asserts the unformatted render. Falsified by reverting `<%_ … _%>`\nto `<% … %>` in one template — both cases fail as expected.\n- `helpers.test.ts` — the `moduleFederation` passthrough and its\ndefault.\n- `cli/migrate/tests/scripts/utils.test.ts` — a template carrying EJS\ncontrol tags keeps them across a version bump; a package name that is\nalso a script key is rewritten only inside the dependency blocks.\n\n### Generated projects\n\nTwo apps scaffolded from the built CLI, a module added to each with\n`add-module`, then each project''s own gates. `@vc-shell/*` deps were\nrewired to `portal:` paths against this branch''s build, matching what\n`scripts/setup-app.ts` does for `apps/`.\n\n```\n$ node dist/index.js mf-off --type standalone --module-name Orders --dashboard\n$ node dist/index.js mf-on  --type standalone --module-name Orders --dashboard --module-federation\n$ (cd each && node dist/index.js add-module reviews)\n\nmf-off: type-check=0 lint=0 build=0\nmf-on:  type-check=0 lint=0 build=0\n```\n\n```\n$ cd mf-off && yarn build\nBuilding application mf-off v.0.0.0 ...\nvite v6.4.3 building for production...\n✓ 282 modules transformed.\ndist/index.html                    6.24 kB │ gzip: 1.23 kB\ndist/index18468.js                 2.60 kB │ gzip: 0.73 kB\n✓ built in 3.21s\n\n$ cd mf-on && yarn build\nBuilding application mf-on v.0.0.0 ...\nvite v6.4.3 building for production...\n✓ 998 modules transformed.\ndist/index.html                             8.86 kB │ gzip: 1.41 kB\ndist/app-vendor-vc-shell-mf-host61928.js    3.71 kB │ gzip: 1.56 kB\ndist/index61928.js                          3.81 kB │ gzip: 0.90 kB\n✓ built in 4.68s\n```\n\nThe MF runtime is present only in the `mf-on` bundle —\n`app-vendor-vc-shell-mf-host*.js`, `module-federation-error-codes*.js`,\nand the `/api/apps/` manifest endpoint. None of them appear in `mf-off`.\n\nBoth `type-check` and `lint` were falsified before being trusted: a\ndeliberate type error and a deliberate unused variable each surfaced,\nand disappeared again on restore.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Loading an actual remote module needs a platform backend serving\n`/api/apps/<appName>/manifest`, so end-to-end remote loading was not\nexercised here. What is verified is that the runtime is wired, bundled,\nand reaches the manifest fetch.\n- Under the local `portal:` flow only, `@vc-shell/mf-host` cannot\nresolve its `\"@vc-shell/mf-config\": \"workspace:*\"` dependency outside\nthe monorepo; the scratch project needed a `resolutions` override.\nPublished packages are unaffected — Yarn rewrites `workspace:*` to a\nreal version on publish — so nothing in the scaffold changes because of\nit. Worth knowing if anyone runs `yarn setup:apps` against an MF-enabled\napp.\n- `cli/create-vc-app`''s own `check:types` reports one pre-existing error\n(`init.test.ts` passes `projectType` to `buildTemplateData`, which does\nnot accept it). Present on `main` too, at the same call site; left alone\nas unrelated.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjwDPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdk4QAGQBJMPrFWpBM4+rCVi7+0ir\n+q6yo4euUAZjBjArGA4jU4gq+xPHhtC+yiLMOyjDnXuqG99AM7WZmgZD/ETpJgi+\nHAzdZohMmZe2IFcyewXAKo4Q9uJLMaKgwdPNMH2TMf/K4iAm6tVIIJEXchJuKPz6\ndM4AbN1u3C6pTh7w2ZXobvHW3uhseHME8K/21Jv7mbS+p2PAgVeaADawh7y2cqlY\nulrHFTJtnTaC45/xLwgASoD46372xs+eDsbVXxBoz5LOWoMG8dBbMpdebaU/fikt\nKkN/2YriSylXEtVLJ8+ZLYiy7C6VUkqKkJwKsQGRGd64UjAAvt0jaNEmlJSWSdty\nv4EwLfmESJs8mMqec9f3c9nN8bJ18PCIsLWNK2V/mY4h7DCPfbBP7+Xhukmtub8D\nNeoAHLiJlH/1MGHawM2CCdcwc5aOL4VYQtWC/EeTFT9/4IN4jZnksMQiIlLcrdPv\nO/oJu2Lk2CYxt/B9wt1lPE3XGzrrCVnf0//TWl2/EqrU5ZnMlYSwF1A37Yie4xYN\nCeznWA1SiXStoTSp2OFAV/AoS+TCcisWNv9rfVwLnbExIxZFMugPifhhcZI/i67S\n8kADswmhcAbeEPCz/HZMzZO+lgvk2r4vnP0nUevO8s9SMFxlH+fqiE4nFFoj2bOc\n03RvtJ2W6hYHLukj27Xw\n=mk86\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T15:05:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDA1ZTM3MDA2YjM4NTMwN2IwNmE5ZjNlYzQzZDM4MzhkMTU3MjNmZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693","sha":"5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693"}],"sha":"05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/05e37006b385307b06a9f3ec43d3838d15723fd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T15:05:45Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T15:05:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(framework): remove the unused global search service (#319)\n\nFollow-up to #312, which marked `createGlobalSearchService` deprecated.\nThat was the wrong call: deprecation protects public contracts, and this\nhas no consumer to protect.\n\n## Why delete rather than deprecate\n\n`createGlobalSearchService` has no callers, is never provided, and there\nis no `useGlobalSearch` composable to reach it. The composable and\n`GlobalSearchKey` were removed earlier (`framework/CHANGELOG.md:496`)\nand only the factory was left behind. Nothing in `framework`, `apps`,\n`cli`, `packages` or `.storybook` calls it.\n\n## Also removed: documentation for things that do not exist\n\nThree places described this as working code:\n\n- `core/README.md` documented a `useGlobalSearch` composable and gave\nits file path as `core/composables/useGlobalSearch/index.ts`. That\ndirectory does not exist.\n- `services.docs.md` listed `GlobalSearchService` in the service table.\n- `vc-app.docs.md` said `useShellBootstrap` bootstraps \"Menu, Toolbar,\nSettings, Dashboard, GlobalSearch\". Wrong twice: `useShellBootstrap`\nprovides the dashboard, app bar mobile buttons and the AI agent, while\nmenu, toolbar, widget and settings are provided earlier by the framework\ninstall. Rewritten to match the code.\n\n`useShellBootstrap.test.ts` also carried a `vi.mock` for\n`core/composables/useGlobalSearch` — a module that does not exist,\nmocking an import the composable never had. Removed.\n\n## Kept\n\nThe `GlobalSearchKey` row in `injection-keys.docs.md`. That table lists\nkeys removed in v1.2.3 and exists to help someone upgrading; it should\nkeep saying the key is gone.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `yarn typecheck` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn format:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | 0 errors, 6 pre-existing warnings |\n| `yarn check:circular` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn check:layers` | exit 0 |\n| `useShellBootstrap` suite | 15 passed |\n\nNet: 7 files, +1/−96.","tree":{"sha":"6f60ea049a59a3e6ea02d3b076ca5139c02cd16f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/6f60ea049a59a3e6ea02d3b076ca5139c02cd16f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f60ea049a59a3e6ea02d3b076ca5139c02cd16f\nparent 5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787756745 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787756745 +0300\n\nchore(framework): remove the unused global search service (#319)\n\nFollow-up to #312, which marked `createGlobalSearchService` deprecated.\nThat was the wrong call: deprecation protects public contracts, and this\nhas no consumer to protect.\n\n## Why delete rather than deprecate\n\n`createGlobalSearchService` has no callers, is never provided, and there\nis no `useGlobalSearch` composable to reach it. The composable and\n`GlobalSearchKey` were removed earlier (`framework/CHANGELOG.md:496`)\nand only the factory was left behind. Nothing in `framework`, `apps`,\n`cli`, `packages` or `.storybook` calls it.\n\n## Also removed: documentation for things that do not exist\n\nThree places described this as working code:\n\n- `core/README.md` documented a `useGlobalSearch` composable and gave\nits file path as `core/composables/useGlobalSearch/index.ts`. That\ndirectory does not exist.\n- `services.docs.md` listed `GlobalSearchService` in the service table.\n- `vc-app.docs.md` said `useShellBootstrap` bootstraps \"Menu, Toolbar,\nSettings, Dashboard, GlobalSearch\". Wrong twice: `useShellBootstrap`\nprovides the dashboard, app bar mobile buttons and the AI agent, while\nmenu, toolbar, widget and settings are provided earlier by the framework\ninstall. Rewritten to match the code.\n\n`useShellBootstrap.test.ts` also carried a `vi.mock` for\n`core/composables/useGlobalSearch` — a module that does not exist,\nmocking an import the composable never had. Removed.\n\n## Kept\n\nThe `GlobalSearchKey` row in `injection-keys.docs.md`. That table lists\nkeys removed in v1.2.3 and exists to help someone upgrading; it should\nkeep saying the key is gone.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `yarn typecheck` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn format:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | 0 errors, 6 pre-existing warnings |\n| `yarn check:circular` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn check:layers` | exit 0 |\n| `useShellBootstrap` suite | 15 passed |\n\nNet: 7 files, +1/−96.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjwDJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABC8QADe9INO/8ekcmd/s+pEwUxYl\nO94oqZDaetO05P+TjKDpmMZNAieE2tAOonF148mYsHlKWuwIUMIiSnL0cbcoEq2k\nRqOrMlBBMEfZVszbniVmhhOVAdrR568RbfA0GV+wqGKgcQiRoieJaeo6LOWJGzlX\nJ+KrEfh9166GrrJwZElErF0J7P0MFdCCj2qdkutNzE25baezO5ESPFsc+PdSZ3XB\nd2WYZm12J2DThYgXSJyUzhDTSzyGliliiE1hMzQSfZxgTawSHihT2mH/SvHy5JR9\nQZ1A1CQDodmtFwWJKZFVt8Bi9qP3g4Fb9dZZjqWWywpXkCbqoeVZ0RBCglliti4V\nAwcY9R+qH8HC5ejYIZQftkZphR4wrVy3cd1uL03EQbEznYaGn/EbYsscIk1axDap\nVP3otuSp6a4EQ7U2b2sijCXI5xnzVG+f+b6XUnSiEeqXnw/7KoggOldnyPXlCUJf\nRT69p2SqC3XzGENncDXP8WnGt6wa6mTdxrLBxWHO9TGypnJXcBoTJjGBsNpmP9h8\nvU3BUWUpEfuKKk5k9oOzF3lEgMeZ6/u0tIV6brGQ/etgVfIyQ09kwMupabx+qssj\n4OVGvd6J13/Ub1dYs6kioYw2WvU4qAWdaLgh1bCezJKV44cRJiGi9C8J7uh/j0zm\nGEAt/KEqrzzydepUGpa7\n=b7jr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T15:05:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDU4OTZjMmYxODMzYzJjNDRhYWU0MmJhZjgxMTgxNmY4ZGY5YmI2OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b","sha":"5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b"}],"sha":"5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5896c2f1833c2c44aae42baf811816f8df9bb693"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:56:10Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:56:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(blade-navigation): drop adapter URL sync tests that #317 made obsolete (#320)\n\n**`main` is currently red.** Three tests fail on a pristine checkout of\n`1a1eecf5c`, with no local changes:\n\n```\nFAIL  useBladeNavigationAdapter.test.ts > URL sync branches > pushes the URL when the opened blade has a url segment\nFAIL  useBladeNavigationAdapter.test.ts > URL sync branches > replaces the URL when closeBlade was not prevented\nFAIL  useBladeNavigationAdapter.guards.test.ts > closeBlade(0) rewrites the URL although the workspace never closes\n```\n\n## How it got in\n\nA semantic conflict between two PRs that were each green:\n\n- **#313** added tests asserting that `useBladeNavigationAdapter` calls\n`syncUrlPush` / `syncUrlReplace` after a stack mutation.\n- **#317** moved URL sync into the blade stack and deleted those calls\nfrom the adapter.\n\nNeither touched the other''s lines, so git merged them cleanly and no\nbranch-level CI caught it: #313 was green before #317 landed, #317 was\ngreen before #313 landed. The failure only exists in the merged state.\n\nWorth noting because the same trap is live for the remaining open PRs:\n**branch CI passing is not evidence that main will pass**, when two\nbranches change opposite sides of the same contract.\n\n## The fix\n\nDelete the `URL sync branches` describe block from the adapter test and\nthe two URL cases from the guards test. Six tests removed, of which only\nthree were failing: the other three were already **vacuous** after #317,\npassing only because zero calls trivially satisfies a\n`not.toHaveBeenCalled()` assertion.\n\n## Nothing is lost\n\n`useBladeStack.url.test.ts`, added by #317, covers the same ground at\nthe level where the behaviour now lives — 23 cases over the full verb\ntable. That includes the two defects the deleted tests were pinning for\nVM-1777:\n\n| deleted adapter test | stack-level equivalent |\n|---|---|\n| `closeBlade(0) rewrites the URL although the workspace never closes` |\n`closeBlade of the workspace still replaces` |\n| (VM-1777 defect 5, never pinned at adapter level) | `openWorkspace\nwith the same workspace still pushes` |\n\n## Kept deliberately\n\nThe `urlSync` module mock in both files. The adapter still imports\n`getTenantPrefix` from it; I removed the mock to check, and the\n`goToRoot` tenant-prefix case fails without it.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| adapter suites | 51 passed (was 54 passed / 3 failed) |\n| `yarn test:unit` | 4322 passed, 3 failing files are the known worktree\npath-resolution baseline (`VcScheduler.style`, `docs-sync/lint`,\n`mf-host/register-remote-modules`) |\n| `yarn typecheck` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn format:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn check:layers` | all pass |\n\nNet: 2 files, −64 lines.","tree":{"sha":"1a8ab2ee944da2fcb9289fa3e5640655c06de405","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/1a8ab2ee944da2fcb9289fa3e5640655c06de405"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a8ab2ee944da2fcb9289fa3e5640655c06de405\nparent 1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787756170 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787756170 +0300\n\nfix(blade-navigation): drop adapter URL sync tests that #317 made obsolete (#320)\n\n**`main` is currently red.** Three tests fail on a pristine checkout of\n`1a1eecf5c`, with no local changes:\n\n```\nFAIL  useBladeNavigationAdapter.test.ts > URL sync branches > pushes the URL when the opened blade has a url segment\nFAIL  useBladeNavigationAdapter.test.ts > URL sync branches > replaces the URL when closeBlade was not prevented\nFAIL  useBladeNavigationAdapter.guards.test.ts > closeBlade(0) rewrites the URL although the workspace never closes\n```\n\n## How it got in\n\nA semantic conflict between two PRs that were each green:\n\n- **#313** added tests asserting that `useBladeNavigationAdapter` calls\n`syncUrlPush` / `syncUrlReplace` after a stack mutation.\n- **#317** moved URL sync into the blade stack and deleted those calls\nfrom the adapter.\n\nNeither touched the other''s lines, so git merged them cleanly and no\nbranch-level CI caught it: #313 was green before #317 landed, #317 was\ngreen before #313 landed. The failure only exists in the merged state.\n\nWorth noting because the same trap is live for the remaining open PRs:\n**branch CI passing is not evidence that main will pass**, when two\nbranches change opposite sides of the same contract.\n\n## The fix\n\nDelete the `URL sync branches` describe block from the adapter test and\nthe two URL cases from the guards test. Six tests removed, of which only\nthree were failing: the other three were already **vacuous** after #317,\npassing only because zero calls trivially satisfies a\n`not.toHaveBeenCalled()` assertion.\n\n## Nothing is lost\n\n`useBladeStack.url.test.ts`, added by #317, covers the same ground at\nthe level where the behaviour now lives — 23 cases over the full verb\ntable. That includes the two defects the deleted tests were pinning for\nVM-1777:\n\n| deleted adapter test | stack-level equivalent |\n|---|---|\n| `closeBlade(0) rewrites the URL although the workspace never closes` |\n`closeBlade of the workspace still replaces` |\n| (VM-1777 defect 5, never pinned at adapter level) | `openWorkspace\nwith the same workspace still pushes` |\n\n## Kept deliberately\n\nThe `urlSync` module mock in both files. The adapter still imports\n`getTenantPrefix` from it; I removed the mock to check, and the\n`goToRoot` tenant-prefix case fails without it.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| adapter suites | 51 passed (was 54 passed / 3 failed) |\n| `yarn test:unit` | 4322 passed, 3 failing files are the known worktree\npath-resolution baseline (`VcScheduler.style`, `docs-sync/lint`,\n`mf-host/register-remote-modules`) |\n| `yarn typecheck` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn format:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn check:layers` | all pass |\n\nNet: 2 files, −64 lines.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjv6KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAD4QABCJwCha73NfDifqUH9EVHJp\nSgmfJ13hkrgmf2Y26Gg6MMjvJDjxuQaoiEFtEW82qyH7CBHEbWbj0miW7ZJvy8I3\nIcAcx0UrfP+35TOC7PpvE2i3E1RvutkxlMN/uobOgXwFKDcaZJlL2+RvWimVH3Ui\nUuHcBY/yzIH/+qVkvzhFYYOiaSMseW+xHrnXuWA4y/+wu2Qx1c8oGpKZPTUESYFZ\n9DSwhvygZoWNlG/XRnrs3rUo8CRFLQHSmsCaA+qYAY69bXXGY2QvkiD6VC8obNdI\n/5RMGLlMHdyppHwM1j+JaDk/SjSspZoKLx5//K+4ev5gTN3ZMCvPSOH1BGKQ6BrP\nTz1Ie6PnsVJsSjMLGOhjotI5Neu+ZTljP6+dRNpsgaYuutvAeKmdde8A8D5FFXEB\nbssAGzI8LGyvy7UgJ0PunmfbIx1sjV+a3/aQbDiW7QthkQlz4n9MMOaUgsnW7mzw\nKsVpJuPn98qSmVcqIXhK1012TQ4FZmGawoYtIyNXgWGCDw+zda2veCPyDYfvTV6N\nQnJCUv3w4J9wx18Er0d92mlNCRyBivV+RBnasscwsiHlE7RRxMljeuATkqVC3JZ+\nOOzsjFdvuajxb31IIwKFI8ZMOUVqZq4m/+WgS0bqf3ZWnWTpNoXqZ4x9x4T/08he\niMtSdIZ48Xqh6igtjEqu\n=CrWV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T14:56:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDVjMzU3NTI4OTUxM2IzODg0MWZiYWMwZDQ1ZGQxMzE5MzNhYjgyMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6","sha":"1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6"}],"sha":"5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5c3575289513b38841fbac0d45dd131933ab820b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:38:57Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:38:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(blade-navigation): make the blade stack own URL sync (VM-1761) (#317)\n\nVM-1761\n\n## The bug\n\nPressing <kbd>Esc</kbd> to close a blade left the address bar pointing\nat the blade that had just been closed. Reload, or copy the URL, and you\nwere back on a blade the user had already dismissed.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`vc-blade-navigation-new.vue` wires the keyboard dispatcher straight to\nthe stack:\n\n```ts\ncloseBlade: (id) => bladeStack.closeBlade(id),\n```\n\nEvery other close path in that same file pairs the mutation with\n`syncUrlReplace()`. This one did not. The existing dispatcher test did\nnot catch it because it drives `createShortcutDispatcher` with\n`closeBlade: vi.fn()`, so nothing downstream of the stack was exercised.\n\nThe real problem is duplication rather than a typo. \"Mutate the stack,\nthen sync the URL with the right verb\" was copied at **11 call sites**\nacross `useBlade`, the legacy navigation adapter and\n`VcBladeNavigation`. One of them was always going to be missed, and\nadding a twelfth call site would have been another chance to miss it.\n\n## The fix\n\n`createBladeStack` takes an optional `UrlSink` and syncs the URL itself\nafter every navigation action. Callers just mutate the stack.\n\n```ts\nexport interface UrlSink {\n  push(): void;\n  replace(): void;\n}\n\ncreateBladeStack(bladeRegistry, hasAccess?, urlSink?: UrlSink)  // defaults to a no-op sink\n```\n\nThe stack names the verb; the sink resolves the location. That split is\ndeliberate: the tenant prefix comes from\n`router.currentRoute.value.params`, so building the location is router\nknowledge and stays on the router side, in `createRouterUrlSink`.\n`createUrlSync` is now a thin wrapper over the same function, so there\nis exactly one place that turns a stack into a URL and the emitted URLs\nare unchanged.\n\n`plugin-v2` is the only production construction site and the only place\nthat has the router.\n\n## Verb table\n\nBehaviour is preserved one-for-one against the deleted call sites. The\ncondition is evaluated *after* the mutation; `hasUrl` means the\nresulting `activeBlade` has a `url` segment.\n\n| Action | Verb | Condition | Replaced call sites |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `openWorkspace` | push | `hasUrl` | `useBlade` `openBlade({\nisWorkspace })`; adapter `openBlade(args, true)` |\n| `openBlade` | push | `hasUrl` | `useBlade` `openBlade`; adapter\n`openBlade` |\n| `coverCurrentBlade` | push | `hasUrl` | `useBlade` `coverWith`;\nadapter `openBlade` with legacy `replaceCurrentBlade: true` |\n| `replaceCurrentBlade` | replace | `hasUrl` | `useBlade` `replaceWith`\n|\n| `closeBlade` | replace | returned `false` (not prevented) | `useBlade`\n`closeSelf`; adapter `closeBlade`; VcBladeNavigation breadcrumb,\n`onClose`, mobile back; **and the Esc path, which had none** |\n| `closeChildren` | replace | unconditional | `useBlade` `closeChildren`\n(its only caller) |\n\nThree details are easy to get wrong and are pinned by tests:\n\n- `closeChildren` replaces unconditionally, including when a guard\nprevents the close and when the parent id is unknown. That is what the\nold call site did.\n- `closeBlade` returns `false` for \"blade not found\" and \"is the\nworkspace\" as well as for a real close, and the old callers synced in\nall three cases.\n- The open verbs fire on non-throwing no-op paths too (`openWorkspace`\nwith the workspace already open, an open blocked by a child''s\nbefore-close guard). A throw still skips the sync, because it propagates\nbefore the sync runs.\n\nMutations that never synced still never sync: `updateBladeQuery`,\n`setBladeTitle`, `setBladeError`, `clearBladeError`, `_restoreStack`,\nthe maximized setters.\n\n## Router guard re-entrancy\n\n`bladeRouterGuard` mutates the stack from inside `router.beforeEach` —\n`clearBladeStackRespectingGuards` loops `closeBlade`, and\n`restoreFromUrl` calls `openWorkspace`/`openBlade`. Those produced zero\nrouter writes before, and a live sink would have made them write back\nfrom inside the guard.\n\n`createRouterUrlSink` exposes `suppressWhile`, and the plugin wraps the\nwhole guard in it: while a navigation is resolving, the URL is the\nsource and the stack does not write back. The guard''s own\n`needsUrlCleanup` redirect still works, because it is a return value\nrather than a sink write.\n\nSuppression is reference-counted, not save-and-restore. Two navigations\ncan overlap (vue-router cancels the pending one, but its async guard\nstill runs to completion, and `beforeClose` guards can hold a window\nopen on a confirmation dialog), and save-and-restore would either\nunsuppress while the other window is still open or leave suppression\nstuck on permanently. There is a regression test for the overlapping\ncase.\n\n## Non-breaking\n\n- The new `createBladeStack` parameter is optional and defaults to a\nfrozen no-op sink, so stacks built without a router (Storybook,\nstandalone mounts, the 11 existing test call sites) behave exactly as\nbefore with no edits.\n- `IBladeStack` gains no members.\n- `createUrlSync`, `buildUrlFromStack`, `parseBladeUrl`,\n`getTenantPrefix` and `buildQueryString` keep their names and\nsignatures. `createUrlSync` is not deprecated; it still has two live\ncallers.\n- `UrlSink`, `NOOP_URL_SINK`, `RouterUrlSink` and `createRouterUrlSink`\nare new, additive exports.\n- No component prop, emit, slot or `defineExpose` key changed. The\nlegacy `useBladeNavigation` surface is untouched.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **`useBladeStack.url.test.ts`** (new, 26 cases): a recording sink over\nthe verb table. Each case pins the verb, the number of writes, and the\nlocation the router would have received at the moment of the call.\nCovers blades with and without a `url`, prevented and unprevented\ncloses, the no-op and permission-denied paths, and that non-navigation\nmutations write nothing.\n- **`urlSync.test.ts`**: new coverage for `createRouterUrlSink`\n(location building, tenant prefix, lazy stack read) and `suppressWhile`\n(nesting, overlap, throw, and a real stack mutation inside the window\nwriting nothing while the next one writes exactly once). `createUrlSync`\ngets its first test.\n- **`vc-blade-navigation.dispatch.test.ts`**: \"Esc closes the blade AND\nreplaces the URL\", driving a real stack with a recording sink instead of\na mocked `closeBlade`. This fails on `main` with `[] !== [\"replace\n/orders\"]`, which is the bug.\n- No existing test needed an edit. `useBlade.test.ts` never asserted URL\nsync, and the adapter test mocks `createUrlSync` without asserting on\nit.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `yarn typecheck` | pass |\n| `yarn lint:check` | pass |\n| `yarn format:check` | pass |\n| `yarn stylelint:check` | pass |\n| `yarn check:circular` | `No circular dependency found` (the stack\nimports no router) |\n| `yarn check:layers` | all 3 checks pass |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | 0 errors, 6 pre-existing warnings |\n| `yarn test:unit` | 4264 passed, 1 failed |\n| `yarn build:framework && yarn test:storybook` | 77 files, 616 passed |\n\nThe single unit failure is `cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts`, a\npre-existing path bug that only reproduces when the checkout lives under\n`.claude/` (it resolves\n`<repo>/.claude/cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/vc-app.md`). It fails\nidentically with these changes stashed. Storybook is unchanged, as\nexpected for a behaviour-preserving change outside the Esc fix.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- `VcBladeNavigation` keeps its own `createUrlSync` for one write that\nis not a stack mutation: the `onMounted` post-restore reconcile, which\nrebuilds the URL after restored blades hydrate their table query into\ntheir descriptors.\n- The `restoreFromUrl` idempotency bail is untouched here.\n- Both are tracked in VM-1762.","tree":{"sha":"80d134a1221c9fcd852257e2f049c16638678da1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/80d134a1221c9fcd852257e2f049c16638678da1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6","verification":{"payload":"tree 80d134a1221c9fcd852257e2f049c16638678da1\nparent 2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787744337 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787744337 +0300\n\nfix(blade-navigation): make the blade stack own URL sync (VM-1761) (#317)\n\nVM-1761\n\n## The bug\n\nPressing <kbd>Esc</kbd> to close a blade left the address bar pointing\nat the blade that had just been closed. Reload, or copy the URL, and you\nwere back on a blade the user had already dismissed.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`vc-blade-navigation-new.vue` wires the keyboard dispatcher straight to\nthe stack:\n\n```ts\ncloseBlade: (id) => bladeStack.closeBlade(id),\n```\n\nEvery other close path in that same file pairs the mutation with\n`syncUrlReplace()`. This one did not. The existing dispatcher test did\nnot catch it because it drives `createShortcutDispatcher` with\n`closeBlade: vi.fn()`, so nothing downstream of the stack was exercised.\n\nThe real problem is duplication rather than a typo. \"Mutate the stack,\nthen sync the URL with the right verb\" was copied at **11 call sites**\nacross `useBlade`, the legacy navigation adapter and\n`VcBladeNavigation`. One of them was always going to be missed, and\nadding a twelfth call site would have been another chance to miss it.\n\n## The fix\n\n`createBladeStack` takes an optional `UrlSink` and syncs the URL itself\nafter every navigation action. Callers just mutate the stack.\n\n```ts\nexport interface UrlSink {\n  push(): void;\n  replace(): void;\n}\n\ncreateBladeStack(bladeRegistry, hasAccess?, urlSink?: UrlSink)  // defaults to a no-op sink\n```\n\nThe stack names the verb; the sink resolves the location. That split is\ndeliberate: the tenant prefix comes from\n`router.currentRoute.value.params`, so building the location is router\nknowledge and stays on the router side, in `createRouterUrlSink`.\n`createUrlSync` is now a thin wrapper over the same function, so there\nis exactly one place that turns a stack into a URL and the emitted URLs\nare unchanged.\n\n`plugin-v2` is the only production construction site and the only place\nthat has the router.\n\n## Verb table\n\nBehaviour is preserved one-for-one against the deleted call sites. The\ncondition is evaluated *after* the mutation; `hasUrl` means the\nresulting `activeBlade` has a `url` segment.\n\n| Action | Verb | Condition | Replaced call sites |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `openWorkspace` | push | `hasUrl` | `useBlade` `openBlade({\nisWorkspace })`; adapter `openBlade(args, true)` |\n| `openBlade` | push | `hasUrl` | `useBlade` `openBlade`; adapter\n`openBlade` |\n| `coverCurrentBlade` | push | `hasUrl` | `useBlade` `coverWith`;\nadapter `openBlade` with legacy `replaceCurrentBlade: true` |\n| `replaceCurrentBlade` | replace | `hasUrl` | `useBlade` `replaceWith`\n|\n| `closeBlade` | replace | returned `false` (not prevented) | `useBlade`\n`closeSelf`; adapter `closeBlade`; VcBladeNavigation breadcrumb,\n`onClose`, mobile back; **and the Esc path, which had none** |\n| `closeChildren` | replace | unconditional | `useBlade` `closeChildren`\n(its only caller) |\n\nThree details are easy to get wrong and are pinned by tests:\n\n- `closeChildren` replaces unconditionally, including when a guard\nprevents the close and when the parent id is unknown. That is what the\nold call site did.\n- `closeBlade` returns `false` for \"blade not found\" and \"is the\nworkspace\" as well as for a real close, and the old callers synced in\nall three cases.\n- The open verbs fire on non-throwing no-op paths too (`openWorkspace`\nwith the workspace already open, an open blocked by a child''s\nbefore-close guard). A throw still skips the sync, because it propagates\nbefore the sync runs.\n\nMutations that never synced still never sync: `updateBladeQuery`,\n`setBladeTitle`, `setBladeError`, `clearBladeError`, `_restoreStack`,\nthe maximized setters.\n\n## Router guard re-entrancy\n\n`bladeRouterGuard` mutates the stack from inside `router.beforeEach` —\n`clearBladeStackRespectingGuards` loops `closeBlade`, and\n`restoreFromUrl` calls `openWorkspace`/`openBlade`. Those produced zero\nrouter writes before, and a live sink would have made them write back\nfrom inside the guard.\n\n`createRouterUrlSink` exposes `suppressWhile`, and the plugin wraps the\nwhole guard in it: while a navigation is resolving, the URL is the\nsource and the stack does not write back. The guard''s own\n`needsUrlCleanup` redirect still works, because it is a return value\nrather than a sink write.\n\nSuppression is reference-counted, not save-and-restore. Two navigations\ncan overlap (vue-router cancels the pending one, but its async guard\nstill runs to completion, and `beforeClose` guards can hold a window\nopen on a confirmation dialog), and save-and-restore would either\nunsuppress while the other window is still open or leave suppression\nstuck on permanently. There is a regression test for the overlapping\ncase.\n\n## Non-breaking\n\n- The new `createBladeStack` parameter is optional and defaults to a\nfrozen no-op sink, so stacks built without a router (Storybook,\nstandalone mounts, the 11 existing test call sites) behave exactly as\nbefore with no edits.\n- `IBladeStack` gains no members.\n- `createUrlSync`, `buildUrlFromStack`, `parseBladeUrl`,\n`getTenantPrefix` and `buildQueryString` keep their names and\nsignatures. `createUrlSync` is not deprecated; it still has two live\ncallers.\n- `UrlSink`, `NOOP_URL_SINK`, `RouterUrlSink` and `createRouterUrlSink`\nare new, additive exports.\n- No component prop, emit, slot or `defineExpose` key changed. The\nlegacy `useBladeNavigation` surface is untouched.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **`useBladeStack.url.test.ts`** (new, 26 cases): a recording sink over\nthe verb table. Each case pins the verb, the number of writes, and the\nlocation the router would have received at the moment of the call.\nCovers blades with and without a `url`, prevented and unprevented\ncloses, the no-op and permission-denied paths, and that non-navigation\nmutations write nothing.\n- **`urlSync.test.ts`**: new coverage for `createRouterUrlSink`\n(location building, tenant prefix, lazy stack read) and `suppressWhile`\n(nesting, overlap, throw, and a real stack mutation inside the window\nwriting nothing while the next one writes exactly once). `createUrlSync`\ngets its first test.\n- **`vc-blade-navigation.dispatch.test.ts`**: \"Esc closes the blade AND\nreplaces the URL\", driving a real stack with a recording sink instead of\na mocked `closeBlade`. This fails on `main` with `[] !== [\"replace\n/orders\"]`, which is the bug.\n- No existing test needed an edit. `useBlade.test.ts` never asserted URL\nsync, and the adapter test mocks `createUrlSync` without asserting on\nit.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `yarn typecheck` | pass |\n| `yarn lint:check` | pass |\n| `yarn format:check` | pass |\n| `yarn stylelint:check` | pass |\n| `yarn check:circular` | `No circular dependency found` (the stack\nimports no router) |\n| `yarn check:layers` | all 3 checks pass |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | 0 errors, 6 pre-existing warnings |\n| `yarn test:unit` | 4264 passed, 1 failed |\n| `yarn build:framework && yarn test:storybook` | 77 files, 616 passed |\n\nThe single unit failure is `cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts`, a\npre-existing path bug that only reproduces when the checkout lives under\n`.claude/` (it resolves\n`<repo>/.claude/cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/vc-app.md`). It fails\nidentically with these changes stashed. Storybook is unchanged, as\nexpected for a behaviour-preserving change outside the Esc fix.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- `VcBladeNavigation` keeps its own `createUrlSync` for one write that\nis not a stack mutation: the `onMounted` post-restore reconcile, which\nrebuilds the URL after restored blades hydrate their table query into\ntheir descriptors.\n- The `restoreFromUrl` idempotency bail is untouched here.\n- Both are tracked in VM-1762.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjtBRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/3QQAA5TZmb7aoenUc/JPDp6T0eF\nvpBxa5tuMMCh3ZJQVCK4L5pSNHga4TfjCPhtLZRJoONz3TPpEX4H8hWj6eNN7uY/\nk3jaJ5Twjd8dYIHRTIyxR2b2n7ud2CwMLFYWeQYhHH/eDZH4UsnPX23Zv6ICHg4+\nEG/oQrktns9otgzO8+X2rOp0AT10DY430nqLBxjcNrdk7uFa+PLJJolL8ceZjg9R\nUjWG0NGxRyTrMlF9E7VKv5/QR0Hisn4k/tBpmAAtxTsn2AL6SU9EC/SkX4bd06YC\nBQ+ziBgNueRDSg7MoE4CFkqo1ZbSErWOPVgnPPQ97ouRqp1+xWyTidG3dka1pSFg\nQwK9KI4YapfghNxpStNwwT9/7D/EZ30nuwYFk498GKND8jUcsGj42AYG2eQ/FO1y\nGPFfnQmy1P4AyHg/kqkdlNPI1lg98ZBBqqSKxuecjiYBUwdz5r3DjUL1wxIIWotx\n2Dqv10UvBIdJT20pu72jHAhlSSrbblzbWAI7ox2udb969rDBGd3Mj6cHHfk+uMg8\nvfrxsyc/e25+H3mmyv6Jv2fF/yzvnU1hEdBrMbxYP0RhYpSjUxJ5o9Kitft6bqd5\nph72/jVmFgdYCctkntAvaHOijx6H/GBZvct+YbKe8aMU4uT547TRLs9d1vPCQC7D\nyPwVpqR4B3eOGNtgy8At\n=rmUA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T11:38:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDFhMWVlY2Y1YzQyZWVhZDFjMzI4YjFmNDcyMWRmZWU2ZGZmOGZmYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700","sha":"2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700"}],"sha":"1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/1a1eecf5c42eead1c328b1f4721dfee6dff8ffa6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:33:16Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:33:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-data-table): export useCellRegistry and register built-in cells once (VM-1756) (#316)\n\nVM-1756\n\n## Problem\n\n`useCellRegistry` is documented as the extension point for custom cell\ntypes — it even ships a `CellRating` example in its docblock — but it\ncould not be imported from the package. The only barrel re-exporting it\nwas `vc-data-table/utils/index.ts`, which nothing in the repo imports,\nso no path reached `framework/index.ts`.\n\nSeparately, the 12 built-in cell registrations lived in the `<script\nsetup>` body of `DynamicCellRenderer.vue`. Because `<script setup>`\ncompiles to `setup()`, those `register()` calls ran on the component''s\n**first mount**, not on import. Any consumer calling\n`useCellRegistry().get(\"money\")` before a table had rendered got\n`undefined`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Export the extension point.** `vc-data-table/index.ts` now\nre-exports `useCellRegistry`, `registerBuiltinCells`,\n`BUILTIN_CELL_TYPES` and the types `CellType`, `BuiltinCellType`,\n`CellTypeConfig`, `CellRegistration`, `UseCellRegistryReturn`. No other\nbarrel needed editing — `organisms/index.ts` → `@ui/components` →\n`framework/index.ts` already carries them.\n- **Register built-ins at module scope.** The 12 registrations move into\n`composables/builtinCells.ts` as `registerBuiltinCells()`, called once\nfrom a plain module-scope `<script lang=\"ts\">` block in\n`DynamicCellRenderer.vue`. Importing the component is now enough; mount\norder no longer matters.\n- **One cell-type union instead of three.** Exporting the registry is\npointless if the exported type rejects the names it exists for, so\n`CellType` is now the 12 built-in literals plus `(string & {})`. It\nlives in `useCellRegistry.ts`, and the two near-identical unions that\nhad drifted alongside it — `VcColumnCellType` in `types.ts` and the\nlocal one in `VcColumn.vue` — become aliases of it. Built-in names keep\nautocomplete. A new narrow `BuiltinCellType` constrains the built-in\nregistration table, so a typo *there* is still a compile error.\n- **Dev warning for unresolved types.** Since a misspelt built-in now\ncompiles and falls back to `CellDefault`, an unresolved type logs a\nwarning naming the type, once per name, in dev builds.\n- Docs: a \"Custom Cell Types\" section in `vc-data-table.docs.md` with\nthe registry API table.\n- Story: `CustomRegisteredCellType` appended to\n`vc-data-table.cell-types.stories.ts`, registering at module scope the\nway an app would.\n- Tests: new `composables/builtinCells.test.ts` (7 cases).\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo public export removed or renamed, no prop/emit/slot/`defineExpose`\nkey changed. Storybook snapshots byte-identical.\n\nTwo behaviour notes worth naming:\n\n- **`clear()` is now permanent.** Registration used to re-run in every\n`DynamicCellRenderer` `setup()`, so a runtime `clear()` self-healed on\nthe next cell mount. It now runs once per module load. Documented in the\nnew docs section.\n- **`VcColumnCellType` is widened.** Every name that was valid before\nstill is, so this is additive for callers passing values in. Code that\ntreats the union as closed — a `switch` with a `never` exhaustiveness\ncheck, or a `Record<VcColumnCellType, T>` mapped type — would need a\ndefault branch. No such use exists in this repo.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll run in a clean worktree off `origin/main`.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `yarn typecheck` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint:check` | exit 0 (`--max-warnings=0`) |\n| `yarn format:check` | `All matched files use Prettier code style!` |\n| `yarn stylelint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn test:unit` | `Test Files 5 failed \\| 470 passed (475)` / `Tests\n3 failed \\| 4233 passed (4236)` — see note |\n| `yarn build:framework && yarn test:storybook` | `Test Files 77 passed\n(77)` / `Tests 617 passed (617)`, no `.snap` file modified |\n| `yarn check:circular` | `✔ No circular dependency found!` |\n| `yarn check:layers` | `All layer checks passed.` |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | `0 errors, 6 warnings` (warnings pre-existing, in\nuntouched files) |\n\n**On the failing unit tests.** Three files fail identically on an\nunmodified checkout of this worktree (verified by stashing every change\nand re-running): `vc-scheduler/VcScheduler.style.test.ts`,\n`packages/mf-host/src/register-remote-modules.test.ts` and\n`cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts`. They are path-resolution failures\ncaused by running from a `git worktree` directory. The other two —\n`useConnectionStatus` and `useNotificationStore` — are the known\ntimeouts under parallel load; run on their own they pass (`Test Files 2\npassed`, `Tests 22 passed`). None of the five touch `vc-data-table`.\n\n**Type-level checks against the built `dist`**, since the point of the\nPR is what consumers can write:\n\n- `const t: CellType = \"rating\"`, `const t: VcColumnCellType =\n\"rating\"`, and `{ type: \"rating\" } satisfies Pick<VcColumnProps,\n\"type\">` all compile under `--strict`.\n- `BUILTIN_CELL_TYPES.includes(\"rating\")` compiles.\n- `const b: BuiltinCellType = \"rating\"` correctly fails with TS2322 —\nthe narrow union stayed narrow.\n- Introducing a typo in the built-in table (`\"mony\"`) fails with TS2820\n\"Did you mean ''money''?\".\n- A probe SFC using `<VcColumn type=\"rating\" />` with a runtime\n`register()` passes `yarn typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe docs section deliberately has no `::storybook` embed. `docs:lint`''s\n`storybook-id-valid` rule validates ids against the published Storybook\nat `vc-shell-storybook.govirto.com`, so a brand-new story id cannot pass\nin the same PR. The embed can be added once this story is published.\n\nTwo things left alone, flagged for a reviewer''s judgement:\n`builtinCells.ts` sits in `composables/` rather than\n`components/cells/`, which is arguable but keeps it next to the registry\nit populates; and there is a pre-existing orphaned JSDoc block at\n`vc-data-table.cell-types.stories.ts:409-418` that predates this change.","tree":{"sha":"70c4ccba0f745706288514f0d2031c8998684628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/70c4ccba0f745706288514f0d2031c8998684628"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700","verification":{"payload":"tree 70c4ccba0f745706288514f0d2031c8998684628\nparent 61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787743996 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787743996 +0300\n\nfix(vc-data-table): export useCellRegistry and register built-in cells once (VM-1756) (#316)\n\nVM-1756\n\n## Problem\n\n`useCellRegistry` is documented as the extension point for custom cell\ntypes — it even ships a `CellRating` example in its docblock — but it\ncould not be imported from the package. The only barrel re-exporting it\nwas `vc-data-table/utils/index.ts`, which nothing in the repo imports,\nso no path reached `framework/index.ts`.\n\nSeparately, the 12 built-in cell registrations lived in the `<script\nsetup>` body of `DynamicCellRenderer.vue`. Because `<script setup>`\ncompiles to `setup()`, those `register()` calls ran on the component''s\n**first mount**, not on import. Any consumer calling\n`useCellRegistry().get(\"money\")` before a table had rendered got\n`undefined`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Export the extension point.** `vc-data-table/index.ts` now\nre-exports `useCellRegistry`, `registerBuiltinCells`,\n`BUILTIN_CELL_TYPES` and the types `CellType`, `BuiltinCellType`,\n`CellTypeConfig`, `CellRegistration`, `UseCellRegistryReturn`. No other\nbarrel needed editing — `organisms/index.ts` → `@ui/components` →\n`framework/index.ts` already carries them.\n- **Register built-ins at module scope.** The 12 registrations move into\n`composables/builtinCells.ts` as `registerBuiltinCells()`, called once\nfrom a plain module-scope `<script lang=\"ts\">` block in\n`DynamicCellRenderer.vue`. Importing the component is now enough; mount\norder no longer matters.\n- **One cell-type union instead of three.** Exporting the registry is\npointless if the exported type rejects the names it exists for, so\n`CellType` is now the 12 built-in literals plus `(string & {})`. It\nlives in `useCellRegistry.ts`, and the two near-identical unions that\nhad drifted alongside it — `VcColumnCellType` in `types.ts` and the\nlocal one in `VcColumn.vue` — become aliases of it. Built-in names keep\nautocomplete. A new narrow `BuiltinCellType` constrains the built-in\nregistration table, so a typo *there* is still a compile error.\n- **Dev warning for unresolved types.** Since a misspelt built-in now\ncompiles and falls back to `CellDefault`, an unresolved type logs a\nwarning naming the type, once per name, in dev builds.\n- Docs: a \"Custom Cell Types\" section in `vc-data-table.docs.md` with\nthe registry API table.\n- Story: `CustomRegisteredCellType` appended to\n`vc-data-table.cell-types.stories.ts`, registering at module scope the\nway an app would.\n- Tests: new `composables/builtinCells.test.ts` (7 cases).\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo public export removed or renamed, no prop/emit/slot/`defineExpose`\nkey changed. Storybook snapshots byte-identical.\n\nTwo behaviour notes worth naming:\n\n- **`clear()` is now permanent.** Registration used to re-run in every\n`DynamicCellRenderer` `setup()`, so a runtime `clear()` self-healed on\nthe next cell mount. It now runs once per module load. Documented in the\nnew docs section.\n- **`VcColumnCellType` is widened.** Every name that was valid before\nstill is, so this is additive for callers passing values in. Code that\ntreats the union as closed — a `switch` with a `never` exhaustiveness\ncheck, or a `Record<VcColumnCellType, T>` mapped type — would need a\ndefault branch. No such use exists in this repo.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll run in a clean worktree off `origin/main`.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `yarn typecheck` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint:check` | exit 0 (`--max-warnings=0`) |\n| `yarn format:check` | `All matched files use Prettier code style!` |\n| `yarn stylelint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn test:unit` | `Test Files 5 failed \\| 470 passed (475)` / `Tests\n3 failed \\| 4233 passed (4236)` — see note |\n| `yarn build:framework && yarn test:storybook` | `Test Files 77 passed\n(77)` / `Tests 617 passed (617)`, no `.snap` file modified |\n| `yarn check:circular` | `✔ No circular dependency found!` |\n| `yarn check:layers` | `All layer checks passed.` |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | `0 errors, 6 warnings` (warnings pre-existing, in\nuntouched files) |\n\n**On the failing unit tests.** Three files fail identically on an\nunmodified checkout of this worktree (verified by stashing every change\nand re-running): `vc-scheduler/VcScheduler.style.test.ts`,\n`packages/mf-host/src/register-remote-modules.test.ts` and\n`cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts`. They are path-resolution failures\ncaused by running from a `git worktree` directory. The other two —\n`useConnectionStatus` and `useNotificationStore` — are the known\ntimeouts under parallel load; run on their own they pass (`Test Files 2\npassed`, `Tests 22 passed`). None of the five touch `vc-data-table`.\n\n**Type-level checks against the built `dist`**, since the point of the\nPR is what consumers can write:\n\n- `const t: CellType = \"rating\"`, `const t: VcColumnCellType =\n\"rating\"`, and `{ type: \"rating\" } satisfies Pick<VcColumnProps,\n\"type\">` all compile under `--strict`.\n- `BUILTIN_CELL_TYPES.includes(\"rating\")` compiles.\n- `const b: BuiltinCellType = \"rating\"` correctly fails with TS2322 —\nthe narrow union stayed narrow.\n- Introducing a typo in the built-in table (`\"mony\"`) fails with TS2820\n\"Did you mean ''money''?\".\n- A probe SFC using `<VcColumn type=\"rating\" />` with a runtime\n`register()` passes `yarn typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe docs section deliberately has no `::storybook` embed. `docs:lint`''s\n`storybook-id-valid` rule validates ids against the published Storybook\nat `vc-shell-storybook.govirto.com`, so a brand-new story id cannot pass\nin the same PR. The embed can be added once this story is published.\n\nTwo things left alone, flagged for a reviewer''s judgement:\n`builtinCells.ts` sits in `composables/` rather than\n`components/cells/`, which is arguable but keeps it next to the registry\nit populates; and there is a pre-existing orphaned JSDoc block at\n`vc-data-table.cell-types.stories.ts:409-418` that predates this change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjs78CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKAIQAJnx86mvIT42L4U1yJKGWF8/\n30QVeLoUihd3qYRaDkAQKVN/Ew59c5wLjEmCkE17+vUs/yvliOB9HrZm07btTfe0\nDKIylItrnV5RdcuNQVj1cAq6GToMzsqNLi9CBOq7XIRAmmZS0BvbnaPQSIDP5pVU\ntmZIIHbb33ztNVsc/k5L2C13K6CFPU02isRTfXv2k46UK7BhV0WZ5weyi7QmUhzw\nYj4uCvImOxNgPqle1T5fa8QWTP47+vI+We/fTLLD9FpRV4QKEwNV2fvDquE6TXRY\npMboPN7NJ1ZY/gvOKZa+sKHRz+ReylqfszS4HotwAEv4L7c94Wq4tfoxYOQkIAxW\nl3h/d3RjK1Agdzk6C038xNkyppDAv6Siue3GqKKVzinqMDrk6c1AetLnYwq0crHf\nt21IZ7/GOvKkhwHlh4Pt4MMC43uWivvuV4LxnwgIJMOCJNu0JXi1ik8lHAPoubun\nSzWwR0kCgv4Jnae95IzmUJp1rPUy65k16ziKtitHnhZXJNeMTnerxmSaUmAy9XNy\n7cI8kczxQvjayyAWBAmm2HL50O8lCWJeOx6SceYd0Z5BBPEBzS0sg5QX0ngEZhYo\nvbKl50ikvloqfANbTThRbQ6oJqWCo0e85IssrCt9wOpX02Ykkdqwr6dlBy/ZuH8e\n3a4nsKAzoUV++iGgyhaf\n=ODk3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T11:33:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDJiNGUwMDQ0MDJkZGQxNDg4YTE4Mzg3ZjdkMmM5OGUwZmQ5NDA3MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c","sha":"61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c"}],"sha":"2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2b4e004402ddd1488a18387f7d2c98e0fd940700"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:18:29Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:18:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(sidebar): fold useMenuExpanded into useSidebarState (VM-1758) (#314)\n\n## Why\n\nSidebar pin/hover state was split across two composables.\n`useSidebarState` called `useMenuExpanded()` and renamed four of its\nmembers, so the app-scoped `localStorage` key, the 200 ms hover debounce\nand the hover ref all lived one module away from the state the shell\nactually reads.\n\nThat split hid a real hazard: `isHoverExpanded` is a fresh `ref(false)`\nper `useMenuExpanded()` call (only the pinned state was shared, and only\nbecause VueUse syncs same-key `useLocalStorage` refs). Anything calling\n`useMenuExpanded()` directly got a *different* hover ref from the one\nthe sidebar renders from. It also left a stale comment claiming\n`UserDropdownButton` depends on that delegation — it does not, it uses\n`useSidebarState()`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`useSidebarState` owns the behaviour.** The storage key, the hover\ndebounce and the `onScopeDispose` cleanup now live in\n`useSidebarState/_internal.ts`. `provideSidebarState()` builds the\nsingle instance the tree injects, so two consumers can no longer\ndiverge.\n- **`useMenuExpanded` is a `@deprecated` adapter.** Identical return\nshape (`isExpanded`, `toggleExpanded`, `isHoverExpanded`,\n`toggleHoverExpanded`) and identical runtime behaviour, mapped onto the\nshared implementation. It still builds its own instance, because it is\npublic and may be called outside the `VcApp` tree where no provider\nexists.\n- **New export `sidebarStorageKey(appName?)`** so callers stop\nrebuilding the key string by hand. `vc-app-shell.stories.ts` dropped its\nlocal copy; its 8 call sites now share one source of truth.\n- Docs updated for both composables; the stale delegation claim is gone.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo breaking changes. Verified against the emitted `.d.ts`:\n\n- `useMenuExpanded/index.d.ts` is surface-identical to `main` —\n`UseMenuExpandedReturn` with the same four members,\n`toggleHoverExpanded: (shouldExpand?: boolean) => void`.\n- `useSidebarState/index.d.ts` still exports `SidebarState`,\n`SidebarActions`, `UseSidebarStateReturn`, `SidebarStateReturn`,\n`provideSidebarState`, `useSidebarState` — nothing removed or retyped.\n`SidebarActions.setHoverExpanded` is still `(value: boolean) => void`.\n`sidebarStorageKey` is the only addition.\n- The factory and its widened type stay in `_internal.ts`, which no\npublic barrel re-exports, so neither reaches `@vc-shell/framework`.\n- Debounce parity is line-by-line: truthiness gate, the `else if (value\n=== false)` branch, the `!==` guard inside the timeout and `HOVER_DELAY\n= 200` are unchanged. The only delta is nulling `expandTimeout` after\n`clearTimeout`, which is not observable.\n\n**The 9 pre-existing `useMenuExpanded` tests pass unedited** — that is\nthe compatibility proof. The diff on that file is a pure append.\n\n## Tests\n\n`useSidebarState/index.test.ts` goes from 7 cases to 20. It no longer\nmocks `useMenuExpanded` (the dependency is gone), which strengthens it:\nthe old mock stubbed the debounce and localStorage out of existence, so\nthe `isExpanded` case was asserting against `ref(false)` stubs. Those\npaths now run for real against jsdom `localStorage` and fake timers.\nAdded: storage-key derivation (explicit name, path-derived, empty\nfallback), pinned-state persistence and read-back, the full hover\ndebounce table, scope-dispose cleanup, and shared-instance invariants.\n\n## Gates\n\n| Gate | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `yarn typecheck` | pass (exit 0) |\n| `yarn lint:check` | pass (exit 0) |\n| `yarn format:check` | pass — \"All matched files use Prettier code\nstyle!\" |\n| `yarn stylelint:check` | pass (exit 0) |\n| `yarn test:unit` | 4242 passed / 1 failed (474 files: 471 passed, 3\nfailed) — see below |\n| `yarn build:framework` | pass (exit 0) |\n| `yarn test:storybook` | **616 passed (77 files)**, snapshots\nbyte-identical (no snapshot file written or changed) |\n| `yarn check:circular` | pass — \"No circular dependency found!\" (705\nfiles) |\n| `yarn check:layers` | pass — all 3 layer checks |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | 0 errors, 6 warnings (all pre-existing, unrelated\nfiles) |\n\nThe 3 `test:unit` file failures are environmental, not from this change.\nThey are `cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts`,\n`vc-scheduler/VcScheduler.style.test.ts` and\n`packages/mf-host/src/register-remote-modules.test.ts` — all resolve\nfixture paths relative to `process.cwd()`, which breaks in a git\nworktree. Confirmed by stashing this branch and running the same command\non pristine `main` in the same worktree: **5 failed files / 3 failed\ntests** there (the same 3, plus the known-flaky `useConnectionStatus`\nand `useNotificationStore` timeouts). This branch is strictly better\nthan its own baseline, and touches none of those files.","tree":{"sha":"283303cb35d6f9ef219020b438e4eee43aae1796","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/283303cb35d6f9ef219020b438e4eee43aae1796"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c","verification":{"payload":"tree 283303cb35d6f9ef219020b438e4eee43aae1796\nparent a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787743109 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787743109 +0300\n\nrefactor(sidebar): fold useMenuExpanded into useSidebarState (VM-1758) (#314)\n\n## Why\n\nSidebar pin/hover state was split across two composables.\n`useSidebarState` called `useMenuExpanded()` and renamed four of its\nmembers, so the app-scoped `localStorage` key, the 200 ms hover debounce\nand the hover ref all lived one module away from the state the shell\nactually reads.\n\nThat split hid a real hazard: `isHoverExpanded` is a fresh `ref(false)`\nper `useMenuExpanded()` call (only the pinned state was shared, and only\nbecause VueUse syncs same-key `useLocalStorage` refs). Anything calling\n`useMenuExpanded()` directly got a *different* hover ref from the one\nthe sidebar renders from. It also left a stale comment claiming\n`UserDropdownButton` depends on that delegation — it does not, it uses\n`useSidebarState()`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`useSidebarState` owns the behaviour.** The storage key, the hover\ndebounce and the `onScopeDispose` cleanup now live in\n`useSidebarState/_internal.ts`. `provideSidebarState()` builds the\nsingle instance the tree injects, so two consumers can no longer\ndiverge.\n- **`useMenuExpanded` is a `@deprecated` adapter.** Identical return\nshape (`isExpanded`, `toggleExpanded`, `isHoverExpanded`,\n`toggleHoverExpanded`) and identical runtime behaviour, mapped onto the\nshared implementation. It still builds its own instance, because it is\npublic and may be called outside the `VcApp` tree where no provider\nexists.\n- **New export `sidebarStorageKey(appName?)`** so callers stop\nrebuilding the key string by hand. `vc-app-shell.stories.ts` dropped its\nlocal copy; its 8 call sites now share one source of truth.\n- Docs updated for both composables; the stale delegation claim is gone.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo breaking changes. Verified against the emitted `.d.ts`:\n\n- `useMenuExpanded/index.d.ts` is surface-identical to `main` —\n`UseMenuExpandedReturn` with the same four members,\n`toggleHoverExpanded: (shouldExpand?: boolean) => void`.\n- `useSidebarState/index.d.ts` still exports `SidebarState`,\n`SidebarActions`, `UseSidebarStateReturn`, `SidebarStateReturn`,\n`provideSidebarState`, `useSidebarState` — nothing removed or retyped.\n`SidebarActions.setHoverExpanded` is still `(value: boolean) => void`.\n`sidebarStorageKey` is the only addition.\n- The factory and its widened type stay in `_internal.ts`, which no\npublic barrel re-exports, so neither reaches `@vc-shell/framework`.\n- Debounce parity is line-by-line: truthiness gate, the `else if (value\n=== false)` branch, the `!==` guard inside the timeout and `HOVER_DELAY\n= 200` are unchanged. The only delta is nulling `expandTimeout` after\n`clearTimeout`, which is not observable.\n\n**The 9 pre-existing `useMenuExpanded` tests pass unedited** — that is\nthe compatibility proof. The diff on that file is a pure append.\n\n## Tests\n\n`useSidebarState/index.test.ts` goes from 7 cases to 20. It no longer\nmocks `useMenuExpanded` (the dependency is gone), which strengthens it:\nthe old mock stubbed the debounce and localStorage out of existence, so\nthe `isExpanded` case was asserting against `ref(false)` stubs. Those\npaths now run for real against jsdom `localStorage` and fake timers.\nAdded: storage-key derivation (explicit name, path-derived, empty\nfallback), pinned-state persistence and read-back, the full hover\ndebounce table, scope-dispose cleanup, and shared-instance invariants.\n\n## Gates\n\n| Gate | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `yarn typecheck` | pass (exit 0) |\n| `yarn lint:check` | pass (exit 0) |\n| `yarn format:check` | pass — \"All matched files use Prettier code\nstyle!\" |\n| `yarn stylelint:check` | pass (exit 0) |\n| `yarn test:unit` | 4242 passed / 1 failed (474 files: 471 passed, 3\nfailed) — see below |\n| `yarn build:framework` | pass (exit 0) |\n| `yarn test:storybook` | **616 passed (77 files)**, snapshots\nbyte-identical (no snapshot file written or changed) |\n| `yarn check:circular` | pass — \"No circular dependency found!\" (705\nfiles) |\n| `yarn check:layers` | pass — all 3 layer checks |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | 0 errors, 6 warnings (all pre-existing, unrelated\nfiles) |\n\nThe 3 `test:unit` file failures are environmental, not from this change.\nThey are `cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts`,\n`vc-scheduler/VcScheduler.style.test.ts` and\n`packages/mf-host/src/register-remote-modules.test.ts` — all resolve\nfixture paths relative to `process.cwd()`, which breaks in a git\nworktree. Confirmed by stashing this branch and running the same command\non pristine `main` in the same worktree: **5 failed files / 3 failed\ntests** there (the same 3, plus the known-flaky `useConnectionStatus`\nand `useNotificationStore` timeouts). This branch is strictly better\nthan its own baseline, and touches none of those files.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjsuFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC8cQABUc1REFJU+wnGU1/OikQxjz\n1V7NbqpuD9mBBnpQBefnjiw/8KmkV08e7jfyTqHs9m3sXDQg1702DZHe0Gbmrwcm\n/Bp6dEtB3kzhP8BP3XrW4xh+WYz5TesCZvWZp1dYPuznyvQ7fE5hs7wlv7t9WtfJ\nf+bE52LBOd6zn61PrvJBD0eMl3kcs3wJucuLkJRYf6jQNNc5oPt/K/ejIIJxFjjo\ndA3mFnzHg7v9TZGwjT4HHfNZbomH1qsQiXIamn/UG5Ua5FW30isMBQTcu1pPCesd\nNuDyFCpq8CuvYxnET/ngKSmupJKtCq7szMeFT2wUv9flobc2/JC2JyBpxYXThdsF\nHnEiFuVvFbsBxAVuQZ3YGf4RlOSnZZ0n5NPP0hsq92l4K99u7ZP0Aipe4DweOuCo\nAOI9HC8gUgJRoVxzPAjW9QKArGTGwc2V1rfZXjARv//xxugRBFAYzxYxM/q/aUvK\nu6lmOUho5X6aNO2ASNMHZesn2ycJeh71424477QJwnXSsrjFT1o3GMDSN2F4Xuta\nHdoAY7EyVOCRrSq6qI69RFX9nv1D1wlTn6G/j4HyvBTaUvDCH0hB9LLq3HuxD1Y5\nwOz3RYgAJjlmj9SL9Lo4spi9coccgTxnnFu8JK4WZRVo65q1LH37YfoVSVQp/k5u\nb+K/X1aO5Qvi1Cn5087M\n=HSlp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T11:18:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDYxZDRiOTNmMWM3MDhkYWQ0YmYwYzIwYzY1YTgzZTAwMDUyMzQ1NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04","sha":"a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04"}],"sha":"61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/61d4b93f1c708dad4bf0c20c65a83e000523455c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T08:06:53Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T08:06:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(blade-navigation): cover legacy adapter guard inversion and URL sync (VM-1760) (#313)\n\n`useBladeNavigationAdapter` translates the legacy index-based\n`IUseBladeNavigation` API onto the new id-based `BladeStack`. Two parts\nof that translation were completely untested and fail silently when\nbroken:\n\n- **`onBeforeClose` inverts the guard boolean.** Legacy `onBeforeClose`\nreturns `false` to *prevent* a close; the new `registerBeforeClose`\nreturns `true` for the same thing. The adapter bridges them with `return\nresult === false` (`index.ts:309-316`). A regression here either lets a\nblade close over unsaved changes or makes it refuse to close at all.\n- **Every legacy entry point takes a blade index** and has to resolve it\nto a descriptor id via `getBladeIdByIndex` (`index.ts:186`) before\ntouching the stack.\n\nTests only — no source changes.\n\n## What is covered\n\n**Guard inversion**, asserted at two levels:\n- a truth table over the guard the adapter hands to\n`registerBeforeClose` (`false` → prevents, `true`/`undefined` → allows,\nasync `false` → prevents), including the blade id it lands on, that a\nsecond registration overwrites the first, and that a throwing legacy\ncallback rejects rather than resolving;\n- a new suite (`useBladeNavigationAdapter.guards.test.ts`) that runs the\nlegacy API against a **real** `createBladeStack`, so the observable\neffect is pinned: a guard returning `false` leaves the blade on the\nstack, `closeBlade` reports prevented, and the URL is not rewritten.\n\n**Also covered:**\n- `openBlade` verb selection — `replaceCurrentBlade: true` →\n`stack.coverCurrentBlade`, no flag → `stack.openBlade` with the active\nblade as parent, `isWorkspace` winning over both, blade-name extraction\nfrom a component;\n- URL sync branches — push only when the opened blade has a `url`,\nreplace only when the close was not prevented;\n- index → id translation for `closeBlade` / `setBladeError` /\n`clearBladeError` / `onParentCall`, including out-of-range no-ops and a\nrejecting parent method;\n- `setNavigationQuery` / `getNavigationQuery` round-trip through\n`window.location.hash`, `${prefix}_${key}` namespacing, foreign\nnamespaces, empty results;\n- `goToRoot` resolution chain — `meta.root` → `aliasOf` → tenant-prefix\nfallback.\n\nThe 5 existing cases are unchanged; the hoisted mock block gained named\nspies so the new tests can assert on the stack calls.\n\nEach assertion was mutation-tested. Ten separate source mutations —\nflipping `result === false`, swapping `coverCurrentBlade` for\n`replaceCurrentBlade`, dropping either URL guard, an off-by-one in\n`getBladeIdByIndex`, dropping the tenant prefix, registering the guard\non the workspace instead of the active blade, dropping the query\nnamespace, removing `decodeURIComponent`, and skipping the URL write for\nindex 0 — each fail at least one test.\n\n## Known coverage gap\n\nNo test mounts a component, so `currentDescriptor` (`index.ts:172`,\n`:180-184`) is always `undefined` and every call resolves the target\nblade through the `activeBlade` fallback. The production path is a call\nfrom inside a blade''s `setup()`, which goes through the injected\n`BladeDescriptorKey` instead. Closing that gap means mounting real\nblades and is worth doing separately.\n\nRelated, and pinned with a comment rather than treated as a bug: called\noutside a blade, the legacy singleton registered `onBeforeClose` on the\nactive *workspace*, while the adapter falls back to the active *blade*.\nFrom inside a blade both target the caller''s own blade.\n\n## Rough edges pinned, not fixed\n\nFour things look wrong. They are pinned as current behaviour with a\ncomment naming the suspicion, so the tests document them without\nchanging anything:\n\n1. **`goToRoot` returns the first alias-less route when no route\ndeclares `meta.root`** (`index.ts:256`). `routes.find((r) =>\nr.aliasOf?.path === mainRoute?.path)` degenerates to `r.aliasOf?.path\n=== undefined` when `mainRoute` is undefined, which every alias-less\nroute satisfies — so it returns `routes[0]` instead of falling through\nto the tenant-prefix path.\n2. **`closeBlade(0)` rewrites the URL for a close that never happened**\n(`index.ts:239-243`). The stack refuses to close index 0\n(`useBladeStack.ts:185`) and returns `false`, which the adapter cannot\ndistinguish from a successful close. Pinned against the real stack, so\nboth halves are proven.\n3. **`setNavigationQuery` un-escapes the query string it just built**\n(`index.ts:346-350`). `decodeURIComponent` is applied to the whole\nstring, undoing `URLSearchParams`'' escaping: `{ keyword: \"a&b\" }` is\nwritten as `offers_keyword=a&b` and reads back as `{ keyword: \"a\" }`\nplus a stray `b` param.\n4. **`setNavigationQuery` destroys other workspaces'' query params.**\n`getNavigationQuery` filters by `${prefix}_`, so foreign namespaces are\nexpected in the hash, but `setNavigationQuery` replaces the whole query\nstring. Related: `getNavigationQuery` runs every value through\n`Number()`, so `\"\"` reads back as `0`, `\"007\"` as `7`, `\"1e3\"` as\n`1000`.\n\n## Gates\n\n```\nyarn typecheck        exit 0\nyarn lint:check       exit 0   (needs a fresh .eslintcache; a stale one reports a phantom import/no-unresolved)\nyarn format:check     exit 0\n\ncd framework && npx vitest run core/composables/useBladeNavigationAdapter\n  Test Files  2 passed (2)\n  Tests       57 passed (57)\n\nyarn test:unit\n  Test Files  3 failed | 472 passed (475)\n  Tests       1 failed | 4280 passed (4281)\n```\n\nThe 3 failing files are pre-existing in a git worktree and unrelated —\nverified by re-running them with this branch''s changes stashed,\nidentical result. They resolve paths against the checkout root:\n`VcScheduler.style.test.ts` (`ENOENT assets/styles/theme/colors.scss`),\n`cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts` (`ENOENT\n.claude/cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/vc-app.md`),\n`packages/mf-host/src/register-remote-modules.test.ts` (cannot resolve\n`@vc-shell/framework/ai-agent`).\n\nVM-1760","tree":{"sha":"d28f6ef6158e5e5a0baef7967d915a8f4fb08ad5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/d28f6ef6158e5e5a0baef7967d915a8f4fb08ad5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04","verification":{"payload":"tree d28f6ef6158e5e5a0baef7967d915a8f4fb08ad5\nparent d823b7d9671c639c4543edba8c8efbdf75d73f22\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787731613 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787731613 +0300\n\ntest(blade-navigation): cover legacy adapter guard inversion and URL sync (VM-1760) (#313)\n\n`useBladeNavigationAdapter` translates the legacy index-based\n`IUseBladeNavigation` API onto the new id-based `BladeStack`. Two parts\nof that translation were completely untested and fail silently when\nbroken:\n\n- **`onBeforeClose` inverts the guard boolean.** Legacy `onBeforeClose`\nreturns `false` to *prevent* a close; the new `registerBeforeClose`\nreturns `true` for the same thing. The adapter bridges them with `return\nresult === false` (`index.ts:309-316`). A regression here either lets a\nblade close over unsaved changes or makes it refuse to close at all.\n- **Every legacy entry point takes a blade index** and has to resolve it\nto a descriptor id via `getBladeIdByIndex` (`index.ts:186`) before\ntouching the stack.\n\nTests only — no source changes.\n\n## What is covered\n\n**Guard inversion**, asserted at two levels:\n- a truth table over the guard the adapter hands to\n`registerBeforeClose` (`false` → prevents, `true`/`undefined` → allows,\nasync `false` → prevents), including the blade id it lands on, that a\nsecond registration overwrites the first, and that a throwing legacy\ncallback rejects rather than resolving;\n- a new suite (`useBladeNavigationAdapter.guards.test.ts`) that runs the\nlegacy API against a **real** `createBladeStack`, so the observable\neffect is pinned: a guard returning `false` leaves the blade on the\nstack, `closeBlade` reports prevented, and the URL is not rewritten.\n\n**Also covered:**\n- `openBlade` verb selection — `replaceCurrentBlade: true` →\n`stack.coverCurrentBlade`, no flag → `stack.openBlade` with the active\nblade as parent, `isWorkspace` winning over both, blade-name extraction\nfrom a component;\n- URL sync branches — push only when the opened blade has a `url`,\nreplace only when the close was not prevented;\n- index → id translation for `closeBlade` / `setBladeError` /\n`clearBladeError` / `onParentCall`, including out-of-range no-ops and a\nrejecting parent method;\n- `setNavigationQuery` / `getNavigationQuery` round-trip through\n`window.location.hash`, `${prefix}_${key}` namespacing, foreign\nnamespaces, empty results;\n- `goToRoot` resolution chain — `meta.root` → `aliasOf` → tenant-prefix\nfallback.\n\nThe 5 existing cases are unchanged; the hoisted mock block gained named\nspies so the new tests can assert on the stack calls.\n\nEach assertion was mutation-tested. Ten separate source mutations —\nflipping `result === false`, swapping `coverCurrentBlade` for\n`replaceCurrentBlade`, dropping either URL guard, an off-by-one in\n`getBladeIdByIndex`, dropping the tenant prefix, registering the guard\non the workspace instead of the active blade, dropping the query\nnamespace, removing `decodeURIComponent`, and skipping the URL write for\nindex 0 — each fail at least one test.\n\n## Known coverage gap\n\nNo test mounts a component, so `currentDescriptor` (`index.ts:172`,\n`:180-184`) is always `undefined` and every call resolves the target\nblade through the `activeBlade` fallback. The production path is a call\nfrom inside a blade''s `setup()`, which goes through the injected\n`BladeDescriptorKey` instead. Closing that gap means mounting real\nblades and is worth doing separately.\n\nRelated, and pinned with a comment rather than treated as a bug: called\noutside a blade, the legacy singleton registered `onBeforeClose` on the\nactive *workspace*, while the adapter falls back to the active *blade*.\nFrom inside a blade both target the caller''s own blade.\n\n## Rough edges pinned, not fixed\n\nFour things look wrong. They are pinned as current behaviour with a\ncomment naming the suspicion, so the tests document them without\nchanging anything:\n\n1. **`goToRoot` returns the first alias-less route when no route\ndeclares `meta.root`** (`index.ts:256`). `routes.find((r) =>\nr.aliasOf?.path === mainRoute?.path)` degenerates to `r.aliasOf?.path\n=== undefined` when `mainRoute` is undefined, which every alias-less\nroute satisfies — so it returns `routes[0]` instead of falling through\nto the tenant-prefix path.\n2. **`closeBlade(0)` rewrites the URL for a close that never happened**\n(`index.ts:239-243`). The stack refuses to close index 0\n(`useBladeStack.ts:185`) and returns `false`, which the adapter cannot\ndistinguish from a successful close. Pinned against the real stack, so\nboth halves are proven.\n3. **`setNavigationQuery` un-escapes the query string it just built**\n(`index.ts:346-350`). `decodeURIComponent` is applied to the whole\nstring, undoing `URLSearchParams`'' escaping: `{ keyword: \"a&b\" }` is\nwritten as `offers_keyword=a&b` and reads back as `{ keyword: \"a\" }`\nplus a stray `b` param.\n4. **`setNavigationQuery` destroys other workspaces'' query params.**\n`getNavigationQuery` filters by `${prefix}_`, so foreign namespaces are\nexpected in the hash, but `setNavigationQuery` replaces the whole query\nstring. Related: `getNavigationQuery` runs every value through\n`Number()`, so `\"\"` reads back as `0`, `\"007\"` as `7`, `\"1e3\"` as\n`1000`.\n\n## Gates\n\n```\nyarn typecheck        exit 0\nyarn lint:check       exit 0   (needs a fresh .eslintcache; a stale one reports a phantom import/no-unresolved)\nyarn format:check     exit 0\n\ncd framework && npx vitest run core/composables/useBladeNavigationAdapter\n  Test Files  2 passed (2)\n  Tests       57 passed (57)\n\nyarn test:unit\n  Test Files  3 failed | 472 passed (475)\n  Tests       1 failed | 4280 passed (4281)\n```\n\nThe 3 failing files are pre-existing in a git worktree and unrelated —\nverified by re-running them with this branch''s changes stashed,\nidentical result. They resolve paths against the checkout root:\n`VcScheduler.style.test.ts` (`ENOENT assets/styles/theme/colors.scss`),\n`cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts` (`ENOENT\n.claude/cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/vc-app.md`),\n`packages/mf-host/src/register-remote-modules.test.ts` (cannot resolve\n`@vc-shell/framework/ai-agent`).\n\nVM-1760","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjp6dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD84QADAi7fLbALHph2rDZquvWLPt\nnZfrGIpT2jwmbpVywkIWSH3zq0ieV925b49sj4c3G1C2bBvAN/RiaXqpTB7PFhzS\nNB6L/oL2tSuJAgB+C9hGRqiVcYDYGMYZl/YRwjWhuwsmQn9WPb/dV7FyfNnkSL5l\numz9WzfyAs8tkW3gHV6+qXmbThr3IynkDPI3vQfkP6U/YCblCtqB304bFJ/tbPfE\nYuijJiobZXFMLKgSxzXQOZ/I9JA0FoYohMk0xUJbHp8bsuZJlvTV6zCSfjMJU9om\npcyqROzqyTtyY+3qYZUvonYNfEXdGzcOVm+CvffMCqrCIN30qyGW4Orbgop75mYZ\nu6KricKQBMUF9jZVU8Sfr1ERZjboB9+3e+jiisX8PhxNGaAVfIcMZiqgEn45Vy4I\nxQeEAnpLOfG47o8FrPkYDvQptIDX3/X/4yKu5C7fTaZyWExUULMlFkoLieaGvQ6Y\nVRK9DIv9rdQJMTHOM+aS0hY58PAo4lfRDvRygBcioeuWAIG8HIH5pThYKrc2WS8G\ny4j7hsA/8b25MDRyUBUxwtI5ul3liAShn/v39yiV37HIrg1eQp663xE8JQZxwwAp\nVxuMT++EDZAvTziTQTzw+R9fuEtABPdG5a/nAH/KD/LeE4gyVzwOlPE78Ie3derb\nlDO9lMOxHNJFFRIQB7Me\n=4Iqc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T08:06:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGEzZDY1MDdkNzVmZDVhZjIzNzgyMTExNjNlMjQwNmZjNDRlYmRiMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/d823b7d9671c639c4543edba8c8efbdf75d73f22","sha":"d823b7d9671c639c4543edba8c8efbdf75d73f22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d823b7d9671c639c4543edba8c8efbdf75d73f22"}],"sha":"a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/a3d6507d75fd5af2378211163e2406fc44ebdb04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/d823b7d9671c639c4543edba8c8efbdf75d73f22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T07:52:10Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T07:52:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(framework): deprecate unused global search service and drop dead filter context (VM-1755) (#312)\n\n`createGlobalSearchService` and `provideToolbarService` are exported\nfrom the public barrels but nothing calls them, and `VcDataTable`\nprovides a `FilterContextKey` that no component ever injects. This marks\nthe two exported helpers deprecated, deletes the unused provide chain,\nand corrects one comment that describes code that no longer works that\nway.\n\nJira: VM-1755\n\n## Deprecated (kept exported)\n\n**`createGlobalSearchService`** —\n`framework/core/services/global-search-service/index.ts`. Zero callers.\nReachable from `@vc-shell/framework` via `core/services/index.ts:4`, so\nit stays exported and only gains JSDoc. No replacement.\n\n**`provideToolbarService`** —\n`framework/core/composables/useToolbar/index.ts`. Reachable through the\ncomposables barrel; in-repo callers are its own unit test and the docs\ntable. Redundant inside a shell app because `VirtoShellFramework` ->\n`createAndProvideServices` already provides the toolbar service. The\nwording deliberately stops short of \"no-op\":\n`createServiceRegistry.provideService()` is inject-**or**-create, so the\ncall still does real work when bootstrapping an isolated tree (stories,\ntests) that has not installed the framework — which is exactly how the\nsibling `provideWidgetService`/`provideDashboardService` are used in\nstories today. Its existing test is untouched and still passes.\n\n## Deleted (internal)\n\n`FilterContext` and `FilterContextKey` in\n`framework/ui/components/organisms/vc-data-table/keys.ts`, plus the\nimport at `VcDataTable.vue:405` and the `provide()` block at `:980-987`.\n\nVerified internal before deleting: `framework/package.json` declares no\nwildcard subpath and no `typesVersions`; `vc-data-table/index.ts`\nre-exports components, a hand-picked list from `./composables`,\n`ColumnCollector` and `export * from \"./types\"` — never `./keys`, and\n`types.ts` does not re-export from `keys.ts` either. Every other\n`keys.ts` consumer imports `TableContextKey` / `ColumnCollectorKey` /\n`FillerWidthKey` / `IsColumnReorderingKey`. No\n`inject(FilterContextKey)` existed anywhere in `framework/`, `apps/`,\n`cli/` or `packages/`.\n\nFive `useDataTableOrchestrator` return members existed only to feed that\nprovide and are dropped from the return interface and the return object:\n`filterValues`, `updateFilter`, `clearFilter`, `clearAllFilters`,\n`activeFilterCount`. The matching keys are removed from the\n`VcDataTable.test.ts` orchestrator double so it stops advertising a\ncontract that no longer exists.\n\n**`hasActiveFilters` is kept** — `VcDataTable.vue:643` reads it in the\nempty-state predicate. A new test in `useDataTableOrchestrator.test.ts`\npins it by driving the real chain `handleColumnFilterApply ->\nupdateFilter -> hasActiveFilters` rather than asserting on the return\nshape.\n\nThe underlying `useFilterState` wiring is untouched: the orchestrator\nstill uses `filterValues`, `updateFilter` and `clearFilter` internally.\n`colFilter`, `updateRangeFilter`, `buildPayload` and all\n`getColumnFilter*` template helpers stay in the return.\n\n`useDataTableOrchestrator` and its return type are not reachable from\nany public entry (`composables/index.ts` does not export them), so\nnarrowing the return is not a breaking change.\n\n## Comment fix\n\n`framework/core/composables/useSidebarState/index.ts:37-38` claimed\n`UserDropdownButton` uses `useMenuExpanded` directly. It calls\n`useSidebarState()` (`user-dropdown-button.vue:61,75`). The delegation\nclause that remains is still accurate.\n\n## Docs\n\n`services.docs.md`, `useToolbar.docs.md` and `global-search-service.md`\nget a deprecation notice so the docs site reflects the JSDoc. The\ngenerated mirrors under `cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/knowledge/docs/` are\ndeliberately **not** hand-edited — `scripts/release-workflow.ts:265`\n(`syncSkillDocs`) wipes and re-copies that tree from\n`framework/**/*.docs.md` on release.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo public export, prop, emit, slot or `defineExpose` key is removed or\nretyped, and no default behaviour changes. Everything deleted here is\nunreachable from `@vc-shell/framework` and from every `exports` subpath.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun in the worktree on the final commit.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `yarn typecheck` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn format:check` | exit 0 — `All matched files use Prettier code\nstyle!` |\n| `yarn stylelint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn check:circular` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn check:layers` | exit 0 — all 3 layer checks pass |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | exit 0 — `0 errors, 6 warnings` (all pre-existing)\n|\n| `yarn test:unit` | `Test Files 3 failed \\| 471 passed (474)` / `Tests\n1 failed \\| 4229 passed (4230)` — see below |\n| `yarn build:framework` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn test:storybook` | exit 0 — `Test Files 77 passed (77)` / `Tests\n616 passed (616)` |\n\n**Snapshots byte-identical.** After `yarn test:storybook`, `git status`\nlisted only the intended source files — no snapshot file was rewritten.\n\n**On the 3 `test:unit` failures.** They are the known worktree-path\nbaseline, not a regression. Stashing this branch''s changes and\nre-running at the same commit reproduces the identical three failures\nwith `Tests 1 failed, 4228 passed (4229)` — one fewer pass, which is\nexactly the test added here. All three are `process.cwd()`-relative\nresolution failures caused by `.claude/worktrees/<name>` sitting two\nlevels deeper than a normal checkout:\n\n- `packages/mf-host/src/register-remote-modules.test.ts` — `Failed to\nresolve import \"@vc-shell/framework/ai-agent\"`\n-\n`framework/ui/components/organisms/vc-scheduler/VcScheduler.style.test.ts`\n— `ENOENT ... assets/styles/theme/colors.scss`\n- `cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts > tracks the public vc-app command\nlist` — `ENOENT ... .claude/cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/vc-app.md`\n\n`yarn docs:lint` needs `yarn workspace @vc-shell/docs-sync run build`\nfirst on a fresh worktree (its `dist/` is gitignored).\n\n## Left alone\n\n`provideMenuService`\n(`framework/core/composables/useMenuService/index.ts:29`) sits in the\nsame position as `provideToolbarService` — eagerly provided at\n`framework/index.ts:170`, called only by its own test — but deprecating\nit was not part of this change. Worth a follow-up so the two stay\nconsistent.\n\nNothing already marked `@deprecated` is removed here; those deletions\nbelong in a major release.","tree":{"sha":"087a97edad2bb0e7fb789de95469ca8ea38189eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/087a97edad2bb0e7fb789de95469ca8ea38189eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/d823b7d9671c639c4543edba8c8efbdf75d73f22","verification":{"payload":"tree 087a97edad2bb0e7fb789de95469ca8ea38189eb\nparent 324cd9b092dc3f198f57c5ef369b8a460c5d93ec\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787730730 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787730730 +0300\n\nchore(framework): deprecate unused global search service and drop dead filter context (VM-1755) (#312)\n\n`createGlobalSearchService` and `provideToolbarService` are exported\nfrom the public barrels but nothing calls them, and `VcDataTable`\nprovides a `FilterContextKey` that no component ever injects. This marks\nthe two exported helpers deprecated, deletes the unused provide chain,\nand corrects one comment that describes code that no longer works that\nway.\n\nJira: VM-1755\n\n## Deprecated (kept exported)\n\n**`createGlobalSearchService`** —\n`framework/core/services/global-search-service/index.ts`. Zero callers.\nReachable from `@vc-shell/framework` via `core/services/index.ts:4`, so\nit stays exported and only gains JSDoc. No replacement.\n\n**`provideToolbarService`** —\n`framework/core/composables/useToolbar/index.ts`. Reachable through the\ncomposables barrel; in-repo callers are its own unit test and the docs\ntable. Redundant inside a shell app because `VirtoShellFramework` ->\n`createAndProvideServices` already provides the toolbar service. The\nwording deliberately stops short of \"no-op\":\n`createServiceRegistry.provideService()` is inject-**or**-create, so the\ncall still does real work when bootstrapping an isolated tree (stories,\ntests) that has not installed the framework — which is exactly how the\nsibling `provideWidgetService`/`provideDashboardService` are used in\nstories today. Its existing test is untouched and still passes.\n\n## Deleted (internal)\n\n`FilterContext` and `FilterContextKey` in\n`framework/ui/components/organisms/vc-data-table/keys.ts`, plus the\nimport at `VcDataTable.vue:405` and the `provide()` block at `:980-987`.\n\nVerified internal before deleting: `framework/package.json` declares no\nwildcard subpath and no `typesVersions`; `vc-data-table/index.ts`\nre-exports components, a hand-picked list from `./composables`,\n`ColumnCollector` and `export * from \"./types\"` — never `./keys`, and\n`types.ts` does not re-export from `keys.ts` either. Every other\n`keys.ts` consumer imports `TableContextKey` / `ColumnCollectorKey` /\n`FillerWidthKey` / `IsColumnReorderingKey`. No\n`inject(FilterContextKey)` existed anywhere in `framework/`, `apps/`,\n`cli/` or `packages/`.\n\nFive `useDataTableOrchestrator` return members existed only to feed that\nprovide and are dropped from the return interface and the return object:\n`filterValues`, `updateFilter`, `clearFilter`, `clearAllFilters`,\n`activeFilterCount`. The matching keys are removed from the\n`VcDataTable.test.ts` orchestrator double so it stops advertising a\ncontract that no longer exists.\n\n**`hasActiveFilters` is kept** — `VcDataTable.vue:643` reads it in the\nempty-state predicate. A new test in `useDataTableOrchestrator.test.ts`\npins it by driving the real chain `handleColumnFilterApply ->\nupdateFilter -> hasActiveFilters` rather than asserting on the return\nshape.\n\nThe underlying `useFilterState` wiring is untouched: the orchestrator\nstill uses `filterValues`, `updateFilter` and `clearFilter` internally.\n`colFilter`, `updateRangeFilter`, `buildPayload` and all\n`getColumnFilter*` template helpers stay in the return.\n\n`useDataTableOrchestrator` and its return type are not reachable from\nany public entry (`composables/index.ts` does not export them), so\nnarrowing the return is not a breaking change.\n\n## Comment fix\n\n`framework/core/composables/useSidebarState/index.ts:37-38` claimed\n`UserDropdownButton` uses `useMenuExpanded` directly. It calls\n`useSidebarState()` (`user-dropdown-button.vue:61,75`). The delegation\nclause that remains is still accurate.\n\n## Docs\n\n`services.docs.md`, `useToolbar.docs.md` and `global-search-service.md`\nget a deprecation notice so the docs site reflects the JSDoc. The\ngenerated mirrors under `cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/knowledge/docs/` are\ndeliberately **not** hand-edited — `scripts/release-workflow.ts:265`\n(`syncSkillDocs`) wipes and re-copies that tree from\n`framework/**/*.docs.md` on release.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo public export, prop, emit, slot or `defineExpose` key is removed or\nretyped, and no default behaviour changes. Everything deleted here is\nunreachable from `@vc-shell/framework` and from every `exports` subpath.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun in the worktree on the final commit.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `yarn typecheck` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn format:check` | exit 0 — `All matched files use Prettier code\nstyle!` |\n| `yarn stylelint:check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn check:circular` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn check:layers` | exit 0 — all 3 layer checks pass |\n| `yarn docs:lint` | exit 0 — `0 errors, 6 warnings` (all pre-existing)\n|\n| `yarn test:unit` | `Test Files 3 failed \\| 471 passed (474)` / `Tests\n1 failed \\| 4229 passed (4230)` — see below |\n| `yarn build:framework` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn test:storybook` | exit 0 — `Test Files 77 passed (77)` / `Tests\n616 passed (616)` |\n\n**Snapshots byte-identical.** After `yarn test:storybook`, `git status`\nlisted only the intended source files — no snapshot file was rewritten.\n\n**On the 3 `test:unit` failures.** They are the known worktree-path\nbaseline, not a regression. Stashing this branch''s changes and\nre-running at the same commit reproduces the identical three failures\nwith `Tests 1 failed, 4228 passed (4229)` — one fewer pass, which is\nexactly the test added here. All three are `process.cwd()`-relative\nresolution failures caused by `.claude/worktrees/<name>` sitting two\nlevels deeper than a normal checkout:\n\n- `packages/mf-host/src/register-remote-modules.test.ts` — `Failed to\nresolve import \"@vc-shell/framework/ai-agent\"`\n-\n`framework/ui/components/organisms/vc-scheduler/VcScheduler.style.test.ts`\n— `ENOENT ... assets/styles/theme/colors.scss`\n- `cli/docs-sync/tests/lint.test.ts > tracks the public vc-app command\nlist` — `ENOENT ... .claude/cli/vc-app-skill/runtime/vc-app.md`\n\n`yarn docs:lint` needs `yarn workspace @vc-shell/docs-sync run build`\nfirst on a fresh worktree (its `dist/` is gitignored).\n\n## Left alone\n\n`provideMenuService`\n(`framework/core/composables/useMenuService/index.ts:29`) sits in the\nsame position as `provideToolbarService` — eagerly provided at\n`framework/index.ts:170`, called only by its own test — but deprecating\nit was not part of this change. Worth a follow-up so the two stay\nconsistent.\n\nNothing already marked `@deprecated` is removed here; those deletions\nbelong in a major release.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjpsqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0UkQAA/v/Xp98yyj3YqfRNPOa9Ss\ngc+lbaO9Q0/Av69IjEBv0cROzZc+gkWgEkLlfAYrgweKYWtvkXNKY0MHzPszXxSj\n+e2AjcUmKIjBHslcOyTuYS4xj2VLlZzFBtIP7izMwlIVyvn9d0nS8j5Kr8uvjojl\nlYB9Cy8W83Ba4wLQGzB8DZxnh/jiw5d10vQXzr3hf3qHrEBZdKoz+oWq8wogyFHg\n8UYwNE3IusEioSK4x/bKwZRp93AW6zQ1VRxrqjQQNlXrpH6KbhJStDRWbyU7RX1R\ngEI7Fo5va0ax58H8OHQN49eJYiI1nfU7ttjRGBItIuFe+Ht9mu+Ed/0OsSMUbgyF\nquKVDVEqjzuBDVBRK7a2Qq7i4tuoSFU16p+koIDfybcDxvlHHLf4lyNlwJh+wsSq\nK