t.com/u/31079468?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vc-ci","id":31079468,"login":"vc-ci","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDc5NDY4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/324cd9b092dc3f198f57c5ef369b8a460c5d93ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:25:04Z","email":"ci@virtocommerce.com","name":"vc-ci"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:25:04Z","email":"ci@virtocommerce.com","name":"vc-ci"},"message":"release: v2.5.0","tree":{"sha":"1b3df9f17743b2e448d8c32835658022d30f2bb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/1b3df9f17743b2e448d8c32835658022d30f2bb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/324cd9b092dc3f198f57c5ef369b8a460c5d93ec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31079468?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vc-ci","id":31079468,"login":"vc-ci","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDc5NDY4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vc-ci","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/324cd9b092dc3f198f57c5ef369b8a460c5d93ec","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDMyNGNkOWIwOTJkYzNmMTk4ZjU3YzVlZjM2OWI4YTQ2MGM1ZDkzZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2964ccbe345297a049407eba384710e3af1703f5","sha":"2964ccbe345297a049407eba384710e3af1703f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2964ccbe345297a049407eba384710e3af1703f5"}],"sha":"324cd9b092dc3f198f57c5ef369b8a460c5d93ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/324cd9b092dc3f198f57c5ef369b8a460c5d93ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2964ccbe345297a049407eba384710e3af1703f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:16:45Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:16:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: cache Playwright browsers for the story tests (#311)\n\n## Problem\n\n`storybook-tests` downloads Chromium from Playwright''s CDN on every run,\nand nothing caches it. That download is usually fast and sometimes not.\nMeasured on the `Install Chromium` step across recent runs:\n\n| Run | Branch | Duration |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 32144859867 | fix/VCST-5671… | 19 s |\n| 32150224146 | main | 20 s |\n| 32150499441 | fix/VCST-5632… | 22 s |\n| 32226928338 | main | 73 s |\n| 32227333537 | main | 33 s |\n| 32227535262 | main | 241 s |\n| 32225221895 | VCST-5248 | **1379 s** |\n| 32227555174 | fix/VCST-5746… | **timed out at 25 min, still\ndownloading** |\n\nThe job''s `timeout-minutes` is 25. When the download is slow, the step\neats the entire budget and the story tests never run — the check reports\nfailure having tested nothing. That is what happened on #310, whose own\ndiff was two ai-agent files.\n\nWorth stating explicitly: this is **not** caused by #309\n(`checkout@v4→v7`, `setup-node@v4→v7`). Those actions have nothing to do\nwith browser downloads, and the fast/slow split straddles that merge —\n33 s and 73 s runs landed on `main` after it. The variance is the CDN.\n\n## Change\n\nCache `~/.cache/ms-playwright`, keyed on the resolved playwright version\nrather than a hash of `yarn.lock`. The browser revision only changes\nwhen playwright does, so an unrelated dependency bump should not throw\nthe cache away.\n\nSystem libraries live outside that directory, so they are installed\neither way:\n\n- cache miss → `playwright install --with-deps chromium`, as before\n- cache hit → `playwright install-deps chromium`, which is seconds\n\nThe existing comment about needing the workspace binary rather than\n`yarn dlx` is preserved — that constraint still holds.\n\n## Note on the first run\n\nThe first run after this merges still pays the download once, to\npopulate the cache. If it happens to land during a slow CDN window it\ncan still hit the 25-minute timeout; a re-run will then find the cache\nwarm.\n\n`timeout-minutes` is deliberately left at 25 — with the cache in place\nthe step should be seconds, and raising the ceiling would just hide a\nfuture regression for longer.","tree":{"sha":"cca6126aea009d8aa9531f145858bedda95b6f36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/cca6126aea009d8aa9531f145858bedda95b6f36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/2964ccbe345297a049407eba384710e3af1703f5","verification":{"payload":"tree cca6126aea009d8aa9531f145858bedda95b6f36\nparent 06cb54b4db449322133f6201e02b3cf7ce4567dd\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787134605 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787134605 +0300\n\nci: cache Playwright browsers for the story tests (#311)\n\n## Problem\n\n`storybook-tests` downloads Chromium from Playwright''s CDN on every run,\nand nothing caches it. That download is usually fast and sometimes not.\nMeasured on the `Install Chromium` step across recent runs:\n\n| Run | Branch | Duration |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 32144859867 | fix/VCST-5671… | 19 s |\n| 32150224146 | main | 20 s |\n| 32150499441 | fix/VCST-5632… | 22 s |\n| 32226928338 | main | 73 s |\n| 32227333537 | main | 33 s |\n| 32227535262 | main | 241 s |\n| 32225221895 | VCST-5248 | **1379 s** |\n| 32227555174 | fix/VCST-5746… | **timed out at 25 min, still\ndownloading** |\n\nThe job''s `timeout-minutes` is 25. When the download is slow, the step\neats the entire budget and the story tests never run — the check reports\nfailure having tested nothing. That is what happened on #310, whose own\ndiff was two ai-agent files.\n\nWorth stating explicitly: this is **not** caused by #309\n(`checkout@v4→v7`, `setup-node@v4→v7`). Those actions have nothing to do\nwith browser downloads, and the fast/slow split straddles that merge —\n33 s and 73 s runs landed on `main` after it. The variance is the CDN.\n\n## Change\n\nCache `~/.cache/ms-playwright`, keyed on the resolved playwright version\nrather than a hash of `yarn.lock`. The browser revision only changes\nwhen playwright does, so an unrelated dependency bump should not throw\nthe cache away.\n\nSystem libraries live outside that directory, so they are installed\neither way:\n\n- cache miss → `playwright install --with-deps chromium`, as before\n- cache hit → `playwright install-deps chromium`, which is seconds\n\nThe existing comment about needing the workspace binary rather than\n`yarn dlx` is preserved — that constraint still holds.\n\n## Note on the first run\n\nThe first run after this merges still pays the download once, to\npopulate the cache. If it happens to land during a slow CDN window it\ncan still hit the 25-minute timeout; a re-run will then find the cache\nwarm.\n\n`timeout-minutes` is deliberately left at 25 — with the cache in place\nthe step should be seconds, and raising the ceiling would just hide a\nfuture regression for longer.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhYKNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4yYQAJzFxNiI1Ls0i5tmCEJAfVp+\nX+mnBvAnXXNrjUdBe8iVWAtg1J004JrwfLohjuHGfJ80oWRNWzmoZE1bRCBpIzWu\nG2D/IS58ADyf7bzoi4O23166HYgrlWyqgkSv4WzXsHwbvKH7VK/i+OqCRchCGpU+\nuzyINdKBxZVyQEo/R20BUc5DZR59+mI4DF0EuKYh7u+G9MU6H5cd10im4L7/y6cq\ngIZKnGtCkoa349zBbhqzS1K46EAOVqui/El5se2LOwdIJIHHRZYo1qOkeKB0Ta4T\nZd45GwVPAWkkEIUZkRLZKnv2Qy3ei+2MsZrCKnXS0DaTR/iwbHoeG/zb71xFNAos\n5Z8nyqZ7cXVx5/Tj72xce8D+i73Bj+6lZxQ9cnP+BFfDKlimb8HIbIWxKEuySpXN\nY77qK6EBa6ZnMw9Aj+QdnBk2w61lJezXcoKoo0PuVbzYj73VIMuJEn65hhTzY7RS\nh8f1q0FJsvX+uZ8pmuUHEbXMERNw4CtmvsEN0VCsejI6Vw8w+f5873umjkXdlKlv\nDMQNWGE1iIZeSquQC/oLirdEeUeVhZshVjGOMsqPe1kWdA4l2bA7tWEFzYM5aZfe\nqGYVqECOxUpyHWf+wZp3mcx1JPsxSk8gtM+zZF8RL/RhMw5nV9UF34PnMZyV5tA8\n7WDKDNKDCPY51bNHWhtd\n=ni3Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T10:16:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2964ccbe345297a049407eba384710e3af1703f5","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDI5NjRjY2JlMzQ1Mjk3YTA0OTQwN2ViYTM4NDcxMGUzYWYxNzAzZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/06cb54b4db449322133f6201e02b3cf7ce4567dd","sha":"06cb54b4db449322133f6201e02b3cf7ce4567dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/06cb54b4db449322133f6201e02b3cf7ce4567dd"}],"sha":"2964ccbe345297a049407eba384710e3af1703f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2964ccbe345297a049407eba384710e3af1703f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/06cb54b4db449322133f6201e02b3cf7ce4567dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:54:46Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:54:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai-agent): claim mod+backslash only while the panel holds focus (#310)\n\nCloses VCST-5746.\n\nReplaces #307, which GitHub auto-closed when its base branch\n(`fix/VCST-5632-popup-reopen-and-inert`) was deleted on merge of #306.\nThe branch has since been rebased onto `main`, so it now carries only\nits own commit.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe panel consumed `mod+\\` whenever it was open, so while the assistant\nwas up there was **no keyboard route to maximize a blade at all** — even\nwith focus demonstrably inside one. That contradicts the targeting model\nthe shell settled on in VCST-5680: a blade shortcut acts on the blade\nholding focus.\n\n## Change\n\nThe chord is claimed only when `document.activeElement` is inside the\npanel; otherwise the event is left alone and the blade dispatcher\nhandles it. Escape is untouched — consuming it while the panel is open\nis what keeps the blade behind from closing.\n\n## Verified live\n\n| Focus location | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Control in the middle blade, panel open | that blade gains\n`vc-blade--maximized`; panel stays `362px` |\n| Panel''s own Maximize control | panel `362px` → `500px`, `--expanded`;\nno blade maximized |\n| Host, panel open | Escape closes the panel, all 3 blades intact —\nunchanged |\n\n## One caveat about the tests\n\nFocus *inside the chat iframe* never reaches the host at all — the\nkeystroke goes to the iframe''s own document, the same barrier as\nVCST-5673. So the branch covering the iframe element is unreachable in a\nbrowser; it passes in jsdom only because there is no cross-origin\nboundary there. Do not read that test as proof of browser behaviour.\n\nExpanding the panel from the keyboard while the chat has focus needs the\nrelay filed as VirtoCommerce/virto-oz#17.\n\n## Verification\n\n`407 files / 3830 tests` green on this branch, rebased onto current\n`main`.","tree":{"sha":"5199f9477b2fb5d8a5c05190a372b60567a092a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/5199f9477b2fb5d8a5c05190a372b60567a092a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/06cb54b4db449322133f6201e02b3cf7ce4567dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 5199f9477b2fb5d8a5c05190a372b60567a092a1\nparent 5b0406f2f9b0950bf69b3ba7d16e312f23efd7c5\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787126086 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787126086 +0300\n\nfix(ai-agent): claim mod+backslash only while the panel holds focus (#310)\n\nCloses VCST-5746.\n\nReplaces #307, which GitHub auto-closed when its base branch\n(`fix/VCST-5632-popup-reopen-and-inert`) was deleted on merge of #306.\nThe branch has since been rebased onto `main`, so it now carries only\nits own commit.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe panel consumed `mod+\\` whenever it was open, so while the assistant\nwas up there was **no keyboard route to maximize a blade at all** — even\nwith focus demonstrably inside one. That contradicts the targeting model\nthe shell settled on in VCST-5680: a blade shortcut acts on the blade\nholding focus.\n\n## Change\n\nThe chord is claimed only when `document.activeElement` is inside the\npanel; otherwise the event is left alone and the blade dispatcher\nhandles it. Escape is untouched — consuming it while the panel is open\nis what keeps the blade behind from closing.\n\n## Verified live\n\n| Focus location | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Control in the middle blade, panel open | that blade gains\n`vc-blade--maximized`; panel stays `362px` |\n| Panel''s own Maximize control | panel `362px` → `500px`, `--expanded`;\nno blade maximized |\n| Host, panel open | Escape closes the panel, all 3 blades intact —\nunchanged |\n\n## One caveat about the tests\n\nFocus *inside the chat iframe* never reaches the host at all — the\nkeystroke goes to the iframe''s own document, the same barrier as\nVCST-5673. So the branch covering the iframe element is unreachable in a\nbrowser; it passes in jsdom only because there is no cross-origin\nboundary there. Do not read that test as proof of browser behaviour.\n\nExpanding the panel from the keyboard while the chat has focus needs the\nrelay filed as VirtoCommerce/virto-oz#17.\n\n## Verification\n\n`407 files / 3830 tests` green on this branch, rebased onto current\n`main`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhWFGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeeQQAA2E1N6l5zm6AF+cmb5PfjbI\ncizPz/Y8IsL+nG+IMtSC4TUJSMSGPDEUTWwoU/qZOdSr9XKdlUNB3IcuMk+geSN5\nlK+cf+f/V+s95wd0X/cgGz9CmMPkdc0Sry+k9ShFtEn8UG6SOJSoAaRdm8JN5c8N\nzFsvjI2IlVQ8kTXvG8L1VE4GI5/RQYIDDvPoOkXExbi29iHQ3ELksRGtmYOd9bk3\nAJiKc1bYFQuZewKnmb9G5KSF/1Kj56usq3QcyH07ey