ps://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/06cb54b4db449322133f6201e02b3cf7ce4567dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5b0406f2f9b0950bf69b3ba7d16e312f23efd7c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:22:32Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:22:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(create-vc-app): make scaffolded apps build and lint out of the box (#302)\n\n## Problem\n\nThree defects reported against the scaffolding, all confirmed:\n\n1. **A generated app did not build.** `Welcome.vue` used `tw-text-s`,\nwhich is not in the framework''s `fontSize` scale (`xxs / xs / sm / base\n/ lg / …`). `@apply` with a non-existent class is a hard PostCSS error,\nnot a silent no-op:\n\n   ```\n[vite:css] [postcss] Welcome.vue?vue&type=style&index=0&lang.scss:20:3:\n     The `tw-text-s` class does not exist.\n   ```\n\n2. **`yarn lint` failed out of the box.** `eslint-plugin-import` and\n`eslint-import-resolver-typescript` were declared in the template''s\n`devDependencies` but never wired into `eslint.config.mjs`, while\n`Welcome.vue` and `routes.ts.ejs` carried `eslint-disable` comments for\n`import/no-unresolved`. ESLint treats a disable directive for an\nunregistered rule as an error:\n\n   ```\n   1:1  error  Definition for rule ''import/no-unresolved'' was not found\n   ✖ 1 problem (1 error)\n   ```\n\n3. **Template code was never linted or formatted.**\n`cli/create-vc-app/src/templates` was listed in both `.prettierignore`\nand the root eslint `ignores`, so even the plain `.ts`/`.vue` files\nthere were unchecked. `prettier --check` flagged 8 files, including a\n`tsconfig.json` with broken indentation.\n\nThe root cause behind all three: templates are `.ejs`, so ESLint and\nPrettier structurally cannot check them. Nothing verified this code, and\nthe extra ignore entries hid even the files that *were* checkable.\n\n## Approach\n\nTemplates cannot be linted directly, so the gate has to be **generate a\nproject and check the output**. That needs two independent layers —\nneither alone is sufficient:\n\n- **EJS whitespace slurping** (`<%_ … -%>`). A bare `<% if %>` on its\nown line emits a blank line into the output. `bootstrap.ts.ejs` and\n`main.ts.ejs` already did this correctly; `routes.ts.ejs` did not,\nproducing output riddled with stray blank lines.\n- **A Prettier pass over the generated tree** (`src/engine/format.ts`),\ncalled from `init` (whole tree) and `add-module` (only the touched\npaths, so it never rewrites files the user owns). This is what\nnormalises the regex splicing in `codegen.ts`.\n\nPrettier alone cannot replace layer 1: it collapses 2+ blank lines to\none but **preserves a single blank line** between statements, so EJS\nartifacts survive a format pass. Layer 1 alone cannot replace layer 2\neither, since it does nothing about the string splicing in `codegen.ts`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Fix `tw-text-s` → `tw-text-sm`; drop the unused `bgImage` import.\n- Wire `eslint-plugin-import` + the typescript resolver in the app\ntemplate and in the monorepo root. `flatConfigs.recommended` must be\nspread **before** the Vue/TS configs (it sets a global\n`languageOptions.ecmaVersion` with no `files` scope and would otherwise\noverride their parsers), and the resolver setting must come **after**\n`flatConfigs.typescript` (which presets a `node` resolver).\n- Disable `import/namespace`, `import/default`,\n`import/no-named-as-default{,-member}`. These parse the *dependency''s*\nsource with espree and produce 48 bogus `Parse errors in imported module\n''@vc-shell/framework''` on a real app. TypeScript already covers them;\n`flatConfigs.typescript` only disables `import/named`.\n- Narrow the `.prettierignore` and root eslint `ignores` entries to\n`**/_yarn`, so the plain template files are covered by `yarn format` and\n`yarn lint` again; format the 8 files this surfaced.\n- Add 8 tests. Four assert that a generated project is Prettier-clean\nacross flag combinations; four assert the raw `renderDir` output is free\nof EJS whitespace artifacts. The second group is required — without it\nthe formatter would silently absorb template bugs.\n- Collapse the duplicate imports that the newly enabled\n`import/no-duplicates` reports (10 framework files, plus three separate\n`from \"vue\"` statements in `PullToRefresh.vue` that `--fix` could not\nmerge).\n\n`framework/index.ts` exports ~18 names both explicitly and via `export\n*` from the same module. That is legal — an explicit export shadows a\nstar export — but `import/export` cannot tell it apart from a real\ncollision, so the rule is disabled for that one file. Cleaning up the\nbarrel is left as a follow-up.\n\n## Second commit: `add-module` codegen\n\nWriting the tests above surfaced that `codegen.ts` — which edits\n*existing* source with regexes — had no test coverage and three defects.\nEach was reproduced before being fixed.\n\n**`add-module` never registered the module.** The anchor was\n`/\\.use\\([A-Z]\\w+,\\s*\\{\\s*router\\s*\\}\\)/`, but the template emits\n`app.use(Orders);`. Nothing matched, `lastMatch` stayed `null`, no\n`app.use()` was inserted — and the command still printed:\n\n```\n✔ Updated src/main.ts — added import & app.use(Reviews)\n```\n\nThe module was imported, unused, and never registered, so the feature\nsilently did nothing. This is current behaviour on `main`, not a\nhypothetical.\n\n**A multi-line trailing import got corrupted.** `insertImport` matched\n`/^import\\s.+$/gm`, which sees only the first line of a multi-line\nimport:\n\n```ts\nimport {\nimport Orders from \"./modules/orders\";   // ← spliced inside the braces\n  notification,\n} from \"@vc-shell/framework\";\n```\n\n**A nested `});` truncated the menu-item match.**\n`/addMenuItem\\(\\{[\\s\\S]*?\\}\\);/` is lazy, so any menu item containing a\ncallback that ends in `});` caused the new item to land inside the\nprevious one''s body.\n\nStructural edits now run against a mask of the source with comment and\nstring contents replaced by spaces and offsets preserved, so a brace or\nsemicolon inside a string cannot be read as syntax. Call boundaries come\nfrom bracket matching instead of a lazy quantifier, nested calls are\nskipped, imports are scanned to their terminating `;`, and insertions\napply highest-offset-first so earlier positions stay valid.\n`addModuleToMain` throws when an anchor is missing rather than reporting\na change it did not make — `add-module` already catches that and prints\nmanual instructions, and the file is left untouched.\n\n`codegen.test.ts` adds 9 cases. Each result is run through Prettier,\nwhich throws on a syntax error; that check alone would have caught two\nof the three defects.\n\n`magicast` — a library for exactly this kind of edit — was declared in\n`cli/create-vc-app/dependencies` and imported nowhere. Removed in a\nfollow-up commit; it also pinned a second copy in the lockfile, since\n`@vitest/coverage-v8` pulls in `magicast@0.5.3` independently and the\nonly other reference is an optional peer dependency. Reintroducing it is\nthe obvious move if `codegen.ts` ever outgrows the\nmask-plus-bracket-matching approach.\n\n## Third commit: a generated app now lints clean\n\n`yarn lint` in a generated project reported seven `no-unused-vars`\nwarnings on placeholder parameters (`query`, `ids`, `id`,\n`setBroadcastFilter`) that the commented-out TODO API calls reference.\nRenaming them to `_query` would break the code the user is meant to\nuncomment, so each gets a scoped `eslint-disable-next-line … -- reason`\n— the idiom the template already uses in `bootstrap.ts.ejs` for the\nunused `app` parameter, and one that disappears once the TODO is\nimplemented.\n\nSilencing those exposed two more warnings that had been invisible,\nbecause `yarn lint` runs `--fix` and was rewriting the freshly generated\nproject on its first run:\n\n- `bootstrap.ts` imported `vue` twice — `App`, then `markRaw` inside the\ndashboard conditional. Now one conditional specifier list, `import {\nApp<% if (dashboard) { %>, markRaw<% } %> } from \"vue\";`.\n- `useList.ts` carried an `eslint-disable-next-line\n@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` aimed at the wrong line and naming a\nrule the template config turns off. ESLint flagged it as an unused\ndirective; removed.\n\nGenerated with and without `--dashboard`, `add-module` run on each: no\nerrors and no warnings in either variant. The dashboard variant also\ntype-checks and builds.\n\n## Verification\n\nScaffolded an app with the built CLI (`standalone`, module, dashboard,\ntenant routes, mocks) plus `add-module`, then ran it for real:\n\n| Step | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `yarn install` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn build` (`vite build` + `vue-tsc`) | **exit 0**,\n`dist/index.html` + `dist/types/` produced |\n| `yarn type-check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint` | exit 0, **0 errors, 0 warnings** |\n| `yarn preview` → HTTP | `200`, correct title, CSS and JS bundles\nserved |\n| Headless boot | Vue mounts, redirects to `#/login`, login form\nrenders, no `pageerror` |\n\nAfter `add-module reviews`, `main.ts` now reads:\n\n```ts\n  app.use(Orders);\n  app.use(Sample);\n  app.use(Reviews);   // ← previously missing entirely\n  app.use(router);\n```\n\nand the app with the registered module still builds, type-checks and\nlints clean.\n\nThe emitted CSS is correct, not merely non-crashing:\n\n```css\n.dashboard-widget-welcome__welcome-description{…;font-size:.875rem;…}\n```\n\n`.875rem` is exactly the `sm` value from `framework/tailwind.config.ts`.\n\n**Negative controls** — each fix was checked to be load-bearing:\n\n- Restoring `tw-text-s` in the built app fails `vite build` with the\nPostCSS error above.\n- Reverting the EJS slurping fails the 4 template tests while the 4\nPrettier tests stay green, confirming the two layers are independent.\n- Disabling `formatGenerated` fails only the 4 Prettier tests.\n\nAll CI gates were run in a **fresh, unbuilt worktree** (matching what CI\nsees): `lint:check`, `format:check`, `stylelint:check`, `typecheck`,\n`check:locales`, `check:circular`, `check:layers` — all exit 0.\nFramework suite: 3791 tests in 403 files pass. CLI suite: 67 tests (was\n50).\n\nThree things made a local green run misleading, which is worth knowing\nfor anyone touching these configs:\n\n- **CI lints without building** (`yarn install --immutable` → `yarn\nlint:check`, no build step in between). Every `@vc-shell/*` workspace\npackage resolves through `main`/`types` fields pointing into `dist/`, so\nnone of them resolve on CI. A leftover `framework/dist` hides this\nlocally.\n- **Resolver fallback to `src/` is platform-dependent.** With the ignore\nnarrowed to `^@vc-shell/framework/`, the Linux runner reported 6\n`import/no-unresolved` errors for `@vc-shell/mf-config` and\n`@vc-shell/config-generator` that macOS did not — reproduced neither by\ndeleting `framework/dist` nor by a clean `yarn install --immutable`.\n`eslint-import-resolver-typescript` v4 uses the native `unrs-resolver`,\nwhich behaves differently per platform. Hence the ignore covers\n`^@vc-shell/` rather than relying on that fallback.\n- **`yarn lint` ≠ `yarn lint:check`.** The former runs `--fix` and\nignores warnings; CI runs the latter with `--max-warnings=0`. A green\n`yarn lint` says nothing about CI.\n\n## Notes\n\nA freshly generated app still reports 8\n`@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` **warnings** (`yarn lint` exits 0).\nThese are intentional stubs: the parameters sit next to commented-out\nTODO API calls that reference them, so renaming to `_query` would break\nthe code the user is meant to uncomment. Left as-is deliberately.","tree":{"sha":"140302ba32f72be91e95e41e093e880dff21a777","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/140302ba32f72be91e95e41e093e880dff21a777"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/5b0406f2f9b0950bf69b3ba7d16e312f23efd7c5","verification":{"payload":"tree 140302ba32f72be91e95e41e093e880dff21a777\nparent 3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787124152 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787124152 +0300\n\nfix(create-vc-app): make scaffolded apps build and lint out of the box (#302)\n\n## Problem\n\nThree defects reported against the scaffolding, all confirmed:\n\n1. **A generated app did not build.** `Welcome.vue` used `tw-text-s`,\nwhich is not in the framework''s `fontSize` scale (`xxs / xs / sm / base\n/ lg / …`). `@apply` with a non-existent class is a hard PostCSS error,\nnot a silent no-op:\n\n   ```\n[vite:css] [postcss] Welcome.vue?vue&type=style&index=0&lang.scss:20:3:\n     The `tw-text-s` class does not exist.\n   ```\n\n2. **`yarn lint` failed out of the box.** `eslint-plugin-import` and\n`eslint-import-resolver-typescript` were declared in the template''s\n`devDependencies` but never wired into `eslint.config.mjs`, while\n`Welcome.vue` and `routes.ts.ejs` carried `eslint-disable` comments for\n`import/no-unresolved`. ESLint treats a disable directive for an\nunregistered rule as an error:\n\n   ```\n   1:1  error  Definition for rule ''import/no-unresolved'' was not found\n   ✖ 1 problem (1 error)\n   ```\n\n3. **Template code was never linted or formatted.**\n`cli/create-vc-app/src/templates` was listed in both `.prettierignore`\nand the root eslint `ignores`, so even the plain `.ts`/`.vue` files\nthere were unchecked. `prettier --check` flagged 8 files, including a\n`tsconfig.json` with broken indentation.\n\nThe root cause behind all three: templates are `.ejs`, so ESLint and\nPrettier structurally cannot check them. Nothing verified this code, and\nthe extra ignore entries hid even the files that *were* checkable.\n\n## Approach\n\nTemplates cannot be linted directly, so the gate has to be **generate a\nproject and check the output**. That needs two independent layers —\nneither alone is sufficient:\n\n- **EJS whitespace slurping** (`<%_ … -%>`). A bare `<% if %>` on its\nown line emits a blank line into the output. `bootstrap.ts.ejs` and\n`main.ts.ejs` already did this correctly; `routes.ts.ejs` did not,\nproducing output riddled with stray blank lines.\n- **A Prettier pass over the generated tree** (`src/engine/format.ts`),\ncalled from `init` (whole tree) and `add-module` (only the touched\npaths, so it never rewrites files the user owns). This is what\nnormalises the regex splicing in `codegen.ts`.\n\nPrettier alone cannot replace layer 1: it collapses 2+ blank lines to\none but **preserves a single blank line** between statements, so EJS\nartifacts survive a format pass. Layer 1 alone cannot replace layer 2\neither, since it does nothing about the string splicing in `codegen.ts`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Fix `tw-text-s` → `tw-text-sm`; drop the unused `bgImage` import.\n- Wire `eslint-plugin-import` + the typescript resolver in the app\ntemplate and in the monorepo root. `flatConfigs.recommended` must be\nspread **before** the Vue/TS configs (it sets a global\n`languageOptions.ecmaVersion` with no `files` scope and would otherwise\noverride their parsers), and the resolver setting must come **after**\n`flatConfigs.typescript` (which presets a `node` resolver).\n- Disable `import/namespace`, `import/default`,\n`import/no-named-as-default{,-member}`. These parse the *dependency''s*\nsource with espree and produce 48 bogus `Parse errors in imported module\n''@vc-shell/framework''` on a real app. TypeScript already covers them;\n`flatConfigs.typescript` only disables `import/named`.\n- Narrow the `.prettierignore` and root eslint `ignores` entries to\n`**/_yarn`, so the plain template files are covered by `yarn format` and\n`yarn lint` again; format the 8 files this surfaced.\n- Add 8 tests. Four assert that a generated project is Prettier-clean\nacross flag combinations; four assert the raw `renderDir` output is free\nof EJS whitespace artifacts. The second group is required — without it\nthe formatter would silently absorb template bugs.\n- Collapse the duplicate imports that the newly enabled\n`import/no-duplicates` reports (10 framework files, plus three separate\n`from \"vue\"` statements in `PullToRefresh.vue` that `--fix` could not\nmerge).\n\n`framework/index.ts` exports ~18 names both explicitly and via `export\n*` from the same module. That is legal — an explicit export shadows a\nstar export — but `import/export` cannot tell it apart from a real\ncollision, so the rule is disabled for that one file. Cleaning up the\nbarrel is left as a follow-up.\n\n## Second commit: `add-module` codegen\n\nWriting the tests above surfaced that `codegen.ts` — which edits\n*existing* source with regexes — had no test coverage and three defects.\nEach was reproduced before being fixed.\n\n**`add-module` never registered the module.** The anchor was\n`/\\.use\\([A-Z]\\w+,\\s*\\{\\s*router\\s*\\}\\)/`, but the template emits\n`app.use(Orders);`. Nothing matched, `lastMatch` stayed `null`, no\n`app.use()` was inserted — and the command still printed:\n\n```\n✔ Updated src/main.ts — added import & app.use(Reviews)\n```\n\nThe module was imported, unused, and never registered, so the feature\nsilently did nothing. This is current behaviour on `main`, not a\nhypothetical.\n\n**A multi-line trailing import got corrupted.** `insertImport` matched\n`/^import\\s.+$/gm`, which sees only the first line of a multi-line\nimport:\n\n```ts\nimport {\nimport Orders from \"./modules/orders\";   // ← spliced inside the braces\n  notification,\n} from \"@vc-shell/framework\";\n```\n\n**A nested `});` truncated the menu-item match.**\n`/addMenuItem\\(\\{[\\s\\S]*?\\}\\);/` is lazy, so any menu item containing a\ncallback that ends in `});` caused the new item to land inside the\nprevious one''s body.\n\nStructural edits now run against a mask of the source with comment and\nstring contents replaced by spaces and offsets preserved, so a brace or\nsemicolon inside a string cannot be read as syntax. Call boundaries come\nfrom bracket matching instead of a lazy quantifier, nested calls are\nskipped, imports are scanned to their terminating `;`, and insertions\napply highest-offset-first so earlier positions stay valid.\n`addModuleToMain` throws when an anchor is missing rather than reporting\na change it did not make — `add-module` already catches that and prints\nmanual instructions, and the file is left untouched.\n\n`codegen.test.ts` adds 9 cases. Each result is run through Prettier,\nwhich throws on a syntax error; that check alone would have caught two\nof the three defects.\n\n`magicast` — a library for exactly this kind of edit — was declared in\n`cli/create-vc-app/dependencies` and imported nowhere. Removed in a\nfollow-up commit; it also pinned a second copy in the lockfile, since\n`@vitest/coverage-v8` pulls in `magicast@0.5.3` independently and the\nonly other reference is an optional peer dependency. Reintroducing it is\nthe obvious move if `codegen.ts` ever outgrows the\nmask-plus-bracket-matching approach.\n\n## Third commit: a generated app now lints clean\n\n`yarn lint` in a generated project reported seven `no-unused-vars`\nwarnings on placeholder parameters (`query`, `ids`, `id`,\n`setBroadcastFilter`) that the commented-out TODO API calls reference.\nRenaming them to `_query` would break the code the user is meant to\nuncomment, so each gets a scoped `eslint-disable-next-line … -- reason`\n— the idiom the template already uses in `bootstrap.ts.ejs` for the\nunused `app` parameter, and one that disappears once the TODO is\nimplemented.\n\nSilencing those exposed two more warnings that had been invisible,\nbecause `yarn lint` runs `--fix` and was rewriting the freshly generated\nproject on its first run:\n\n- `bootstrap.ts` imported `vue` twice — `App`, then `markRaw` inside the\ndashboard conditional. Now one conditional specifier list, `import {\nApp<% if (dashboard) { %>, markRaw<% } %> } from \"vue\";`.\n- `useList.ts` carried an `eslint-disable-next-line\n@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` aimed at the wrong line and naming a\nrule the template config turns off. ESLint flagged it as an unused\ndirective; removed.\n\nGenerated with and without `--dashboard`, `add-module` run on each: no\nerrors and no warnings in either variant. The dashboard variant also\ntype-checks and builds.\n\n## Verification\n\nScaffolded an app with the built CLI (`standalone`, module, dashboard,\ntenant routes, mocks) plus `add-module`, then ran it for real:\n\n| Step | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `yarn install` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn build` (`vite build` + `vue-tsc`) | **exit 0**,\n`dist/index.html` + `dist/types/` produced |\n| `yarn type-check` | exit 0 |\n| `yarn lint` | exit 0, **0 errors, 0 warnings** |\n| `yarn preview` → HTTP | `200`, correct title, CSS and JS bundles\nserved |\n| Headless boot | Vue mounts, redirects to `#/login`, login form\nrenders, no `pageerror` |\n\nAfter `add-module reviews`, `main.ts` now reads:\n\n```ts\n  app.use(Orders);\n  app.use(Sample);\n  app.use(Reviews);   // ← previously missing entirely\n  app.use(router);\n```\n\nand the app with the registered module still builds, type-checks and\nlints clean.\n\nThe emitted CSS is correct, not merely non-crashing:\n\n```css\n.dashboard-widget-welcome__welcome-description{…;font-size:.875rem;…}\n```\n\n`.875rem` is exactly the `sm` value from `framework/tailwind.config.ts`.\n\n**Negative controls** — each fix was checked to be load-bearing:\n\n- Restoring `tw-text-s` in the built app fails `vite build` with the\nPostCSS error above.\n- Reverting the EJS slurping fails the 4 template tests while the 4\nPrettier tests stay green, confirming the two layers are independent.\n- Disabling `formatGenerated` fails only the 4 Prettier tests.\n\nAll CI gates were run in a **fresh, unbuilt worktree** (matching what CI\nsees): `lint:check`, `format:check`, `stylelint:check`, `typecheck`,\n`check:locales`, `check:circular`, `check:layers` — all exit 0.\nFramework suite: 3791 tests in 403 files pass. CLI suite: 67 tests (was\n50).\n\nThree things made a local green run misleading, which is worth knowing\nfor anyone touching these configs:\n\n- **CI lints without building** (`yarn install --immutable` → `yarn\nlint:check`, no build step in between). Every `@vc-shell/*` workspace\npackage resolves through `main`/`types` fields pointing into `dist/`, so\nnone of them resolve on CI. A leftover `framework/dist` hides this\nlocally.\n- **Resolver fallback to `src/` is platform-dependent.** With the ignore\nnarrowed to `^@vc-shell/framework/`, the Linux runner reported 6\n`import/no-unresolved` errors for `@vc-shell/mf-config` and\n`@vc-shell/config-generator` that macOS did not — reproduced neither by\ndeleting `framework/dist` nor by a clean `yarn install --immutable`.\n`eslint-import-resolver-typescript` v4 uses the native `unrs-resolver`,\nwhich behaves differently per platform. Hence the ignore covers\n`^@vc-shell/` rather than relying on that fallback.\n- **`yarn lint` ≠ `yarn lint:check`.** The former runs `--fix` and\nignores warnings; CI runs the latter with `--max-warnings=0`. A green\n`yarn lint` says nothing about CI.\n\n## Notes\n\nA freshly generated app still reports 8\n`@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` **warnings** (`yarn lint` exits 0).\nThese are intentional stubs: the parameters sit next to commented-out\nTODO API calls that reference them, so renaming to `_query` would break\nthe code the user is meant to uncomment. Left as-is deliberately.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhVm5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIp8QAB5W3x6gKGYZ8ThtjP7Uqprv\noHdjit8FkktKsNFa4o1uH6nA8j+QI9ryk88gkS3POfAK4OHCOufQ/1ZfxsgDNV/R\nJHAGxmQa3TcSlwkeNuzWeHmxXbJVAZszbdMfGytAB5m9JWFk/i7kVNB436ENpcB+\n0Euec/JmZkJrGzwDWkvuqNnHO8DIx+Cck++LARfYyDwXK4bp5ytdxFQU/wF9ApTL\nfVN4QX2p03YpF/S1+sKfdjrr0ZB3X4L5KsrGb8K6J25J4o1tbQEzVM+pXzFzuQ7R\nFqj7Bb6tFXErxd4dHVqDSvQdEbwKYn0KWhfpzY9Im5LV/IAuMBthHqWrs04Qckve\nkNlwLOB13e7PZ+sMDBT7b7kb9nzCB8/d+pAzbyu5HOibYyuicOX/z3O1lluOc8LN\nyVBvw4O1aE0qpola/RdpPC/vTSIgRgbCF7ksTwylKIqdatalSflLq+bQgCHsVwQP\nacVvSwLy5Uaf55QpZQNQdkxHpkexywGToE/CqbB0i4kIZjH4mjd+QSg4R7nZ119J\nT5V1peyXE4DB8ilnrITQ38mJ0C/m2/Eeu7vZvk/ghTM04dgAdXJhHSeOLnFhdoDl\nGWJeTrGrtjxFSvqL/if1GOKHG9SPNMmD6ehc69AVU+wfdqmq7nEw0YLHSYpzp8/+\noDOaI/FOS4eKIBCs/BPO\n=/EFu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T07:22:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/5b0406f2f9b0950bf69b3ba7d16e312f23efd7c5","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDViMDQwNmYyZjliMDk1MGJmNjliM2JhN2QxNmUzMTJmMjNlZmQ3YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86","sha":"3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86"}],"sha":"5b0406f2f9b0950bf69b3ba7d16e312f23efd7c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/5b0406f2f9b0950bf69b3ba7d16e312f23efd7c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:19:57Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:19:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): reset the popup close lifecycle on reopen and isolate secondary roots (#306)\n\nCloses VCST-5632 remainder. Two parts of the ticket were still open\nafter #284/#286.\n\n## 1. Reopening a popup left it in a closing state\n\n`closing` stayed `true` and the fallback timer from the previous close\nwas still armed. Opening now cancels that timer and clears the flag, and\n`finalize` only removes an instance that is actually closing — so a\nleave transition from an earlier close cannot unmount a popup that has\nbeen reopened in the meantime.\n\nThe original opener is kept on reopen, and focus restore still runs from\nthe single `removeInstance` path.\n\nNote the mechanism differs from the original theory in the ticket: the\npopup does **not** get unmounted by the stale timer. It stays mounted\nbut stuck in a closing state. The fix addresses what actually happens.\n\n## 2. `inert` missed two secondary roots\n\nIsolation reached the blade stack but not:\n\n- the AI panel, which is a sibling of the stack\n- the mobile slide-out menu, which lives outside the inert top-bar root\n\nBoth now receive the state explicitly rather than relying on\nTransition/Teleport attribute fallthrough, which does not reach the real\nroot element.\n\n## Deliberately not added\n\nA focus trap for a maximized blade. It is not a modal, and trapping Tab\nin a non-modal region cuts the user off from the browser chrome. `inert`\non everything behind it is what 2.4.3 / 4.1.2 ask for. This was argued\nin VCST-5670''s description and is recorded here so the omission is\nexplicit rather than silent.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Live: with a blade maximized, both the AI panel and the primary\nnavigation report `inert`, and the panel''s own controls are correctly\nunfocusable in that state\n- `403 files / 3799 tests` green on this branch alone","tree":{"sha":"69b2bce1ceda9ea5d788417471cf3ef95b2edb4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/69b2bce1ceda9ea5d788417471cf3ef95b2edb4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86","verification":{"payload":"tree 69b2bce1ceda9ea5d788417471cf3ef95b2edb4a\nparent 565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787123997 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787123997 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): reset the popup close lifecycle on reopen and isolate secondary roots (#306)\n\nCloses VCST-5632 remainder. Two parts of the ticket were still open\nafter #284/#286.\n\n## 1. Reopening a popup left it in a closing state\n\n`closing` stayed `true` and the fallback timer from the previous close\nwas still armed. Opening now cancels that timer and clears the flag, and\n`finalize` only removes an instance that is actually closing — so a\nleave transition from an earlier close cannot unmount a popup that has\nbeen reopened in the meantime.\n\nThe original opener is kept on reopen, and focus restore still runs from\nthe single `removeInstance` path.\n\nNote the mechanism differs from the original theory in the ticket: the\npopup does **not** get unmounted by the stale timer. It stays mounted\nbut stuck in a closing state. The fix addresses what actually happens.\n\n## 2. `inert` missed two secondary roots\n\nIsolation reached the blade stack but not:\n\n- the AI panel, which is a sibling of the stack\n- the mobile slide-out menu, which lives outside the inert top-bar root\n\nBoth now receive the state explicitly rather than relying on\nTransition/Teleport attribute fallthrough, which does not reach the real\nroot element.\n\n## Deliberately not added\n\nA focus trap for a maximized blade. It is not a modal, and trapping Tab\nin a non-modal region cuts the user off from the browser chrome. `inert`\non everything behind it is what 2.4.3 / 4.1.2 ask for. This was argued\nin VCST-5670''s description and is recorded here so the omission is\nexplicit rather than silent.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Live: with a blade maximized, both the AI panel and the primary\nnavigation report `inert`, and the panel''s own controls are correctly\nunfocusable in that state\n- `403 files / 3799 tests` green on this branch alone","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhVkdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyK0QAK0CnWjcR5ztOn6+nNbrP/0y\n+/ezH1vbv6bhF2HRoz5lUPP0FDe4gWkhPuR4PlceUMNfG7s1Y2DdJfaOK8ichQwd\nbyXPuv24aN/VndvZtsAC/FgCMUOrXIKf/Hm2d2tZ90Bd38S+T0TnxK8mx1EqA1JF\nea+0zujZUdZZeoXE5W/tfZAYYc12MACPN8wB2iwrUv9I6CGxBsqrkFl9TOo6xBBD\n6vsoyrFU7+rPPEMsqQk24AvPBxZg13nu2WhFWggLP2HA4ZNxw525LwpgF3yYd/cd\nRGUHA5c74IMfjYrqPnkWPzihoOH2YC5CLMBe+sZJF6rLh79nVYzZusXumrqKKYe2\nSqfAIhkq1Aaa284AHrlw6Pn7gfMEvHLaH9hCFVOqFXEafS0Zs7Lc5qrxBmqs7PqH\nGkN68+YGRlcNrkdOZSn1EG07PQmlx88vx8F8rm7TAUPYmZEupLZyxhpfL/RylUNd\nJ9yW3Gh+YhQhAMx307j1zHoKFhBKvS3sGUnELn7d5xjf2/pOyoWr2kUZ3V/AX5eo\nEdmIsWW3I7l0+BIgKGkLG+E9rFEQbnQIZ5Ux0tzWA+iHPHq/fkg6R6UcA1Y7olEp\nQHaTkmDK81YMKtIiZd1PdiffLLWT9gD1OV51Jl0DKv7MyJDxz+GsMohdrI5TNv/a\nL3KBR5DJ5SnsiMxBr8xR\n=kLIk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T07:19:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDNjZDI3NjFhYWU5ZjM2ZDUxYzU5YzYzNzdmOWE0MzE4ZTgxZWVlODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015","sha":"565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015"}],"sha":"3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/3cd2761aae9f36d51c59c6377f9a4318e81eee86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56427313?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrewEhlo","id":56427313,"login":"AndrewEhlo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDI3MzEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewEhlo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:14:35Z","email":"56427313+AndrewEhlo@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Andrew"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:14:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: bump deprecated actions (VCST-5248) (#309)\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What does this PR do? Brief description of the change and\nmotivation. -->\n\n## Related Issues\n\n<!-- Closes #issue-number. Remove section if not applicable. -->\n\n## Test Plan\n\n<!-- How was this tested? Check all that apply. -->\n\n- [ ] `yarn check` passes locally\n- [ ] `yarn workspace @vc-shell/framework run test` passes\n- [ ] Manual UI verification in Storybook or vendor-portal app (if\napplicable)\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n<!-- Any breaking changes for consumers? If none, write \"None.\" -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] PR title follows [Conventional\nCommits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) (`feat:`, `fix:`,\n`docs:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`, `test:`, `perf:`, `ci:`, `build:`,\n`style:`, or `revert:`)\n- [ ] Documentation updated (`README.md` / `*.docs.md`)\n- [ ] Tests added or updated\n- [ ] No new ESLint warnings (`yarn lint:check`)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Changes are limited to workflow action pins and publish-script\nresilience; no application runtime or auth logic changes.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Updates CI/CD workflows to newer **GitHub Actions** versions\n(`actions/checkout` and `actions/setup-node` to **v7**,\n`amannn/action-semantic-pull-request` to **v6**, `actions/github-script`\nto **v9**, and Docker build/login/push actions to **v4/v7**) across\n`ci`, docs lint, PR title, publish, storybook, and sync-docs workflows.\n> \n> **`scripts/publish-packages.ts`** now wraps `npm publish` with up to\n**3 attempts** and a **15s** delay to handle transient registry **409\nConflict** errors when multiple packages publish in sequence. After a\nfailure it checks the registry with `npm view` and **skips** if that\nversion is already published, so retries and partial runs do not fail on\n**403** duplicate publishes.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n8ac73ada19c83494a1659bd3718a44aa993e6a9f. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Maksim <maxim.zinchuk@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"b24d058c6322d318e331b2923db63159d9b974fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/b24d058c6322d318e331b2923db63159d9b974fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015","verification":{"payload":"tree b24d058c6322d318e331b2923db63159d9b974fa\nparent c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44\nauthor Andrew <56427313+AndrewEhlo@users.noreply.github.com> 1787123675 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787123675 +0300\n\nci: bump deprecated actions (VCST-5248) (#309)\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What does this PR do? Brief description of the change and\nmotivation. -->\n\n## Related Issues\n\n<!-- Closes #issue-number. Remove section if not applicable. -->\n\n## Test Plan\n\n<!-- How was this tested? Check all that apply. -->\n\n- [ ] `yarn check` passes locally\n- [ ] `yarn workspace @vc-shell/framework run test` passes\n- [ ] Manual UI verification in Storybook or vendor-portal app (if\napplicable)\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n<!-- Any breaking changes for consumers? If none, write \"None.\" -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] PR title follows [Conventional\nCommits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) (`feat:`, `fix:`,\n`docs:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`, `test:`, `perf:`, `ci:`, `build:`,\n`style:`, or `revert:`)\n- [ ] Documentation updated (`README.md` / `*.docs.md`)\n- [ ] Tests added or updated\n- [ ] No new ESLint warnings (`yarn lint:check`)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Changes are limited to workflow action pins and publish-script\nresilience; no application runtime or auth logic changes.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Updates CI/CD workflows to newer **GitHub Actions** versions\n(`actions/checkout` and `actions/setup-node` to **v7**,\n`amannn/action-semantic-pull-request` to **v6**, `actions/github-script`\nto **v9**, and Docker build/login/push actions to **v4/v7**) across\n`ci`, docs lint, PR title, publish, storybook, and sync-docs workflows.\n> \n> **`scripts/publish-packages.ts`** now wraps `npm publish` with up to\n**3 attempts** and a **15s** delay to handle transient registry **409\nConflict** errors when multiple packages publish in sequence. After a\nfailure it checks the registry with `npm view` and **skips** if that\nversion is already published, so retries and partial runs do not fail on\n**403** duplicate publishes.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n8ac73ada19c83494a1659bd3718a44aa993e6a9f. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Maksim <maxim.zinchuk@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhVfbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAIkQAJ9xQIx99BLEYkQ0P/5uX1FU\nSpHJ72WskgIzk2bLN1G3wyICRuJoUNCt+MtNNiHL0tB8mfoF5w1UJtvBXUmgseP2\ngO/B6LafHgYLdQx7CeZtsVAEKmkMYgIww8u2kB/Pvz8EkI7a6iuDLvA9+xtjzfc+\nxVUc0C5pHhGzUwL5CMtjV4oF2ivFvjAaoFx6RbFOlEEVxvDhM0i0LKRRqCqB6wPh\nYYxWb2D2BH/ZzZfPD5s2ZxlgMjQDub8PrD8sKVYjo2Q3YpNoyAMDAcC0Jue/FCr3\nes1b0/tQL2zM/yy/PVXG4d1zogw6/4u+nDBtaDV8HOenaiaCbkSmuQeN0jTQzXtC\nY9AeLyEDG4WF/5FGKSra5LCrMvK/+uXzVnQqHhgICfrnKED6V3FA4fDe0h/GYBEr\n/vWQPO80L013kFKg4lQ13ZUU7p8JFe6994hIXY3kyXcKRyLjmT73vJxYWOWoZn07\nnpVXDNpQW3SDh0oi98iTn6R8i8RgTpYdynZdAi/WY8XGf3liOWamdtumOYHIog5K\nQC/XEAUhRC8uyD+sijTjf40/g4cNQOjtL2F+LLjlx7/1uveglDmqeF2OiwMghIf5\nAqD7rXngueCaSfzfTyPiWOkRigkuFo3MtQ7OmMzWRmdtTqOfNmVlZn559DSfOY5o\nxRbFU7DIsDLKwRbPLNqC\n=Rm8y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T07:14:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDU2NWIwNWE1N2ViMWMxYTRhZDFhODE0OWI0NTM5ZGIzODA3MTIwMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44","sha":"c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44"}],"sha":"565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/565b05a57eb1c1a4ad1a8149b4539db380712015"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:44:47Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:44:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): stop blade loading from unmounting the control that has focus (#301)\n\nAddresses VCST-5670. Two unrelated failures behind one symptom — focus\ndropped to `<body>`, so the next Tab restarted from the top of the\ndocument (WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order).\n\n## 1. Save\n\n**Not** the Save button disabling itself. `ToolbarBaseButton` never sets\nnative `disabled` — only a class and a guard in `handleClick`. Verified:\nafter a save the button is `disabledClass: true, nativelyDisabled:\nfalse`.\n\nThe real cause: `loading` is provided blade-wide from `vc-blade.vue`,\nand every control swaps itself for a skeleton — toolbar buttons in\n`BladeToolbar.vue:11`, and **every field** through `vc-input.vue:4`''s\n`bladeLoading` branch. A save raises that flag, so the focused element\nis unmounted. That also takes the field out from under a user who was\ntyping, which is why `Ctrl/Cmd+S` loses focus by the same route.\n\nA skeleton stands in for content that has not rendered yet. Once the\nblade has shown real content, `loading` means something is in flight,\nand replacing the controls then is wrong on its own terms — design\nsystems keep the control mounted and show its pending state in place\n(`LoadingButton` in MUI, `loading` on Ant Design''s Button,\nspinner-in-button in Bootstrap and Carbon). Skeletons are for initial\nload.\n\nSo `useBladeSkeleton` makes the skeleton available exactly once, before\nthe first render of real content. After that, `loading` is reported\nthrough `aria-busy` and each control''s own pending state —\n`ToolbarBaseButton` already has `isWaiting`.\n\n**No module changes.** Consumers keep passing a single `loading` prop.\n\n## 2. Sign-in\n\nThe route watcher in `vc-app.vue` could never catch it: `/login` and the\nshell are sibling routes, so the watcher is created *after* that\nnavigation has finished, and the workspace mounts later still — when the\napp reports ready — without a further route change. The workspace\nelement appearing is the signal, so watch that. The route watcher stays\nfor route changes within a mounted shell.\n\n## Measured, not assumed\n\nLocal vendor-portal against the real API, reading\n`document.activeElement` at each transition:\n\n| Transition | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| sign-in | `<body>` | `main.vc-app__workspace` |\n| open workspace | menu button | unchanged |\n| open details blade | table row in blade | unchanged |\n| Maximize | `[aria-label=\"Restore\"]` | unchanged |\n| **Save** (POST 200) | **`<body>`** |\n**`button.vc-blade-toolbar-base-button`** |\n\nMy first Save measurement was void and discarded — the button was still\n`--disabled`, so the click hit the early return and nothing saved. The\nform has to be dirtied first for the measurement to mean anything.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 4 new tests for `useBladeSkeleton`, 2 for the sign-in watcher\n(including one that pins it *not* stealing focus when something already\nholds it) — all written first and observed failing\n- `vitest run ui/components/organisms/vc-app\nui/components/organisms/vc-blade` — 399 passed / 42 files. The\n`BladeToolbar` tests that assert skeleton replacement and mobile removal\nstill pass: they exercise the initial load, which is unchanged.\n- Full suite: 4411 passed, 2 failed — `useConnectionStatus` and\n`useNotificationStore`, both pre-existing 5s timeouts under parallel\nload that pass in isolation and fail identically without this change.\n- `yarn typecheck` exit 0; eslint, prettier, `check:locales`,\n`check:layers` pass\n\n## Not covered\n\n**Mobile.** `useToolbarRegistration` filters disabled items out of the\ntoolbar on mobile only, so a Save that disables itself is removed from\nthe DOM by a route the skeleton latch does not touch. Showing disabled\nitems on mobile is a product change rather than an a11y repair, so it is\nleft alone — flagging it rather than burying it. The mobile measurement\nitself is also unverified: the mobile toolbar hides items behind an\nexpandable menu and needs a different driver.\n\n---\n\n## Update: second commit — re-arm the skeleton when the entity changes\n\nFound while re-verifying the open VCST board. The one-shot latch fixed\nthe focus loss but went one step too far: a blade instance that switches\nto a **different entity in place** then rendered the second entity with\nno loading skeleton at all, because the latch had already been set by\nthe first.\n\nThe latch now resets on a change of entity context, keyed on\n`BladeDescriptor.param`. Query state and descriptor identity are\ndeliberately excluded, so paging, filtering and sorting cannot re-arm\nit.\n\nThe distinction that matters: a save-style loading cycle — same entity,\n`loading` raised again — must **not** re-arm the skeleton, or this\nchange would silently restore the very bug this PR fixes. Both\ndirections are now pinned by tests.\n\n### Re-verified live on a local vendor-portal against a real API\n\n```\nSave (Enter on the toolbar button)\n  0 skeleton mutations\n  focus stays on button.vc-blade-toolbar-base-button\n  the Color field keeps its DOM node (not remounted)\n\nEntity switch (offer dd54b307 -> bb4e5f1c in the same blade)\n  skeleton re-appears for the newly opened entity\n```\n\n`404 files / 3798 tests` green on this branch alone.","tree":{"sha":"23a070164b5de0b311cb11b64e5e0a38a2b30c42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/23a070164b5de0b311cb11b64e5e0a38a2b30c42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44","verification":{"payload":"tree 23a070164b5de0b311cb11b64e5e0a38a2b30c42\nparent ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787064287 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787064287 +0300\n\nfix(a11y): stop blade loading from unmounting the control that has focus (#301)\n\nAddresses VCST-5670. Two unrelated failures behind one symptom — focus\ndropped to `<body>`, so the next Tab restarted from the top of the\ndocument (WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order).\n\n## 1. Save\n\n**Not** the Save button disabling itself. `ToolbarBaseButton` never sets\nnative `disabled` — only a class and a guard in `handleClick`. Verified:\nafter a save the button is `disabledClass: true, nativelyDisabled:\nfalse`.\n\nThe real cause: `loading` is provided blade-wide from `vc-blade.vue`,\nand every control swaps itself for a skeleton — toolbar buttons in\n`BladeToolbar.vue:11`, and **every field** through `vc-input.vue:4`''s\n`bladeLoading` branch. A save raises that flag, so the focused element\nis unmounted. That also takes the field out from under a user who was\ntyping, which is why `Ctrl/Cmd+S` loses focus by the same route.\n\nA skeleton stands in for content that has not rendered yet. Once the\nblade has shown real content, `loading` means something is in flight,\nand replacing the controls then is wrong on its own terms — design\nsystems keep the control mounted and show its pending state in place\n(`LoadingButton` in MUI, `loading` on Ant Design''s Button,\nspinner-in-button in Bootstrap and Carbon). Skeletons are for initial\nload.\n\nSo `useBladeSkeleton` makes the skeleton available exactly once, before\nthe first render of real content. After that, `loading` is reported\nthrough `aria-busy` and each control''s own pending state —\n`ToolbarBaseButton` already has `isWaiting`.\n\n**No module changes.** Consumers keep passing a single `loading` prop.\n\n## 2. Sign-in\n\nThe route watcher in `vc-app.vue` could never catch it: `/login` and the\nshell are sibling routes, so the watcher is created *after* that\nnavigation has finished, and the workspace mounts later still — when the\napp reports ready — without a further route change. The workspace\nelement appearing is the signal, so watch that. The route watcher stays\nfor route changes within a mounted shell.\n\n## Measured, not assumed\n\nLocal vendor-portal against the real API, reading\n`document.activeElement` at each transition:\n\n| Transition | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| sign-in | `<body>` | `main.vc-app__workspace` |\n| open workspace | menu button | unchanged |\n| open details blade | table row in blade | unchanged |\n| Maximize | `[aria-label=\"Restore\"]` | unchanged |\n| **Save** (POST 200) | **`<body>`** |\n**`button.vc-blade-toolbar-base-button`** |\n\nMy first Save measurement was void and discarded — the button was still\n`--disabled`, so the click hit the early return and nothing saved. The\nform has to be dirtied first for the measurement to mean anything.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 4 new tests for `useBladeSkeleton`, 2 for the sign-in watcher\n(including one that pins it *not* stealing focus when something already\nholds it) — all written first and observed failing\n- `vitest run ui/components/organisms/vc-app\nui/components/organisms/vc-blade` — 399 passed / 42 files. The\n`BladeToolbar` tests that assert skeleton replacement and mobile removal\nstill pass: they exercise the initial load, which is unchanged.\n- Full suite: 4411 passed, 2 failed — `useConnectionStatus` and\n`useNotificationStore`, both pre-existing 5s timeouts under parallel\nload that pass in isolation and fail identically without this change.\n- `yarn typecheck` exit 0; eslint, prettier, `check:locales`,\n`check:layers` pass\n\n## Not covered\n\n**Mobile.** `useToolbarRegistration` filters disabled items out of the\ntoolbar on mobile only, so a Save that disables itself is removed from\nthe DOM by a route the skeleton latch does not touch. Showing disabled\nitems on mobile is a product change rather than an a11y repair, so it is\nleft alone — flagging it rather than burying it. The mobile measurement\nitself is also unverified: the mobile toolbar hides items behind an\nexpandable menu and needs a different driver.\n\n---\n\n## Update: second commit — re-arm the skeleton when the entity changes\n\nFound while re-verifying the open VCST board. The one-shot latch fixed\nthe focus loss but went one step too far: a blade instance that switches\nto a **different entity in place** then rendered the second entity with\nno loading skeleton at all, because the latch had already been set by\nthe first.\n\nThe latch now resets on a change of entity context, keyed on\n`BladeDescriptor.param`. Query state and descriptor identity are\ndeliberately excluded, so paging, filtering and sorting cannot re-arm\nit.\n\nThe distinction that matters: a save-style loading cycle — same entity,\n`loading` raised again — must **not** re-arm the skeleton, or this\nchange would silently restore the very bug this PR fixes. Both\ndirections are now pinned by tests.\n\n### Re-verified live on a local vendor-portal against a real API\n\n```\nSave (Enter on the toolbar button)\n  0 skeleton mutations\n  focus stays on button.vc-blade-toolbar-base-button\n  the Color field keeps its DOM node (not remounted)\n\nEntity switch (offer dd54b307 -> bb4e5f1c in the same blade)\n  skeleton re-appears for the newly opened entity\n```\n\n`404 files / 3798 tests` green on this branch alone.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhG/fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjw8QAIPVE74g/HIk9noplmh4R13D\nqTAQhPhL5Vz5APP39xD2OWUoMfSDpsR/v0B5jPS4dMoEFUSO4x48Inu4rLOwGGlu\nRSUG6910qBg57F/irGs3NjQQBqGmn0gv+b15m160C/eGKfOdJuPS6ON9DA7gfTzc\n7gOFjoFVz2Vfm4NwU+h9BxaN24J/kRXC4h4YAGzEDne0yVfbFA3FuaduwfFPad2A\nhgjDvbZGaC1ODrx3RnOpLncj16q9VyFDaG13CjImKD3TpcU7UaTGAL+PFGTSsPfP\nwOIpJP7UpECgWCd+yU5jyHAI+zztNDzwrmS3OmPEWZqx93XUoCKxos+qXbEryaY+\ntg7B3IaBSg93csfcuEGKFz9IR6p7dl8yCbaX0sNzuF4QNPcLqWdfJjnBu2Yg2w3+\nbXY+Vq7V4Irso4bQpyIY41ESe3S/AEPw77BAt3keU0asLKHzaqFR7wqul0z9aGwP\noaXNZE7+NDZUJlTWviXoCVl1rzNVMb9MQB9V5HN6GxoOVgs7R35dKTgiyxPoZxBV\nKSfqv15b6s2LMbMllmPiLSF1kvyr4XehPgur/geGC8zgeyghTHcCfnx8iN/uX69T\n/s+PD2UBVQTFUWZI3t007HY5vtuhULsoqdQimkvgAsbasiXXuh8Gojcq5U6U2w7N\nZpRm7Y/KEc1HCE+uLtGn\n=NxH1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T14:44:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGMwYjA3MDA3ZGZhNWY5MDA2OGJhYmZmOTk3ZDRmZTUzMzQ0YWRjNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8","sha":"ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8"}],"sha":"c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c0b07007dfa5f90068babff997d4fe53344adc44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:40:21Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:40:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(a11y): guard three shipped fixes that nothing was pinning (#308)\n\nNo production code changed.\n\n## Why\n\nFound while re-verifying the open VCST board. VCST-5596, VCST-5672 and\nVCST-5677 are all correctly fixed in the source — but reverting any of\nthem left the suite green, so nothing was protecting them. Each now has\na test that fails on revert.\n\n| Ticket | Guard |\n| --- | --- |\n| VCST-5596 | the blade overflow trigger''s 24px minimum box, asserted on\nthe compiled CSS — axe cannot see it because of the 2.5.8 spacing\nexception |\n| VCST-5677 | the scheduler''s own dark-theme surface token, so the\ntoolbar and weekday header cannot silently return to a light background\n|\n| VCST-5672 | the TimelineView story keeping the stateful renderer, so\nits toolbar cannot regress to emitting without updating the grid |\n\n## Also\n\nRecords at the framework boundary what `useDynamicProperties` produces\nfor a cleared value: `values: []`.\n\nThat is the evidence VCST-5679 needs. The client demonstrably sends the\nempty array — confirmed against the real request body on vcmp-dev — so\nthe value that survives a save is not being dropped on this side of the\nwire. A direct `GET` after saving showed the property still set, and in\nfact **accumulating duplicates** on a property declared `multivalue:\nfalse`. That ticket belongs to the backend; this test pins our half of\nthe contract so it cannot drift while the server side is investigated.\n\n## Verification\n\n`406 files / 3795 tests` green on this branch alone.","tree":{"sha":"ce0711728db40cacf4e96b193c66965437fa24d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/ce0711728db40cacf4e96b193c66965437fa24d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8","verification":{"payload":"tree ce0711728db40cacf4e96b193c66965437fa24d8\nparent 9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787064021 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787064021 +0300\n\ntest(a11y): guard three shipped fixes that nothing was pinning (#308)\n\nNo production code changed.\n\n## Why\n\nFound while re-verifying the open VCST board. VCST-5596, VCST-5672 and\nVCST-5677 are all correctly fixed in the source — but reverting any of\nthem left the suite green, so nothing was protecting them. Each now has\na test that fails on revert.\n\n| Ticket | Guard |\n| --- | --- |\n| VCST-5596 | the blade overflow trigger''s 24px minimum box, asserted on\nthe compiled CSS — axe cannot see it because of the 2.5.8 spacing\nexception |\n| VCST-5677 | the scheduler''s own dark-theme surface token, so the\ntoolbar and weekday header cannot silently return to a light background\n|\n| VCST-5672 | the TimelineView story keeping the stateful renderer, so\nits toolbar cannot regress to emitting without updating the grid |\n\n## Also\n\nRecords at the framework boundary what `useDynamicProperties` produces\nfor a cleared value: `values: []`.\n\nThat is the evidence VCST-5679 needs. The client demonstrably sends the\nempty array — confirmed against the real request body on vcmp-dev — so\nthe value that survives a save is not being dropped on this side of the\nwire. A direct `GET` after saving showed the property still set, and in\nfact **accumulating duplicates** on a property declared `multivalue:\nfalse`. That ticket belongs to the backend; this test pins our half of\nthe contract so it cannot drift while the server side is investigated.\n\n## Verification\n\n`406 files / 3795 tests` green on this branch alone.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhG7VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYhAQAEIdRr+2RdTnpTYbDWZ/HDVW\ncu5cuXsoDToXlmBxb4t5K7z0gpqxTonCX4sqzeNPuy04Se1laAtfehKwCfmYm5qy\niCRbC9ZsR5ShJJUF2/XlOy51Sm7phcAVC/DXIuzPvXosD48KJXHGLjcpVO3eBznb\nVz4Xt1hD+MiRW7KQ45Ska+4fnT/QDvMJa0CN97rSNMNdR/OOV28YvgHLO9I4sLY1\nkEfM7wrjVLGjjUXN4kGMIrC5ebgdb1HIyV3MDNW/+acBMaBf/xqKb7WPGnIRi65E\nSGbahN0wG7LqnRpRgyrRHJU8cjuhJ0etJfeS6zAPZd63o16vOvrX2BjPUzH5BIi5\n1FhW+dDIoOZuDAPxv8PWh9x/14VekHnQIMSqmE6Wa0w+CZ8OLkGqJhHMpUGhY2ua\nJxZauOv0sG+0SPIHsypOU9qItwkr612HCVlIOpEqtRSt/ZRFpziTrhjTZvU/AYDT\nveCo5sIil+q4TLcE5INdGYMtVK2vMsQL7U1j7DgBuMFOysEL167ff2xh9YlougBs\n8UgA0zqmgAQOeRbPYtoFyHjUyb5ISUXGP8fzIxI7I7bpe+FvUhFrXtr3+6qvw2se\nKFqvMz+YhHkBRVqQNZ765hlH5WKQMOI3mq7wn6v4/FsbkOJpCPY3K9OjWonHGKZI\n9L2vcqhY3tXraKnRjb68\n=oeF1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T14:40:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGVlMDNkNTA0YzIyMGZjNTM0NTA4MDllMzIxNzBlZjEyODQ2ZGRmYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770","sha":"9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770"}],"sha":"ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/ee03d504c220fc53450809e32170ef12846ddfc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:40:12Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:40:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai-agent): validate the sender window, not just its origin (#305)\n\nPart of VCST-5673 — the half that is fixable in this repository.\n\n## Problem\n\n`createMessageTransport` checked `event.origin` against `allowedOrigins`\nbut never checked `event.source`. Any window served from an allowed\norigin could send `CLOSE_PANEL` — another tab, a nested frame, an\nopener. Proven by a test that fails without this change: a message from\nan unrelated window called `closePanel` once.\n\n## Change\n\nIncoming messages must now come from the expected window as well: the\nregistered iframe''s `contentWindow` normally, `window.parent` in\nembedded mode.\n\n## What is NOT fixed here, and why it cannot be\n\nThe rest of the ticket — Escape and Ctrl/Cmd+I being inert while the\nchat holds focus — is not fixable in this repository. The keystroke is\ndelivered to the iframe''s own document, so the host never observes it.\n`ai-agent.docs.md:128` states this, and the relay snippet at `:133`\nbelongs in the chat app, which lives in a separate repository.\n\nVerified live against the real VirtoOz panel: with focus inside the\niframe neither Escape nor Ctrl/Cmd+I closes the panel; with focus on the\nhost, Escape closes the panel **and leaves the blade behind it open**,\nwhich is the correct existing behaviour and is unchanged.\n\nA follow-up ticket in the chat app''s repository is needed for the relay.\n\n## Also\n\nPins the header''s tab order, since the documented fallback route out of\nthe chat is Shift+Tab to the header''s Close button.\n\n## Verification\n\n`403 files / 3795 tests` green on this branch alone.","tree":{"sha":"9fa0a9a34ef286b4440f34401d22d83b45592631","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/9fa0a9a34ef286b4440f34401d22d83b45592631"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770","verification":{"payload":"tree 9fa0a9a34ef286b4440f34401d22d83b45592631\nparent 86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787064012 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787064012 +0300\n\nfix(ai-agent): validate the sender window, not just its origin (#305)\n\nPart of VCST-5673 — the half that is fixable in this repository.\n\n## Problem\n\n`createMessageTransport` checked `event.origin` against `allowedOrigins`\nbut never checked `event.source`. Any window served from an allowed\norigin could send `CLOSE_PANEL` — another tab, a nested frame, an\nopener. Proven by a test that fails without this change: a message from\nan unrelated window called `closePanel` once.\n\n## Change\n\nIncoming messages must now come from the expected window as well: the\nregistered iframe''s `contentWindow` normally, `window.parent` in\nembedded mode.\n\n## What is NOT fixed here, and why it cannot be\n\nThe rest of the ticket — Escape and Ctrl/Cmd+I being inert while the\nchat holds focus — is not fixable in this repository. The keystroke is\ndelivered to the iframe''s own document, so the host never observes it.\n`ai-agent.docs.md:128` states this, and the relay snippet at `:133`\nbelongs in the chat app, which lives in a separate repository.\n\nVerified live against the real VirtoOz panel: with focus inside the\niframe neither Escape nor Ctrl/Cmd+I closes the panel; with focus on the\nhost, Escape closes the panel **and leaves the blade behind it open**,\nwhich is the correct existing behaviour and is unchanged.\n\nA follow-up ticket in the chat app''s repository is needed for the relay.\n\n## Also\n\nPins the header''s tab order, since the documented fallback route out of\nthe chat is Shift+Tab to the header''s Close button.\n\n## Verification\n\n`403 files / 3795 tests` green on this branch alone.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhG7MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZuYQAGnAFWIRsaLa2/2+k+FVO54s\nmTz1GoGKegFQvmj5yiKZ/dOE03GvxGCO93gDTnHJmSdevjsC7NPZRq9IVYPWBPYV\nQuB4uu+sh1uideTEXqNek8dsw5JCRwjyEaZ8sTKyKjBUslHAoyjgijkHMRD8Hifs\n/iLBRi/rkS9Duwd6ORzj8UCyTQrK82uBS+ROgMDUraNWhCllcf1duRvLCdBZ+OnH\nYlFG7o8cHI5g7vKdASPb5ydhfyD+I6LH7Ee1V6SwOjX53svcKN6a844kZbQZtJZN\nf4dFzEfA1fwGv4TMDLJQDpEnnG3EIzDto+oFS5fa/RRZHw/DYWjFQayGJ7P8yQH6\n+jRqWidE0ev4Jb2slTkVitd3wiTGR5JbimiN2R6gyfRw9/ezRCn6MgMiecrIyKo0\nNEjoYbelePkZpTskeTzsQSD23L4GVZufu6lAwd+EopQThVdztZ2HRFZSCbF6qurj\ntWqPBnTn193bdr3z8HCOJ3EfgQRjPVjlhu2P5p7otqCTijbhmtLxT4RugJTIcqku\na4wfFF8UHO2mOvvxBL23KTwCJx6a7C864iqV5B2OGVFpVxWQLzOmWyNLoMWA0Btg\nPnRRcDJXwGHeiSl5ezagP6ZdmCQ5Rpg0F0sUWXMwftkdvN9vsOfYITT82YP5JVAu\n7+kdmLAwtlz7XunBFJoy\n=mL/x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T14:40:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDlhZWEzZGVlMzY3YWNmZjA4ZTFkMGJlNWMwZTAyMjBhMDU2ZjM3NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d","sha":"86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d"}],"sha":"9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9aea3dee367acff08e1d0be5c0e0220a056f3770"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:40:01Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:40:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-scheduler): expose the \"+N more\" overflow as a named dialog (#304)\n\nCloses VCST-5671.\n\n## Problem\n\nOn a day with more than three events, the overflow indicator and every\nevent inside it were reachable by mouse only. #287 turned both into real\nbuttons; three parts of the ticket were still open:\n\n- the panel had no `role` and no accessible name, so a screen reader\nannounced an unlabelled group\n- focus never entered the panel when it mounted already open — which is\nhow it appears after activating \"+N more\"\n- Escape left focus on `<body>` instead of returning it to the trigger\n\nEach is now covered by a test that fails without the fix.\n\n## Change\n\n- `role=\"dialog\"` plus a localized accessible name on the overflow panel\n- focus moves to the first event on initial mount as well as on\nsubsequent opens\n- Escape is consumed locally, so it closes the popover without also\nclosing the blade behind it\n\n`VcPopover` is a shared molecule, so dialog semantics are **opt-in\nprops** rather than baked in — other consumers keep the plain panel they\nhave today.\n\nThe accessible name goes through vue-i18n (`VC_SCHEDULER.MORE_EVENTS`,\nen + de). A hardcoded English label is the defect VCST-5668 filed, so it\nwas not an option here.\n\n## Why the automated gate did not catch this\n\naxe reports zero violations on this story: it cannot see a click handler\non a non-semantic element, and it cannot see a focus transition. The\ncoverage added here is explicit interaction assertions instead.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `403 files / 3795 tests` green on this branch alone\n- `yarn check:locales` passes with the new key in both locales","tree":{"sha":"af3b32550b5db41be0b068b5ea6a1e2a8ab36e38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/af3b32550b5db41be0b068b5ea6a1e2a8ab36e38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d","verification":{"payload":"tree af3b32550b5db41be0b068b5ea6a1e2a8ab36e38\nparent 761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787064001 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787064001 +0300\n\nfix(vc-scheduler): expose the \"+N more\" overflow as a named dialog (#304)\n\nCloses VCST-5671.\n\n## Problem\n\nOn a day with more than three events, the overflow indicator and every\nevent inside it were reachable by mouse only. #287 turned both into real\nbuttons; three parts of the ticket were still open:\n\n- the panel had no `role` and no accessible name, so a screen reader\nannounced an unlabelled group\n- focus never entered the panel when it mounted already open — which is\nhow it appears after activating \"+N more\"\n- Escape left focus on `<body>` instead of returning it to the trigger\n\nEach is now covered by a test that fails without the fix.\n\n## Change\n\n- `role=\"dialog\"` plus a localized accessible name on the overflow panel\n- focus moves to the first event on initial mount as well as on\nsubsequent opens\n- Escape is consumed locally, so it closes the popover without also\nclosing the blade behind it\n\n`VcPopover` is a shared molecule, so dialog semantics are **opt-in\nprops** rather than baked in — other consumers keep the plain panel they\nhave today.\n\nThe accessible name goes through vue-i18n (`VC_SCHEDULER.MORE_EVENTS`,\nen + de). A hardcoded English label is the defect VCST-5668 filed, so it\nwas not an option here.\n\n## Why the automated gate did not catch this\n\naxe reports zero violations on this story: it cannot see a click handler\non a non-semantic element, and it cannot see a focus transition. The\ncoverage added here is explicit interaction assertions instead.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `403 files / 3795 tests` green on this branch alone\n- `yarn check:locales` passes with the new key in both locales","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhG7BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuPIQAAAQufDZkddZykSMiMHl5nl+\nctDqzghShmqmFqcHKkVgI/oXJa+I3GdTNKn2c3O6wibS30+R2axtU+1UupTtMXAc\nS67Cv0AMu2C5xlaX6ugRtW0Rd1uFCzrKtm+LVKkTEwWOnX1jpVMf2pU8r19VCqyL\nB+hA+WIdkdDtcuD+Mvu0L/jxWW/Vo35nlLMKhl3ESP1ywD1R5/QzhD1Mu8ETabBK\nrEL2+Jm/gdfZWSM5+MtLJRl3xF3OE2NK7DtNjr/SM5yy8Jobz9DEcFlT5iYoHe25\nV7DvLSyp24jb7i+q/da1uwZd/9hGKHPS+QNKgBpnlr/iyh9926sQFa2H4vQj64Gg\n2qeaIkA5qv1qvFfPIhipxht37jjSxlO6M5gJ6ji+YJdFcLd/Xu5g3HmMGtNQDCTV\nk8gHzAooRbqsLnue2xQKxsDWv2r/CMJyujRPW1i2ipBqkYWVMVUezVB1ZRfsHU3j\nwb8oDOhtWGWpz91Il2UzdBeQRjLIH1KS8NHZx+Z8USh1VDqjVqe25Ik1MwrK1Bpg\nerWIRHBRYcZfgWY7cRsTUPZiDaiKOy4fB7woE0KhE+h8Ilx6qAdY3Cx6M5o3jkw2\nP4aOQBs5ENPtaMPzknefVxPLMB+jWAKvseAJB2e5kcZjwdhiveM74rUptClqXMn0\nA4Y/sipg6sO1c/hc56do\n=jKs9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T14:40:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDg2ZGVmMTZlMjkzOWUwN2E2NGEyZWJhZjYwMGZlM2QwYjdkMzZkOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4","sha":"761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4"}],"sha":"86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/86def16e2939e07a64a2ebaf600fe3d0b7d36d8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:39:36Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:39:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dashboard): let keyboard events reach controls inside a widget (#303)\n\nCloses VCST-5600 remainder.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe keyboard reorder added in #272/#283 attached its handler to the\nwhole grid item and never checked where the event came from.\n`onWidgetKeydown` `preventDefault()`s Enter and Space unconditionally —\nand that also cancels the synthetic click a native `<button>` receives,\nso every control inside a widget was dead to the keyboard.\n\nMeasured on a local vendor-portal, focus on the Orders widget''s \"90D\"\nbutton, Enter:\n\n```\nbuttonClicked: false       pressedAfter: null\nwidgetLabelAfter: \"Orders, widget 2 of 5. Picked up. Arrow keys move...\"\n```\n\n\"Add product\", \"Add offer\" and the 7D/30D/90D range buttons were all\nunreachable. A fix for 2.5.7 had broken 2.1.1 one level down.\n\nSecond defect in the same handler: picking up a second widget overwrote\n`grabbedOrigin`, so the first could no longer be restored — measured, A\nstayed at `(1,6)` instead of returning to `(0,0)`.\n\n## Change\n\n- Widget shortcuts run only when the grid item itself owns the event, so\ndescendants keep Enter, Space, Escape and the arrow keys.\n- Starting a new move cancels the unfinished one first, which puts that\nwidget back and leaves no invisible half-grabbed state.\n\n## Not changed\n\nEscape restoring displaced neighbours. Real gridstack compaction is\nreversible — moving a widget back pulls the others with it, verified\nlive across five widgets — so no extra layout snapshot is needed. A test\nthat asserted otherwise was modelling its own one-way mock and has been\nremoved.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Live: focus the \"90D\" button, Enter → `buttonClicked: true`,\n`aria-pressed: \"true\"`, widget not grabbed; Enter on the item itself\nstill grabs, ArrowRight still moves; grabbing B returns A to `(0,0)`\n- `403 files / 3800 tests` green on this branch alone\n- New tests cover buttons, links, inputs, selects, textareas,\ncontenteditable, custom tabindex controls, arrows while grabbed, and the\nsecond-grab case","tree":{"sha":"cc0d3598d3bbec8e69314923211dd038b5571302","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/cc0d3598d3bbec8e69314923211dd038b5571302"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4","verification":{"payload":"tree cc0d3598d3bbec8e69314923211dd038b5571302\nparent c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1787063976 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787063976 +0300\n\nfix(dashboard): let keyboard events reach controls inside a widget (#303)\n\nCloses VCST-5600 remainder.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe keyboard reorder added in #272/#283 attached its handler to the\nwhole grid item and never checked where the event came from.\n`onWidgetKeydown` `preventDefault()`s Enter and Space unconditionally —\nand that also cancels the synthetic click a native `<button>` receives,\nso every control inside a widget was dead to the keyboard.\n\nMeasured on a local vendor-portal, focus on the Orders widget''s \"90D\"\nbutton, Enter:\n\n```\nbuttonClicked: false       pressedAfter: null\nwidgetLabelAfter: \"Orders, widget 2 of 5. Picked up. Arrow keys move...\"\n```\n\n\"Add product\", \"Add offer\" and the 7D/30D/90D range buttons were all\nunreachable. A fix for 2.5.7 had broken 2.1.1 one level down.\n\nSecond defect in the same handler: picking up a second widget overwrote\n`grabbedOrigin`, so the first could no longer be restored — measured, A\nstayed at `(1,6)` instead of returning to `(0,0)`.\n\n## Change\n\n- Widget shortcuts run only when the grid item itself owns the event, so\ndescendants keep Enter, Space, Escape and the arrow keys.\n- Starting a new move cancels the unfinished one first, which puts that\nwidget back and leaves no invisible half-grabbed state.\n\n## Not changed\n\nEscape restoring displaced neighbours. Real gridstack compaction is\nreversible — moving a widget back pulls the others with it, verified\nlive across five widgets — so no extra layout snapshot is needed. A test\nthat asserted otherwise was modelling its own one-way mock and has been\nremoved.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Live: focus the \"90D\" button, Enter → `buttonClicked: true`,\n`aria-pressed: \"true\"`, widget not grabbed; Enter on the item itself\nstill grabs, ArrowRight still moves; grabbing B returns A to `(0,0)`\n- `403 files / 3800 tests` green on this branch alone\n- New tests cover buttons, links, inputs, selects, textareas,\ncontenteditable, custom tabindex controls, arrows while grabbed, and the\nsecond-grab case","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhG6oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsu0QAEAr482AxoOpp3EpFOsZkJq/\n5RxDGhYjAj/SR6PAmF+4306M+JFrE6kJiOdSF5glnhTVy5kiUZ5lzJGD7ne+N6xK\n8J4KqjwJkYxIofWMMuDnTnYKYAPDzgyP+yPGrcgrgQVvquiFBpDiC18X/TjnQ1SN\n/t6Mkdvyt47uV7HeL8+HtHREZY2FgLidBvuiZmxRyHZurpnPm2c10TlSCJ6oQCTk\nXpYQ8ZyJ2i19Mw8y4aSyQs6NM3r9NtN8PdahPQCqQR87xh4qKoMJO4YWtGlIh2Cj\nm6OI13En5lK6aEqZIhdu5J8hWQA0giYrkk1U4pI0gpDTYiElnyn245EduvMn2nQ6\nZXDGuoUOStzzI5Krp4K/ZYqTvZC88tSv7OQJdze11wxrFOKNV8R3DWlpqpTo75zj\nXfIqo+D8q1Cv9WbEM1SccVzqlzNQ4a/awQG0CbHPb+z+D7mtUZuFDqT6/xNqs3bD\nejynCkjbQW9qRugp5Nmg4MbldL96yfdMDseONpK6/UID4YrClFOzQR2DhQBXv6WU\nEgcJLhzaBC9NiwtyisBZjC/WiC3QjTvQHnJNK6FOWg8vP8upe38Vpa5lAUhOO1wk\nTX5+wdCMXaa1rLY9wzJxmC0vyH93RJWQnGT37HC4Cwy1kHKPnrDDXkXDVUFzYfs0\nKzguhy82m04vUl2ASxcv\n=q+Uw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T14:39:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDc2MWUyYWMzNTJmNGYzM2M3NjQ2NjAyOTQyN2ZjOWY0MGM3NzkxYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00","sha":"c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00"}],"sha":"761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/761e2ac352f4f33c76466029427fc9f40c7791c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:44Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(composables): add useLatestRequest for latest-wins sequencing (#300)\n\nCloses VCST-5666 (VM-1747).\n\n## Gap\n\nThe framework covers loading state, error state and error notification\n(`useAsync`, `useLoading`, `useErrorHandler`) but nothing for **request\nsequencing**. `useAsync` runs its inner action and rethrows; it has no\nnotion of a superseded call, so a slow earlier response overwrites a\nnewer one.\n\nEvery blade that combines a search field, pagination and a details pane\nneeds this:\n\n- typing in search fires overlapping requests and the slowest one wins;\n- clicking row A then row B can leave A''s details on screen;\n- a response arriving after the blade closed writes into a disposed\nstate.\n\nvc-module-pagebuilder had to write its own helper (4 call sites across\ntwo modules).\n\n## Why a separate composable, not `latest: true` on `useAsync`\n\nThe ticket offered both. The option does not work, for a concrete\nreason: `useAsync.action` returns `Promise<Result>`, and a superseded\ncall **has no `Result` to give**.\n\n- resolve `undefined` → breaks the `Result` type; every caller must\nnull-check\n- reject with a sentinel → collides with the error/notification path\n`useAsync` already owns, and every caller must catch and re-check it\n- never settle → the `await` hangs and its `finally` never runs, so\nloading flags stick\n\nRxJS `switchMap` gets away with latest-wins only because an observable\ncan decline to emit. A promise must settle. Putting the check at the\ncall site is what makes \"do nothing\" expressible:\n\n```ts\nif (!request.isCurrent()) return;\n```\n\nAn opt-in on `useAsync` remains possible later, if it returns a\ndiscriminated result (`{ status: \"superseded\" } | { status: \"ok\", value\n}`) rather than a bare `Result`. This composable is the layer that would\nsit under it.\n\n## Discards, does not cancel\n\nThe generated nswag clients build their own `RequestInit` internally and\ncall `this.http.fetch(url_, transformedOptions_)` — there is **no\n`AbortSignal` parameter** on any generated method, so there is nothing\nto cancel through. Cancellation would need the client regenerated with a\nsignal, which is a separate change. Aborting additionally saves the\nround trip; discarding only fixes correctness, which is what this ticket\nis about.\n\n## API\n\n```ts\nconst search = useLatestRequest();\n\nasync function load(criteria) {\n  const request = search.begin();\n  try {\n    const result = await client.search(criteria);\n    if (!request.isCurrent()) return;   // a newer search won\n    items.value = result;\n  } finally {\n    request.complete();\n  }\n}\n\nsearch.invalidate();  // on selection change\n// dispose() runs itself when the owning scope stops\n```\n\nSemantics ported from the pagebuilder helper, which is proven in\nproduction. Two deliberate deviations:\n\n- **`pending` is a readonly ref**, not an `onPendingChange` callback —\nwatchable, renderable, and it composes with `useLoading`. A caller\nwanting the callback writes `watch(pending, cb)`.\n- **Self-disposes via `onScopeDispose`** when created inside a component\nor effect scope, which covers the third symptom the ticket lists without\nthe caller remembering to wire it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 8 tests, written first and observed failing through the real code path\n(`Error: not implemented`)\n- Covers: newest-wins, the real overlapping-timers race (slow 20ms vs\nfast 0ms — only `fast` is applied), `pending` lifecycle, a superseded\nrequest **not** clearing `pending`, idempotent `complete`, `invalidate`,\npermanent `dispose`, and scope teardown\n- `vitest run core/composables` — 503 passed / 52 files\n- `yarn typecheck` exit 0; `yarn docs:lint` 0 errors; eslint clean;\n`madge --circular` on `core/composables`: none\n- pre-commit `check:locales` and `check:layers` pass\n\nDocs: `useLatestRequest.docs.md` with the two rules that make it correct\n(check `isCurrent()` **after** the await; `complete()` in a `finally`)\nand the corresponding common mistakes.\n\nAdditive only — no existing API changed.","tree":{"sha":"16c17bdf3a0685e17a4dc986d281d647dadf4d49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/16c17bdf3a0685e17a4dc986d281d647dadf4d49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00","verification":{"payload":"tree 16c17bdf3a0685e17a4dc986d281d647dadf4d49\nparent 2e928761fd00092bc9a82fd3a202c04f91c2e40c\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786630964 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786630964 +0300\n\nfeat(composables): add useLatestRequest for latest-wins sequencing (#300)\n\nCloses VCST-5666 (VM-1747).\n\n## Gap\n\nThe framework covers loading state, error state and error notification\n(`useAsync`, `useLoading`, `useErrorHandler`) but nothing for **request\nsequencing**. `useAsync` runs its inner action and rethrows; it has no\nnotion of a superseded call, so a slow earlier response overwrites a\nnewer one.\n\nEvery blade that combines a search field, pagination and a details pane\nneeds this:\n\n- typing in search fires overlapping requests and the slowest one wins;\n- clicking row A then row B can leave A''s details on screen;\n- a response arriving after the blade closed writes into a disposed\nstate.\n\nvc-module-pagebuilder had to write its own helper (4 call sites across\ntwo modules).\n\n## Why a separate composable, not `latest: true` on `useAsync`\n\nThe ticket offered both. The option does not work, for a concrete\nreason: `useAsync.action` returns `Promise<Result>`, and a superseded\ncall **has no `Result` to give**.\n\n- resolve `undefined` → breaks the `Result` type; every caller must\nnull-check\n- reject with a sentinel → collides with the error/notification path\n`useAsync` already owns, and every caller must catch and re-check it\n- never settle → the `await` hangs and its `finally` never runs, so\nloading flags stick\n\nRxJS `switchMap` gets away with latest-wins only because an observable\ncan decline to emit. A promise must settle. Putting the check at the\ncall site is what makes \"do nothing\" expressible:\n\n```ts\nif (!request.isCurrent()) return;\n```\n\nAn opt-in on `useAsync` remains possible later, if it returns a\ndiscriminated result (`{ status: \"superseded\" } | { status: \"ok\", value\n}`) rather than a bare `Result`. This composable is the layer that would\nsit under it.\n\n## Discards, does not cancel\n\nThe generated nswag clients build their own `RequestInit` internally and\ncall `this.http.fetch(url_, transformedOptions_)` — there is **no\n`AbortSignal` parameter** on any generated method, so there is nothing\nto cancel through. Cancellation would need the client regenerated with a\nsignal, which is a separate change. Aborting additionally saves the\nround trip; discarding only fixes correctness, which is what this ticket\nis about.\n\n## API\n\n```ts\nconst search = useLatestRequest();\n\nasync function load(criteria) {\n  const request = search.begin();\n  try {\n    const result = await client.search(criteria);\n    if (!request.isCurrent()) return;   // a newer search won\n    items.value = result;\n  } finally {\n    request.complete();\n  }\n}\n\nsearch.invalidate();  // on selection change\n// dispose() runs itself when the owning scope stops\n```\n\nSemantics ported from the pagebuilder helper, which is proven in\nproduction. Two deliberate deviations:\n\n- **`pending` is a readonly ref**, not an `onPendingChange` callback —\nwatchable, renderable, and it composes with `useLoading`. A caller\nwanting the callback writes `watch(pending, cb)`.\n- **Self-disposes via `onScopeDispose`** when created inside a component\nor effect scope, which covers the third symptom the ticket lists without\nthe caller remembering to wire it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 8 tests, written first and observed failing through the real code path\n(`Error: not implemented`)\n- Covers: newest-wins, the real overlapping-timers race (slow 20ms vs\nfast 0ms — only `fast` is applied), `pending` lifecycle, a superseded\nrequest **not** clearing `pending`, idempotent `complete`, `invalidate`,\npermanent `dispose`, and scope teardown\n- `vitest run core/composables` — 503 passed / 52 files\n- `yarn typecheck` exit 0; `yarn docs:lint` 0 errors; eslint clean;\n`madge --circular` on `core/composables`: none\n- pre-commit `check:locales` and `check:layers` pass\n\nDocs: `useLatestRequest.docs.md` with the two rules that make it correct\n(check `isCurrent()` **after** the await; `complete()` in a `finally`)\nand the corresponding common mistakes.\n\nAdditive only — no existing API changed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfdM0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP1AQAAxcgwn427rCKclmQvWUrxkr\nhLQ04Pg/BptoZy1XwrEXGpO6IATPz1ktFKnTXkTMoCtuufLFm8h2lu/4Q+pRldKa\nA059CzvCEzbROonhP6vut+/wEgOo9Ikf74EaDpZDVbt69H0ZTS1FMp8iB4QIGqXz\nTE6ubHslVDmTaaPqfZGSiqOigNd5mwILOd69iSOaSxiQk8wQhE2xd2hCqmrGLrYV\nkqrn3FC8kX4/UduBCtqQG+6sk86yCVTPghpbc+2YnFmbZDsIOOM5zA4Kt4azOe3Q\nFM+P1NmbB0D4hR8Jwa+AtjoBvbgGDPxJumDhEdet/K+w+7lUCrTKjK2xsnnFhqod\nh3g9pt1IQg8kovKzbiKn5533IQqGY/M3bgRwLqadwvTRBnOekspjvYaDFcreWIIr\nMr3uTNuj88FAj6XAbrbc+7T+Vwtwvhl3eyIW7XnKl8IHAeaEC5uYJNReTfUdof2t\nMycChiKu3jJOKaFcM8lCMk4NQePA1EFsjrW7ySJKJhxBig99n7nei/YLtkHOZJDf\ndwx9XEOl7UzyyGG/KgaR6VqsgGDTz8hKpMGh/iqRmcnkW8Fu3XIk24n4IQXXo+Se\nBCuRfJNNXyT0O36c2AUs07bi3AkxOHigsUmuK/KMwsVcSdJ7QU138Uue671YsbKu\n9+V7zUAGmcC3oPM7cvN/\n=NAUA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T14:22:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGMxZGU5Njk3MjU1OTVlZTlkNmY3NmFjNDg2YjVmMGU3OTIzNzljMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/2e928761fd00092bc9a82fd3a202c04f91c2e40c","sha":"2e928761fd00092bc9a82fd3a202c04f91c2e40c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2e928761fd00092bc9a82fd3a202c04f91c2e40c"}],"sha":"c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/c1de969725595ee9d6f76ac486b5f0e792379c00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2e928761fd00092bc9a82fd3a202c04f91c2e40c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:37Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(popup): render dialog messages as text unless html is opted into (#299)\n\nCloses VCST-5665 (VM-1746).\n\n## Problem\n\n`showConfirmation` / `showError` / `showInfo` passed the message\nstraight through as a string slot, and `vc-popup-container.vue:14-18`\nrenders string slots with `v-html`. Modules build these messages by\ninterpolating server data into a translation, so an entity name was\ntreated as markup:\n\n- a product named `<h1>Clearance</h1>` restyles the delete confirmation;\n- a name carrying `<a href=\"…\">` adds a working link to a dialog the\nuser is meant to trust;\n- `<img src=…>` is allowed too.\n\n**This is not XSS.** DOMPurify with an allowlist sits in front of it,\nand `script` / `on*` handlers never survive. It is dialog spoofing on a\ndestructive action.\n\n## Change\n\nMessages now go through a render function, which the container sends\ndown its `<component :is>` branch, so Vue escapes them. Opt back in per\ncall:\n\n```ts\nshowError(t(\"TEAM.ERRORS.USER_EXIST\", { email }), { html: true });\n```\n\n**Explicit slots are untouched.** `usePopup({ slots: { default:\n\"<p>…</p>\" } })` still renders sanitized HTML — HTML in a popup slot is\na deliberate feature (`cf52cf741`), and the existing test for it still\npasses. Only the three message helpers changed.\n\nNo container change was needed: the string-vs-component discrimination\nalready existed.\n\n## Blast radius — measured, not estimated\n\nAcross `framework`, `apps`, `packages` and `cli`, **exactly one caller\npasses markup**: vendor-portal''s `showEmailExistsError` on\n`TEAM.PAGES.DETAILS.POPUP.ERROR.MESSAGE.USER_EXIST` — `\"An e-mail\naddress <b>{email}</b> already registered in the system.\"`\n\nEvery other call site passes a plain translated string. A scan of all\nlocale values in `framework/locales` and `apps/vendor-portal/**/locales`\nfound only two containing tags, and the other one\n(`PRODUCTS…CATEGORY.TOOLTIP`, with `<br>`) feeds a `:tooltip` prop, not\na popup.\n\nThat one call site is itself an instance of this bug — the email is\nuser-entered and lands inside `<b>`. It needs `{ html: true }` (or,\nbetter, the bold dropped). **It lives under `/apps/`, which\n`.gitignore:72` excludes, so it cannot be fixed in this PR.**\n\nAfter this change it renders its tags literally, which is visible\nimmediately rather than silent.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest run core/composables/usePopup shell/_internal/popup` — 69\npassed / 6 files\n- 4 new tests, written first and observed failing (`expected ''string''\nnot to be ''string''`): the three helpers keep the message off the\n`v-html` path, and `{ html: true }` still passes the raw string\n- One container test pins the mechanism: a render-function slot renders\n`Delete <h1>Big</h1>?` as text with no `<h1>` in the DOM\n- `yarn typecheck` exit 0; `yarn docs:lint` 0 errors; pre-commit\n`check:locales` and `check:layers` pass\n- `usePopup.docs.md` updated — this is a public API change\n\n### Full-suite note\n\n`npx vitest run` reports 2 failures — `useConnectionStatus` and\n`useNotificationStore`, both 5s timeouts on a dynamic `await import()`.\nThey are **not** from this change: they pass in isolation (1.4s), and\nthey fail identically with these changes stashed. Pre-existing\nload-dependent flakiness in the full parallel run.\n\n## Versioning\n\nBehaviour change to a default, no API removed — minor, not breaking.\nConsumers who deliberately pass HTML add `{ html: true }`.","tree":{"sha":"fd22e3c8abd21debb39f72ec242ef294f23f652a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/fd22e3c8abd21debb39f72ec242ef294f23f652a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/2e928761fd00092bc9a82fd3a202c04f91c2e40c","verifi