38ce6e23a0cc9c3e0b3d665df12ea0dca"}],"sha":"2e928761fd00092bc9a82fd3a202c04f91c2e40c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/2e928761fd00092bc9a82fd3a202c04f91c2e40c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/bd938a138ce6e23a0cc9c3e0b3d665df12ea0dca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:30Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(blade-navigation): target keyboard shortcuts at the focused blade (#298)\n\nCloses VCST-5680.\n\n## The ticket''s premise was wrong, and it changes the fix\n\nVCST-5680 says `Ctrl/Cmd+\\` always expands the topmost blade \"unlike\n`Ctrl/Cmd+S`, which correctly targets the active/topmost-with-focus\nblade (VCST-5530 SC-04)\".\n\nThere is no focus-based targeting anywhere in this layer.\n`createShortcutDispatcher` resolves **one** blade id from\n`useBladeStack.activeBlade` and uses it both for the built-ins and for\n`getToolbarItems(bladeId)` — so `Ctrl/Cmd+S` and `Ctrl/Cmd+\\` had\nidentical targeting. And `activeBlade` (`useBladeStack.ts:51-56`) walks\nthe stack backwards and returns the last **visible** blade, i.e. the\ntopmost:\n\n```ts\nconst activeBlade = computed(() => {\n  for (let i = _blades.value.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    if (_blades.value[i].visible) return _blades.value[i];\n  }\n  return undefined;\n});\n```\n\nThe only `document.activeElement` read in blade-navigation / shortcuts\nis `isTextInputFocused()` in `match.ts:92`, which only blocks bare-key\nshortcuts inside inputs.\n\nThe gap surfaced on expand and not on save because expanding a *middle*\nblade is a thing you want, while saving one is rare — during SC-04 the\nfocused blade was presumably also the topmost.\n\nSo this PR adds focus-based targeting where none existed, for all blade\nshortcuts.\n\n## Why not fix `activeBlade` itself\n\n`activeBlade` also decides the `parentId` of a newly opened blade\n(`useBladeStack.ts:147`) and backs `replaceCurrentBlade` /\n`coverCurrentBlade`. Making it focus-dependent would re-parent blades\nbased on where the caret happens to sit. The fix goes at the\ndispatcher''s `getActiveBlade` seam instead; `activeBlade` is untouched.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. `VcBladeSlot` stamps `data-blade-id` on the blade root — the same\nattribute fallthrough that already delivers `inert`.\n2. `resolveShortcutTargetBlade` walks up from `document.activeElement`\nto the nearest marker and returns that blade.\n3. It falls back to the topmost blade when focus is outside every blade,\nwhen the marker names a blade no longer in the stack (the DOM outlives\nthe descriptor during teardown), or when the match is not visible.\n\nA blade layout with two roots would drop the attribute and degrade to\ntoday''s behaviour rather than break.\n\n**The fallback is a hot path, not an edge case.** Per VCST-5670, focus\nsits on `<body>` after sign-in, Maximize and Save — until that lands,\nthe fallback fires often.\n\n## Behaviour changes QA must check\n\nBeyond the reported defect, this deliberately changes two things:\n\n- **`Ctrl/Cmd+S` now saves the focused blade**, not the topmost. Please\nre-run VCST-5530 SC-04.\n- **With focus in the workspace blade, `Ctrl/Cmd+\\` is now a no-op** —\nthe workspace has no `parentId`, so it is not expandable, and the\nshortcut no longer reaches past it to the topmost blade. This follows\nfrom \"act on the focused blade\"; flagging it because it is user-visible.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full framework suite: **4388 passed / 479 files**\n- `focus-target.test.ts` — 5 new tests, written first and observed\nfailing through the real code path (`Error: not implemented`), covering\nthe hit, both fallbacks, no-focus, and the not-visible case\n- `vc-blade-slot.test.ts` — new test pinning the marker, asserted\nthrough the same constant the resolver reads so the two cannot drift\n- `yarn typecheck` exit 0; eslint clean; `madge --circular` on the\nblade-navigation tree: none\n- pre-commit `check:locales` and `check:layers` pass\n\nNot verified automatically: real focus + real keydown in a running app.\nThat needs the live recipe (`yarn build:framework`, then `cd\napps/vendor-portal && yarn serve`) with a 3-blade chain, which is how\nthe ticket was found.","tree":{"sha":"fecad1b10d4d0650de4d4c3b8341e29d9d946d3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/fecad1b10d4d0650de4d4c3b8341e29d9d946d3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/bd938a138ce6e23a0cc9c3e0b3d665df12ea0dca","verification":{"payload":"tree fecad1b10d4d0650de4d4c3b8341e29d9d946d3b\nparent 9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786630950 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786630950 +0300\n\nfix(blade-navigation): target keyboard shortcuts at the focused blade (#298)\n\nCloses VCST-5680.\n\n## The ticket''s premise was wrong, and it changes the fix\n\nVCST-5680 says `Ctrl/Cmd+\\` always expands the topmost blade \"unlike\n`Ctrl/Cmd+S`, which correctly targets the active/topmost-with-focus\nblade (VCST-5530 SC-04)\".\n\nThere is no focus-based targeting anywhere in this layer.\n`createShortcutDispatcher` resolves **one** blade id from\n`useBladeStack.activeBlade` and uses it both for the built-ins and for\n`getToolbarItems(bladeId)` — so `Ctrl/Cmd+S` and `Ctrl/Cmd+\\` had\nidentical targeting. And `activeBlade` (`useBladeStack.ts:51-56`) walks\nthe stack backwards and returns the last **visible** blade, i.e. the\ntopmost:\n\n```ts\nconst activeBlade = computed(() => {\n  for (let i = _blades.value.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    if (_blades.value[i].visible) return _blades.value[i];\n  }\n  return undefined;\n});\n```\n\nThe only `document.activeElement` read in blade-navigation / shortcuts\nis `isTextInputFocused()` in `match.ts:92`, which only blocks bare-key\nshortcuts inside inputs.\n\nThe gap surfaced on expand and not on save because expanding a *middle*\nblade is a thing you want, while saving one is rare — during SC-04 the\nfocused blade was presumably also the topmost.\n\nSo this PR adds focus-based targeting where none existed, for all blade\nshortcuts.\n\n## Why not fix `activeBlade` itself\n\n`activeBlade` also decides the `parentId` of a newly opened blade\n(`useBladeStack.ts:147`) and backs `replaceCurrentBlade` /\n`coverCurrentBlade`. Making it focus-dependent would re-parent blades\nbased on where the caret happens to sit. The fix goes at the\ndispatcher''s `getActiveBlade` seam instead; `activeBlade` is untouched.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. `VcBladeSlot` stamps `data-blade-id` on the blade root — the same\nattribute fallthrough that already delivers `inert`.\n2. `resolveShortcutTargetBlade` walks up from `document.activeElement`\nto the nearest marker and returns that blade.\n3. It falls back to the topmost blade when focus is outside every blade,\nwhen the marker names a blade no longer in the stack (the DOM outlives\nthe descriptor during teardown), or when the match is not visible.\n\nA blade layout with two roots would drop the attribute and degrade to\ntoday''s behaviour rather than break.\n\n**The fallback is a hot path, not an edge case.** Per VCST-5670, focus\nsits on `<body>` after sign-in, Maximize and Save — until that lands,\nthe fallback fires often.\n\n## Behaviour changes QA must check\n\nBeyond the reported defect, this deliberately changes two things:\n\n- **`Ctrl/Cmd+S` now saves the focused blade**, not the topmost. Please\nre-run VCST-5530 SC-04.\n- **With focus in the workspace blade, `Ctrl/Cmd+\\` is now a no-op** —\nthe workspace has no `parentId`, so it is not expandable, and the\nshortcut no longer reaches past it to the topmost blade. This follows\nfrom \"act on the focused blade\"; flagging it because it is user-visible.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full framework suite: **4388 passed / 479 files**\n- `focus-target.test.ts` — 5 new tests, written first and observed\nfailing through the real code path (`Error: not implemented`), covering\nthe hit, both fallbacks, no-focus, and the not-visible case\n- `vc-blade-slot.test.ts` — new test pinning the marker, asserted\nthrough the same constant the resolver reads so the two cannot drift\n- `yarn typecheck` exit 0; eslint clean; `madge --circular` on the\nblade-navigation tree: none\n- pre-commit `check:locales` and `check:layers` pass\n\nNot verified automatically: real focus + real keydown in a running app.\nThat needs the live recipe (`yarn build:framework`, then `cd\napps/vendor-portal && yarn serve`) with a 3-blade chain, which is how\nthe ticket was found.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfdMmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAStEQAFH9rLOEzuda0v6mYCJqZhdg\nBPAB0Y/MnjP/8a4ZmGrtz9icsXsavFSrETMZo2NH1tJaxkkGN+XfgdkBwlpxCkcv\nZhjCIHbp7eT6B1CpOrGSHbwMbgSd+IRMSpln27+x7gGtfa63AdzLDy5H0RHDoy7b\nLTbfo9BmD1nzJC4FRCTVf2JLyUwtmnSrZqXrgOJLoKV64ZKxkbvNSkVUrXvicNEU\nYDBp5I2mGIn3GGQTpPXCGRO2ZIrPOmO6PlXLkhcHy+3B8pgG0MsA5nhaIL1ux2EO\nHDfr8YaGl79JvpbJ9sjvQsJj8DjYb4JDBe4j/2tXhxHKSRSy274Uu8Em3FfbQonQ\nrIJit+5Wpn3AKCT6bhqWnVCENGoYMtiotKAT9KNhAvOvQ1kqTIDylUi/BspQF+wT\nkI1A3eLdu2G76hKUFCvrJc0i2i9HseI8RW1sCjEEABlcN0a+ohXkljz+8okRpkLU\nm/VPgcPfd7bRiJnw7e5yehBZF5lZAfYxMMpc7wn8pbUDOd3aJ5iVnW0VbB67ZSy6\n5EAg6RkDAWeASDPeezn/coNsJRDEIUu02wNDQk3BdnG19zSM+a5kW1ZbQ1EjqB9J\npzG5m0maSrZqm3E77p7wrE1/ZGWAbs220mWXh1bSFnkg75eaAdn3JxoHsskGz/G0\nwWjNLNIQBGIdOqrd/6tK\n=LBcf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T14:22:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/bd938a138ce6e23a0cc9c3e0b3d665df12ea0dca","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGJkOTM4YTEzOGNlNmUyM2EwY2M5YzNlMGIzZDY2NWRmMTJlYTBkY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d","sha":"9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d"}],"sha":"bd938a138ce6e23a0cc9c3e0b3d665df12ea0dca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/bd938a138ce6e23a0cc9c3e0b3d665df12ea0dca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:22Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-app): localize the sidebar menu toggle''s aria-label (#297)\n\nCloses VCST-5668 (VM-1749).\n\n## Problem\n\n`SidebarHeader.vue:76` announced a hardcoded English string, bypassing\nvue-i18n:\n\n```vue\n:aria-label=\"isMenuOpen ? ''Close menu'' : ''Open menu''\"\n```\n\nA German user got an English announcement from a screen reader on a\nprimary navigation control. The notification bell two elements above it\nalready goes through `$t`.\n\nNot a WCAG failure on its own — the control has an accessible name, so\n4.1.2 passes — but it breaks 3.1.2 Language of Parts in spirit and was\ninconsistent with every neighbouring control.\n\n## Namespace choice\n\nThe ticket suggested reusing `COMPONENTS.ORGANISMS.VC_BLADE.CLOSE_MENU`.\nI added a dedicated `OPEN_MENU`/`CLOSE_MENU` pair under\n`COMPONENTS.ORGANISMS.VC_APP` instead:\n\n- **That key is already taken.**\n`vc-blade/_internal/toolbar/ToolbarMobile.vue:60` uses it for the blade\ntoolbar''s mobile menu. Sharing it would couple two unrelated controls —\nrewording one would silently change the other''s screen-reader\nannouncement.\n- **`OPEN_MENU` has to be created either way** (it exists in no\nnamespace), so reuse would split the pair: `CLOSE_MENU` from `VC_BLADE`,\n`OPEN_MENU` from `VC_APP`.\n- **`VC_APP` matches local convention** — `NOTIFICATIONS` is already\nused in this same file.\n\nGerman values are real translations (`Menü öffnen` / `Menü schließen`),\nnot English copies, so they add no backlog for VCST-5669.\n\n## Sweep\n\nThe ticket asked whether this was the last one. `grep -rn ''aria-label=\"''\nframework/ui framework/shell --include=''*.vue'' | grep -v '':aria-label=''`\nnow returns nothing — it was.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest run ui/components/organisms/vc-app/_internal/sidebar` — 40\npassed / 3 files\n- `yarn check:locales` — in sync\n- `yarn typecheck` — exit 0; eslint and prettier clean; pre-commit\n`check:layers` passes\n\nTwo tests written first, one per toggle state, observed failing with\n`expected ''Open menu'' to be ''COMPONENTS.ORGANISMS.VC_APP.OPEN_MENU''` —\nthe suite stubs `$t` to return the key, so a raw English string in that\nassertion is exactly the defect.","tree":{"sha":"e0ad95c7b05b9ccb66531325f5a7d434a041c5f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/e0ad95c7b05b9ccb66531325f5a7d434a041c5f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d","verification":{"payload":"tree e0ad95c7b05b9ccb66531325f5a7d434a041c5f3\nparent 229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786630942 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786630942 +0300\n\nfix(vc-app): localize the sidebar menu toggle''s aria-label (#297)\n\nCloses VCST-5668 (VM-1749).\n\n## Problem\n\n`SidebarHeader.vue:76` announced a hardcoded English string, bypassing\nvue-i18n:\n\n```vue\n:aria-label=\"isMenuOpen ? ''Close menu'' : ''Open menu''\"\n```\n\nA German user got an English announcement from a screen reader on a\nprimary navigation control. The notification bell two elements above it\nalready goes through `$t`.\n\nNot a WCAG failure on its own — the control has an accessible name, so\n4.1.2 passes — but it breaks 3.1.2 Language of Parts in spirit and was\ninconsistent with every neighbouring control.\n\n## Namespace choice\n\nThe ticket suggested reusing `COMPONENTS.ORGANISMS.VC_BLADE.CLOSE_MENU`.\nI added a dedicated `OPEN_MENU`/`CLOSE_MENU` pair under\n`COMPONENTS.ORGANISMS.VC_APP` instead:\n\n- **That key is already taken.**\n`vc-blade/_internal/toolbar/ToolbarMobile.vue:60` uses it for the blade\ntoolbar''s mobile menu. Sharing it would couple two unrelated controls —\nrewording one would silently change the other''s screen-reader\nannouncement.\n- **`OPEN_MENU` has to be created either way** (it exists in no\nnamespace), so reuse would split the pair: `CLOSE_MENU` from `VC_BLADE`,\n`OPEN_MENU` from `VC_APP`.\n- **`VC_APP` matches local convention** — `NOTIFICATIONS` is already\nused in this same file.\n\nGerman values are real translations (`Menü öffnen` / `Menü schließen`),\nnot English copies, so they add no backlog for VCST-5669.\n\n## Sweep\n\nThe ticket asked whether this was the last one. `grep -rn ''aria-label=\"''\nframework/ui framework/shell --include=''*.vue'' | grep -v '':aria-label=''`\nnow returns nothing — it was.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest run ui/components/organisms/vc-app/_internal/sidebar` — 40\npassed / 3 files\n- `yarn check:locales` — in sync\n- `yarn typecheck` — exit 0; eslint and prettier clean; pre-commit\n`check:layers` passes\n\nTwo tests written first, one per toggle state, observed failing with\n`expected ''Open menu'' to be ''COMPONENTS.ORGANISMS.VC_APP.OPEN_MENU''` —\nthe suite stubs `$t` to return the key, so a raw English string in that\nassertion is exactly the defect.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfdMeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGoMQAELxaNI1ULFtyGHo+53JAlBa\nmy6/N90vdk4qnn9cuIrqnSD3YA6Tzg/+CKkxm7+qncK/TZdVARD7lgTO/yl0Ve05\nD/YQtjgnmLNbBxgRBfvPM6y+rEYdf30yJWRNIs0kNFsNpgESL+aL7+Shpz9HZiNQ\n1/Alh0Sw+kcuCJRcd50uhlI4qBgdOr7k6HcMW4NAmxkw64R9SNd2N/KEERVnkYDP\nMLcjdkww1xszHGCHEzznGF95CKplCDaklMyO/z6HkF0j7URvXYVQ+9nauWwPb4uz\nmSVkC13Luzac2QdCNK2wHOz3h2QdNHlaz8k/jobgWM+BkjIP2Vh2n7PxqIhCBuga\n0xuo136q0Z3Std0mHS+QFGNW8AR7zdkYcD6aR8X1YwoB7mTK5Y6FXWQuJGAqzk9a\ncwxNFpRQEJIM4teV+/cALjlcVi1+3n/QZ1Yr58EWrxyG3j8rqC4KY3pGWH5oGFmH\npVg1JjWF988l6OtO/W26If27+qpAJZNWMMCISN3aTYKnj6GOu9aPrAV3VAEs61k7\n2Lc+xR4zrYYYwbDrJuM4ePfRmtFsQ0TGGp2vMkEywnMwUvmERStRhFUx1da40isw\n6edaV3Smiw0raU/+b1gZ3kwp8sRmJJHUIW0f9r8Wk+Y43LWwSc+bjtrIIeCQKD6b\nChMdAb0YZcRkRIs+mXnX\n=LMCr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T14:22:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDllMmFiYzJkZTA1NmJiNGE2MTEwYTA4NjdlM2QzYjY0N2EwMmU2NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3","sha":"229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3"}],"sha":"9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9e2abc2de056bb4a6110a0867e3d3b647a02e66d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:14Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:22:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): add autocomplete tokens to every password field outside login (#296)\n\nCloses VCST-5667 (VM-1748).\n\n## Problem\n\nPR #280 added `autocomplete` to the login page. The other password\nscreens never got it.\n\nWithout `autocomplete=\"new-password\"` on a new-password field, browsers\nand password managers may autofill the **current** password into it and\noffer to save the old one back — the user submits a value they never\ntyped. This is the mechanism behind WCAG 3.3.8 Accessible\nAuthentication, and 1.3.5 Identify Input Purpose (AA) applies to these\nfields.\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Tokens |\n| --- | --- |\n| `shell/auth/ChangePasswordPage/.../ChangePassword.vue` |\n`current-password`, `new-password` ×2 |\n| `shell/auth/InvitePage/.../Invite.vue` | `username` on the pre-filled\nemail, `new-password` ×2 |\n| `shell/auth/ResetPasswordPage/.../ResetPassword.vue` | `new-password`\n×2 |\n| `shell/components/change-password/change-password.vue` |\n`current-password`, `new-password` ×2 |\n\n### The fourth file is not in the ticket\n\nThe ticket''s file list came from a grep of `framework/shell/auth/`,\nwhich misses `framework/shell/components/change-password` — the form\nbehind the user-menu **Change password** button, wired in through\n`useShellBootstrap`. Same defect, and it is the path users actually\ntake: the auth page only serves a forced change at sign-in. Flagging it\nhere rather than filing a near-duplicate ticket.\n\n### Why a prop and not an attribute\n\n`vc-input` sets `inheritAttrs: false` and binds leftover attrs to its\nwrapping `div`, so a plain `autocomplete` attribute would never reach\nthe native `input`. It has to go through the declared prop (added in\n#280). `vc-input.test.ts` already pins that; the new page tests pin the\ntoken on each field.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest run shell/auth shell/components/change-password` — 83 passed /\n10 files, clean output\n- `yarn typecheck` — exit 0\n- eslint + prettier clean; pre-commit `check:locales` and `check:layers`\npass\n- Completeness check: `grep -rl ''type=\"password\"''` over `framework`\nreturns exactly 5 files; all now carry tokens (the fifth is `Login.vue`\nfrom #280)\n\nTests were written first and observed failing (`undefined` in place of\nevery token) before the markup was touched.\n\n## Needs manual QA\n\nThe acceptance criterion \"a password manager offers to generate/save a\nnew password, and does not prefill the new-password field with the\ncurrent one\" cannot be automated — it needs a real browser with a real\npassword manager. Recipe: `yarn build:framework`, then `cd\napps/vendor-portal && yarn serve`.\n\n## Docs\n\nNo docs change, matching #280 — the page docs did not record the tokens\nthere either, the public API is unchanged, and the prop is documented in\n`vc-input.docs.md`.","tree":{"sha":"80bd67220a5a49acfaf4b2ea169f268fac2f7fcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/80bd67220a5a49acfaf4b2ea169f268fac2f7fcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 80bd67220a5a49acfaf4b2ea169f268fac2f7fcb\nparent 57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786630934 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786630934 +0300\n\nfix(auth): add autocomplete tokens to every password field outside login (#296)\n\nCloses VCST-5667 (VM-1748).\n\n## Problem\n\nPR #280 added `autocomplete` to the login page. The other password\nscreens never got it.\n\nWithout `autocomplete=\"new-password\"` on a new-password field, browsers\nand password managers may autofill the **current** password into it and\noffer to save the old one back — the user submits a value they never\ntyped. This is the mechanism behind WCAG 3.3.8 Accessible\nAuthentication, and 1.3.5 Identify Input Purpose (AA) applies to these\nfields.\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Tokens |\n| --- | --- |\n| `shell/auth/ChangePasswordPage/.../ChangePassword.vue` |\n`current-password`, `new-password` ×2 |\n| `shell/auth/InvitePage/.../Invite.vue` | `username` on the pre-filled\nemail, `new-password` ×2 |\n| `shell/auth/ResetPasswordPage/.../ResetPassword.vue` | `new-password`\n×2 |\n| `shell/components/change-password/change-password.vue` |\n`current-password`, `new-password` ×2 |\n\n### The fourth file is not in the ticket\n\nThe ticket''s file list came from a grep of `framework/shell/auth/`,\nwhich misses `framework/shell/components/change-password` — the form\nbehind the user-menu **Change password** button, wired in through\n`useShellBootstrap`. Same defect, and it is the path users actually\ntake: the auth page only serves a forced change at sign-in. Flagging it\nhere rather than filing a near-duplicate ticket.\n\n### Why a prop and not an attribute\n\n`vc-input` sets `inheritAttrs: false` and binds leftover attrs to its\nwrapping `div`, so a plain `autocomplete` attribute would never reach\nthe native `input`. It has to go through the declared prop (added in\n#280). `vc-input.test.ts` already pins that; the new page tests pin the\ntoken on each field.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest run shell/auth shell/components/change-password` — 83 passed /\n10 files, clean output\n- `yarn typecheck` — exit 0\n- eslint + prettier clean; pre-commit `check:locales` and `check:layers`\npass\n- Completeness check: `grep -rl ''type=\"password\"''` over `framework`\nreturns exactly 5 files; all now carry tokens (the fifth is `Login.vue`\nfrom #280)\n\nTests were written first and observed failing (`undefined` in place of\nevery token) before the markup was touched.\n\n## Needs manual QA\n\nThe acceptance criterion \"a password manager offers to generate/save a\nnew password, and does not prefill the new-password field with the\ncurrent one\" cannot be automated — it needs a real browser with a real\npassword manager. Recipe: `yarn build:framework`, then `cd\napps/vendor-portal && yarn serve`.\n\n## Docs\n\nNo docs change, matching #280 — the page docs did not record the tokens\nthere either, the public API is unchanged, and the prop is documented in\n`vc-input.docs.md`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfdMWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWqkQAErNzinxf5ck0W3ZD20iOHxW\nq2cSDvRIG9ofyvxlzo6rvUkYG9guJPMoBn2MemQ6fCaMC6KivkopfTe7kwZc7GoF\nIbky/juMv1Nke/bn3pugIl/zSvwt+6hY7nScOQifjs7H/E6bPHqgnX8zg0o99fwD\nluu3dwHQQeRtI39D2/gMdFKdWs73jGIIJ7SNrzjCZtj4JzKI+xrDad1Xpymhkjvt\nzZlBeuC2gpMuo3orEZw8Xs6ARF7UvbEKDOz4ISV0WELYm1kZhWo3GXSOIkh1DIFs\nvzWy6NqM6vzdiv7KLR+LRW52f7+Hk3tuQskxsp2sy3fazvXhkxeRAS/+70g1Igzr\nnbxrNPW7+wQzBy32Ng7xUqLW3jcshmSj+SiGVBdHGC8qrdkWP8n086EVi/OA/6Uz\nhO3WOtpgvdmLQfpaPMP0QgbCfIb/dZry/zJtIM6/+SExVnr5XpAu8b+d3IWVnSWt\nalFcHuKT1SukTG6J/eiD3anPNFTTFmXJnl/EEkrKSfqoXqXryT1SLT5SxNzd3+Ii\nz2lQ4eMb+BZJ4A1hzvmc7obK0sbLhJbbKABrRPWGkSb1ic/elekxR0E8Q8Aaue0S\n+wHAkyJz+5+nwStCJDv9aCgK1h9mri2Ekv8Rz742XF3ZmPb45hndrnw6TYLvbmNd\nE5YHw1oz7MUVRvunPD6u\n=4wGV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T14:22:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDIyOWY0NjgzMjZlOTY1MGFiMjRmZGQ5MGE4Njk4YTdmZTM4YWQ0ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e","sha":"57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e"}],"sha":"229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/229f468326e9650ab24fdd90a8698a7fe38ad4e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T12:24:21Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T12:24:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(pagination): make restoredPage optional and deprecate writing currentPage (#295)\n\nFollow-up to **VM-1745** / **VCST-5664**. Two changes to the same\ninterface — one is a regression fix for what #294 shipped, the other is\nthe deprecation that ticket asked for.\n\n## 1. Regression: `restoredPage` was required, and that broke a consumer\n\n#294 added `restoredPage` as a **required** property. That breaks anyone\nwho builds `UseDataTablePaginationReturn` by hand — and that pattern\nexists: vendor-portal''s `useProductsManager` composes a facade that\nre-exposes whichever pagination is active (catalog view vs product view)\nas this interface.\n\n```\nsrc/modules/products/composables/useProductsManager/index.ts(69,9):\nerror TS2741: Property ''restoredPage'' is missing in type ''{ currentPage: number; ... }''\nbut required in type ''UseDataTablePaginationReturn''.\n```\n\n**Why the root `yarn typecheck` missed it:** vendor-portal types against\n`framework/dist`, not the framework source, and the dist was still built\nfrom before the change. The break only appears after a framework rebuild\n— so a green CI on #294 proved nothing about consumers.\n\nNow optional. Verified the whole way round: rebuilt the framework\n(`restoredPage?: number` in\n`dist/ui/composables/useDataTablePagination.d.ts`), then ran\nvendor-portal''s own `type-check` — passes.\n\n## 2. Deprecate assigning to `currentPage`\n\nThree ways to change the page, with different effects:\n\n| | `onPageChange` | URL slice |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `goToPage(n)` | fires | written |\n| `setPage(n)` | no | written |\n| `pagination.currentPage = n` | **no** | written |\n\nThe URL is written in all three, because that watch fires on any change\nto the ref. So assignment is a **silent duplicate of `setPage`** — it\nleaves the paginator on page N with page 1''s rows, the same symptom as\nthe bug #294 fixed, but with no URL restore involved.\n\nImplemented as a writable `computed` that warns and delegates to\n`setPage`. Reading is untouched (`reactive()` unwraps a writable\ncomputed the same as a ref). Internal callers use the raw ref, so the\nrestore path and `goToPage`/`setPage`/`reset` never trip the warning —\nthere is a test for that. The interface property carries `@deprecated`,\nso editors strike it through.\n\n### Why not readonly\n\nA production Vue build drops a write to a readonly reactive property\n**silently**. Making it readonly would leave existing consumers —\nvendor-portal''s facade among them — unable to change the page, with no\nerror thrown and no test failing. Turning this into a hard error belongs\nin a major version, with the consumer sweep that implies.\n\n## Tests\n\nFive added (22 → 25): assignment warns, moves the page, updates `skip`,\nand does not fire `onPageChange`; `goToPage`/`setPage`/`reset` do not\nwarn; the internal restore seed does not warn.\n\n## Gates\n\nFramework unit suite **3763 tests / 401 files** · `yarn typecheck` ·\nvendor-portal `type-check` (against a rebuilt dist) · `check:locales` ·\n`check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\nRelates to VM-1745, VCST-5664","tree":{"sha":"bfab1321455529b759e4b34d4d7e6a86d53b0287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/bfab1321455529b759e4b34d4d7e6a86d53b0287"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e","verification":{"payload":"tree bfab1321455529b759e4b34d4d7e6a86d53b0287\nparent 46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786623861 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786623861 +0300\n\nfix(pagination): make restoredPage optional and deprecate writing currentPage (#295)\n\nFollow-up to **VM-1745** / **VCST-5664**. Two changes to the same\ninterface — one is a regression fix for what #294 shipped, the other is\nthe deprecation that ticket asked for.\n\n## 1. Regression: `restoredPage` was required, and that broke a consumer\n\n#294 added `restoredPage` as a **required** property. That breaks anyone\nwho builds `UseDataTablePaginationReturn` by hand — and that pattern\nexists: vendor-portal''s `useProductsManager` composes a facade that\nre-exposes whichever pagination is active (catalog view vs product view)\nas this interface.\n\n```\nsrc/modules/products/composables/useProductsManager/index.ts(69,9):\nerror TS2741: Property ''restoredPage'' is missing in type ''{ currentPage: number; ... }''\nbut required in type ''UseDataTablePaginationReturn''.\n```\n\n**Why the root `yarn typecheck` missed it:** vendor-portal types against\n`framework/dist`, not the framework source, and the dist was still built\nfrom before the change. The break only appears after a framework rebuild\n— so a green CI on #294 proved nothing about consumers.\n\nNow optional. Verified the whole way round: rebuilt the framework\n(`restoredPage?: number` in\n`dist/ui/composables/useDataTablePagination.d.ts`), then ran\nvendor-portal''s own `type-check` — passes.\n\n## 2. Deprecate assigning to `currentPage`\n\nThree ways to change the page, with different effects:\n\n| | `onPageChange` | URL slice |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `goToPage(n)` | fires | written |\n| `setPage(n)` | no | written |\n| `pagination.currentPage = n` | **no** | written |\n\nThe URL is written in all three, because that watch fires on any change\nto the ref. So assignment is a **silent duplicate of `setPage`** — it\nleaves the paginator on page N with page 1''s rows, the same symptom as\nthe bug #294 fixed, but with no URL restore involved.\n\nImplemented as a writable `computed` that warns and delegates to\n`setPage`. Reading is untouched (`reactive()` unwraps a writable\ncomputed the same as a ref). Internal callers use the raw ref, so the\nrestore path and `goToPage`/`setPage`/`reset` never trip the warning —\nthere is a test for that. The interface property carries `@deprecated`,\nso editors strike it through.\n\n### Why not readonly\n\nA production Vue build drops a write to a readonly reactive property\n**silently**. Making it readonly would leave existing consumers —\nvendor-portal''s facade among them — unable to change the page, with no\nerror thrown and no test failing. Turning this into a hard error belongs\nin a major version, with the consumer sweep that implies.\n\n## Tests\n\nFive added (22 → 25): assignment warns, moves the page, updates `skip`,\nand does not fire `onPageChange`; `goToPage`/`setPage`/`reset` do not\nwarn; the internal restore seed does not warn.\n\n## Gates\n\nFramework unit suite **3763 tests / 401 files** · `yarn typecheck` ·\nvendor-portal `type-check` (against a rebuilt dist) · `check:locales` ·\n`check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\nRelates to VM-1745, VCST-5664","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfbd1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2WEQAA01GcplfD5K89FxD919IPw0\nRGTe71aA8xTfpK1HiN8JIjqTQrIg8AJDDfk+RHqXYOI1OMva710pQJbNn8vkm/Hu\nlQu2cnax53MccrnOoiVbGD2EemC88YbZUhO2SuN56P/Cmv6vghG5Lk4qHz5xcowM\n1C94auGuvX81+gCkT0ZPV7afOkRsHMHXSdbkqYi9juw0DXy/hQHB7RFo43HGIjAO\nr+jsbaT6ocaC76CCvJ2XON6Sp+ApKmDW+/YuhHx+dHxoC/Y9lp2gbo3sXEmuy9fr\nsaZdT3wNCuf+6y9vbwQh0CrCs46b+IdLCive4aoHLeNjdZ/gJ9RVs43rIyYsequP\nemq24ICV6TvL3wKyE4+3E/9WHKsasb2jEidKX1cM+6IBTBUZ5Wq3kP+zJ0SDmfcL\nxsUdyVRV2FPG7lForiaqzzUnHS0EvyvH0pyeQYm//9RmnxpaRA5twZxRu6WYtcKR\nG5VLMQqqT1zcdqIzqtFSR+uqH61SfdqiChzi+Q4WJ91TYJ7d0C1hbZF3kRIj2X/e\nlEeIV0Fv5JrG2fW2RmU0Nqe3km65b8qCHX6Kf5d2sk62xNj57Fg29PdEJV2/BZg6\nMvyKXLgZdpRLVOE5Dy8znhtpVJ9OzJCESpuCLgLJI4qsVXmdY8rAoQmW8JoSCv0u\nlVl46FJjQL1Sx/4J2VGa\n=djFA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T12:24:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDU3MTA0YzMzZjhjZDU0NGM3NTU5MjQ3NjA2NjBmNWI4OTM2ZmUzMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982","sha":"46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982"}],"sha":"57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/57104c33f8cd544c755924760660f5b8936fe30e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T09:23:58Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T09:23:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ai-agent): let the chatbot ask the shell to close the panel (#292)\n\nAddresses **VCST-5673**. Read the scope note before merging: the shell\ncan only supply half of this fix, and that is a property of the browser,\nnot a shortcut taken here.\n\n## Why the host cannot fix this alone\n\nA keystroke is delivered to the document that owns the focused element.\nThe AI panel is a **cross-origin iframe** — that is why `allowedOrigins`\nexists — so once the chatbot takes focus, its key events are not\nobservable from the shell by any means. The panel''s `Escape` and\n`Ctrl/Cmd+I` handlers listen on the host `document`\n(`VcAiAgentPanel.vue`), so they simply never fire.\n\nWorth stating explicitly, because the ticket suggests the iframe\n\"captures focus\" as an a11y measure: **nothing in the shell moves focus\ninto the iframe** — there is not a single `focus()` call in the whole\nplugin. The chatbot autofocuses its own input on load, which is\nreasonable for a chat UI and is what puts focus out of the host''s reach.\n\n## Change\n\n`CLOSE_PANEL` added to the chat-to-shell protocol, wired exactly like\n`NAVIGATE_TO_APP`: a callback passed into the transport, dispatched only\nafter the existing origin validation.\n\n```js\n// in the embedded chatbot\nwindow.parent.postMessage({ type: \"CLOSE_PANEL\" }, \"https://your-shell-origin.example.com\");\n```\n\nClosing a panel exposes no data, and the sender''s origin is already\nchecked before the message is acted on, so this adds no risk beyond the\nmessages the bridge accepts today.\n\n## The other half\n\n`ai-agent.docs.md` now carries the relay snippet the embedded app needs\n— it must forward its own `Escape` / `Ctrl+I`. **Until VirtoOz ships\nthat, the reported STR still fails.** The ticket should stay open on\ntheir side, or be split.\n\n## The fallback that exists today\n\nThere is already a keyboard route out, which the ticket did not mention:\n`Shift+Tab` from the chat''s first focusable element leaves the iframe\nand lands on the panel header''s Close button, which is properly\nfocusable (`tabindex=\"0\"`, `role=\"button\"`, `aria-label`, Enter/Space\nhandlers). So this is a usability gap rather than a hard WCAG 2.1.1\nfailure — consistent with the ticket''s Medium severity. Documented,\nbecause \"there is a way out\" is worth knowing while the relay is not\nshipped.\n\n## Gates\n\nai-agent plugin tests **53** (3 added: allowed origin closes, disallowed\norigin ignored, generic handlers still notified) · `yarn typecheck` ·\n`check:locales` · `check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\nNot verified live: the reproduction needs the deployed AI panel on\nvcmp-dev, and the half that makes it observable is not shipped yet. What\nis verified is the protocol path, by test.\n\nRelates to VCST-5673","tree":{"sha":"d17689f412ac682f7680703c24f6a7a24933da04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/d17689f412ac682f7680703c24f6a7a24933da04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982","verification":{"payload":"tree d17689f412ac682f7680703c24f6a7a24933da04\nparent 9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786613038 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786613038 +0300\n\nfeat(ai-agent): let the chatbot ask the shell to close the panel (#292)\n\nAddresses **VCST-5673**. Read the scope note before merging: the shell\ncan only supply half of this fix, and that is a property of the browser,\nnot a shortcut taken here.\n\n## Why the host cannot fix this alone\n\nA keystroke is delivered to the document that owns the focused element.\nThe AI panel is a **cross-origin iframe** — that is why `allowedOrigins`\nexists — so once the chatbot takes focus, its key events are not\nobservable from the shell by any means. The panel''s `Escape` and\n`Ctrl/Cmd+I` handlers listen on the host `document`\n(`VcAiAgentPanel.vue`), so they simply never fire.\n\nWorth stating explicitly, because the ticket suggests the iframe\n\"captures focus\" as an a11y measure: **nothing in the shell moves focus\ninto the iframe** — there is not a single `focus()` call in the whole\nplugin. The chatbot autofocuses its own input on load, which is\nreasonable for a chat UI and is what puts focus out of the host''s reach.\n\n## Change\n\n`CLOSE_PANEL` added to the chat-to-shell protocol, wired exactly like\n`NAVIGATE_TO_APP`: a callback passed into the transport, dispatched only\nafter the existing origin validation.\n\n```js\n// in the embedded chatbot\nwindow.parent.postMessage({ type: \"CLOSE_PANEL\" }, \"https://your-shell-origin.example.com\");\n```\n\nClosing a panel exposes no data, and the sender''s origin is already\nchecked before the message is acted on, so this adds no risk beyond the\nmessages the bridge accepts today.\n\n## The other half\n\n`ai-agent.docs.md` now carries the relay snippet the embedded app needs\n— it must forward its own `Escape` / `Ctrl+I`. **Until VirtoOz ships\nthat, the reported STR still fails.** The ticket should stay open on\ntheir side, or be split.\n\n## The fallback that exists today\n\nThere is already a keyboard route out, which the ticket did not mention:\n`Shift+Tab` from the chat''s first focusable element leaves the iframe\nand lands on the panel header''s Close button, which is properly\nfocusable (`tabindex=\"0\"`, `role=\"button\"`, `aria-label`, Enter/Space\nhandlers). So this is a usability gap rather than a hard WCAG 2.1.1\nfailure — consistent with the ticket''s Medium severity. Documented,\nbecause \"there is a way out\" is worth knowing while the relay is not\nshipped.\n\n## Gates\n\nai-agent plugin tests **53** (3 added: allowed origin closes, disallowed\norigin ignored, generic handlers still notified) · `yarn typecheck` ·\n`check:locales` · `check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\nNot verified live: the reproduction needs the deployed AI panel on\nvcmp-dev, and the half that makes it observable is not shipped yet. What\nis verified is the protocol path, by test.\n\nRelates to VCST-5673","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfY0uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAijoQAGMmmjet8tXV2ydOX+09ylQQ\nmk5PkR40Tf0fvM+UW76AhKzKw1yRP9juOTQ3lxP0LSxSDlnStr8zLCwk9xLpEYTl\nekqoSecK1c36sTC4emebz1W2m2Nslh8uAWV/9fFrhLtZFkYEZrGoE1H/lkT1XaxJ\nExNN/kZcLWlJi0b6Ja/cy6fCfHc0DYfSJjEB79cuTk1WsYPHjAh4hI070tiwbuK8\naTOXhgrX3A2NKiR2cZAz1p2jJhGdZzb0YSsbvPsD+bkkh9kFxZgU3okzlvrJGv8S\nR2EsVK/bg+ebh5uZz6FQlOqtHakIljTsxsOOFPUykNWjUGCfmRFio5aILZ1BWWit\ngRogXIQPjPLQsF1wnz//0EysZt1EM0nOmDFeC15NNuobIDCd8JRFPK87tlrXKGQU\np/+Os6INPrL+3LgIJXJnSM5d18fVMESZY/Km70PD8916GG+CJyPabup8KofR24Ia\nye2+HmEUjLAQSSTovPn9cyJX+L/mOGU78jl2iA6dmd+RL2q6+g3bFzoDeFAweOj3\nk4kdhRszlY9jnf39DqKsxdWVLxXEA4uRZbMfCztKq4pCDOnujSqm/QxZTPnA5hVX\n6F2qGpeQ8rN8ZCFUBIIEGeiXrBCJ11gDpUMSPtKHpdAXjPM6uuiOFZdGuJWEen9y\nG7Ae6z5QbXaS1je7xWol\n=AJJ2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T09:24:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDQ2MDk4ZTUwMGMzYzkyMzAwOTIwMDkxMzUzNGVlYjljNzk1NmQ5ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802","sha":"9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802"}],"sha":"46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/46098e500c3c923009200913534eeb9c7956d982"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T08:10:11Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T08:10:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(pagination): tell the consumer when the page came from the URL (#294)\n\nFixes **VM-1745** / **VCST-5664**, found while reviewing\nvc-module-pagebuilder PR #159.\n\n## Problem\n\nWith `stateKey` set, the composable seeds the page from the blade URL\nusing `setPage`, which deliberately does **not** fire `onPageChange` —\nfiring it would cause a duplicate load. That part is correct. The gap is\nthat nothing told the consumer a restore had happened.\n\nSo a blade issuing an unconditional first load at `skip: 0` ends up with\nthe paginator on page N and page 1''s rows. There is no error, no\nwarning, and clicking page N is a no-op because it is already the active\npage — the state is not easy to get out of.\n\nReproduce in vc-module-pagebuilder (shared components blade): go to page\n2, reload the browser.\n\n## Worth being precise about\n\n**`skip` was already correct after a restore.** `setPage` runs before\nthe composable returns, so `pagination.skip` reflects page N at setup.\nThe defect is purely that the caller had no reason to use it instead of\na hardcoded `skip: 0`.\n\nThat is why this ships as a signal plus documentation rather than a\nbehaviour change.\n\n## Change\n\n| | |\n| --- | --- |\n| `restoredPage` | the page seeded at setup, or `undefined` |\n| warning | logged when `stateKey` is set but no `TableQueryState`\nprovider is in scope |\n| docs | the first-load contract, stated as a rule |\n\nThe docs now say plainly: **with `stateKey`, the first load must start\nat `pagination.skip`**, and passing it unconditionally is correct\nwhether or not a restore happened. `restoredPage` is for code that needs\nto branch.\n\n### Options not taken\n\n**Firing `onPageChange` on restore** (the ticket''s second suggestion)\nwould change behaviour for every existing consumer to fix a problem only\nsome of them have — those that hardcode `skip: 0`. Consumers that\nalready read `skip` would start loading twice.\n\n**Making `currentPage` readonly.** The ticket rightly notes there are\nthree ways to change the page with different side effects (`goToPage`\nfires, `setPage` does not, direct assignment does not). Tightening that\nbreaks any consumer assigning to it, so it is a separate decision, not a\ndrive-by in a bugfix.\n\n## The silent-provider case\n\n`stateKey` only works inside a blade. Outside one — and in unit tests —\n`inject(TableQueryStateKey, undefined)` yielded `undefined` and the\nentire feature vanished: no sync, no restore, no message.\nIndistinguishable from \"the URL had no page\". It now warns, naming the\nkey.\n\nTesting that needed a local `vi.mock(\"@core/utilities\", …)`, because the\nglobal test setup stubs `createLogger` with fresh spies per call — as\nthat setup file itself instructs for cases like this.\n\n## Tests\n\nFour added to `useDataTablePagination.test.ts` (18 → 22): restored page\nis reported and `skip` matches it; `restoredPage` stays `undefined` when\nthe URL carried no page; a missing provider warns and names the key; a\npresent provider does not warn.\n\n## Gates\n\nFramework unit suite **3753 tests / 401 files** · `yarn typecheck` ·\n`check:locales` · `check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\nRelates to VM-1745, VCST-5664","tree":{"sha":"c985f44a194093921a41c0933dc9f3b9f611f3fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/c985f44a194093921a41c0933dc9f3b9f611f3fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802","verification":{"payload":"tree c985f44a194093921a41c0933dc9f3b9f611f3fe\nparent caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786608611 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786608611 +0300\n\nfix(pagination): tell the consumer when the page came from the URL (#294)\n\nFixes **VM-1745** / **VCST-5664**, found while reviewing\nvc-module-pagebuilder PR #159.\n\n## Problem\n\nWith `stateKey` set, the composable seeds the page from the blade URL\nusing `setPage`, which deliberately does **not** fire `onPageChange` —\nfiring it would cause a duplicate load. That part is correct. The gap is\nthat nothing told the consumer a restore had happened.\n\nSo a blade issuing an unconditional first load at `skip: 0` ends up with\nthe paginator on page N and page 1''s rows. There is no error, no\nwarning, and clicking page N is a no-op because it is already the active\npage — the state is not easy to get out of.\n\nReproduce in vc-module-pagebuilder (shared components blade): go to page\n2, reload the browser.\n\n## Worth being precise about\n\n**`skip` was already correct after a restore.** `setPage` runs before\nthe composable returns, so `pagination.skip` reflects page N at setup.\nThe defect is purely that the caller had no reason to use it instead of\na hardcoded `skip: 0`.\n\nThat is why this ships as a signal plus documentation rather than a\nbehaviour change.\n\n## Change\n\n| | |\n| --- | --- |\n| `restoredPage` | the page seeded at setup, or `undefined` |\n| warning | logged when `stateKey` is set but no `TableQueryState`\nprovider is in scope |\n| docs | the first-load contract, stated as a rule |\n\nThe docs now say plainly: **with `stateKey`, the first load must start\nat `pagination.skip`**, and passing it unconditionally is correct\nwhether or not a restore happened. `restoredPage` is for code that needs\nto branch.\n\n### Options not taken\n\n**Firing `onPageChange` on restore** (the ticket''s second suggestion)\nwould change behaviour for every existing consumer to fix a problem only\nsome of them have — those that hardcode `skip: 0`. Consumers that\nalready read `skip` would start loading twice.\n\n**Making `currentPage` readonly.** The ticket rightly notes there are\nthree ways to change the page with different side effects (`goToPage`\nfires, `setPage` does not, direct assignment does not). Tightening that\nbreaks any consumer assigning to it, so it is a separate decision, not a\ndrive-by in a bugfix.\n\n## The silent-provider case\n\n`stateKey` only works inside a blade. Outside one — and in unit tests —\n`inject(TableQueryStateKey, undefined)` yielded `undefined` and the\nentire feature vanished: no sync, no restore, no message.\nIndistinguishable from \"the URL had no page\". It now warns, naming the\nkey.\n\nTesting that needed a local `vi.mock(\"@core/utilities\", …)`, because the\nglobal test setup stubs `createLogger` with fresh spies per call — as\nthat setup file itself instructs for cases like this.\n\n## Tests\n\nFour added to `useDataTablePagination.test.ts` (18 → 22): restored page\nis reported and `skip` matches it; `restoredPage` stays `undefined` when\nthe URL carried no page; a missing provider warns and names the key; a\npresent provider does not warn.\n\n## Gates\n\nFramework unit suite **3753 tests / 401 files** · `yarn typecheck` ·\n`check:locales` · `check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\nRelates to VM-1745, VCST-5664","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfXvjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMCUQAJK9YoO3gr6GVjL063dvcGil\nAw4IoEBPdxD5Mfmd0LkNpgv4UB2JrXMdthER0gzKI+V5eF2ORJHlI/l+aLxbyaCC\nf2R35YFtM6nKbdKnb7tOGQwW0CfZoeszUNPRLFnrvl91wiasf4+MtYIcASwhis9A\n4fVsoE/mwNUe9xDcEA+zoBnrJacAjHUJEFN0D2Jp2NwWklH9XK43zsNDV7z49CkD\nmT4sgiEjb6dTl+G4HlWzkpuk94915no5C5cfcstcFEXms2dLLJTgDHyE7h3vRKcK\nQKLpFUendWS+m2+C5dFpIJIonXlXFv+FWsOJYGHbxIdBaEg+w2aggMNCL580iH5w\n/8HPF8FvR1q4T6533eEvGcw7kbNJkp/HV8xIaQj8tnFffOMSfacDvUc+JPFSwgvl\njUVDP2Q30ez/chaVYZ82cKNoFnG3QuYxRa3NlW+5RHTbannXkQ5WaqYJcQWl1QGy\n09/ZLL92X7ikvkISNMh+5eewaOUnNOsfWGl/59L9D15xOYWgdmZmFtxUNYyr76W+\nS7dfyXrts3XTuvo5mg6rPeAFIHTh3AiMhZg2nlIE60DKNuHBn0FAAowBSEHBQPZk\njzMccclGRu8qwPmGS9IKTQ2DFdsbI0MG+3Pu5G8CzrxPNyY+R9KKqrcfzeyzePtH\n6SMoTxZSmKOiyO/0NiWt\n=Ru8x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T08:10:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDljZjU1NDhiODI0YTFkNTVhODQ5MzUxYzIxYmI2YzJhNDA2NmE4MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3","sha":"caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3"}],"sha":"9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9cf5548b824a1d55a849351c21bb6c2a4066a802"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T08:09:46Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T08:09:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(error): keep a non-JSON response body out of the short error message (#293)\n\nFixes **VM-1744** / **VCST-5663**, found while reviewing\nvc-module-pagebuilder PR #159.\n\n## Problem\n\nNSwag-generated API clients throw `ApiException`, whose `response` is\nthe **raw body as a string**, not an object:\n\n```ts\nexport class ApiException extends Error {\n  status: number;\n  response: string;   // raw body\n}\n```\n\n`parseError`''s Axios branch assumed an object and recursed into it,\nlanding in the string branch. When the body was not JSON, `JSON.parse`\nthrew and the whole body became `DisplayableError.message`.\n\nModules render `parseError(e).message` directly, and so does `useAsync`.\nSo a 500 answered with an ASP.NET developer exception page, or an HTML\nerror page from a proxy or load balancer, put the entire document into\nthe toast and the blade banner.\n\n## Change\n\nThe exception is matched **before** the Axios branch — structurally, not\nby class, since `ApiException` is generated per client. The short\nmessage becomes `\"<status>: <exception message>\"` and the body goes into\n`details`, which is what `DisplayableError` separates the two for.\n\n## Two things left deliberately unchanged\n\n**A JSON body is still delegated as before,** so the platform''s own\n`message` / `exceptionMessage` keeps winning. Parsing that out is useful\nexisting behaviour, and this defect is only about bodies that are not\nJSON.\n\n**No status prefix was added to that JSON path.** It would have been\neasy to make every message read `\"400: Name is required\"`, but that\nchanges the wording of every API error in every app for no benefit to\nthis ticket.\n\n## Side effect worth knowing\n\n`useAsync` derives its notification dedup id from `message.slice(0, 80)`\n(`useAsync/index.ts:65`). Two different markup bodies share their first\n80 characters — `<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>…` — so distinct\nerrors collapsed into a single toast. Short status lines do not collide.\nThere is a test for it.\n\n## Tests\n\nFour added:\n\n| Case | Asserted |\n| --- | --- |\n| HTML body | short message is `500: …`, no `<html>` in it, body in\n`details` |\n| two markup bodies, different statuses | first 80 chars of the messages\ndiffer (the dedup case) |\n| JSON body | still yields the platform''s message, unprefixed |\n| empty body | falls back to the exception''s own message |\n\nThe existing Axios test still passes unchanged — its `response` is an\nobject, so the new guard does not match it.\n\n## Gates\n\nFramework unit suite **3753 tests / 401 files** · `yarn typecheck` ·\n`check:locales` · `check:layers`.\n\nRelates to VM-1744, VCST-5663","tree":{"sha":"643f525a46096a6add14cb1127d8314d628ecb41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/643f525a46096a6add14cb1127d8314d628ecb41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3","verification":{"payload":"tree 643f525a46096a6add14cb1127d8314d628ecb41\nparent 9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786608586 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786608586 +0300\n\nfix(error): keep a non-JSON response body out of the short error message (#293)\n\nFixes **VM-1744** / **VCST-5663**, found while reviewing\nvc-module-pagebuilder PR #159.\n\n## Problem\n\nNSwag-generated API clients throw `ApiException`, whose `response` is\nthe **raw body as a string**, not an object:\n\n```ts\nexport class ApiException extends Error {\n  status: number;\n  response: string;   // raw body\n}\n```\n\n`parseError`''s Axios branch assumed an object and recursed into it,\nlanding in the string branch. When the body was not JSON, `JSON.parse`\nthrew and the whole body became `DisplayableError.message`.\n\nModules render `parseError(e).message` directly, and so does `useAsync`.\nSo a 500 answered with an ASP.NET developer exception page, or an HTML\nerror page from a proxy or load balancer, put the entire document into\nthe toast and the blade banner.\n\n## Change\n\nThe exception is matched **before** the Axios branch — structurally, not\nby class, since `ApiException` is generated per client. The short\nmessage becomes `\"<status>: <exception message>\"` and the body goes into\n`details`, which is what `DisplayableError` separates the two for.\n\n## Two things left deliberately unchanged\n\n**A JSON body is still delegated as before,** so the platform''s own\n`message` / `exceptionMessage` keeps winning. Parsing that out is useful\nexisting behaviour, and this defect is only about bodies that are not\nJSON.\n\n**No status prefix was added to that JSON path.** It would have been\neasy to make every message read `\"400: Name is required\"`, but that\nchanges the wording of every API error in every app for no benefit to\nthis ticket.\n\n## Side effect worth knowing\n\n`useAsync` derives its notification dedup id from `message.slice(0, 80)`\n(`useAsync/index.ts:65`). Two different markup bodies share their first\n80 characters — `<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>…` — so distinct\nerrors collapsed into a single toast. Short status lines do not collide.\nThere is a test for it.\n\n## Tests\n\nFour added:\n\n| Case | Asserted |\n| --- | --- |\n| HTML body | short message is `500: …`, no `<html>` in it, body in\n`details` |\n| two markup bodies, different statuses | first 80 chars of the messages\ndiffer (the dedup case) |\n| JSON body | still yields the platform''s message, unprefixed |\n| empty body | falls back to the exception''s own message |\n\nThe existing Axios test still passes unchanged — its `response` is an\nobject, so the new guard does not match it.\n\n## Gates\n\nFramework unit suite **3753 tests / 401 files** · `yarn typecheck` ·\n`check:locales` · `check:layers`.\n\nRelates to VM-1744, VCST-5663","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfXvLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKi0QAI3/2a3SqrJSrookdQCShyZe\nQ4ntAYOBNv3I4mj33qsHftFdJgjoQZgIahqulWvbt+4fXP9Y9ykODFoXqlLCB9Rl\nsIGYY4HbUANLwOI9/AT49FmIksH/gEG1atU4SFy6txutBi/86RFLrz8FflVk6CDC\nPNBfWl9WflA/qn4EjkY8BwG8slkAekfNJV2twzQP3FSOCXtCt437WiHMAl876llj\nllmnarpH7GrUcrKYiA7OCh3C04Re09CAocR/++/hDJ+zVRANF1rwy0GVXslb8KUc\nHOOyufByrucZ1m1dNuHgHT5gE7MNhyYt6GYmAZWfPSiytQjGohwGrAtDcTXCdwPC\nPzXpbEuOCYBcWxmNA/2KE2pWDTW0sN8bfOnqPdUo2aL5cA+u7IeUYlvrvjuS6Jh0\noZl9gXJYLRjeTWd+mMlHugWHiVzVxu6VIJDiGwTPyai1ykYJWxIQ4fPxNSyXE80R\nDAOaLqjqQC3JuTSXUwrFztuO9BfzCcniIHVq0cXzkocIYK/EJ5EhtjRyMV3MFt1c\nHLIoKZLyHiPq+ZN6V5s63JGBWYX2MWJI0hz+T6jsospLiJDoHGj37/lbAgNBf7ow\nfDcHatXCFC3W0AAFc0+OMCfV6bEapzEViTeAhMgMfA3hjdmBOeGk+B1MxOHwTfhn\nsC6hYFq8NR/4Ep5+lukw\n=7V5h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T08:09:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGNhZjAxNTA0ZjkwNmI3Y2UxMzI4Y2I0YjViNzAzYzQwMThlNWJmZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96","sha":"9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96"}],"sha":"caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/caf01504f906b7ce1328cb4b5b703c4018e5bfd3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T08:08:11Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T08:08:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(interceptors): stop handing the login page''s HTML to API callers (#291)\n\nFixes **VCST-5688**, filed during VCST-5598 verification.\n\n## Problem\n\nSome platform configurations answer an unauthenticated API call with a\nredirect to the login page instead of a 401. `fetch` follows it\ntransparently, so the interceptor sees a 200 carrying HTML. It correctly\nrecognises the dead session, latches, signs out and redirects — and then\n**returns the login page to every caller anyway**.\n\nEach caller then tried to `JSON.parse` a document. On the dashboard''s\nsix concurrent widget calls that produced **1 session-expiry toast plus\n4 × `SyntaxError: Unexpected token ''<'', \"<!DOCTYPE \"... is not valid\nJSON`**, so the only message that tells the user what happened was\nstacked behind four meaningless ones.\n\nVCST-5598''s own acceptance — one sign-out and one expiry notification\nper burst — was already met. This is a separate defect in what the user\nactually sees.\n\n## Change\n\nA login-page response now rejects with `SessionExpiredError` instead of\nbeing returned. Failing the request is the honest answer: it returned no\ndata. Every request in the burst fails identically, so even a consumer\nthat does surface the error shows one message rather than one per\nrequest — `useAsync` already suppresses it while the expiry flag is set,\nand de-duplicates by message.\n\nTwo deliberate limits:\n\n- **Gated on the expiry flag.** A login page seen while nobody is signed\nin is still returned unchanged: before sign-in that is an expected\nanswer, not a session death, and failing those requests would break the\npre-auth flow.\n- **A 401 is still returned unchanged.** Its body is not a document, so\nnothing parses markup, and callers may legitimately branch on the status\nthemselves. Only the HTML-page path changes.\n\n## A trap worth knowing about\n\nThe sign-in POST goes to `/api/platform/security/login`, whose pathname\nmatches the login-page pattern — so its own 200 looks exactly like a\nsession death to `looksLikeLoginPage`. It survives only because\n`useUser.signIn` calls `resetSessionExpired()` **before** issuing the\nrequest (`useUser/index.ts:185`, request at `:188`). Swap that order and\nsign-in breaks with this change in place. Added a test that fails if it\nis ever swapped.\n\n## Note on how far this was verified\n\nThe original report was produced with a fault-injected response on the\ndeployed build, because this platform cannot produce the 302→HTML\ntrigger naturally (see VCST-5598). I did not re-run that injection: it\nmeans driving a shared dev environment, and the defect is provable from\nthe code path — the interceptor returned `response` on the login-page\nbranch.\n\nWhat I could not confirm by reading is which layer raised those four\ntoasts. `useAsync` both suppresses while the flag is set *and*\nde-duplicates by the first 80 characters of the message, so four\nidentical parse errors coming through it would have collapsed into one\ntoast. They did not, so they arrived by some other path. That is exactly\nwhy the fix is at the source rather than another consumer-side\nsuppression: no caller ever receives the document, so it does not matter\nwhich layer would have reported it.\n\n## Gates\n\nFramework unit suite **3748 tests / 401 files** · interceptor suite 16\n(3 added, 2 tightened) · `yarn typecheck` · `check:locales` ·\n`check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\nRelates to VCST-5688","tree":{"sha":"82bed939525241e273557a89e60e354525376a74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/82bed939525241e273557a89e60e354525376a74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96","verification":{"payload":"tree 82bed939525241e273557a89e60e354525376a74\nparent a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786608491 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786608491 +0300\n\nfix(interceptors): stop handing the login page''s HTML to API callers (#291)\n\nFixes **VCST-5688**, filed during VCST-5598 verification.\n\n## Problem\n\nSome platform configurations answer an unauthenticated API call with a\nredirect to the login page instead of a 401. `fetch` follows it\ntransparently, so the interceptor sees a 200 carrying HTML. It correctly\nrecognises the dead session, latches, signs out and redirects — and then\n**returns the login page to every caller anyway**.\n\nEach caller then tried to `JSON.parse` a document. On the dashboard''s\nsix concurrent widget calls that produced **1 session-expiry toast plus\n4 × `SyntaxError: Unexpected token ''<'', \"<!DOCTYPE \"... is not valid\nJSON`**, so the only message that tells the user what happened was\nstacked behind four meaningless ones.\n\nVCST-5598''s own acceptance — one sign-out and one expiry notification\nper burst — was already met. This is a separate defect in what the user\nactually sees.\n\n## Change\n\nA login-page response now rejects with `SessionExpiredError` instead of\nbeing returned. Failing the request is the honest answer: it returned no\ndata. Every request in the burst fails identically, so even a consumer\nthat does surface the error shows one message rather than one per\nrequest — `useAsync` already suppresses it while the expiry flag is set,\nand de-duplicates by message.\n\nTwo deliberate limits:\n\n- **Gated on the expiry flag.** A login page seen while nobody is signed\nin is still returned unchanged: before sign-in that is an expected\nanswer, not a session death, and failing those requests would break the\npre-auth flow.\n- **A 401 is still returned unchanged.** Its body is not a document, so\nnothing parses markup, and callers may legitimately branch on the status\nthemselves. Only the HTML-page path changes.\n\n## A trap worth knowing about\n\nThe sign-in POST goes to `/api/platform/security/login`, whose pathname\nmatches the login-page pattern — so its own 200 looks exactly like a\nsession death to `looksLikeLoginPage`. It survives only because\n`useUser.signIn` calls `resetSessionExpired()` **before** issuing the\nrequest (`useUser/index.ts:185`, request at `:188`). Swap that order and\nsign-in breaks with this change in place. Added a test that fails if it\nis ever swapped.\n\n## Note on how far this was verified\n\nThe original report was produced with a fault-injected response on the\ndeployed build, because this platform cannot produce the 302→HTML\ntrigger naturally (see VCST-5598). I did not re-run that injection: it\nmeans driving a shared dev environment, and the defect is provable from\nthe code path — the interceptor returned `response` on the login-page\nbranch.\n\nWhat I could not confirm by reading is which layer raised those four\ntoasts. `useAsync` both suppresses while the flag is set *and*\nde-duplicates by the first 80 characters of the message, so four\nidentical parse errors coming through it would have collapsed into one\ntoast. They did not, so they arrived by some other path. That is exactly\nwhy the fix is at the source rather than another consumer-side\nsuppression: no caller ever receives the document, so it does not matter\nwhich layer would have reported it.\n\n## Gates\n\nFramework unit suite **3748 tests / 401 files** · interceptor suite 16\n(3 added, 2 tightened) · `yarn typecheck` · `check:locales` ·\n`check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\nRelates to VCST-5688","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfXtrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6HcQADd6YI1YxuadlS2+ysus5Vmk\nieqkdmBuO2ZcztaHHQGof8uvjinwedftXOHvceKuPUL1tSJUh5XTIIqO4e3XilTY\nmGhfBM3RkPPo/vXWxbzhOZdYgFs94kduUawzyZveryZsCNu9lj6XRFkv/QTcEpbZ\nsz97aNuj6sSJoA40en4m7JitZRj8f1haN4txz7JfsSWDzAJ5LiKCakFM24v6pJYj\ndazRB/i1uSiD5+XU4hYJYXtjSEInqPacrobKewrgeUco+fp1NtogENWsc5RTMEAe\nWRlHwEKcrjC0Wt+KZ6L2RM9U2mI1cAGcTfBLbOKBWiCKSvfu5p8t+1kBMIoSEJO3\n3fYLBYGua9wiUQLFl/ER3a1VnVPDko4Ob7EUcmzbZj+j/NH2K6X0CT0ZnsVKlbWd\nz5s/AzN3AxUM9ehZYP+hQ2BnBvrvlNcNlzaVql/kWRWchsWG9TULbdJgPNmXrzlg\n5SHFKJImsS2JUpZrbC8QlTLUYk6nJhVCK+P7NS+LJPABLEaSKaDrrMx6gFC1U+pA\nIwbFZX/lhWwX+uJATbiaZvwWLtHM90KTiQo/BqHpj9AtU+R3BmWBRf4gi8qkmvFl\nUhYpj0vNIaymHmLjB2WowWM4wu60BntXgAJwL7gJoHbhAIHf3CJ8V9quMn7jnE2y\nWKCsuBZWqoQ+yhur0+kJ\n=u0Kz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T08:08:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDk3OTU5NTVkMjYwNTgxMjFmMGI0NmFhZjUzZmMxOTQ2YjFjY2VmOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761","sha":"a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761"}],"sha":"9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/9795955d26058121f0b46aaf53fc1946b1ccef96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:41:43Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:41:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-scheduler): announce all-day events up to their last inclusive day (#288)\n\nFixes **VCST-5678**, filed from the VcScheduler QA pass.\n\n## Problem\n\nAn all-day `end` is exclusive: an event ending at midnight runs through\nthe *previous* calendar day. The layout code\n(`useSchedulerEvents.weekSegments`) and the quick-info popover\n(`MonthEventPopover.dateRangeLabel`) both applied that rule. The month\nevent bar and the timeline did not — they formatted `end` raw.\n\nResult: for a one-day all-day event on Jul 15, the chip announced `\"Esc\nRetest: Jul 15, 2026 – Jul 16, 2026\"` while the popover for the same\nevent said `\"July 15th, 2026\"`. Two surfaces describing the same event\ndifferently, and the announced range was a day longer than the event.\n\n## Change\n\n| File | What |\n| --- | --- |\n| `MonthEventBar.vue` | subtract 1 ms before formatting; collapse a\nsingle-day span to one date |\n| `SchedulerTimelineView.vue` | same, but only for all-day events —\ntimed events keep their real times |\n| `useTimelineTimeGrid.ts` | export `isAllDayEvent` so the view can\nbranch on it |\n\nMonth bars only ever render all-day spans — `weekSegments` skips\neverything else — so they apply the rule unconditionally. The timeline\nrenders both kinds, so it needs the predicate. That predicate already\nexisted twice (here and in `useSchedulerEvents`); exporting the existing\none avoids a third copy.\n\n## Tests\n\nFour added. The existing bar test asserted only that the label\n*contains* the title, which is exactly why this shipped:\n\n- one-day all-day event → single date, no range separator\n- multi-day all-day event → exact string, last inclusive day\n- timeline all-day bar → single date, no meaningless `12:00 AM`\n- timeline timed event → start and end times preserved\n\n## Deliberately not changed: the editor''s End field\n\nThe ticket also notes the built-in editor shows `7/16/2026` for a\nsingle-day event. That field is a two-way binding on `local.end`, so\nshowing the inclusive day means converting back to exclusive on save —\nget that wrong and it writes dates that are off by one, on every save.\nIt is also a product question rather than a labelling one: should an\nall-day event ending Jul 15 display \"Jul 15\" or \"Jul 16\" in an editable\nfield?\n\nLeft as-is and flagged on the ticket rather than changed quietly inside\nan `aria-label` fix.\n\n## Gates\n\nScheduler unit tests **194** (28 files) · story suite for VcScheduler\n**22** · `yarn typecheck` · `stylelint` · `check:locales` ·\n`check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\n`vc-scheduler.docs.md` now states the inclusive-end rule for announced\nlabels, since the exclusive/inclusive distinction is the whole defect.\n\nRelates to VCST-5678","tree":{"sha":"41ecfb3386777d4d0f700e577ca42e87024b17ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/41ecfb3386777d4d0f700e577ca42e87024b17ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761","verification":{"payload":"tree 41ecfb3386777d4d0f700e577ca42e87024b17ed\nparent 49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786545703 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786545703 +0300\n\nfix(vc-scheduler): announce all-day events up to their last inclusive day (#288)\n\nFixes **VCST-5678**, filed from the VcScheduler QA pass.\n\n## Problem\n\nAn all-day `end` is exclusive: an event ending at midnight runs through\nthe *previous* calendar day. The layout code\n(`useSchedulerEvents.weekSegments`) and the quick-info popover\n(`MonthEventPopover.dateRangeLabel`) both applied that rule. The month\nevent bar and the timeline did not — they formatted `end` raw.\n\nResult: for a one-day all-day event on Jul 15, the chip announced `\"Esc\nRetest: Jul 15, 2026 – Jul 16, 2026\"` while the popover for the same\nevent said `\"July 15th, 2026\"`. Two surfaces describing the same event\ndifferently, and the announced range was a day longer than the event.\n\n## Change\n\n| File | What |\n| --- | --- |\n| `MonthEventBar.vue` | subtract 1 ms before formatting; collapse a\nsingle-day span to one date |\n| `SchedulerTimelineView.vue` | same, but only for all-day events —\ntimed events keep their real times |\n| `useTimelineTimeGrid.ts` | export `isAllDayEvent` so the view can\nbranch on it |\n\nMonth bars only ever render all-day spans — `weekSegments` skips\neverything else — so they apply the rule unconditionally. The timeline\nrenders both kinds, so it needs the predicate. That predicate already\nexisted twice (here and in `useSchedulerEvents`); exporting the existing\none avoids a third copy.\n\n## Tests\n\nFour added. The existing bar test asserted only that the label\n*contains* the title, which is exactly why this shipped:\n\n- one-day all-day event → single date, no range separator\n- multi-day all-day event → exact string, last inclusive day\n- timeline all-day bar → single date, no meaningless `12:00 AM`\n- timeline timed event → start and end times preserved\n\n## Deliberately not changed: the editor''s End field\n\nThe ticket also notes the built-in editor shows `7/16/2026` for a\nsingle-day event. That field is a two-way binding on `local.end`, so\nshowing the inclusive day means converting back to exclusive on save —\nget that wrong and it writes dates that are off by one, on every save.\nIt is also a product question rather than a labelling one: should an\nall-day event ending Jul 15 display \"Jul 15\" or \"Jul 16\" in an editable\nfield?\n\nLeft as-is and flagged on the ticket rather than changed quietly inside\nan `aria-label` fix.\n\n## Gates\n\nScheduler unit tests **194** (28 files) · story suite for VcScheduler\n**22** · `yarn typecheck` · `stylelint` · `check:locales` ·\n`check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\n\n`vc-scheduler.docs.md` now states the inclusive-end rule for announced\nlabels, since the exclusive/inclusive distinction is the whole defect.\n\nRelates to VCST-5678","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfIYnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgTgQAGEmh37uNGcExXtlqB1qwEjI\nKwS9wI8QMzORy1lpyIZPNShXlvW8maM26Zkx/KCSwMnwI9Ub2d8NoTN16Kf3UB8B\nygxJJvgXnaMY2O9TCS+s5bnGMGpejnRoWI4IAsSzqvtCLZJigFCwJasHULcmxt3W\nMx1IEFsDjrMUsKHbEXUw3MZUoD7ewR3db9JrvwqzkVjJKrV9ynlw/pNeZcYLZOTr\nkSiVvmORWxZ5jEd2fNMDIKBg7g1BRpldnrQffm5cF3hYourvjnqsFFxiobXPqvq4\nJNIomjetpnr/JKkNrrmjvVmcYfMgFrvuVLAYEtrPZKPbiP2Tao7TitSpti/t7W9M\nVGo4BXZktq3rUb2tzIRjFrA7vmlYAqww6v2cjeMm6haXlIODSerm1fk3qt50eHg6\nS1U1rTlbD9SDACXFtsl1SgJo8mJxIJsdhpyMSfmDO/OHR4eEAZ6rvgpuECEw0kzX\nia5q5/NbhuLxGXCXctbllGcsjjlMKY8nWvwjTg9zEY33sFoAQ/3rZYfqie8ZZ/Sr\nmpH15H2Kw/Z/OKQ71JHqgk3spA+VaVRWwYQN0fI7sxq8o4Iq+VBov9WoI51L2XtB\nSfBWpFiyUAPFFug2AydlfPytWrHtBduPhAsC0qNNPdN91/+qhoPscxI+CMHcIqfE\npPyTdt+8pdOxETFhxefX\n=AOLk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T14:41:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKGE1MWMxMzU2ZjkyOWQ1ZjdmOGExNzkyNWMzNTE3OTI2Mzk5YWI3NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4","sha":"49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4"}],"sha":"a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/a51c1356f929d5f7f8a17925c3517926399ab761"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:23:00Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:23:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-scheduler): make the TimelineView story''s toolbar actually switch views (#290)\n\nFixes **VCST-5672**, filed from the VcScheduler QA pass.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `TimelineView` story is specifically about switching views from its\nown toolbar, but it used the meta-level args-bound render, which leaves\n`date`/`view` frozen — the comment above `renderInteractive` in the same\nfile already spells that out. So the toolbar emitted `update:view` into\nnothing: the grid stayed on Timeline Day, the header kept its date, and\n`aria-pressed` never moved.\n\nQA''s diagnosis was right — this is a story-authoring gap, not a\ncomponent defect. It still matters, because the published Storybook is\nthe component''s documentation surface, and there it reads as a broken\ncomponent.\n\n`TimelineDay`, `TimelineWeek` and `TimelineToday` already used\n`renderInteractive`. This story was the only one that did not.\n\n## Change\n\nOne line: `render: renderInteractive`.\n\n## Audit of the rest of the file\n\nTwo other stories also use the frozen render, and both are correct as-is\n— worth recording so nobody \"fixes\" them later:\n\n| Story | Uses frozen render because |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ReadOnly` | it is about selecting/clicking events, which is internal\ncomponent state, not args |\n| `EmitMode` | it explicitly asks the reader to watch the Actions panel;\nnothing should change on screen |\n\n`TimelineView` was the only mismatch between what a story claims and\nwhat it wires.\n\n## Verification\n\nIn a running Storybook, clicking \"Timeline Week\" in the component''s own\ntoolbar:\n\n| | Before the click | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| day header columns | 1 | 7 |\n| toolbar title | `15 July 2026` | `13 – 19 Jul 2026` |\n| `aria-pressed` | `Timeline Day` | `Timeline Week` |\n\nPressing Next then advances the title to `20 – 26 Jul 2026`, confirming\ndate navigation writes back too.\n\n## Gates\n\nVcScheduler story suite **22** · `eslint` · `check:locales` ·\n`check:layers`.\n\nRelates to VCST-5672","tree":{"sha":"ab04cb9b493a50f31470e986c61659b27ad20439","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/ab04cb9b493a50f31470e986c61659b27ad20439"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4","verification":{"payload":"tree ab04cb9b493a50f31470e986c61659b27ad20439\nparent 30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786544580 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786544580 +0300\n\nfix(vc-scheduler): make the TimelineView story''s toolbar actually switch views (#290)\n\nFixes **VCST-5672**, filed from the VcScheduler QA pass.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `TimelineView` story is specifically about switching views from its\nown toolbar, but it used the meta-level args-bound render, which leaves\n`date`/`view` frozen — the comment above `renderInteractive` in the same\nfile already spells that out. So the toolbar emitted `update:view` into\nnothing: the grid stayed on Timeline Day, the header kept its date, and\n`aria-pressed` never moved.\n\nQA''s diagnosis was right — this is a story-authoring gap, not a\ncomponent defect. It still matters, because the published Storybook is\nthe component''s documentation surface, and there it reads as a broken\ncomponent.\n\n`TimelineDay`, `TimelineWeek` and `TimelineToday` already used\n`renderInteractive`. This story was the only one that did not.\n\n## Change\n\nOne line: `render: renderInteractive`.\n\n## Audit of the rest of the file\n\nTwo other stories also use the frozen render, and both are correct as-is\n— worth recording so nobody \"fixes\" them later:\n\n| Story | Uses frozen render because |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ReadOnly` | it is about selecting/clicking events, which is internal\ncomponent state, not args |\n| `EmitMode` | it explicitly asks the reader to watch the Actions panel;\nnothing should change on screen |\n\n`TimelineView` was the only mismatch between what a story claims and\nwhat it wires.\n\n## Verification\n\nIn a running Storybook, clicking \"Timeline Week\" in the component''s own\ntoolbar:\n\n| | Before the click | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| day header columns | 1 | 7 |\n| toolbar title | `15 July 2026` | `13 – 19 Jul 2026` |\n| `aria-pressed` | `Timeline Day` | `Timeline Week` |\n\nPressing Next then advances the title to `20 – 26 Jul 2026`, confirming\ndate navigation writes back too.\n\n## Gates\n\nVcScheduler story suite **22** · `eslint` · `check:locales` ·\n`check:layers`.\n\nRelates to VCST-5672","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfIHECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7DIQAHZ5baJuJyoudbTbbcuoDnXb\nrHLcF0qYq5e4kXfEsjDKJS9NAzTQyyjAf7kW6q9pG/rZpGKL2LA49B2aEzfKMcxg\n8+Z3us4u5rc1La1fbykl9NJpGE+2VIR6COpCXowhhgOxxVKsQSjAR1aXqctiTOgm\nwJU7rbmXUnwBH3rY6ZMWNBd5vCI49FokvjSeIXSLaK4RteCLsYRX1PNxI8NVUWES\nR6aDDxyZ/jDqp4PBexI17TQgvjkhV4lCzWEYuMkxQANQz9isP6zU51FGuvLhkl4O\nqo0M+/B6r3pL1CsGh3TkdLsVGyPH41kmQi98P9nxNDViAkC/513J8MUYu2QUGPwD\nM2Wj5yBZnXJH0Jg3H2mnxOwoNM2kIf+nEpPhnBXD+ijDuCyiWxZ7bSYLR8f03o/H\n5cSxB+2B/phl+JQJ0+iYrr43P+UOBv81xyhMCeXgcTxGkMqXnozBVQxoSv8kmNQ/\nBzWeathNuYJsz3O84CbaRcIB/0ogz43utunhx/Coq3+em32bp6MOszz677WU5RBN\nnr7QOYQ+6uGH7TeJ5eogV7iFufi0B8P1ObM2LZNtFgBhGJfAYbLJPVxU/aMqgiPA\nERerQcqG8f9TdI0tnOk6kIOr43enSaVnqcYpqcrp/IQKP3aafCnG2bGuxb2qJ9nS\nFv8aK5WvljAjEKwNk4Sz\n=MXLT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T14:23:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDQ5NDkyZjhlZjJkZTBjNGVjNmQ1Y2QzZWFmZTY3ZGE2MzQ0YWJiYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c","sha":"30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c"}],"sha":"49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/49492f8ef2de0c4ec6d5cd3eafe67da6344abba4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63730586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maksimzinchuk","id":63730586,"login":"maksimzinchuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzMwNTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maksimzinchuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:16:25Z","email":"63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maksim Zinchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:16:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vc-scheduler): paint the component''s own surface so dark theme is legible (#289)\n\nFixes **VCST-5677**, filed from the VcScheduler QA pass.\n\n## Problem\n\n`VcScheduler` draws its own border and border-radius — it presents as a\ncard — but painted no background. Only the day cells painted theirs. So\nthe toolbar and the weekday header, which have no background of their\nown, fell through to whatever sat behind the component.\n\nOn a themed host surface that looks correct, which is why the vendor\nportal never showed it. On a plain page it breaks in dark theme: the\ntheme variables flip, the foreground becomes near-white, and the\nbackdrop stays the browser''s white.\n\nMeasured on the Default story (`data-theme=\"dark\"` applied by the\nStorybook theme decorator):\n\n| Element | Dark theme, before | Dark theme, after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `.vc-scheduler` | `rgba(0,0,0,0)` | `rgb(36,42,46)` |\n| toolbar / weekday header | `rgba(0,0,0,0)` → white page behind |\ninherits the card surface |\n| foreground | `rgb(235,235,235)` | unchanged |\n| **contrast** | **≈1.1:1** | **12.2:1** |\n\n`.vc-scheduler__day-cell` was `rgb(31,36,40)` throughout — unaffected,\nsince it paints itself. That asymmetry is exactly what made the toolbar\nand header look broken while the grid below them looked right.\n\nWCAG 1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum), AA — needs 4.5:1.\n\n## Change\n\nOne rule on the root, using the same token the day cells already use, so\nthe whole card is one surface in both themes:\n\n```scss\n--scheduler-surface-color: var(--additional-50, #fff);\nbackground: var(--scheduler-surface-color);\n```\n\nExposed as a custom property to match the existing\n`--scheduler-border-color`, so a host can override it, and documented in\nthe CSS Custom Properties table.\n\n## Why CI did not catch this\n\n`color-contrast` is disabled in the story axe config as a documented\ndesign decision (the brand palette is governed separately), so no gate\nevaluates this class of defect. Worth remembering when judging how much\nthe green story suite proves — it found nothing here, and there was a\n1.1:1 contrast failure on a shipped component.\n\n## Gates\n\nScheduler unit tests **190** (28 files) · VcScheduler story suite **22**\n· `stylelint` · `check:locales` · `check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\nVerified by measuring computed styles in both themes, before and after,\nrather than by eye.\n\nRelates to VCST-5677","tree":{"sha":"42ed45bfa17afb082e4172c397833cbcefccd679","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/trees/42ed45bfa17afb082e4172c397833cbcefccd679"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/git/commits/30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c","verification":{"payload":"tree 42ed45bfa17afb082e4172c397833cbcefccd679\nparent 6e512da0161caf997f8b3a7067518c0e2baac807\nauthor Maksim Zinchuk <63730586+maksimzinchuk@users.noreply.github.com> 1786544185 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786544185 +0300\n\nfix(vc-scheduler): paint the component''s own surface so dark theme is legible (#289)\n\nFixes **VCST-5677**, filed from the VcScheduler QA pass.\n\n## Problem\n\n`VcScheduler` draws its own border and border-radius — it presents as a\ncard — but painted no background. Only the day cells painted theirs. So\nthe toolbar and the weekday header, which have no background of their\nown, fell through to whatever sat behind the component.\n\nOn a themed host surface that looks correct, which is why the vendor\nportal never showed it. On a plain page it breaks in dark theme: the\ntheme variables flip, the foreground becomes near-white, and the\nbackdrop stays the browser''s white.\n\nMeasured on the Default story (`data-theme=\"dark\"` applied by the\nStorybook theme decorator):\n\n| Element | Dark theme, before | Dark theme, after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `.vc-scheduler` | `rgba(0,0,0,0)` | `rgb(36,42,46)` |\n| toolbar / weekday header | `rgba(0,0,0,0)` → white page behind |\ninherits the card surface |\n| foreground | `rgb(235,235,235)` | unchanged |\n| **contrast** | **≈1.1:1** | **12.2:1** |\n\n`.vc-scheduler__day-cell` was `rgb(31,36,40)` throughout — unaffected,\nsince it paints itself. That asymmetry is exactly what made the toolbar\nand header look broken while the grid below them looked right.\n\nWCAG 1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum), AA — needs 4.5:1.\n\n## Change\n\nOne rule on the root, using the same token the day cells already use, so\nthe whole card is one surface in both themes:\n\n```scss\n--scheduler-surface-color: var(--additional-50, #fff);\nbackground: var(--scheduler-surface-color);\n```\n\nExposed as a custom property to match the existing\n`--scheduler-border-color`, so a host can override it, and documented in\nthe CSS Custom Properties table.\n\n## Why CI did not catch this\n\n`color-contrast` is disabled in the story axe config as a documented\ndesign decision (the brand palette is governed separately), so no gate\nevaluates this class of defect. Worth remembering when judging how much\nthe green story suite proves — it found nothing here, and there was a\n1.1:1 contrast failure on a shipped component.\n\n## Gates\n\nScheduler unit tests **190** (28 files) · VcScheduler story suite **22**\n· `stylelint` · `check:locales` · `check:layers` · `docs:lint` 0 errors.\nVerified by measuring computed styles in both themes, before and after,\nrather than by eye.\n\nRelates to VCST-5677","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfIA5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADzgQABb0bP+9UzBpV51dVJImGoJj\nIf42aUdwNRZjv//kmto0cBOn80QJWEMgYgufyP7+ZiA555mC0450+PZvtfDHDcJo\nZgtg2lhNZRr6MaWrxcuNBYnwA60pNyfVwInSrIhBVCKImnzFx2JGErPfkTbYSNiQ\nriFXjb+W5m1r0toPxczJD152KancTSNCWZuUeG0QkrFm181VySlsuvtHdT3shELX\nbV3pjYcf7ipH3ty2o7iqK1RC9vXBq5IZQNbOi+9/Odq0RNBk3cSfizTY5YlNQ3zj\n+T7XWQa+68xyCziwcWiAvRy6jKUB5yCwloSzrpmm+M9qyhGnNGeDkpS/w/LLEal8\np7G+Grs5U44ZckoguwS4f6V4j5A9x1k/vVQFEusUygW3p6Q5LN+KZQglZNKBqmLK\nmR7Du/OT9D2KbztcHLxNfHnh1Fh/olGgGrHVSFarHNkwqzBhePI31ohH1xKZpJqs\nWG7wX7w2DK9E4i92XRe/LH2ZB4nBUUyWH5Fwg8FZwVurMpkO1UMKobEfxBr70P6i\nY3N6rmSlyS1IL2FjisNg/F9ubvyf70/T58meWEXE8BzsruA8MwZw4hvpHKxi8Ngm\n0BgKE15WpM0HnaYjECe+S7GSOQZ0cfHG+t3DAFRok80o8NFgjtoobWnFVQXKbYiJ\nRtwsSO5i3ZwL/7W/bGvc\n=n3I/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T14:16:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c","node_id":"C_kwDOFRn0ndoAKDMwMjc5YmY1MjgzYzEzOTBiMjI3YzhhNTA4YWY3MDU2NmNmMDRlMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commit/6e512da0161caf997f8b3a7067518c0e2baac807","sha":"6e512da0161caf997f8b3a7067518c0e2baac807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/6e512da0161caf997f8b3a7067518c0e2baac807"}],"sha":"30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits/30279bf5283c1390b227c8a508af70566cf04e0c"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-shell/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=386bac18be966e5ebf976eda22dd523d55299291&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A39%3A28.090Z"}');
